window.DR_DATA=window.DR_DATA||{};window.DR_DATA["lore"]=[{"id":"kw-50077","title":"Sand Eaters","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_27_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Cabal legions that have invaded Sol.\n\nAs a military empire, the Cabal show no mercy towards humanity. Once they established their foothold in the region, the Sand Eaters immediately launched an attack on Veridia—the first step in their occupation of the entire Red Sea Rift. However, Iron Lord Saladin led a squad of Lightbearer under the Iron Banner to Veridia. The Lightbearers' arrival would throw a massive wrench into the Sand Eaters' plans to occupy the Rift."}]},{"id":"kw-60126","title":"The Iron Champion","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A Lightbearer who represents the Iron Lords in one-on-one duels against Warlords.\n\nThe Iron Champion is a product of war, intended to put an end to it. Wanting to avoid more unnecessary casualties, Lord Radegast issued a challenge to all Warlords: a fair one-on-one duel to decide the outcome of an entire battle. This meant the Iron Lords needed to select a duelist who couldn't—and wouldn't—lose.\nIn her first years as a Lightbearer, Lady Jolder was held captive by a Warlord named Yekaterina and forced to fight in her ring called \"the Kraav.\" This hardship would forge her into the master duelist she is today. Ever since she took the title of Iron Champion, she has never once let her allies down, for she has defeated every Warlord who has dared to accept her challenge."}]},{"id":"kw-50013","title":"Splicers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A technological alliance of cutting-edge scientists among the Fallen.\n\nUpon realizing that the major Houses in the Long Drift were using Riis's legacies to fight amongst themselves, the Archpriests of the Splicers convened and came to the consensus that control over technology was imperative to preventing the Eliksni from destroying themselves before they could retrieve the Great Machine. Thus, the techno-priests would determine the level of technology available to a House. And so, while the Splicers had no intention of chasing power, they were secretly and practically influencing the social patterns of their entire society."}]},{"id":"kw-60062","title":"Jiangshi Metro Communications Hub","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A crucial global communications hub located in Jiangshi Metro. It has seen better days.\n\nThe hub appears to be missing some key parts. The Jiangshi Metro guerrillas are searching for relevant resources and materials to get it back online."}]},{"id":"kw-40013","title":"Ayuela","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_12_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"Leader of the guerrilla scout team in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nBoth of her parents were killed by the Fallen, so Ayuela holds a bitter hatred of their kind. Because of the nominal lord Radegast offering limited support for her home, Ayuela also has a deep prejudice against the Iron Lords.\nUnder the training of her adoptive father, Mu Ying, Ayuela has been learning about wilderness survival, scouting, weaponry since she was a child. As a result, she became a skilled veteran at a young age."}]},{"id":"kw-10068","title":"Jaren 4","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h303_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Appears indifferent, but won't turn a blind eye to those in life-threatening danger—if he believes their life to be saving, that is."}]},{"id":"kw-60127","title":"The White Tiger General","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An exclusive title held by the general of the Samarkand militia.\n\nWhen the Lightbearer Xuan Wei served the Warlord Kāmihā, he was dispatched to Samarkand to stop the advance of Iron Lord Timur and his army. Following his arrival, Xuan Wei trained the local militia into a powerful and disciplined troop of elites, which he called the \"Tiger's Claws\" in reference to the Eastern guardian deity of soldiers, the White Tiger. Naturally, \"White Tiger General\" became the title held by the troop's leader."}]},{"id":"kw-60063","title":"Icy Lake","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_103_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Once a reservoir that supported Jiangshi residents' industry and daily life back in the Golden Age, it was frozen over during the climate change caused by the Collapse.\n\nRecent investigations by Lightbearers have confirmed the existence of a malicious alien army lurking beneath the frozen lake. Judging from their appearance and habits, they may be the monsters rumored to \"haunt the Moon\"—the Hive."}]},{"id":"kw-60128","title":"Mysterious Cargo","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Strange cargo being escorted by the Cabal.\n\nThe Cabal dug this object up in the drilling zone. They treat it with great importance, even assigning an escort to bring the \"cargo\" back. To put an end to the threat at its root, Wolf intercepted the cargo from the garrisoned Cabal. Upon finding it, Zev discovered it was being kept in a box made from a unique material that prevents her from scanning to see what is inside."}]},{"id":"kw-60064","title":"Temporal Rift","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A rift in Haven that transcends time and space.\n\nAccording to local scholar Mishra's reports, more and more Lightbearers are claiming to have entered the rift, though they have fortunately returned unharmed."}]},{"id":"kw-60065","title":"Artifact of Riis","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A powerful artifact from the Fallen's home world, Riis.\n\nThough it is currently located in the wreckage of a Ketch that crashed in Jiangshi Metro, the House of Devils are trying to retrieve it."}]},{"id":"kw-60066","title":"Artifact of Riis","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A powerful artifact from the Fallen's home world, Riis.\n\nThe artifact was overloaded with Light and broken during the fight in the Ketch wreckage. It seems that only through paracausal forces capable of turning back time can the Riis-made parts needed to repair it be found."}]},{"id":"kw-50012","title":"Splicers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A technological alliance of cutting-edge scientists among the Fallen.\n\nBack in the Golden Age of Riis, the Splicers were engineering sects, religious in nature and without actual power, composed of pioneering scientists who worshiped the Great Machine and controlled the vast majority of the Eliksni's high-end technology. However, after the Whirlwind arrived and the Long Drift began, these controllers of Riis's legacies found themselves being pulled by forces on all sides. The techno-priests dispatched to the major Houses gradually rose to higher ranks, particularly the Archons."}]},{"id":"kw-60067","title":"Artifact of Riis","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A powerful artifact from the Fallen's home world, Riis.\n\nAfter finding two special components with the help of the Nine and an Ahamkara's magic, Kevarrh, her heart filled with a sense of honor, was able to repair the relic."}]},{"id":"kw-60068","title":"Jiangshi Metro Communications Hub","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A crucial global communications hub located in Jiangshi Metro. It has seen better days.\n\nIt is missing a key component called a quantum tuner, a Golden Age device capable of quantum signal processing and transmission."}]},{"id":"kw-60069","title":"Data Center","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A lab located in the outskirts of Jiangshi Metro. It houses a great deal of research and data from humanity's Golden Age."}]},{"id":"kw-50101","title":"Harvesters","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Heavy transport aircraft used by the Cabal for battlefield support.\n\nThe spacious cabin of a Harvester is enough to accommodate an entire Cabal combat squad, and it has enough power to transport a Goliath Tank. Although they are nominally transport spacecraft, some Harvesters are also equipped with homing missiles, letting them provide supporting fire from above after completing their transport duties."}]},{"id":"kw-60070","title":"Jiangshi Metro Data Archaeologists","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A group who tried to use Golden Age technology to restore Jiangshi Metro.\n\nFourteen years ago, they infiltrated the Data Center to retrieve the records and technology stored within, which would aid in human civilization's revival.\nThe archaeologists were protected by a group of Lightbearers serving under Radegast, and following several conflicts with the Fallen, they were forced to disband, putting an end to the retrieval efforts."}]},{"id":"kw-60071","title":"Jiangshi Metro Communications Hub","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A crucial global communication hub located in Jiangshi Metro. It has seen better days.\n\nThough Radegast and Wolf seized the quantum tuner from Belaaks-1, Devil Sentry, it appears Golden Age permission from the Lanyue Space Station is still needed before the communications hub can get back online."}]},{"id":"kw-50031","title":"Hive","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_25_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A race of terrifying, ancient alien arthropods.\n\nSince the Golden Age, there has been a legend circulating on Earth: \"the Moon's haunted.\" This legend may have originated from the tragic K1 Dig Site accident, though Taketori Industry also discovered the chitinous shells of alien creatures during Project Lunarin. But throughout the Golden Age, no one came into contact with the Hive.\nBut they are real, lurking beneath the surface, waiting for the day when they will finally emerge."}]},{"id":"kw-60072","title":"Lanyue Space Station","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_104_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A space station that humans built during the Golden Age, reached via Jiangshi Metro's Space Elevator.\n\nSeemingly following orders from the Splicers and Issakis, the Fallen have been looting Jiangshi Metro's Golden Age tech and materials, using this steady stream of resources to convert this Lanyue station into a space fortress, which he dubbed the \"Eclipse Monolith.\"\nJiangshi Metro is no match for such a massive Fallen army."}]},{"id":"kw-50010","title":"Archons","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A mechanical cleric leader in Fallen society and one of the three leaders of a House.\n\nThey serve as the conduit connecting the Fallen and their mechanical creations, communicating the Kell's wishes to the Prime Servitor. As part of their day-to-day duties, they maintain the Prime Servitor as well as keep it safe.\nWithout the Archon's protection, the Prime Servitor would be left vulnerable, putting the entire House at risk."}]},{"id":"kw-60073","title":"Jiangshi Metro Communications Hub","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A crucial global communication hub located in Jiangshi Metro. It has seen better days.\n\nWith the quantum tuner and the Golden Age permission, Jiangshi Metro's communications hub is finally back online. Now, Haven can use this hub to connect with other human settlements."}]},{"id":"kw-60074","title":"Knowledge Synthesizer","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An online knowledge management system with main servers located in Haven's Archives.\n\nThe Knowledge Synthesizer is open to all visitors for free and provides summaries of the knowledge and information archivists have collected over years of work. With more and more Lightbearers coming to Haven, it has become an excellent way for them to understand the world."}]},{"id":"kw-60075","title":"Shadowshaper Duels","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A card game that started at Haven's \"Bad Old Time\" tavern and has rapidly been gaining popularity.\n\nShadowshaper Duels' cards feature Lightbearers, mortal warriors, and enemies of the Light. From a certain perspective, it's become a way to quickly understand these factions. The owner of Bad Old Time, Wu Ming, claims he designed this game personally."}]},{"id":"kw-50099","title":"Goliath Tanks","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_72_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Heavy suspended tanks piloted by the Cabal.\n\nGoliath Tanks' main guns are their 110mm \"Planet Crackers\"—weapons powerful enough to destroy bunkers and trigger shockwaves when fired. They are also outfitted with various light weapons, including machine gun turrets and missile launchers, letting them adapt to various battlefield conditions. The Goliath Tanks' suspension thrusters provide bursts of acceleration and unexpected maneuverability, but they can also be exploited as the tanks' only weak spots."}]},{"id":"kw-60076","title":"The Whisperers","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A neutral intelligence network born during the Dark Age, created by and primarily comprised of Ghosts.\n\nThis Ghost-led organization collected and controlled the flow of information, even exerting influence over the Lightbearers partnered with those Ghosts to impact the outcome of the Dark Age on some level..\nDue to the network's nature and Ghost leadership, most forces are wary and even hostile towards the Whisperers, leading their members to conceal their identities."}]},{"id":"kw-60077","title":"Iron Wolves","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The Iron Lords' hand-picked second-in-command and successors.\n\nLightbearers may possess immortal bodies, but after experiencing the cruelties of the Dark Age, the Iron Lords know all too well that their lives are not necessarily without end. They may not fear death, but they know that the Iron Banner's ideals must survive even if they do not. Thus, each Iron Lord picks a trusted Lightbearer to uphold their ideals in their stead if misfortune befalls them."}]},{"id":"kw-60078","title":"The Iron Champion","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A Lightbearer who represents the Iron Lords in one-on-one duels against Warlords.\n\nThe Iron Champion is a unique title granted by the Iron Lords, and its holder one of a kind among its ranks.\nAll manner of legends surrounding the champion, Lady Jolder, have spread around the Iron Lords' territories. Some of her heroic feats have been subject to some unavoidable exaggeration, but there is one tale that nobody doubts: Lady Jolder became Iron Champion by defeating all of her fellow Iron Lords in one-on-one duels."}]},{"id":"kw-60079","title":"Veridia's Miners","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The most represented occupation among Veridia's residents.\n\nIn the Dark Age, Veridia was one of the most important logistical support areas for the Iron Lords, as the high-quality minerals mined here provided a solid foundation for the Iron Lords' battles. However, with the arrival of Cabal, the mining zone fell into enemy hands, and they were struggling to maintain the Sentinel's Light barrier due to a lack of Radiancite. Driven by both their values and the pressure to survive, the miners here are willing to risk being captured and venture deep into the mines to bring back Radiancite—the key to their protection."}]},{"id":"kw-60080","title":"The Veridian Union","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The actual governing body of Veridia, composed of representatives from each of Veridia's industries.\n\nIn peacetime, these elected leaders representing the town's different industries would hold regular meetings to discuss matters and, ultimately, come to a final agreement through democratic means under the union president's leadership.\nThis parliamentary model had already taken shape during Lord Gareth's rule over Veridia. Afterwards, Gareth was nominally only the military leader of Veridia—until he succumbed to madness and monopolized power, at which the union, too, existed in name only.\nAfter Gareth was ultimately overthrown, the people restored the original political model."}]},{"id":"kw-50033","title":"Hidden Swarm","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_25_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A branch of the Hive led by Prince Crota, the Eater of Hope.\n\nEarly on, when Crota was just born, Oryx explained his purpose and duty to him. In his words, a false god known as the Traveler spread false hope throughout the universe, and it was the duty of the Hive to put an end to it. Years later, Crota, who had been promoted to prince, led his brood to the Moon. There, they took root and multiplied, ready to launch their destined attack on Earth."}]},{"id":"kw-60082","title":"Red Sea Rift","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_108_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An area with abundant ore deposits and materials salvageable from sunken ships.\n\nThe Red Sea Rift is part of Saladin's territory, and its wealth of minerals makes it a logistically key location for the Iron Lords. In recent years, however, it has been the victim of a Cabal invasion."}]},{"id":"kw-50092","title":"Phalanx","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_65_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Cabal soldiers equipped with huge shields.\n\nPhalanx soldiers are used more for defense than offense, often defending strongholds or blocking incoming fire for their comrades. That doesn't mean they cannot attack, though. When in close proximity, a Phalanx can deliver heavy shield bashes powerful enough to make those who underestimate them pay a painful price for their recklessness."}]},{"id":"kw-60083","title":"Veridia","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_109_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A human settlement built beneath the wreckage of the largest cargo ship in the Red Sea Rift, \"The Veridia.\"\n\nGareth founded Veridia, a place rich in resources thanks to the Golden Age cargo ships scattered on the dry seabed, during the Dark Age. Despite its small population, Veridia is a self-sustaining human settlement with its main industry centered around mineral extraction. As such, the town is home to a good deal of personnel who support transportation, maintenance, and other services for daily living. Their work all circles back to mining in one way or another."}]},{"id":"kw-60084","title":"Veridia","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_109_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A human settlement built beneath the wreckage of the largest cargo ship in the Red Sea Rift, \"The Veridia.\"\n\nAfter the death of his friend Gareth, Saladin's strong wish to protect Veridia was fulfilled through Harrow's abilities. This led its people to discover the Sentinel's hand and Radiancite at the cost of a Cabal invasion, with the aliens brought by the very ore that aided Veridia. This ability also corrupted Saladin, making him paranoid, dictatorial, and unwilling to receive help from Haven and Radegast.\nVeridia's fate was entirely altered by but one single wish."}]},{"id":"kw-50053","title":"Niviks-3","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The Fallen Servitor that tried to capture Jiangshi Metro Town Hall.\n\nIt's hard to ascertain why it suddenly attacked Jiangshi Metro Town Hall. The only lead may be the large amount of Golden Age construction materials kept nearby."}]},{"id":"kw-60086","title":"Massive Skeleton","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_110_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The skeletal remains of an unknown creature perched in the Red Sea Rift. Their size far exceeds that of any creature known to human biologists.\n\nThe skull of this skeleton was pierced by the Sentinel's weapon, but its own bone spikes are deeply embedded in the mech's body. After dying alongside its foe, its shattered bones scattered throughout the Red Sea Rift. According to the locals, when approaching these bone fragments, people always hear faint whispers and see strange illusions. They believe these anomalies to be omens of misfortune."}]},{"id":"kw-60087","title":"Veridia Forest","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A human-occupied region in the Red Sea Rift.\n\nReferred to as a \"forest\" due to the numerous wind-worn stone pillars dotting it, this place is also home to many caves originally submerged in shallow waters and the remnants of numerous Golden Age cargo ships.\nThe whole region was once a hub of human activity, but the Cabal invasion forced many people to abandon their homes and gather in Veridia. They are eager to restore their former lives."}]},{"id":"kw-50047","title":"Ogres","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_57_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A kind of giant monster created from unhatched Thralls through the Wizards' depraved rituals.\n\nAfter undergoing a \"rebirthing\" ritual, these creatures mutate into \"Reborns\" that possess great power and can even use magical abilities. They shoot out rays of Void energy from their mutated heads that can tear apart anything in their path in the blink of an eye. The existence of these creatures is visual proof of the magical atrocities the Hive are capable of."}]},{"id":"kw-60088","title":"The Weathered Caves","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_112_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A cave near Veridia that has experienced years of wind erosion.\n\nA broken limb of the Sentinel now rests here. The caverns beneath the wreckage lead to a flat area in the mountain, adjacent to some artificial buildings that seem to be very old and decorated with mysterious patterns.\nOddly enough, the elderly residents of Veridia do not recall these buildings being there before."}]},{"id":"kw-60089","title":"Harrow's Hideout","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A secluded cave not far from Veridia.\n\nUnion President Harrow has set up a simple camp here, hoping to shield her mind from the never-ending barrage of voices. She even set up a noise generator to try drowning them out, but it doesn't seem to have yielded great results."}]},{"id":"kw-60090","title":"Nexus Interface","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A hidden point of connection between the Vex Network and reality, located beneath the Sentinel wreckage. The Vex used this as a passage to invade the Red Sea Rift.\n\nAfter Harrow accidentally activated the Axis Mind Zephyrus, the Vex launched a full-scale invasion of the Red Sea Rift. Wolf fought hard to defeat it, but ultimately, Zephyrus retreated into the Vex Network. Only by entering the Nexus Interface and eliminating the Axis Mind can Veridia truly be saved from the Vex."}]},{"id":"kw-50116","title":"Minotaur","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_81_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A heavy Vex ground unit.\n\nThe Minotaur's heavy armor lets it withstand more firepower and charge into enemy lines for close range, powerful attacks. They even have teleportation modules installed, further increasing their aggressiveness. Once a Minotaur locks onto you, you'll find it difficult to evade its relentless pursuit."}]},{"id":"kw-60091","title":"Gareth's Memorial","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A memorial Saladin made for Gareth, located in a secluded part of the Red Sea Rift.\n\nGareth's belongings were also kept here."}]},{"id":"kw-60092","title":"The Drill","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A giant drilling rig the Cabal are using to seize minerals in the Red Sea Rift.\n\nThe Sand Eaters' target in the Red Sea Rift is clear: local mineral resources. After driving away the humans who originally mined here, the Cabal expanded the operation tenfold by bringing in their specialized, giant drilling rig, letting them mine day and night. The ore extracted by the giant cantilever and gear-shaped excavation head is sent to the smelting plant called the Foundry, located next to the mine. After smelting, a portion is left to ensure sufficient army reserves, while the rest is transported to Mars to support their war against the Vex."}]},{"id":"kw-60093","title":"The Foundry","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_114_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A Cabal smelting facility located in Firebase Minos.\n\nWhen the Sand Eaters arrived at the Red Sea and occupied the human residents' mines, they expanded the original smelting operation and assigned the ruthless supervisor and slave driver, Tog'urk, to manage it. This forgemaster has always been committed to maximizing casting efficiency in order to better serve the Cabal war machine."}]},{"id":"kw-60094","title":"Sandbreaker Outpost","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A small Cabal outpost located in front of Firebase Minos.\n\nThe Sandbreaker Outpost is located along the essential route between Veridia Forest and Firebase Minos. With it, the Cabal can monitor human military movements and have a rallying point prepared for their troops, making it of extraordinary strategic significance.\nThe Sand Eaters and the Veridians have been constantly fighting over it during their ongoing conflict in the Red Sea Rift."}]},{"id":"kw-60095","title":"Firebase Minos","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_115_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A military building complex built by the Sand Eaters once they arrived at the Red Sea Rift. It also serves as their local command center.\n\nThis is a typical Cabal military base; the exterior of the building is painted with legion iconography, while the interior houses buildings with different functions such as combat command centers, barracks, tank battalions, and defensive artillery. Trenches have also been constructed around the firebase, but by far its most notable feature is the giant cannon above the base's main building."}]},{"id":"kw-40022","title":"Saladin","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_13_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Iron Lords' founders and the military leader of Veridia.\n\nAfter joining hands with Felwinter to overthrow the notorious Warlord Citan, the Iron Lords began to rise in earnest. In the subsequent Iron Crusade, Saladin conquered the territories of several hostile Warlords including the Nile Delta and its surrounding areas. During the Fallen invasion, he took the minor lord of Bayda-Benghazi, Finnala, as his \"Iron Wolf\" and began his rule over the region."}]},{"id":"kw-50135","title":"Sivks, the Saboteur.","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A ruthless baron wreaking havoc atop the space elevator.\n\nIn the wake of Wolf's attack on the space station and thwarting of the House of Devils' scheme, the Fallen still cling to their ambitions to reclaim it. Baron Siphogos is even more ambitious, as well as more brutal, than his kin. That which he cannot capture, he will instead destroy. With this firmly in mind, he took advantage of the Lightbearers' absence and led a squadron to invade the top of the space elevator, where they would try to sabotage the Iron Lords' newly established communications network."}]},{"id":"kw-60096","title":"Research Center","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A building that hosts the Sand Eaters' research into the Light and its applications.\n\nEver since he discovered the Sentinel and Radiancite, Commander Buhr has been trying to use the Light to strengthen his army. He even expanded one of the firebase's buildings to accommodate his research and experiments, but due to disagreements with Tog'urk, it has yet to be fully utilized. Perhaps only once his adversary disappears can Buhr receive all the support he needs."}]},{"id":"kw-60097","title":"Cannon Emplacement Base","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The base of a giant cannon above Firebase Minos.\n\nAlthough each Valus has their own command style, most would be happy to install a giant cannon when atop their firebase. However, few know about the fatal flaws in the cannon emplacement base's power supply."}]},{"id":"kw-50049","title":"Belaaks, Devil Sentry","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_45_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The mechanical monster created by the Splicers at the Lanyue 5 Factory.\n\nBelaaks has the appearance of a Heavy Shank, but its firepower and armor are unmatched among the Fallen's machines—even the most outstanding Lightbearers cannot fight the Devil Sentry head-on."}]},{"id":"kw-60098","title":"Radiancite","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_111_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A special ore unique to Veridia.\n\nThe molecular structure of Radiancite is influenced by Light radiation, causing the ore itself to contain Light. It can be cast in the same way as other metals, but it can also be used as a source of Light. Miners in the Red Sea Rift have found that Radiancite is more likely to be found near the Sentinel."}]},{"id":"kw-60099","title":"Sentinel's Hand","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_109_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A limb that broke off from the Sentinel. When activated, it can shield Veridia with a barrier of Light.\n\nIt's speculated that this hand was torn from the Sentinel's body during its battle with the unknown creature. For a long time, the arm was seen only as an interesting landmark of the Red Sea Rift. When the Cabal invaded, though, Saladin keenly took note of the connection between the shield generator in Sentinel's hand and the Light while wielding the Light in combat himself. Later on, the Sentinel's Light barrier was activated using Radiancite, giving Veridia a huge advantage in the battles to come."}]},{"id":"kw-50107","title":"Radiolarian Fluid","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The biological components that make up individual Vex.\n\nWhat few people know is that the Vex are not truly robots. Their metal limbs are actually just a kind of \"shell,\" while their true \"brain\" is a group of microorganisms living in milky white radiolarian, all of whom share a collective consciousness.\nEach individual Vex keeps this liquid preserved inside a solution chamber. Although the position of the chamber varies between types of Vex, damaging it reduces their metal exoskeleton's functionality."}]},{"id":"kw-60100","title":"Gareth's Lantern","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An ancient artifact resembling a lantern.\n\nDuring a mining operation, two miners discovered a strange glowing object in a cave in the Red Sea Rift. They placed the object into a handheld lantern and gifted it to Gareth, who was still lord of the Red Sea Rift at the time."}]},{"id":"kw-60102","title":"Illusion-Generating Psions","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Psions guarding something in the Weathered Caves who have the ability to generate illusions.\n\nZev believes it's highly unlikely the Cabal mastered this level of data visualization technology without having come into contact with some sort of external network."}]},{"id":"kw-60103","title":"Strange Box","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A mysterious object guarded by a group of Cabal in the Weathered Caves.\n\nThis cube-like floating object features patterns that match the sealed door of the Weathered Caves. Harrow speculates that whatever lies behind the door drew the Cabal here. Can this box be \"opened?\" Is the item inside the \"key\" to that sealed door?\nHarrow took the box without offering much explanation. Was this the real reason she went into the caves? Did she know about the box all along?"}]},{"id":"kw-60104","title":"Sentinel Armor","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The fruits of Buhr and the Sand Eaters' study of the Light.\n\nSentinel armor is cast from armor cut from the Sentinel itself and allows the wearer to briefly wield the Light, even if they aren't favored by the Traveler. For paracausal entities already wielding the Light, the Sentinel armor greatly enhances their innate powers."}]},{"id":"kw-60105","title":"The Minos Cannon","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A giant cannon located atop Firebase Minos.\n\nThis type of artillery is standard equipment at many Cabal firebases. Its scale alone is enough to intimidate most enemies, and the cannon is powerful enough to destroy most any threat.\nFollowing Buhr's breakthrough in his study of the Light, he developed shells using Sentinel technology capable of destroying Veridia's Light barrier."}]},{"id":"kw-40012","title":"Mu Ying","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_11_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The current commander-in-chief of Jiangshi Metro's guerrillas and the leader of mortals in the settlement.\n\nMu Ying is responsible for the day-to-day operations and strategies of the guerrillas as well as communication with Lord Radegast. The harsh natural environment and years of battling the Fallen have left him physically and mentally exhausted. Worsening circumstances have led him to contemplate the worst case scenario: the complete fall of Jiangshi Metro.\nMu Ying and Ayuela's parents were once close friends. After they both passed away, Mu Ying raised Ayuela as his own daughter."}]},{"id":"kw-60106","title":"Entropy Vibration Tower","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A device capable of emitting shockwaves matching those emitted by Sentinel armor, breaking through it via resonance.\n\nBuhr's Sentinel armor uses a special energy defense system. Fortunately, Donovan-17's entropy vibration tower, which he made using a Cabal phase converter, could disable it."}]},{"id":"kw-60107","title":"Guardians","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"As the Dark Age approached its end, the Iron Lords' ideals, shaped through the hard work and trials of countless Lightbearers, finally saw the light of day. No longer do cruel Warlords rule, and no longer do humans have to fight their battles alone. Now, they unite at the foot of the Last City and face all Earth's incoming enemies together. At last, an era of light is being ushered in.\nAnd in that bright future, those Lightbearers will refer to themselves with a new title conveying their responsibility: Guardians."}]},{"id":"kw-60108","title":"Warlords","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"In the Dark Age and early City Age, Lightbearers used their powers to conquer areas across Earth.\n\nAs more alien forces entered Sol, the Warlords, who were hostile towards one another during the Dark Age, realized they struggled to fend off these extraterrestrial foes on their own, especially given the enemy's high-tech equipment and aerial advantages. Many lesser Warlords fell to the invaders, and even the more prominent ones were eventually dragged into endless battles of attrition.\nThe lords of old had begun to feel the pressure of survival looming above them."}]},{"id":"kw-60109","title":"Sentinel Wreckage","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_95_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A Light-hallowed ground formed by the remnants of a Sentinel.\n\nThe wreckage in the Red Sea Rift is one of the many Sentinel remnant humans found after the Dark Age, maintaining the stance from its final battle against an unknown creature to this day. The Sentinel has been here ever since humans first arrived in the Red Sea Rift Valley after the Collapse, and although no one knows the reasons for its initial arrival and eventual fall, they surmise it to be related to the massive skeleton coiled tightly around its body."}]},{"id":"kw-50061","title":"Tracer Shanks","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_36_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A type of Shank equipped with a wire rifle.\n\nTracer Shanks can fire from especially long distances and unexpected angles, and they're also capable of easily bypassing cover. Nevertheless, they are still very fragile."}]},{"id":"kw-60110","title":"Sentinels","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_91_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"One of mankind's incredible Golden Age creations.\n\nIn order to ensure their mechs were foolproof in any situation, the researchers at Taketori Industry developed technology capable of releasing Light in a specific form and shaping it. These generators were installed on various parts of the Sentinels and could be enabled in specific scenarios, generating paracausal barriers capable of withstanding any known attacks."}]},{"id":"kw-40029","title":"Harrow","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_14_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"President of the Veridian Union.\n\nHarrow is able to hear people's wishes, then these wishes become reality with unpredictable costs. The only way to prevent this is refusing to hear the wishes, which is why Harrow moved out of Veridia and into a secluded cave, where she attempts to further block the sounds with noise generators.\nThe strange box that she and Wolf discovered in the Weathered Caves was the result of Wolf's unexpected wish; while the Vex are indeed capable of defeating the Cabal, it comes at the cost of their invasion of Veridia."}]},{"id":"kw-60111","title":"Ahamkara","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_6_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Powerful, magical, shape-shifting creatures.\n\nWhat many people do not know is that an Ahamkara's powers will not dissipate with the death of their corporeal bodies; their remains still hold the ability to invoke the Anthem Anatheme and grant wishes. However, without the Ahamkara's consciousness holding it in check, the magic energy becomes even more chaotic, more disorderly, to the point where it can even distort the surrounding environment. This often results in the generation of illusions and the altering of nearby objects' appearances."}]},{"id":"kw-40006","title":"Xûr","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Emissary of the enigmatic \"Nine.\"\n\nWith a face of dancing tentacles and a misty asphalt-like substance atop a humanoid form that seems just barely held together by his clothes, Xûr is an entity that is almost impossible to comprehend with conventional biological knowledge. No one knows precisely when he appeared in Haven.\nIn the extremely limited communications with him, he has claimed to serve a group of entities called the Nine and has come to Haven in search of Lightbearers to take part in certain challenges. But what exactly are the Nine? This remains a mystery—perhaps even to Xûr himself."}]},{"id":"kw-10067","title":"Jaren 3","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h303_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Never breaks his promises."}]},{"id":"kw-60112","title":"Iron Lords","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A group of Lightbearer seeking to end the Warlords' tyranny.\n\nThe Iron Lords are a close-knit military alliance and one of the most powerful forces on Earth at present. Most of Iron Lords have their own territories, some of which were seized from the Warlords during the Iron Crusade, while others were originally occupied by enlightened Warlords who came to agree with the Iron Lords' ideals during the organization's expansion. Jiangshi Metro and the Red Sea Rift, ruled by Xuân Yến and Gareth respectively, are examples of the latter."}]},{"id":"kw-40011","title":"Wu Ming","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The somewhat shaggy boss of Bad Old Time.\n\nThis nameless man once ran a tavern at the Iron Lords' stronghold at the foot of Felwinter Peak. When Radegast decided to move his territory to Haven, Wu Ming moved along with him, taking up his old trade once more.\nIn addition to serving regular drinks, Wu Ming often teaches his patrons to play a card game. Thanks to his promotion, the game has become popular among Haven residents and Lightbearers alike."}]},{"id":"kw-60113","title":"The Traveler","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_88_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A spherical paracausal entity beyond human comprehension.\n\nWhen the Speaker saw the broken Lumifly cocoon, she shared a dream of the Traveler as she perceived it:\n\"I've seen it, in the Traveler's dreams...\"\n\"I heard the Light shivering, crying out... The dream pained as it swelled...\"\n\"For a moment, the cosmos was a sea of white, as if engulfed by luminescence. I heard the Traveler's gentle sobs. Its wounds... They were singing.\"\n\"Once all the voices fell silent, the Lumiflies...flew out from within its fractures.\"\nHer words seem to be describing some manner of calamity."}]},{"id":"kw-60114","title":"Parhelion Wing","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Tan-2's Relic.\n\nParhelion Wing is a sword Relic with an affinity for Solar Light. It was once owned by the Warlord Yannick-11, who used it to scorch any who would oppose him with expert skill. Faced with an impending final death, Yannick-11 transferred his consciousness into his Relic. Following his demise, Tan-2 found the sword, and when he attempted to wield it with his own Light, Yannick-11's mind became parasitically attached to his own memory core."}]},{"id":"kw-10064","title":"Helhest's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h309_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Is trying to search Earth for traces of her pre-risen Life, but her efforts have so far been in vain."}]},{"id":"kw-60115","title":"Telencephal Band","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Ning Fei's headband.\n\nNing Fei has been wearing this headband ever since he first rose in the Light. He cannot take it off, as if it's become one with his body. Even trickier still are the unpredictable hallucinations it causes. Ning Fei and Claudia have been searching for a way to combat its dangerous nature for years."}]},{"id":"kw-50059","title":"Sorriks","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_19_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A Fallen treasure hunter who came to the crashed Ketch in search of an artifact from Riis.\n\nIn actuality, the Splicers are likely secretly manipulating such warriors into retrieving lost Riis technology and preventing it from falling into what they would deem the wrong hands."}]},{"id":"kw-60116","title":"Telencephal Band","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Ning Fei's headband.\n\nTo keep Ning Fei safe whenever he hallucinates, Claudia installed a backdoor in the headband, letting Ning Fei see \"fractures\" in the illusion. As long as he destroys three rifts, Claudia can locate him within the illusory space and help him return to reality."}]},{"id":"kw-60117","title":"Telencephal Band","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Ning Fei's headband.\n\nNing Fei and Claudia discovered that the headband was actually part of a \"sensory enhancement experiment\" intended to create a Speaker. The experiment itself came with a backdoor, though, in the form of a lab chip representing permissions, which could turn the headband's features off. The Servitor hiding out in the Ketch wreckage—Yuriiks-7—is the keeper of this chip."}]},{"id":"kw-50021","title":"Umbliks Prime","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_24_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Prime Servitor of the House of Devils.\n\nAfter the destruction of Maliks, the former Prime Servitor, in a surprise attack by the Iron Lady, a Servitor named Umbliks-7 was hastily modified into the Prime Servitor to take its place and fill the gap. But due to the urgency, Umbliks-7's transformation was incomplete and not ideal in terms of both computing power and Ether production, so the Splicers had long intended to replace it."}]},{"id":"kw-60118","title":"Telencephal Band","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Ning Fei's headband.\n\nWhen she revived Ning Fei, Claudia unintentionally gained partial control authority over the headband. Although she cannot shut it down, she can activate its \"correction function,\" which Claudia may use when Ning Fei acts out."}]},{"id":"kw-50112","title":"Goblins","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_77_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A basic Vex combat unit.\n\nThe Axis Minds often use Goblins as cannon fodder. A single Goblin doesn't pose much of a threat, but when they work together, they can turn the tides on the battlefield."}]},{"id":"kw-60119","title":"Consciousness Lockdown Unit","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An illusory space created by Yuriiks-7.\n\nYuriiks pulls all entities wearing the telencephal band into this illusory space as soon as they enter the Ketch wreckage. Without outside interference, they will be eternally lost in the hallucination."}]},{"id":"kw-60120","title":"Consciousness Lockdown Unit","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An illusory space created by Yuriiks-7.\n\nA flaw in the experiment has resulted in a connection forming between most of the subjects' consciousness lockdown units."}]},{"id":"kw-50122","title":"Light-Suppressing Technology","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A Cabal countermeasure that temporarily cuts off the connection between a Light-empowered entity and the Light itself.\n\nThe Cabal have encountered Light-empowered civilizations more than once during the expansion of their cosmic empire. To them, the Light is one of many entities in the universe, neither sacred nor mysterious, and capable of being countered through research."}]},{"id":"kw-60121","title":"Lanyue Mass Spectrometer","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An analysis system installed at the Lanyue 5 Factory.\n\nLanyue's mass spectrometer is equipped with a Golden Age AI capable of performing functional and material analysis on various technological creations. It can not only assist Ning Fei in analyzing the experimental chip kept by Yuriiks-7, but also provide technical support when fighting against the Fallen in Jiangshi Metro."}]},{"id":"kw-40060","title":"Mara Sov","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"Queen of the Reef's Awoken, and an enchanting ruler and politician.\n\nMara Sov was one of the first of the Awoken. Following several coups, the wise, callous, and farsighted Mara took the throne, which she still maintains to this day.\nThe Awoken had originally stayed within the Distributary, but under Mara's leadership, the Awoken, still caring for the fate of their kin, returned to Sol. They have not yet made direct contact with the survivors on Earth; rather, they evaluate Sol's current situation from their hidden enclave in the Reef."}]},{"id":"kw-60122","title":"Sensory Enhancement Experiment","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A human experiment that tried to create Speakers.\n\nDuring the Dark Age, some scientists attempted to artificially create Speakers to commune with the Traveler. Due to the pain and hallucinations that Speakers often experience when receiving information from the Traveler, these scientists set up labs in various locations where subjects would wear headbands that artificially created pain and hallucinations in an attempt to establish the connection.\nThe experiment was not the success they'd hoped for, and the related files fell into Fallen hands following their invasion."}]},{"id":"kw-40001","title":"Radegast","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_4_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"Chief Iron Lord, Dragonkeeper, Lord of Haven, Enemy of Tyranny, Liberator...\n\nRadegast has many prestigious titles, and he has also proven time and time again with his strength that he deserves them. Ever since he raised the Iron Banner and created the Iron Lords, he had been dedicated to one goal: bringing human civilization back to its glory days, by any means necessary.\nNow, Radegast takes command of Haven, welcoming all like-minded Lightbearers to join his cause."}]},{"id":"kw-60123","title":"Haven Forums","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An online forum frequented by Haven's residents.\n\nThough it uses a somewhat outdated BBS format, from lost-and-found postings to socializing, it covers everything one could possibly want from such a platform, making it a great place to kill time. However, it's also home to several urban legends—take care not to get fooled."}]},{"id":"kw-40058","title":"SVAPNA","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A cruel, cunning, and cold Ahamkara, as well as Estela and Bréc's mutual enemy.\n\nWhen Svapna realized a part of her deceased brother still lingered in this world, she tried once more to destroy Bréc by cruelly fulfilling Estela's wish—a wish \"to end this life.\" A tsunami and ensuing flood destroyed the village and took everyone's lives with it. Estela was no exception. With her death, Bréc's power also suffered a severe blow.\nBut the wish and its repercussions remain to this day. Whenever Estela settles down and prepares to live a stable life, disaster strikes, killing everyone around her."}]},{"id":"kw-60124","title":"British Isles","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The islands making up Great Britain, reduced to rubble by the Fallen's attack.\n\nIn the Dark Age, ambitious yet wicked Lightbearers quickly rose to become Warlords, staking their claim on territories all over the world. Britain was no exception. The Warlords of Wales and England formed opposing alliances based out of Beaumaris Castle and the city of London respectively. Despite the ever-present threat of the Fallen, the two sides chose instead to war with each other, with mortals becoming a key resource to compete for. The bloodshed continued until the death of Walter, leader of the Welsh faction.\nThe Warlord alliances crumbled in a series of assassinations. Shortly afterward, the Fallen seized their chance and launched an all-out invasion of London that engulfed the city in a sea of flames. Many Lightbearers and mortals alike were forced to abandon their homeland, passing through Calais and fleeing into Old Europe."}]},{"id":"kw-60125","title":"Metal Phage Nanobots","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A type of self-aware, self-adaptive, and self-organizing nanobot controlled by electronic signals.\n\nBy receiving programming instructions, these robot clusters can consume and decompose the vast majority of metals. Evidence suggests this technology was used in the early Golden Age to process space debris in Earth's orbit.\nNot long ago, the Sand Eaters discovered multiple arsenals hidden beneath the Red Sea Rift, and inside them were tons of nanobot-equipped missiles. They plan to transport these weapons elsewhere in preparation for another round of attacks on humanity."}]},{"id":"kw-60129","title":"Mysterious Cargo","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Strange cargo being escorted by the Cabal.\n\nAfter seizing the strange box, something strange happened: Wolf and Zev found themselves trapped in an endless loop. Just as they were at wits' end, an unfamiliar Lightbearer appeared and told them this was a trap set by an Ahamkara. It turns out the mysterious cargo was part of an Ahamkara's spine, which had tricked Wolf into making a wish and resulted in the Lightbearer being trapped."}]},{"id":"kw-60130","title":"Ahamkara Runes","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Wishes can take many forms, but regardless of language or culture, runes are the most favored way of all.\n\nThere are several ways to wish upon an Ahamkara: thinking it, speaking it, or using any known form of text to write it out. The Ahamkara can grasp the keywords \"wish\" or \"want\" regardless of form and make that wish reality.\nPeople have realized that using runes to make wishes grants a more accurate result compared with other methods. Thus, different cultures developed their own unique wishing runes. This type is one that has been passed down in the Red Sea Rift.\nYou may hope to prevent your wish from being twisted, but bear in mind that the Ahamkara are quite willing to rise to the challenge."}]},{"id":"kw-50076","title":"Sand Eaters","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_27_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Cabal legions that have invaded Sol.\n\nAfter failing to gain the upper hand against the Vex for some time, the legion's leadership decided to expand the scale of the war. In order to obtain the necessary additional military support, the legion decided to dispatch several teams to search for resources on other planets in Sol. One of those teams found that Earth's Red Sea Rift was home to abundant mineral deposits, including Radiancite. They sprang into action and drove away the humans residing there with overwhelming military force, quickly occupying the main drilling zone of the Red Sea Rift."}]},{"id":"kw-60131","title":"Wishing Altar","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An altar Zelpachad hid in the Red Sea Rift. Only those with wishes may approach.\n\nWhile following Nora's trail, Estela found an Ahamkara's altar on the Red Sea's coral. It was built by Zelpachad and protected by her magic, ensuring only those with wishes to make could access it."}]},{"id":"kw-60132","title":"SPITEFUL WHISPER","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The remains of a dead Ahamkara. To this day, it still speaks of its lingering resentment.\n\nEstela wields this skeleton as her Relic. Due to the unique, magical nature of the Ahamkara, Estela has been plagued by auditory and visual hallucinations ever since her Light merged with the Relic. A pretentious, mysterious, and inflammatory voice is always whispering in her ears, telling her things she wouldn't otherwise be privy to."}]},{"id":"kw-60133","title":"Veridian Transport Team","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A team of drivers in Veridia, responsible for transporting ore.\n\nThe Red Sea Rift's mines are somewhat far from Veridia. Once Radiancite is mined, it's loaded onto the trucks to be transported back to town, where it's used to power the barrier on the Sentinel's hand.\nThe team is typically formed of three people and three trucks. Its members have at least basic combat capabilities, and the schedule isn't set. Given the smaller scale of their operation and flexible timetables, the team's transport success rate is near 90%."}]},{"id":"kw-10041","title":"Umeko's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h310_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Nobody has seen what she looks like beneath her mask."}]},{"id":"kw-60134","title":"The City of Water","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A former fortress city on the Mediterranean.\n\nWhen the Mediterranean region fell, a new city rose from the ruins of Old Venice. After gathering nearly all of the humans around the Adriatic Coast together, the City of Water became the region's largest fortress city.\nTheir natural geographic advantage enabled them to fend off multiple Fallen attacks, but several decades ago, it suddenly became a ghost town."}]},{"id":"kw-50064","title":"Bruisers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_42_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Fierce warriors seen as \"Ketchkillers.\"\n\nDuring the Long Drift, Fallen society became one where the strong preyed on the weak. The Bruisers were highly praised for how they bravely charged forward in combat, especially their leaders, who were skilled at close-quarters fighting. To show off their martial prowess, many Bruisers intentionally wear little armor. This choice symbolizes their confidence in their strength and technique, but it also serves a practical purpose, as their lightweight equipment lets them maximize propulsion and transmission device efficiency. This greatly improves ambush speed, enabling these warriors to tear through enemy defenses at lightning speed."}]},{"id":"kw-60135","title":"The City of Water","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A former fortress city on the Mediterranean.\n\nIt's said the Fallen rallied their forces across southern Europe and formed an allied army of multiple Houses, all swearing to take down the City of Water, the last fortress standing in the Mediterranean.\nIn the end, the Fallen razed the city to the ground, and it's said that only a Warlord leader named Rossi-11 survived."}]},{"id":"kw-50095","title":"Centurion","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_68_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A core position commander in a Cabal legion.\n\nSome Centurions are promoted Decurions, but the majority are veterans who managed to survive hundreds of battles. They don armor that balances protection and mobility; this enables them to fight on the front lines, where they defend alongside the Phalanx troops, use Psions to issue orders, and command Gladiators to charge at the right time. Sometimes, they even personally attack enemy lines. Among countless fronts, it is these frontline sergeants who form the unrelenting backbone of the Empire's legions."}]},{"id":"kw-60136","title":"The City of Water","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A former fortress city on the Mediterranean.\n\nIn terms of administration, the City of Water's ruling Warlords made most of the decisions, and their lieutenant was responsible for the execution of orders. This lieutenant was referred to as the security officer and was a strong military presence with exceptional administrative processing capabilities.\nFrom the City of Water's establishment to its fall, the position was constantly held by a mortal named MacDuff."}]},{"id":"kw-20005","title":"The Mystery of Jiangshi's Fresh Water","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_100_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"After the Collapse, Jiangshi Metro was ravaged by a blizzard for three months straight, with temperatures suddenly dropping 30 to 40 degrees. The greenhouse, once used for extraterrestrial botany research, became the only place where plants could grow.\nBut a mystery has forever remained unresolved: the snow here has always contained excessive heavy metals, so where does the fresh water essential for both agriculture and drinking come from?"}]},{"id":"kw-50074","title":"Legions","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Units that make up the Cabal empire's military.\n\nFollowing the race's unification, what were once Cabal tribes gradually evolved into legions. As a highly militarized society, these legions form the foundation of the Cabal empire's power. Each legion is led by a Primus, and depending on a legion's unique situation, the command structure also includes a number of deputy officers of different ranks, including Valus, Val, Bracus, and more. Some legions may even form sub-regiments."}]},{"id":"kw-60137","title":"The City of Water","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A former fortress city on the Mediterranean.\n\nThe City of Water's ultimate downfall began with a conflict between its two lords. Rossi-11 insisted on defending the city to the death, while Darius-5 argued to abandon it and live on. The argument escalated, and Darius-5 accidentally killed Rossi-11's Ghost, resulting in their friend and ally's death. Leaderless against the allied Fallen army, the City of Water finally met its demise."}]},{"id":"kw-60138","title":"Detector Drone","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A type of common scanning equipment.\n\nThese detector-equipped drones are piloted via remote control and typically used to scan dangerous places or areas humans cannot easily reach. The Veridian miners use them to find Radiancite."}]},{"id":"kw-60139","title":"The Whisperers","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A neutral intelligence network born during the Dark Age, created by and primarily comprised of Ghosts.\n\nThe organization's ultimate pursuit is to lead a group of the most powerful, kindhearted, and just Lightbearers to build an ideal world and push humankind towards a new Golden Age."}]},{"id":"kw-60140","title":"Felwinter Peak","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A mountain in Old Russia, ruled by Lord Felwinter.\n\nOnce a peak near an Old Russia launch site, people built the Eastern Observatory atop what would eventually become Felwinter Peak. The observatory lost its usefulness during the Collapse and was eventually taken over by a Warlord. Felwinter killed the Warlord ruler, occupied the Eastern Observatory, and renamed it Felwinter Peak. After he joined the Iron Lords, he allowed them to build the Iron Temple, which would be used for meetings, at its summit, turning Felwinter Peak into one of the organization's crucial strongholds."}]},{"id":"kw-10034","title":"Tan-2's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h104_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Sometimes uses his Light to heal others...but not always."}]},{"id":"kw-30008","title":"Blinding Shell","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_conch_a02","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"Better shield your eyes.\"\n\nFrom scattered bone fragments to the enigmatic Radiancite, the Red Sea Rift is filled with objects influenced by paracausal forces. These colorful shells were discovered when wanderers first returned to this dry stretch of seabed, but it wasn't until the Lightbearers' arrival that people realized the shells presented the three manifestations of the Light. Although the Light contained within them is minimal, their unique appearance has made them highly sought-after collectibles. However, only the most attentive of people can collect all six varieties."}]},{"id":"kw-60141","title":"The Iron Temple","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A stronghold at the summit of Felwinter Peak, where the Iron Lords host important meetings.\n\nAfter Felwinter's joining, the Iron Lords banded together to build the Iron Temple atop Felwinter Peak, where the organization would first convene. In commemoration of the occasion, banners bearing the likeness of the Iron Lords who attended this first meeting hang in the temple. The Lords depicted are Radegast, Saladin, Felwinter, Skorri, Jolder, Efrideet, Timur, Silimar, Gunnora, and Dryden."}]},{"id":"kw-60142","title":"The Reef","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An asteroid belt located within Sol and the territory of the Awoken ruled by Queen Mara Sov.\n\nWhen the Awoken left the Distributary and returned to Sol, they settled in the asteroid belt called the Reef. There, they formed their own governing body, which is led by Mara Sov."}]},{"id":"kw-60143","title":"The Crows","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A secretive intelligence organization serving under Mara Sov, notorious for turning their operatives into merciless machines focused solely on carrying out their missions.\n\nInitially, Mara Sov founded this organization, which served directly under her, to build her own intelligence network and deal with matters in which she ought not show her face. But as the network grew and its internal factions expanded, the Crows began slipping from Mara's grasp. Some among them have begun intentionally avoiding Mara as they carry out missions, further polarizing conflicts in the Reef."}]},{"id":"kw-60144","title":"\"The Outreachers\"","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An Awoken faction in the Reef whose goal is to bring Awoken technology back to Earth and establish contact with their kin.\n\nOut of concern for humanity's fate, Mara Sov led the Awoken back to Sol. But ever since settling down in the Reef, Mara has yet to decide whether she should reveal their new home's existence and make contact with Earth. This caused some of the Awoken advocating for outreach to establish their own faction. With \"the White Queen\" at its helm, they are committed to carrying out their mission.\nTheir rival faction, which would rather keep hidden, is called \"the Isolationists.\""}]},{"id":"kw-60145","title":"The Sandy Mines","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Red Sea Rift's most famed Radiancite mines, known for its high quantity and quality of ore.\n\nIt provided Veridia with a wealth of resources until the Cabal's Sand Eaters came and used unstoppable force to occupy it. The loss of the Sandy Mines was the catalyst for the full-scale conflict that ensued between Veridia and the Cabal.\nFollowing the occupation, the Sandy Mines became a crucial production base for the Sand Eaters. Constant streams of Radiancite are mined here, transported to the Foundry for processing, then ultimately becoming fuel for the Cabal's massive war machines."}]},{"id":"kw-50097","title":"Colossi","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_70_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The most dangerous of Cabal units.\n\nOnly the tallest and strongest Cabal are qualified to wear such heavy armor, wield such massive Gatling-style guns, and serve as a Colossus. Their hulking bodies make these armored soldiers tower over the battlefield, and the specialized radios they carry let them constantly relay the situation on the battlefield to the command center and deliver instructions to other combat units."}]},{"id":"kw-60146","title":"Radiancite Smugglers","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Traders who ignore Veridia's restrictions on the ore trade, privately transporting and selling both Radiancite and relevant materials.\n\nThe rarer, more valuable, and more difficult to obtain an object is, the more these hyenas are drawn to it. What they're chasing is never the differentials of legal market prices, but the completely unregulated profits available through the black market."}]},{"id":"kw-60147","title":"Veridia's Unemployed Miners","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Downtrodden people who lost their jobs when the Cabal occupied many of the Red Sea Rift's mines.\n\nFor them, things like adequate food and clothing are but the most basic of difficulties they face. Most unemployed miners have little choice but to give up their dignity in order to make a living... Others, however, have chosen to set aside their morals."}]},{"id":"kw-50001","title":"Fallen","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_23_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An extraterrestrial race humans called the Fallen, but who refer to themselves as the Eliksni.\n\nOnce a peaceful and noble race living on the planet Riis, they too were enlightened by the Traveler until it came to Sol. With its blessing, the Eliksni enjoyed their own Golden Age.\nHowever, a catastrophic event they called the \"Whirlwind\" would nearly destroy their civilization, leading to their fall from grace."}]},{"id":"kw-50002","title":"The Long Drift","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The Fallen's large-scale migration, which started in pursuit of the Traveler.\n\nWhen the \"Great Machine\" left Riis, the Eliksni developed an obsession with retrieving it. At the instigation of some fanatics, they boarded their Ketches and recklessly pursued the Traveler. However, a lack of consideration and planning quickly depleted their supplies. Then came plunder and war between their Houses.\nThis would come to be known as the \"Long Drift\"—the Eliksni version of the Dark Age."}]},{"id":"kw-50003","title":"Riis","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The home planet of the Fallen before they \"fell.\"\n\nThe Eliksni describe it as something akin to the Garden of Eden, with all the lakes and rivers carefully planned to flow between lush fields, and towering buildings blended in with the mountains. Vessels sped through the pink sky in an orderly fashion. Every inch of the entire planet looked as if it had been carefully carved out and polished by a gentle sculptor.\nNow, it is but a distant dream."}]},{"id":"kw-50004","title":"The Whirlwind","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A catastrophic event that destroyed the once glorious civilization of the Eliksni.\n\nIn the fragmented and incomplete accounts from the time, the Eliksni suddenly realized one day that their \"Great Machine\" had left Riis. Then, the entire planet was engulfed by a hurricane that tore through mountains and oceans, all while a horrific alien army also launched an attack on the entire planet.\nSimultaneously struck by both nature and invaders, Riis would ultimately perish."}]},{"id":"kw-10073","title":"Efrideet 1","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h312_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"The Youngest Iron Lady"}]},{"id":"kw-50005","title":"Houses","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Fundamental organizations that make up Fallen society.\n\nHumanity has already encountered several Fallen Houses. It is said that they once had names far more elegant than the likes of the \"House of Devils,\" that they were once composed of scholars, engineers, and gardeners... However, over the centuries of spaceflight, conflicts often erupted between the Houses over resources, with many being forever lost in the echoes of the Long Drift.\nAnd the survivors' former identities were as changed and forgotten as their names."}]},{"id":"kw-50006","title":"House of Devils","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_23_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A Fallen House that invaded Jiangshi Metro.\n\nAfter the first wave of their attack was thwarted by the Iron Lady at the cost of her own life, the House of Devils started to plunder and destroy Jiangshi Metro. Like termites, they leave only destruction in their wake."}]},{"id":"kw-10051","title":"Estela's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h108_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Always appears where rumors of Ahamkara presence are."}]},{"id":"kw-50007","title":"Ether","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A substance necessary for the Fallen's survival.\n\nEther is a cold, fluorescent substance that exists in a gaseous state at ambient temperature. This substance once existed in abundance in Riis's natural environment, but can now only be created by Servitors.\nIf its supply is sufficient, the Fallen can grow to a very large size. Its dearth has greatly weakened the physical strength of the Fallen. Were it not for the shortage, mankind may be facing even more formidable foes."}]},{"id":"kw-50008","title":"Ether","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A substance necessary for the Fallen's survival.\n\nAfter they left Riis, the social order of the Fallen shifted to one based on a limited chain of Ether distribution—the Prime Servitor creates the Ether, the Archon maintains the Servitor, and the Kell holds the power to distribute it. The nobles are allocated a large amount of Ether, while the lower-ranking members are given just barely enough to survive. Although the Kell is the nominal ruler, the Archon and the Prime Servitor also wield great influence, leading to a delicate balance between the three heads of the Houses."}]},{"id":"kw-10069","title":"Kabr, the Resolute's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h211_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Through countless adventures, he's become more determined, yet also calmer."}]},{"id":"kw-50009","title":"Kell","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The title enjoyed by the political and military leaders of the Fallen Houses.\n\nIn addition to handling the internal politics of their House and commanding the military, the Kell also controls the House's Ether distribution. This is the basis of their power, with sufficient sustenance allowing them to be close to the physical limits of the Fallen in terms of size. Typically, in the \"dog-eat-dog\" society of the Fallen after the Long Drift, the Kell is the most powerful warrior in a House."}]},{"id":"kw-50011","title":"Prime Servitors","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_24_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The \"deities\" worshiped by Fallen Houses.\n\nPrime Servitors play a vital role in the religion and logistics of the Fallen Houses. They can transform matter and energy into Ether on which the Fallen depend. Their powerful computing abilities also make them critical to the Fallen's space travel, usually serving as navigators on long interstellar voyages. The vessel piloted by the navigating Kell is often honored with the name of the House's Prime Servitor."}]},{"id":"kw-10018","title":"Attal's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h105_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"\"Feeds\" a metal bird with Light and sees it as a symbol of peace."}]},{"id":"kw-50014","title":"Ketches","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Giant starships built by the Fallen that can be used to navigate deep space.\n\nHaving lived solely within these giant starfaring ships throughout the centuries of the Long Drift, many generations of the Fallen consider the Ketches their home. In fact, in the language of the Fallen, \"Ketch\" and \"family\" are the same word.\n\nThough most of the Ketches have fallen into disrepair after long periods of interstellar travel, they still have a great deal of significance in Fallen culture."}]},{"id":"kw-50015","title":"Ketches","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Giant starships built by the Fallen that can be used to navigate deep space.\n\nThe Ketches may be homes to the Fallen, but to other races, they are seen as powerful space-sailing warships. Their massive hulls house not only Fallen, but also various attack vessels like Skiffs and Walkers. A Ketch's arrival on a battlefield is akin to the arrival of an army."}]},{"id":"kw-50016","title":"Skiffs","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Small yet speedy aircraft created by the Fallen.\n\nNormally kept at bases or inside larger vessels, Skiffs can be used to rapidly deploy combat units, including soldiers and Walkers, for battle. In addition to their use as cargo ships, Skiffs are equipped with two Arc plasma cannons as well as grenade launchers, letting them provide air support for Fallen soldiers in combat. Skiffs may have an aerial advantage in battles against humans, but their threat can be reduced by destroying their main cannons—provided ground firepower is sufficient."}]},{"id":"kw-50017","title":"Pikes","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Single-seat ground vehicles used by the Fallen.\n\nPikes are usually armed with two Arc machine guns firing high-velocity rounds, while some heavy Pikes are also fitted with grenade launchers. The Pike's specialized engine allows it to perform extremely nimble accelerations and rolls. Because of their mobility, the Fallen often ride Pikes in packs for looting purposes.\nIn large-scale battles, however, they are typically used for distracting and flanking enemies."}]},{"id":"kw-10014","title":"Jolder's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h204_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Wields an ornate shield as her Relic."}]},{"id":"kw-50018","title":"\"Eclipse Monolith\"","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_106_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A Lanyue space station modified by Issakis, Archpriest of the Splicers.\n\nOnce the Fallen fleet arrived in Earth's orbit, they immediately spotted the towering Lanyue Space Elevator. Every House leader who saw it understood its strategic value. Soon, a battle for the station at the top of the space elevator was fought between the Fallen Houses, and in the end, it was the House of Devils that emerged victorious. After years of modification and operation by the Archpriest of the Splicers, Issakis, it has become one of the most important strongholds of the House of Devils in Sol.\nIf the Eclipse Monolith is activated, it can attack anywhere on Earth, and the disconnected Space Elevator will fall, crushing Jiangshi Metro and any who fail to evacuate it."}]},{"id":"kw-50019","title":"Vanok, the Arclite","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_18_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A techno-priest of the House of Devils.\n\nVanok was also a member of the Splicers. At the behest of one of the higher-ups of the organization, Vanok used Riis technology to transform the Jiangshi Weather Control Facility, which was originally used for cloud dispersal and artificial rainfall, into the \"Fulminator,\" a device capable of creating large-scale and prolonged thunderstorms."}]},{"id":"kw-50020","title":"Sorriks","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_19_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A Fallen treasure hunter who came to the crashed Ketch in search of an artifact from Riis.\n\nIn Fallen society, treasure hunters are known for their avid interest in the Riis's Golden Age technology.\nUpon hearing that a Riis artifact was suspected to have been found in the crashed Ketch in Jiangshi Metro, Sorriks quickly arrived on the scene, ready to recover the Riis-born legacy. However, he seems to be backed by an even stronger force..."}]},{"id":"kw-60021","title":"Void","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Void is gravity, the fundamental force that exists between all matters with mass. \n\nLightbearers can release the Light in the form of Void energy, creating black holes, warping space, absorbing matter and energy, or creating force fields that insulate against impact."}]},{"id":"kw-50022","title":"Issakis, Fourth Archpriest of the Splicers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_21_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An Archpriest in the Conclave of Archbishops, the leadership of the Splicers, and head of the House of Devils in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nCurrently, nothing is known about him, though Sorriks did mention a high-ranking member of the Splicers called \"the Martyr\" in his communications.\nIssakis seems to have not directly taken part in the House of Devils' invasion of Jiangshi Metro, but he and the Splicers may be influencing their operations from behind the scenes."}]},{"id":"kw-50024","title":"Dregs","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_33_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Soldiers of the lowest rank among the Fallen.\n\nDregs are soldiers who, in a traditional ritual used for humiliation and submission, have a pair of arms cut off. Driven by a mixture of shame and ambition, they tend to be very aggressive in battle, but lacking the protection of fine equipment, only a lucky few survive to be promoted and allowed to regrow their arms.\nSome higher-ranking Fallen officers who suffer major defeats are also punished by having their arms cut off and being demoted to Dregs."}]},{"id":"kw-50025","title":"Vandals","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_38_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Soldiers that have a slightly higher status in the Fallen society than Dregs.\n\nThe Shock Rifles that Vandals wield have a longer range than normal rifles, making them quite formidable marksmen, and their four arms enable some of them to use melee weapons for self-defense.\nThey are the main force of the Fallen, but they are also just normal soldiers. In a head-on firefight, they aren't much tougher than the Dregs."}]},{"id":"kw-50026","title":"Captain","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_41_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Elite warriors who command the Fallen troops in battle on the front lines.\n\nCaptains oversee troops during designated combat missions or personally lead Vandals and Marauders during attacks. They typically have the finest weapons and armor and are equipped with shield generators and short-distance teleportation devices, making them much tougher to take down.\nDespite being \"fallen,\" some of the honor and pride of the nobility of Old Riis can still be seen in these brave warriors."}]},{"id":"kw-50027","title":"Shanks","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_35_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Small combat drones made by the Fallen.\n\nAs a race proficient in electronics and engineering, the Fallen often use various kinds of electromechanical combat units. These multifunctional drones have a variety of uses ranging from scouting to providing supporting fire and baiting out enemies. A single Shank is usually easily dealt with, but when they swarm together, they pose quite the threat."}]},{"id":"kw-40057","title":"SVAPNA","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A cruel, cunning, and cold Ahamkara, as well as Estela and Bréc's mutual enemy.\n\nBréc and Svapna were twin siblings. Despite both being typical Ahamkara, Svapna was far crueler and greedier than Bréc. When the besieged Bréc sought help from Svapna, she betrayed him by fulfilling a Warlord's wish that a certain Ahamkara perish. Thus did Bréc meet his end, dying in resentment and hatred. Driven by intense obsession, part of his consciousness clung to his bones, which after many twists and turns, ended up in a coastal village in Old Spain. There, his bones became revered as a \"holy artifact\" that only the village's oracle, a young girl named Estela, could commune with."}]},{"id":"kw-60019","title":"Arc","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Arc is an electric field discharge, a fundamental physical phenomenon associated with electric charge and electromagnetic fields.\n\nLightbearers can release the Light in the form of Arc energy, conducting powerful currents to create plasma missiles, pulse explosions, and even pure plasma surges."}]},{"id":"kw-50028","title":"Exploder Shank","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_37_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A special kind of Shank that self-destructs, dealing immense damage to the Fallen's foes.\n\nShanks are largely treated as expendable, destroyed nearly just as quickly as they are unleashed and typically usable only once. In some cases, however, they are not completely scrapped, and because repairing them would not be worth the resources, Fallen engineers \"recycle\" damaged Shanks and load them with high-power explosives. They are then re-deployed in battle, where they serve their House one last time in the form of a suicide attack."}]},{"id":"kw-40056","title":"Claire and Hubert","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"Estela's former adoptive brother and sister.\n\nFor as long as she can remember, Estela has been wandering, searching for a place to rest her weary feet. When her Ghost first revived her, her youthful appearance would sometimes cause her to be harassed, but more often than not, it would lead people to look after her.\nClaire, Hubert, and their parents just so happened to be such people. They took Estela in and treated her as family. But the wish Estela made in her past life would still come back to haunt her. A flash flood swept everything away—Claire, Hubert, their parents, the entire village... Estela, revived by her Ghost, would be left as the lone survivor."}]},{"id":"kw-50029","title":"Walkers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_21_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Six-legged, self-propelled tanks equipped with a full arsenal, making them adaptable to a variety of battlefields.\n\nThe Walkers' front-mounted Arc machine guns can carry out high-speed strafing with wide coverage, while the heavy gun on top fires highly explosive Solar ammunition to strike large areas. The missile silo on the side of the main gun can fire a barrage of small missiles to counter aerial threats, and as a form of self-defense, they can create a wide-range Arc pulse to repel enemies in their blind spots. What's more, they are also capable of being carried on Skiffs for rapid deployment on the battlefield. All of these factors combined make them veritable ultimate war machines."}]},{"id":"kw-20017","title":"Jiangshi's Weather Woes","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_101_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"Jiangshi Metro has suffered from blizzards since the Collapse, but recently, the already awful weather has taken a turn for the worse.\nFor the past few months, the guerrillas have encountered sudden storms and lightning strikes them with deadly precision during every patrol of Jiangshi Metro and its surroundings.\nCould someone be behind these inexplicable tempests? And if so, when will they reveal themselves?"}]},{"id":"kw-50030","title":"Servitors","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_44_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Large, spherical, floating machines that act as the Fallen's support units in combat.\n\nServitors have an important place in Fallen religion, and they are no less useful in combat. These semi-intelligent, floating machines can fire large Void energy projectiles or even high-energy Solar rays to scorch their foes. But more importantly, Servitors offer assistance to nearby Fallen combat units, for instance, providing shields that absorb damage. When Servitors appear on the battlefield, their impact is often greater than their individual efforts."}]},{"id":"kw-50032","title":"Hive","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_25_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A race of terrifying, ancient alien arthropods.\n\nThe Hive are creatures that live in symbiosis with the Worms, beings aligned with a paracausal power. Their predecessors were the Krill, a group of weak arthropods with a lifespan of only 10 years on the planet of Fundament. When they were still in the feudal era, their Osmium Court suffered an invasion and was nearly wiped out.\nThe kingdom's princesses fled into the depths of Fundament's oceans. There, they found Worm Gods in captivity, and driven by a strong desire for revenge, they swallowed the Worms. Thus the Hive were born."}]},{"id":"kw-50034","title":"Worms","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The dielectric beings that connect the Hive with paracausal powers.\n\nThese ancient supernatural parasites are the medium through which the Hive connect with the powers they now wield. Through a negotiation between the princesses of the Osmium Court and the Worm Gods, the Worms entered into a symbiotic relationship with the Krill, the species that would become the Hive. The parasites gain supernatural power through their hosts, while the Hive gain access to paracausal powers. However, the Worms' voracious appetites force the Hive to hunt constantly, making them a threat to all."}]},{"id":"kw-60012","title":"Sentinels","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_91_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"One of mankind's incredible Golden Age creations.\n\nAlthough the Sentinels do not speak, it is said that each of them has a consciousness of its own. They independently identified targets that may threaten human civilization and rooted them out. However, when the Collapse came, not even the Sentinels could escape. They gradually collapsed in the paracausal catastrophe that ravaged the globe, leaving only their wreckage. The Sentinel roaming near Haven is believed to be the only one that survived the Collapse."}]},{"id":"kw-50035","title":"Hive Princes","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The supreme rulers of the Hive.\n\nThough they are given the title of prince, they are still just individuals with paracausal powers. Their power comes from a chain of tithes constructed paracausal magic, with one-tenth of the power gained by each Hive being paid in tribute to their superior. As such, the progenitors of the Hive—known then as the princesses of the Osmium Court—became the contemporary Hive's chief gods. Crota is the newest Hive God to join the ever-growing pantheon."}]},{"id":"kw-10040","title":"Gwynn's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h103_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"No villain can escape her \"final judgment.\""}]},{"id":"kw-30002","title":"Albert II","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_monkey_a02","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"Look—the horizon!\"\n\nThe pre-Golden Age period of exploration saw many animals sent to space before human astronauts, including sheep, rabbits, mice, dogs, and of course, monkeys. After the Lanyue Space Elevator of the Golden Age was built, Jiangshi Aeronautic Campus released a collection of dolls to commemorate the \"Space Monkeys,\" with each corresponding to a primate who soared into the skies as part of humanity's early space experiments. Though production has long since ended, one can still see the positive spirit of Golden Age humans within each of these plushies."}]},{"id":"kw-50036","title":"Hive Princes","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The supreme rulers of the Hive.\n\nBecoming a prince among the Hive requires the ability to create one's own Throne World—\"pocket universes\" formed within the Ascendant Realm, which obey the laws and rules of their creator and house their soul. As long as a Hive God is not killed within their own Throne World, they can reappear in the material universe time and time again."}]},{"id":"kw-60006","title":"Golden Age","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A period of prosperity that spanned several generations of human history.\n\nIn the millennia following the arrival of the Traveler in Sol, humanity's technological levels rose to unprecedented heights. Driven and even taught by the Traveler, government agencies, private organizations, and enterprises alike developed and produced a variety of miraculous technologies, and breakthroughs of different scientific theories were being made daily. All terraformed planets in Sol had been colonized, and plans for colonization of other galaxies were underway.\nHowever, all of this came to an end with the arrival of the Collapse."}]},{"id":"kw-50037","title":"Ir Anûk","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"One of the famous twin Deathsinger daughters of Oryx.\n\nIt was the twins who created the prototype of the Oversoul, and it was she who created the Annihilator Totem to assist Crota when he fought back against the Vex invading Oryx's Throne World. She possesses an understanding of the Ascendant Realm that far surpasses that of others, leading Crota to summon her to his side and assist in the perfecting of his own Throne World."}]},{"id":"kw-20041","title":"AWOL Commander, Sand Eaters in Conflict","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_27_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"When the highest commander of the Sand Eaters, Zau'ul, suddenly disappeared with no apparent reason, chaos overtook the Cabal's internal affairs. Two important officers, Field Commander Buhr and Forgemaster Tog'urk, began competing for command of the Red Sea Rift firebase. It's difficult to determine whether this disagreement is a general power struggle or a difference in military development strategies. Tog'urk, who prefers to solve problems with steel and flames, uses giant drilling rigs and smelting plants day and night to seize metals and minerals and transform them into war machines. For reasons yet unknown, though, Buhr has tightened his grip over the supply of Radiancite, and he's shown a clear interest in the Sentinel's remains."}]},{"id":"kw-40055","title":"NORA","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A mortal girl who hopes her shattered family can be made whole again.\n\nNora spoke her wish to the \"Wish-Granter\" with sincerity, but the creature granting it turned out to be the Ahamkara Zelpachad. The wish-dragon cruelly twisted her wish and took her sight in order to \"grant\" it. Now, she will \"no longer see\" her father's sadness."}]},{"id":"kw-50038","title":"Crota","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The first heir of the Taken King, Oryx.\n\nFor the Hive, love is war and death. The three chief gods of the Hive have a special way of showing their kinship: through endless war. To stay on top of this competition, Oryx realized that he needed heirs to continue his bloodline and, more importantly, provide him with a steady stream of tithes.\nCrota was thus the first to be born. He would be followed by the twins Ir Anûk and Ir Halak, as well as Nokris, who was eventually banished."}]},{"id":"kw-40054","title":"NORA","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A mortal girl who hopes her shattered family can be made whole again.\n\nNora once had a happy family. She had kind and loving parents, as well as a best friend—a stuffed bear hand-sewn by her mother.\nBut after her mother died in an accident, her father fell into a deep depression. Nora tried her best to help him emerge from the grief, but all of her attempts ended in failure.\nOne day, however, a magical creature calling itself the \"Wish-Granter\" found Nora and promised to turn her hopes into reality..."}]},{"id":"kw-50039","title":"Crota","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The first heir of the Taken King, Oryx.\n\nWhen Crota was born, Oryx gave him nothing but his name and a sword. Everything had to be acquired by himself. And Crota, being a Hive prince, grew from death wrought by his own hands, learning from his sisters, and overcoming the obstacles his father had deliberately put in his way. He revels in power and longs to test his limits.\nKnowing this mindset, the Witch Queen Savathûn laid a trap for her nephew..."}]},{"id":"kw-40045","title":"Kyle","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The former right-hand man of Walter, the Warlord ruler of Wales. He now goes by \"Balder.\"\n\nKyle and his fellow Lightbearers Manfred and Jeffrey previously served Walter. As his deputies, they were responsible for punishing disobedient prisoners. Kyle was a reverent, obsequious presence at Walter's side, offering advice and suggestions for torturing prisoners, but never displaying his own use of the Light. It was through his cunning and caution that Kyle survived Gwynn's slaughter at Beaumaris Castle.\nHaving avoided a final death, Kyle fled to London, but the Fallen's invasion soon followed. He managed to hide from the alien pursuers in London's underground tunnels, but the assault left his Ghost badly damaged. Realizing his own weakness, Kyle sought help from mortals. He gathered a group of survivors and led them to escape the British Isles, after which they began a lengthy journey..."}]},{"id":"kw-10036","title":"Tan-2's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h104_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Often talks to himself in a strange way."}]},{"id":"kw-50040","title":"Crota","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The first heir of the Taken King, Oryx.\n\nCrota unleashed his power recklessly. Using his sword, he cleaved a rift in space, the other side of which connected to the Vex network. A swarm of Vex invaded Oryx's Throne World under the leadership of an Axis Mind named Quria.\nThrough a lengthy stalemate, the Vex gradually learned the rules of the Throne World and adapted to them. Even with the help of his sisters, Crota was unable to hold them back, and Oryx's Throne World was in grave danger."}]},{"id":"kw-40044","title":"Walter","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A Warlord leader who occupied the Welsh mountains.\n\nWalter was an ambitious and exceedingly cruel tyrant who seized all key facilities and transportation routes in Northwest Wales. With Beaumaris Castle at its center, he kept a tight grip on his territory.\nWales was subject to a strict class structure under Walter, and with the blood dragon as his seal, he held king-like rights. The Lightbearers he ordered about were not his slaves, but his hatchet men; as for the Lightless, he saw them as little more than talking livestock. Beaumaris Castle was a place of extreme luxury, but beyond its walls, mortals lived in abject poverty, treated as expendable resources by their ruler."}]},{"id":"kw-50041","title":"Crota","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The first heir of the Taken King, Oryx.\n\nThe conflict in the Throne World was on the verge of spiraling out of control. Alerted by the Worm God Eir, Oryx left the front lines of the raging battle behind to return to his Throne World. After using the power of the Taken, Quria and the Vex were finally defeated. To punish his son's transgressions, Oryx cast Crota into the Vex network before closing the rift.\nCrota was thus forced to wander the Nexus, growing stronger in a never-ending battle."}]},{"id":"kw-50042","title":"Crota","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 5","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The first heir of the Taken King, Oryx.\n\nThrough the Vex portal, Crota traveled through time and space, bringing calamity and destruction to countless worlds. In the process, he grew to understand his father, and instead of complaining, he began to form his own brood, sending more and more tithes to his father. Eventually, he reached the Moon—the Pale Star he had been told about as a child. He knew that his wanderings were over. It was here that he would deliver the greatest offering to his father."}]},{"id":"kw-60036","title":"Morgran's Prey","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A challenge set up by Lord Radegast.\n\nAfter accidentally acquiring the young Ahamkara, Radegast soon discovered how unstable the power of wishes could be. To prevent unforeseen mishaps brought about by Morgran's power while still satisfying his hunger, Radegast designed a challenge called Morgran's Prey. As its captives yearn for freedom, and Lightbearers for greater power, Morgran draws spiritual energy from them. On rare occasions, some lucky captives have been freed in this way."}]},{"id":"kw-50043","title":"Thrall","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_48_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The most common and low-rank combatants of the Hive, and one of the most basic forms of the race.\n\nAfter hatching from their cocoons, these skeleton-like soldiers can move at extremely fast speeds and use their sharp claws to attack their enemies. Thralls are usually hatched in large numbers and attack in groups to overwhelm their opponents. If they aren't immediately killed and grow strong enough, surviving Thrall can become Acolytes."}]},{"id":"kw-50044","title":"Acolytes","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_50_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A form evolved from Thrall who have collected enough paracausal energy.\n\nThey possess basic intelligence and have grown three eyes, enabling them to use basic firearms as well as heed orders. This allows them to survive longer on the battlefield. If they can survive long enough, they will have the chance to further evolve into either Wizards or Knights."}]},{"id":"kw-50045","title":"Wizards","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_56_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Once Acolytes have survived enough battles, they have the opportunity to advance to a higher form. Among them, some choose to become Wizards.\n\nThese powerful spellcasters levitate in the air, making it easy to observe the situation on the battlefield, perform magical attacks, or give orders to their underlings.\nOutside of combat, the Wizards' most important role is to produce offspring. The most basic form of Hive—the Thrall—are hatched from the egg pods they spawn."}]},{"id":"kw-50046","title":"Knights","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_54_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"While some Acolytes who ascend to their next form choose to become Wizards, others choose to become Knights. These elite warriors equipped with sturdy armor are the backbone of the Hive army.\n\nKnights wield a variety of weapons depending on the mission, letting them form a solid defense line against enemy onslaughts or charge forward to break through enemy positions.\nKnights are all elites who emerged from years of bloody battles, making them formidable foes on the battlefield."}]},{"id":"kw-50091","title":"Scorpius","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_64_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Automatic turrets capable of firing high-velocity heavy ammunition, often deployed by the Cabal to defend fixed positions."}]},{"id":"kw-30001","title":"Albert I","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_monkey_a01","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"That's right! I was the first!\"\n\nThe pre-Golden Age period of exploration saw many animals sent to space before human astronauts, including sheep, rabbits, mice, dogs, and of course, monkeys. After the Lanyue Space Elevator of the Golden Age was built, Jiangshi Aeronautic Campus released a collection of dolls to commemorate the \"Space Monkeys,\" with each corresponding to a primate who soared into the skies as part of humanity's early space experiments. Though production has long since ended, one can still see the positive spirit of Golden Age humans within each of these plushies."}]},{"id":"kw-10037","title":"Gwynn's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h103_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"A maiden of death clad in black armor."}]},{"id":"kw-30003","title":"Gordo","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_monkey_a03","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"Alright, humans. No bugging me after this mission's over, you hear?\"\n\nThe pre-Golden Age period of exploration saw many animals sent to space before human astronauts, including sheep, rabbits, mice, dogs, and of course, monkeys. After the Lanyue Space Elevator of the Golden Age was built, Jiangshi Aeronautic Campus released a collection of dolls to commemorate the \"Space Monkeys,\" with each corresponding to a primate who soared into the skies as part of humanity's early space experiments. Though production has long since ended, one can still see the positive spirit of Golden Age humans within each of these plushies."}]},{"id":"kw-30004","title":"Miss Able","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_monkey_a04","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"Shhh. She's resting.\"\n\nThe pre-Golden Age period of exploration saw many animals sent to space before human astronauts, including sheep, rabbits, mice, dogs, and of course, monkeys. After the Lanyue Space Elevator of the Golden Age was built, Jiangshi Aeronautic Campus released a collection of dolls to commemorate the \"Space Monkeys,\" with each corresponding to a primate who soared into the skies as part of humanity's early space experiments. Though production has long since ended, one can still see the positive spirit of Golden Age humans within each of these plushies."}]},{"id":"kw-40038","title":"Kevarrh","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_5_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A Fallen who has allied herself with Haven.\n\nRadegast places extraordinary trust in Kevarrh, even allowing her to lead a special combat unit composed of Fallen prisoners who willingly surrendered. These Fallen come from different Houses, some of which even hate each other, but Kevarrh still unites them under the same banner.\nOf course, the occasional rebellion still occurs, but Kevarrh always manages to limit the impact within her troops, and there are very few situations that truly require Radegast's intervention."}]},{"id":"kw-10035","title":"Tan-2's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h104_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Is investigating some extremely dangerous research in Jiangshi Metro."}]},{"id":"kw-30005","title":"Miss Baker","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_monkey_a05","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"Mom was quite the adventurer back in her day, kids!\"\n\nThe pre-Golden Age period of exploration saw many animals sent to space before human astronauts, including sheep, rabbits, mice, dogs, and of course, monkeys. After the Lanyue Space Elevator of the Golden Age was built, Jiangshi Aeronautic Campus released a collection of dolls to commemorate the \"Space Monkeys,\" with each corresponding to a primate who soared into the skies as part of humanity's early space experiments. Though production has long since ended, one can still see the positive spirit of Golden Age humans within each of these plushies."}]},{"id":"kw-30006","title":"Sam","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_monkey_a06","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"I can take care of myself. I'm a doctor, after all.\"\n\nThe pre-Golden Age period of exploration saw many animals sent to space before human astronauts, including sheep, rabbits, mice, dogs, and of course, monkeys. After the Lanyue Space Elevator of the Golden Age was built, Jiangshi Aeronautic Campus released a collection of dolls to commemorate the \"Space Monkeys,\" with each corresponding to a primate who soared into the skies as part of humanity's early space experiments. Though production has long since ended, one can still see the positive spirit of Golden Age humans within each of these plushies."}]},{"id":"kw-30007","title":"Shocking Shell","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_conch_a01","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"Don't touch it—you'll get shocked.\"\n\nFrom scattered bone fragments to the enigmatic Radiancite, the Red Sea Rift is filled with objects influenced by paracausal forces. These colorful shells were discovered when wanderers first returned to this dry stretch of seabed, but it wasn't until the Lightbearers' arrival that people realized the shells presented the three manifestations of the Light. Although the Light contained within them is minimal, their unique appearance has made them highly sought-after collectibles. However, only the most attentive of people can collect all six varieties."}]},{"id":"kw-30009","title":"Healing Shell","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_conch_a03","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"Hold it in your hand, and you'll feel a radiating warmth.\"\n\nFrom scattered bone fragments to the enigmatic Radiancite, the Red Sea Rift is filled with objects influenced by paracausal forces. These colorful shells were discovered when wanderers first returned to this dry stretch of seabed, but it wasn't until the Lightbearers' arrival that people realized the shells presented the three manifestations of the Light. Although the Light contained within them is minimal, their unique appearance has made them highly sought-after collectibles. However, only the most attentive of people can collect all six varieties."}]},{"id":"kw-30010","title":"Scalding Shell","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_conch_a04","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"Hot hot hot!\"\n\nFrom scattered bone fragments to the enigmatic Radiancite, the Red Sea Rift is filled with objects influenced by paracausal forces. These colorful shells were discovered when wanderers first returned to this dry stretch of seabed, but it wasn't until the Lightbearers' arrival that people realized the shells presented the three manifestations of the Light. Although the Light contained within them is minimal, their unique appearance has made them highly sought-after collectibles. However, only the most attentive of people can collect all six varieties."}]},{"id":"kw-50081","title":"Commanders","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A non-standard position in a Cabal legion.\n\nAlthough a Valus has the qualifications to appoint commanders as their own deputies, not all of them will do so. Some Valus believe doing so will contribute to favorable mission outcomes, while others believe that appointing deputies will weaken their authority. Commanders are usually only responsible for the execution of specific tactical objectives and do not have substantial power. Only in the absence of their Valus will they briefly be qualified to make decisions."}]},{"id":"kw-30011","title":"Singularity Shell","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_conch_a05","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"I wouldn't say it's heavy. It's more like it's drawing in everything around it.\"\n\nFrom scattered bone fragments to the enigmatic Radiancite, the Red Sea Rift is filled with objects influenced by paracausal forces. These colorful shells were discovered when wanderers first returned to this dry stretch of seabed, but it wasn't until the Lightbearers' arrival that people realized the shells presented the three manifestations of the Light. Although the Light contained within them is minimal, their unique appearance has made them highly sought-after collectibles. However, only the most attentive of people can collect all six varieties."}]},{"id":"kw-30012","title":"Invisible Shell","sub":"Collectibles","quality":null,"art":"data_collect_conch_a06","filters":{"Kind":"Collectibles"},"body":[{"p":"\"Huh? Where is it...?\"\n\nFrom scattered bone fragments to the enigmatic Radiancite, the Red Sea Rift is filled with objects influenced by paracausal forces. These colorful shells were discovered when wanderers first returned to this dry stretch of seabed, but it wasn't until the Lightbearers' arrival that people realized the shells presented the three manifestations of the Light. Although the Light contained within them is minimal, their unique appearance has made them highly sought-after collectibles. However, only the most attentive of people can collect all six varieties."}]},{"id":"kw-50048","title":"Splicers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A technological alliance of cutting-edge scientists from the Fallen.\n\nAs a member of the Splicers, Vanok transformed the Jiangshi Weather Control Facility into a Fulminator capable of creating thunderstorms, perhaps in order to limit the range of activities of the Jiangshi Metro guerrillas.\nThe Treasure Hunter Sorriks was also operating under Splicer Archpriest Issakis's orders, trying to recover an old Riis artifact from the wreckage of the Ketch. The Splicers must be plotting something behind these activities."}]},{"id":"kw-10007","title":"Ikora's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h102_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Prefers brute force over precise techniques when it comes to breaking barriers."}]},{"id":"kw-50051","title":"Ascendant Realm","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A paraversal dimension related to certain paracausal powers.\n\nThe Ascendant Realm is a borderless space that usually exists as a Throne World.\nEntities within the Ascendant Realm are variable and are maintained by their own willpower. Strong wills will turn into physical forms, creating bizarre and twisted scenes."}]},{"id":"kw-60027","title":"The Nine","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An extremely mysterious group of entities that we know precious little about.\n\nThey created a special space and sent out a mysterious emissary to invite Lightbearers. They are unlikely to be Earth-based entities and have never revealed their true identities. Their existence seems to transcend the limits of time and space. They show a strong interest in Lightbearers, but what exactly are they, and what is their purpose? No one knows for sure."}]},{"id":"kw-50052","title":"Sabikis, the Patroller","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_17_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The Fallen Captain that had been chasing Zev in the Old City.\n\nThis elite warrior from the House of Devils seems determined to control the Old City."}]},{"id":"kw-50054","title":"House of Devils","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_23_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The Fallen House that invaded Jiangshi Metro.\n\nUnlike the other Houses, many of the Devils have modified themselves with electronic implants and have more harmonious relations with machines like Servitors and Shanks. The elder of the House of Devils must be a fan of technology."}]},{"id":"kw-50055","title":"Issakis, Fourth Archpriest of the Splicers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_21_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An Archpriest in the Conclave of Archbishops, the leadership of the Splicers, and head of the House of Devils in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nHe monopolized the transformation of the upper station of the Lanyue Space Elevator. Aside from giving orders to the members of the Splicers, Issakis is rarely seen in battles, opting instead to spend his time at the Eclipse Monolith conducting his fanatical experiments.\nIssakis doesn't trust others, keeping the only authorization of the Eclipse Monolith to himself. Finish him, and the Splicers' plan will collapse in on itself."}]},{"id":"kw-50056","title":"Issakis, Fourth Archpriest of the Splicers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_21_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An Archpriest in the Conclave of Archbishops, the leadership of the Splicers, and head of the House of Devils in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nIt won't be so easy to assassinate Issakis since there are three forces that provide him non-stop protection: the garrison in the upper level of the Space Elevator, the drones at the Space Port, and the monster grown in the laboratory."}]},{"id":"kw-50057","title":"Issakis, Fourth Archpriest of the Splicers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_21_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An Archpriest in the Conclave of Archbishops, the leadership of the Splicers, and head of the House of Devils in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nIssakis is now located in a cabin that is part of the Eclipse Monolith's assembly line—a place once used to produce backup components for the space station, but which has been repurposed into a Fallen weapons factory.\nIssakis is likely not here to supervise production, though..."}]},{"id":"kw-60057","title":"Relic","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Powerful devices driven by Light.\n\nGenerally speaking, a Lightbearer determines their combat style when finding their \"destined Relic.\" These items are considered left by bygone Lightbearers and have passed hands several times, as if guided by a certain spiritual power. But in recent years, so-called artificial Relics have also proven reliable in combat. It seems that what we know about Light and its utilization in combat is only the tip of the iceberg."}]},{"id":"kw-50058","title":"Issakis, Fourth Archpriest of the Splicers","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 5","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_21_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An Archpriest in the Conclave of Archbishops, the leadership of the Splicers, and head of the House of Devils in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nIn the assembly line of the Eclipse Monolith, Issakis merged his consciousness with a Walker, becoming a complete cyborg. He has now returned to his command post, where he will carry out the next phase of his fanatical plan."}]},{"id":"kw-50060","title":"Wretches","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_34_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Lower-ranked Fallen soldiers who wield Arc-enhanced spears.\n\nThese Fallen have been stripped even of the right to hide behind cover. Armed with only a spear, all they can do is charge at their enemies head-on. Wretches may have slightly stronger protection than the Dregs, but they end up dying in even greater numbers."}]},{"id":"kw-50062","title":"Marksmen","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_39_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Fallen troops that snipe their enemies from a distance.\n\nThe harsh environments experienced by the Eliksni during the Long Drift caused them to gradually abandon their civilized nature and traditions, and in the early days, hatchlings with birth defects were left behind. However, some were unwilling to succumb to their fate, instead picking up the heavy wire rifles and training their marksmanship tirelessly. In the end, their shocking accuracy won them their Houses' acceptance.\nThe deep-rooted discrimination they face often distorts their psyche, and they see hunting prey as a way to vent their frustrations."}]},{"id":"kw-50063","title":"Marauder","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_40_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Comparatively tall Fallen who have the standard four arms.\n\nThese underhanded warriors wield cloaking technology and melee weapons, sneaking onto the battlefield and delivering deadly strikes to unsuspecting enemies. Their combat style leads to a higher survival rate compared to other Fallen units, which is why many Captains are promoted from Marauder."}]},{"id":"kw-50065","title":"Brigands","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_43_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Fallen equipped with Scorch Cannons and heavy armor.\n\nThese extremely selfish warriors force their underlings to act as flesh shields, firing slow but deadly explosives from the rear and deliberately avoiding any close range risks. The Bruisers may hate them, but the Brigands' high survival rate proves time and time again that the brutal strategy of treating subordinates as expendable is not without its merits."}]},{"id":"kw-50066","title":"Heavy Shanks","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_45_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A variant of Shank capable of providing Fallen troops with heavier firepower.\n\nDuring the Long Drift, a lack of resources forced the Fallen to recycle waste materials. This gave rise to the development of unconventional technologies such as Heavy Shanks, which combines standard Shank configurations with shells made from fragments of destroyed Servitors. With the Splicers' technology, once-sacred machines are given new life."}]},{"id":"kw-50067","title":"Cursed Thrall","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_49_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A variant of Thrall whose most obvious features are their chilling screams and their arms, which are always wrapped around their chests.\n\nInstead of striking with their claws as ordinary Thrall do, they detonate near their target, significantly harming nearby people or objects. They do not use their claws to strike enemies like ordinary Thrall, but instead detonate when approaching, causing significant damage to nearby people or objects. They rarely rush towards their targets, instead preferring an ambush approach."}]},{"id":"kw-50068","title":"Zealots","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_51_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A group of Acolytes who fight at close quarters.\n\nThe Hive adhere to Sword Logic in which one ascends through the ranks via slaughter. Acolytes are an ascended form of Thrall, and in combat, most would prefer to avoid the front lines in order to save their own lives. However, some special Acolytes believe they can achieve ascension by appeasing the Hive deities, which they do by fighting enemies at close range. Their fanaticism is not blind sacrifice, though, for paracausal energies grants them the ability to heal during battle. This emboldens the Zealots, turning the art of violence into a ritual of sacrifice."}]},{"id":"kw-50069","title":"Shrieker","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_52_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A variant of Hive with a metal body and an energy core inside.\n\nWe are still unsure whether Shriekers, vigilant sentinels deployed in Hive lairs to watch for enemy invasions, are creatures or machines. Some people believe there is a soul imprisoned within them, while others believe them to be entities of pure magic. No matter what they are, they launch high-speed barrages of energy at enemies as soon as they spot them, so they must be eliminated quickly."}]},{"id":"kw-50070","title":"Inquisitors","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_53_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Preachers and judges among the Hive.\n\nAlthough Sword Logic is the only truth in Hive society, heresy still exists. The purpose of these judges, whose bodies are engraved with magical runes and who constantly chant the Hive gods' words, is to maintain the purity of Hive beliefs.\nTheir fanatical faith enables them to unleash astonishing power, both internally and externally, when on the brink of death to ensure any and all heretics fall before their guns, proving the irrefutable truth of the Sword Logic with conquest, slaughter, and plunder."}]},{"id":"kw-60032","title":"Haven","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_90_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The stronghold of Iron Lord Radegast.\n\nAfter finding the Traveler again and discovering a growing encampment being built by survivors of the Collapse beneath it, Radegast was overwhelmed with joy, seeing it as a guarantee that he could realize his lifelong ambition. He abandoned his original territory in Eastern Europe and spent nearly 20 years building a refuge under the Tree of Light next to this emerging \"city,\" which would become today's Haven."}]},{"id":"kw-50071","title":"Tomb Ships","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The Hive's transport vessels.\n\nTomb Ships seem to have some form of teleportation capability, which lets them enter and exit areas with wormholes."}]},{"id":"kw-50072","title":"Cabal","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_27_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A hulking alien race with a brutal nature.\n\nThe society of this militarized cosmic empire is one that upholds ancient traditions. The emperor and military leaders stay on Torobatl, issuing orders to their legions, expanding the empire's borders, and conquering all those within their reach. The Cabal have enslaved countless races throughout the galaxy.\nFollowing the Collapse, several Cabal legions set their sights on Sol."}]},{"id":"kw-60042","title":"Shifting Gates","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A vault of technological treasures from humanity's Golden Age, reached via Shifting Gate connections.\n\nWhen the Collapse came, human civilization was nearly wiped out, and Bastra was no exception. But rumors that the Shifting Gate connects to all of the Golden Age's most treasured legacies persisted among what remained of human society. Donovan-17, a former Bastra technician who survived the Collapse, has the power to reactivate it. He travels among the major forces, recruiting Lightbearers to join him on his quest to find the lost treasures of the Golden Age in the Shifting Gates."}]},{"id":"kw-10005","title":"Ikora's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h102_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Used to wander during the Dark Age, dueling with unjust Warlords."}]},{"id":"kw-50073","title":"Torobatl","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The home planet of the Cabal empire.\n\nThis used to be a wild, harsh planet. Boundless deserts and wastes composed its main continent, and landwhales large enough to devour entire cities swam through its seas of sand, but ultimately, the Cabal conquered it. It's said that Torobatl was not the empire's first capital, but rather, the capital was moved here once a new emperor took the throne."}]},{"id":"kw-50075","title":"Sand Eaters","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_27_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Cabal legions that have invaded Sol.\n\nThe Sand Eaters' main force is located on Mars. While they were conquering the planet, they alarmed the Vex programming collective located there—the Virgo Prohibition—and sparked an immediate conflict. The number of Vex reinforcements pouring out from their network interface drastically exceeded the legion command's expectations, and they've since fallen into a prolonged tug of war."}]},{"id":"kw-50078","title":"Firebases","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The collective term for the military structures built by the Cabal in territories they occupy.\n\nA firebase is usually managed by a Valus. The buildings forming the firebase are largely uniform and serve specific operational objectives, such as frontline defense, training, or logistical support."}]},{"id":"kw-10059","title":"Finnala's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h207_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Treasures those closest to her."}]},{"id":"kw-50079","title":"Primus","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The highest commander of a Cabal legion.\n\nThe Primus must coordinate and make decisions on all aspects of a legion's operations, including strategic planning, personnel appointments and dismissals, recruitment of new troops, and logistical support. They are top-notch warriors, as evidenced by their ability to wield the legion's most advanced weaponry, but a Primus does not typically appear on the front lines. They are heavily protected by their subordinates, for if a legion is without its Primus, it will inevitably fall into turmoil."}]},{"id":"kw-50080","title":"Valus","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An executor of military orders at the command of the Primus.\n\nIf the Primus is the brains of a Cabal legion, then the Valus is its strongest hand. These are the individuals actually fighting on the front lines and turning strategic goals into results. Once a Valus has fully demonstrated their abilities, they may become a candidate for Primus. This typically leads them to complete their missions by any means necessary."}]},{"id":"kw-60046","title":"Ketch Wreckage","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_102_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Remnants of a House of Devils Ketch that crashed in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nDuring the centuries of the Long Drift, the Ketch, named after the House of Devils's former Prime Servitor Maliks, led the House's starships across the sea of stars. Through great hardship, it finally arrived at Earth, only to crash during an attack on Jiangshi Metro.\nYears later, the Ketch's wreckage's automated defenses went haywire, making the whole place filled with deadly traps. Despite the threat, there are still many who are attracted by the rumored lost treasure of the Kell and are willing to risk their lives to enter the ship."}]},{"id":"kw-10001","title":"Kabr's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h202_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"So passionate and frank it can be headache-inducing."}]},{"id":"kw-10002","title":"Kabr's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h202_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Is better at protecting his companions than attacking enemies head-on."}]},{"id":"kw-10003","title":"Kabr's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h202_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Often searching for opportunities to go on heroic adventures at Haven's tavern."}]},{"id":"kw-10004","title":"Kabr's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h202_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Used to go by another name."}]},{"id":"kw-40067","title":"ASTERI","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The name of the Speaker before she took her current post.\n\nAsteri was born on an island in the southern Aegean Sea. At that time, the waters and islands belonged to Rita-4, a Warlord who, like others of her ilk, was cruel, ruthless, and set in her ways. Despite the Warlord's tyrannical rule, Asteri, a mortal child growing up on the seaside, found joy even in hardship. She had a family that, despite living in poverty, was still filled with love, as well as a somewhat unusual group of friends—Ghosts who had yet to find their Lightbearers.\nIt was only when the Iron Lord Efrideet came to that distant island that Asteri learned that she was no ordinary girl. She was a Speaker."}]},{"id":"kw-10006","title":"Ikora's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h102_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Keen on exploring the unknown and a skilled wielder of the universe's Void energy."}]},{"id":"kw-40017","title":"Liang Xing","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The founder of the Jiangshi Metro guerrillas and a mortal warrior who fought alongside Xuân Yến in the battle to overthrow Yannick.\n\nLiang Xing did not trust Xuân Yến in the beginning. Worried that Xuân Yến would become a tyrant just like Yannick, he established an armed force of mortals. However, time eventually proved Xuân Yến's morality, and the guerrillas also recognized her rule.\nLiang Xing eventually died in a raid on the House of Devils' Ketch, after which Mu Ying took over his duties."}]},{"id":"kw-10008","title":"Ikora's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h102_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Is currently investigating certain horrors that may threaten Sol."}]},{"id":"kw-50082","title":"Buhr","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_128_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"One of the leaders in charge of the Red Sea Rift Sand Eaters following Valus Zau'ul's disappearance.\n\nBuhr was once Zau'ul's deputy and the commander of Firebase Minos. He seized command of the firebase without the Valus's knowledge, and now, he will stop at nothing to keep his position and finish what Zau'ul failed to do: quashing the \"lowly inhabitants\" of the Red Sea Rift and conquering the territory completely."}]},{"id":"kw-50083","title":"Buhr","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_28_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The leader of the Red Sea Rift Sand Eaters following Valus Zau'ul's disappearance and Tog'urk's defeat at the hands of the Lightbearers.\n\nAfter fully seizing control of the Red Sea Rift Sand Eaters, Buhr no longer has to hide his strong interest in the Sentinel and the Light. He created an automated assembly line to dismantle the Sentinel wreckage and, through a series of simulation experiments, developed Sentinel armor capable of significantly enhancing Cabal soldiers' combat prowess."}]},{"id":"kw-50084","title":"Tog'urk","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_29_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The manager of the Cabal's Foundry and one of the leaders in charge of the Red Sea Rift Sand Eaters following Valus Zau'ul's disappearance.\n\nHe is a \"traditional\" Cabal officer who is accustomed to solving problems with flames and cannons. Tog'urk scoffed at Buhr's interest in the Sentinel, seeing it as unconventional. He not only publicly accused Buhr of being \"cowardly,\" but also secretly seized his military supplies. The power struggle between the two officers has greatly weakened the legion."}]},{"id":"kw-50085","title":"Vulpes, Array Bulwark","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A customized prototype Goliath Tank.\n\nThis Goliath Tank, equipped with enhanced collision and firepower capabilities, was developed at Buhr's personal request.\nOne of his adversary's subordinates, Thagrius, expressed his willingness to help Buhr research the Light. In order to confirm this technician's abilities, Buhr requested a custom Goliath Tank. Needless to say, the results far exceeded Buhr's expectations."}]},{"id":"kw-40068","title":"ASTERI","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The name of the Speaker before she took her current post.\n\nIn accordance with the Iron Lords' creed, Efrideet challenged Rita-4 to a duel, with the village as their wager. After a hard-fought victory, Efrideet approached Asteri and her family and declared that she would take them to a new and better home. However, on the night the residents were packing to leave, Rita-4 set fire to the village. In her eyes, the existence of anything that didn't belong to her was meaningless.\nEfrideet only had time to save a few of the villagers and Asteri, whose parents had perished in the blaze."}]},{"id":"kw-10013","title":"Jolder's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h204_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"An unparalleled duelist and warrior whose looks can kill."}]},{"id":"kw-40018","title":"Alechio","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"Ayuela's mother and the leader of the data archaeologists in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nAlthough Alechio disappeared when Ayuela was still a child, the memories of living with her mother still influence her to this day."}]},{"id":"kw-50123","title":"Hexguards","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_55_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A variant of Hive Knight, transformed by a paracausal ritual.\n\nIn a fierce battle between the Hive and a certain civilization blessed by the Light, some Knights were transformed by a ritual, giving their chitin shells the strength to withstand the Light's impact, and equipping them with shields pieced together from the remains of their brethren as well as swords capable of absorbing an enemy's vitality to heal the wielder. The price they must pay, however, is the ceaseless pain brought by the permanent fusion of their bodies and shells. This mutation has forced the Hexguards to abandon long-range weapons, as their only respite is extracting vitality from foes via their blades."}]},{"id":"kw-10015","title":"Jolder's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h204_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"The proud owner of a one-of-a-kind title awarded by the Iron Lords: Iron Champion."}]},{"id":"kw-10016","title":"Jolder's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h204_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Seems to be searching for an intelligent weapon of the Golden Age for a certain reason."}]},{"id":"kw-10017","title":"Attal's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h105_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Wears traditional Moroccan garments and metal accessories."}]},{"id":"kw-10019","title":"Attal's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h105_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Close to a Lightbearer with an oppressive temperament."}]},{"id":"kw-10020","title":"Attal's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h105_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Teaches human language to Eliksni refugees."}]},{"id":"kw-10021","title":"Maru's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h206_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Was once a notorious pirate sailing the South Pacific."}]},{"id":"kw-10022","title":"Maru's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h206_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Has a bounty on her head after plundering the Warlords."}]},{"id":"kw-10023","title":"Maru's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h206_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Among the first Lightbearers to be revived."}]},{"id":"kw-60059","title":"Photon Reactors","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A Sentinel's energy core, a creation of Light from the Golden Age."}]},{"id":"kw-40065","title":"Maln","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A Radiancite smuggler and \"old friend\" whom Jaren has traveled thousands of miles to kill personally.\n\nMaln once traveled with Marco, and the two brought the newly revived Jaren with them as they wandered the Mojave Desert. This should have been a band of sworn brothers, yet ultimately, the trio fell apart due to betrayal, with Maln killing Marco and crushing his Ghost with his own two hands. Jaren resolved to avenge Marco, but Maln, knowing he was outmatched, always stayed hidden, with his tracks only occasionally showing up where seedy deals would take place. This went on until the present, with Jaren having finally tracked him down in the Red Sea Rift.\nIn order to create an opportunity to meet him face-to-face, Jaren has prepared to have Bobak and his uncles bait him out with a Radiancite trade."}]},{"id":"kw-10024","title":"Maru's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h206_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Skillfully uses a variety of methods to achieve her goals."}]},{"id":"kw-10025","title":"Ning Fei's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h305_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Wears a unique headband and wields a staff as his Relic."}]},{"id":"kw-10026","title":"Ning Fei's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h305_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Leaves traces of Arc where he fights. Those he attacks usually find wounds on their backs."}]},{"id":"kw-40046","title":"The Survivor","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"An adult Eliksni from a House of no real renown.\n\nBased on the contents of the communicator he dropped, his House was at a disadvantage in a conflict with the House of Devils and seems to have not fared well."}]},{"id":"kw-10027","title":"Ning Fei's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h305_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Acts recklessly and does whatever he pleases. Often has conflicts with his Ghost."}]},{"id":"kw-40053","title":"MERLO","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A helpless father who will do anything to get his missing daughter back.\n\nHis daughter made a wish to the so-called \"Wish-Granter\" hoping to bring her father out from the shadow of grief left by her mother's death. But the Ahamkara Zelpachad twisted this innocent wish, resulting in Merlo completely forgetting his beloved wife. Now, Zelpachad has also taken Nora."}]},{"id":"kw-10028","title":"Ning Fei's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h305_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Is searching for an embedded chip with special functions in Jiangshi Metro."}]},{"id":"kw-50086","title":"Thagrius","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The Tech Adjutant serving under Buhr.\n\nThagrius was once a talented technician under Tog'urk, but he was constantly suppressed. Feeling dissatisfied with his superior and noting the conflict between Buhr and Tog'urk, he seized the opportunity to join forces with Buhr by building him a custom Goliath Tank according to his specifications. Now he holds the title of Tech Adjutant and is fully committed to uncovering the secrets of the Sentinel and the Light for his new superior."}]},{"id":"kw-50087","title":"Psion","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_60_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Soldiers with psychic abilities who hail from a race conquered and enslaved by the Cabal.\n\nPsions belonged to a species with an independent culture until the Cabal conquered them and forcibly incorporated them into their empire. This resulted in the near-complete loss of their traditions and beliefs.\nPsions' psychic abilities are only allowed to be used as weaponry in service of their masters. There was a point where, like any other enslaved race, they were denied political rights within the empire. It was only recently when the new emperor ascended the throne that some of them became free citizens and were able to join the army."}]},{"id":"kw-60015","title":"Exos","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Mechanical beings possessing human consciousness, created during the Golden Age.\n\nFrom the pre-Golden Age to the Golden Age, countless people have come up with various hypotheses on how to achieve immortality. One of the more popular ones was to import human consciousness into machines.\nDuring the Golden Age, countless people attempted it, yet only one was successful—the founder of Bray Tech, Clovis Bray I. In the Deep Stone Crypt of Europa, the first Exo to possess human consciousness was born."}]},{"id":"kw-50088","title":"Legionary","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_61_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Cabal soldiers equipped with pressurized combat suits and heavy artillery. They are the basic combat units of a legion's forces.\n\nLegionaries obey the orders of field sergeants and carry out all manner of tasks on the battlefield with great flexibility, sometimes advancing the front line and other times defending strongholds. Their helmets are equipped with an emergency medical system that uses gel to lessen impact, stabilize injuries, and stop bleeding."}]},{"id":"kw-50089","title":"Vigile","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_62_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Cabal soldiers who wield shotguns and jetpacks.\n\nVigiles are riot officers in the imperial police force who suppress slave uprisings on major planets. Their capabilities don't lend themselves to large-scale, front lines battles, but their brutal efficiency leads many commanders to incorporate them into as special agents, using their fierce and radical combat style to broaden the legion's available tactics."}]},{"id":"kw-50093","title":"Incendiors","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_66_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Cabal heavy infantry equipped with magma launchers. Spec-ops units within a legion.\n\nIncendiors can use their magma launchers to scorch enemies in a wide range or use sudden bursts of flames to repel nearby foes, making them extremely dangerous enemies at close range. If one can detonate the fuel tanks at their backs, though, they'll get a taste of their own medicine."}]},{"id":"kw-10033","title":"Tan-2's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h104_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"A young Exo who wields a sword-like Relic."}]},{"id":"kw-40035","title":"Gareth","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Red Sea Rift's former lord and the founder of Veridia.\n\nIn the Dark Age, the supplies carried by sunken ships scattered throughout the Red Sea Rift attracted the attention of mortals and Lightbearers. For a long time, the Red Sea Rift was a Lightbearer battlefield. Among those fighting for control of the area was Gareth, the one who valued the safety and wellbeing of mortals the most. He established a basic settlement beneath the wreckage of a ship called \"The Veridia,\" from which the future democracy of its namesake developed.\nAfter Veridia began to take shape, Gareth met Saladin and Radegast near the Red Sea Rift. He immediately joined the Iron Lords, becoming a member of their brotherhood."}]},{"id":"kw-10038","title":"Gwynn's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h103_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Reaps her enemies' souls using a scythe as tall as she is."}]},{"id":"kw-60060","title":"Sparrow","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_92_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A single-seat hover vehicle used to traverse long distances quickly."}]},{"id":"kw-10039","title":"Gwynn's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h103_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"A silent Lightbearer with a chatty Ghost."}]},{"id":"kw-10042","title":"Umeko's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h310_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Seems to be affiliated with a mysterious organization."}]},{"id":"kw-10043","title":"Umeko's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h310_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Is particularly fond of Ghosts."}]},{"id":"kw-40037","title":"Gareth","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Red Sea Rift's former lord and the founder of Veridia.\n\nNo one knows what happened between Radegast and Gareth when they confronted each other in the Red Sea Rift.\nWhen Saladin arrived at the scene, the battle had already ended, and Gareth was nowhere to be found. All that was left was his dead Ghost.\nRadegast has never spoken about what happened that day, and Gareth was ultimately deemed deceased."}]},{"id":"kw-10044","title":"Umeko's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h310_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"The more someone working with her trusts her, the more likely they are to hate her after the fact."}]},{"id":"kw-40036","title":"Gareth","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Red Sea Rift's former lord and the founder of Veridia.\n\nAt some point, Gareth gradually became obsessed with gaining more and more power. His obsession led him down the path of dictatorship, and he enslaved the people of Veridia until the Iron Lords put an end to his rule.\nGareth once owned an antique that looked like a lantern. Radegast believes this object was twisted by paracausal forces and became the source of the former Iron Lord's downfall."}]},{"id":"kw-10045","title":"Xuan Wei's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h205_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"A stalwart Eastern warrior, said to be resurrected from millennia ago."}]},{"id":"kw-10046","title":"Xuan Wei's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h205_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Fights with Arc Light-enhanced martial arts."}]},{"id":"kw-10047","title":"Xuan Wei's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h205_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Once opposed the Iron Lords."}]},{"id":"kw-40041","title":"Yannick-11","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The last Warlord to rule Jiangshi Metro.\n\nTan-2 re-activated Parhelion Wing and entered its data to find the last remnant of Yannick-11's consciousness and return it to his own memory core. Now they are back where they started, with the two minds sharing a single body."}]},{"id":"kw-10048","title":"Xuan Wei's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h205_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Wants to acquire a Light barrier generator like that on the Red Sea Rift Sentinel's arm."}]},{"id":"kw-10049","title":"Estela's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h108_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Wields a rather curious Relic made of bone and has a seemingly mute Ghost."}]},{"id":"kw-40047","title":"The Survivor","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"An adult Eliksni from a House of no real renown.\n\nThe survivor fled with the House's few surviving children in tow, searching for hope. They are currently in danger and in desperate need of a Servitor that can provide Ether. The survivor happened to meet Attal and received her promise to help fix a Servitor."}]},{"id":"kw-10050","title":"Estela's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h108_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Seems to avoid forming relationships with others."}]},{"id":"kw-10052","title":"Estela's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h108_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Is able to easily grasp what others are thinking."}]},{"id":"kw-40028","title":"Harrow","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_14_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"President of the Veridian Union.\n\nHarrow cracked the secret of the box at her residence in a secluded cave and took its contents away. She used it not only to open the sealed door inside the Weathered Caves, but also to activate and control a group of mechanical life forms driven by a hive mind and capable of traveling through time and space: the Vex. For some reason, Harrow believes these machines to be Veridia's only chance at ridding itself of the Cabal."}]},{"id":"kw-10053","title":"Rossi-11's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h109_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Wears the mask of an exile, yet dresses in the robes of a noble."}]},{"id":"kw-40019","title":"Alechio","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"Ayuela's mother, leader of the data archaeologists in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nAfter Radegast withdrew the Lightbearers protecting the data archaeologists, Alechio returned to the Fallen-occupied Data Center alone and programmed a firewall that the invaders would never be able to crack, preserving the technologies of the Golden Age until Ayuela would find them fourteen years later."}]},{"id":"kw-10054","title":"Rossi-11's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h109_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Detains foes with threads, fighting in a practiced and efficient manner."}]},{"id":"kw-40042","title":"???","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A legendary Lightbearer renowned for his erudition.\n\nPeople the world over tell tales of this Lightbearer. They speak of a sharp mind rivaled only by his immense power, and of the numerous books he's written on the Light. His keen farsightedness makes him something of a sage in the eyes of many, but his temperament and attitude tend to draw their ire."}]},{"id":"kw-10055","title":"Rossi-11's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h109_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Often appears when the residents of the Red Sea Rift are in trouble."}]},{"id":"kw-40033","title":"Khalid","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Lightbearers under the Iron Banner who Saladin brought with him to Veridia.\n\nAs an intelligence officer under Saladin's command, he's responsible for compiling and analyzing intel collected by the militia. He provides not only support for the formulation of Saladin and Finnala's battle plans, but also guidance to all Lightbearers who come to the Red Sea Rift to confront the Cabal.\nKhalid hasn't found his own Relic capable of channeling the Light yet and is thus rarely present on the battlefield, but his contributions to the battles in the Red Sea Rift are no less invaluable."}]},{"id":"kw-10056","title":"Rossi-11's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h109_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Came to Veridia in search of someone from the past."}]},{"id":"kw-40032","title":"Shira","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_15_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The current representative of the Veridian Union's miners.\n\nShira said she has a way for us to gain the upper hand against the Cabal: plundering one of their Goliath Tanks and appoint a genius mechanic who previously came into contact with Cabal machinery while captive—that being herself—to drive it. No matter how imaginative or convoluted her ideas may be, Shira proved her expertise on the applications of machinery, both human and Cabal, during this operation."}]},{"id":"kw-10057","title":"Finnala's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h207_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Lord Saladin's loyal and dependable Iron Wolf."}]},{"id":"kw-40039","title":"Yannick-11","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The last Warlord to rule Jiangshi Metro.\n\nAccording to Yannick-11's original plan, Parhelion Wing should have destroyed the wielder's consciousness upon being activated by the Light. However, plans changed, forcing him to share a body with a hotheaded kid. Using a method that could separate the two minds as a cover story, he tricked Tan-2 into activating his lab's control system, which would thoroughly delete the boy's consciousness and let him take sole control of the Exo body."}]},{"id":"kw-10058","title":"Finnala's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h207_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Methodical in both speech and actions, and a strict adherent to law and order in Veridia."}]},{"id":"kw-10060","title":"Finnala's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h207_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Seems to hail from the Sahara, but rarely mentions her hometown."}]},{"id":"kw-40020","title":"The Speaker","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A mysterious child who wears a unique mask. She is said to be capable of communicating with the Traveler.\n\nIn the Golden Age, the chosen Speakers were able to perceive the Traveler's dreams. However, ever since the Collapse, the wounded Traveler has appeared unable to communicate normally. This resulted in incomprehensible information flooding the Speakers' minds and driving them to insanity. Only a few found a way to make the dreams clearer.\nNowadays, there are very few surviving Speakers."}]},{"id":"kw-10061","title":"Helhest's Bio I","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h309_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Lord Felwinter's Iron Wolf, hailing from the distant Felwinter Peak."}]},{"id":"kw-10062","title":"Helhest's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h309_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Better at communicating with machines and data than humans."}]},{"id":"kw-40034","title":"Azizah Hassan","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"Veridia's archivist.\n\nAzizah has been in charge of Veridia's files and public records ever since Lord Gareth's rule. Being able to access classified documents has given her an understanding of the Red Sea Rift's unusual phenomena far surpassing that of other townspeople."}]},{"id":"kw-10063","title":"Helhest's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h309_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Possesses a keen understanding of Awoken technology."}]},{"id":"kw-10065","title":"Jaren 1","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h303_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Almost always wears a hat and sunglasses."}]},{"id":"kw-10066","title":"Jaren 2","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h303_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Carries a hand cannon infused with Light yet unable to fire normal bullets."}]},{"id":"kw-10070","title":"Kabr, the Resolute's Bio II","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h211_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Has formed a solid fireteam with two friends he met on his adventures."}]},{"id":"kw-10071","title":"Kabr, the Resolute's Bio III","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h211_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"No longer obsessed with becoming a hero, he now focuses on honing himself."}]},{"id":"kw-10072","title":"Kabr, the Resolute's Bio IV","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h211_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Seems particularly interested in researching the Vex."}]},{"id":"kw-10074","title":"Efrideet 2","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h312_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Undefeated in every marksmanship contest to date."}]},{"id":"kw-40062","title":"Bobak","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"An orphan who was taken in by a pair of Veridia's unemployed miners.\n\nBobak encountered Jaren while the latter was tracking down Maln. Hoping to save his trapped uncles, he became an important part of Jaren's plans to lure out Maln."}]},{"id":"kw-60008","title":"Dark Age","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A period of great disorder following the Collapse.\n\nAfter the Collapse, the Traveler fell into a long hibernation. At this time, human civilization had been nearly wiped out. The old order no longer existed and was instead replaced by the laws of the jungle, where the strong prey on the weak. Violent conflicts over the few remaining resources frequently erupted among the survivors.\nIt was an era filled with slaughter, looting, slavery, and death. For the almost immortal Lightbearer Warlords, their time had come."}]},{"id":"kw-10075","title":"Efrideet 3","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h312_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"Seems to have great rapport with every Iron Lord."}]},{"id":"kw-40005","title":"Donovan-17","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_8_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A technician from the Golden Age.\n\nAfter the Collapse, human civilization was almost wiped out, and many miraculous technologies were lost. It was with extreme luck that a few personnel who were familiar with Golden Age technologies survived, giving their technologies the potential of a second chance.\nDonovan-17 was one such technician. As a former employee of Bastra, Donovan can manipulate the Shifting Gate, enabling Lightbearers to travel across space and explore the various ruins of the Golden Age."}]},{"id":"kw-60023","title":"Guerrillas of Jiangshi Metro","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The main armed forces of Jiangshi Metro.\n\nAfter the Warlord Yannick-11 was overthrown by Lady Xuân Yến, the mortals gained the right to bear arms and orchestrate their own defense. The guerrillas were initially established in fear of their new ruler following in Yannick's tyrannical footsteps, but over time, the militia organization gradually discovered her to be nothing like the brutal warlord and thus abandoned their hidden purpose. After Lady Xuân Yến joined the Iron Lords, the guerrillas gave her their complete trust and obeyed her leadership."}]},{"id":"kw-10076","title":"Efrideet 4","sub":"Lightbearer","quality":null,"art":"data_yx_h312_inset_b_01","filters":{"Kind":"Lightbearer"},"body":[{"p":"The Relic is forged from branches of the Tree of Light."}]},{"id":"kw-50090","title":"War Beast","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_63_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Creatures native to Torobatl, which the Cabal have trained as combat units.\n\nThese ferocious, violent animals are widely used by Cabal legions for reconnaissance, raids, or as cannon fodder in melee battles. In battle, these beasts launch non-stop, fierce attacks on their enemies, trying to tear their flesh from their bones with their sharp teeth and claws. A War Beast won't let up until either it or its target is dead."}]},{"id":"kw-50094","title":"Decurions","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_67_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A reserve officer position that has existed since before the Cabal wielded firearms.\n\nDecurions are mostly young officers with solid theoretical knowledge but a lack of practical experience. Their responsibilities mainly involve accumulating said experience by guarding their superiors and occasionally leading troops in battle. Their equipment also focuses on defense and long-range support. Advancements in technology have seen their traditional metal armor upgraded to power armor and their javelins replaced by cluster rocket launchers, but the Decurion position itself remains to this day."}]},{"id":"kw-50096","title":"Gladiator","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_69_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Elite Cabal warriors who wield melee weapons.\n\nThe worship of violence is innate among the Cabal, and thus their ancient culture of gladiatorial competitions remains to this day. The winners, wielding blades instead of guns and rising from bloodbaths treated as sport, stand out as superstars among Cabal society and elite melee warriors among the legions' ranks. Once a Gladiator is close, few creatures can survive their blades."}]},{"id":"kw-50098","title":"Juggernauts","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_71_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Special, heavily armored soldiers equipped with improved high-caliber heavy ammunition launchers.\n\nEven for the hulking Cabal, these high-caliber launchers, which are typically mounted to vehicles, are too heavy. Legion technicians may have greatly reduced the weapons' weight so that individual soldiers can wield them too, but only the strongest Cabal manage to do so—especially given their armor must be equipped with additional decompression devices.\nThese heavily armed and armored units are called \"Juggernauts,\" a fitting name given their appearance and destructive power."}]},{"id":"kw-50100","title":"Interceptors","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Single-unit floating vehicles used for Cabal offenses.\n\nInterceptors can launch two explosive shells simultaneously. Despite being slower than Sparrows or Pikes, their thrusters allow for brief bursts of acceleration. Due to their superior maneuverability compared to Goliath Tanks, Interceptors are often used to combat infantry and lightweight enemy vehicles.\nThe vehicles provide very little protection for the ones piloting them, so targeting their Psion drivers is far more efficient than trying to destroy the Interceptor itself."}]},{"id":"kw-60037","title":"Iron Bar","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An arena located near Haven where Lightbearers can challenge on another, managed by Iron Bard Skorri.\n\nIn the Dark Age, the Crucible was a bloody arena for settling personal grudges between Lightbearers. With her territory not far from it, Skorri witnessed many battles between Lightbearers. After joining the Iron Lords, she was appointed by Radegast to train the Lightbearer recruits who joined the Iron Banner. Based on her own experiences and out of personal interest and a need for inspiration, Skorri would create an arena that lets Lightbearers grow and learn from fierce battles in setting that prohibits harm to their Ghosts. This is how the Iron Bar came to be."}]},{"id":"kw-50102","title":"Vex","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_30_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The first extraterrestrial race that humans truly encountered.\n\nAs early as the Golden Age, when humans first landed on other planets in Sol, they discovered these strange robots often gathering around ancient ruins. Some institutions researched them and, surprisingly, found them capable of traveling through time and space. Even more chilling, though, is that they can achieve a certain degree of foresight and control over the future by creating simulations."}]},{"id":"kw-50103","title":"Programming Collectives","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Groups of Vex that share a single consensus.\n\nAlthough the Vex do indeed use a hive mind, there is not just one \"brain\" doing the thinking. Among the Vex are multiple chains of thought that govern different Vex collectives. The vast majority of thought chains do share some kind of consensus, but there are also situations where a certain collective contradicts the Vex's collective consciousness.\nBut is the emergence of such heresy intentional on the part of the collective consciousness? The answer is currently unknown."}]},{"id":"kw-60031","title":"Old City Theater","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A large, well-preserved building in the Old City.\n\nJudging by the posters left here, many plays were staged here during the Golden Age. Though the laughter and tears that used to fill its hall are long gone, it still offers a glimpse into the lives of humans during the height of civilization."}]},{"id":"kw-50104","title":"Virgo Prohibition","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_30_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A Vex collective the Sand Eaters encountered when they first arrived on Mars and began their expansion.\n\nThe legion's commanders deemed the Virgo Prohibition's numbers to be low when they first exchanged fire, and thus went on the offense. However, the Virgo Prohibition immediately responded by summoning reinforcements from their network that far exceeded the Cabal's expectations. Interestingly, the number of Vex reinforcements summoned is always just enough to hold the front line in a fixed area, ensuring no extra force is wasted."}]},{"id":"kw-50105","title":"The Vex Network","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A massive simulated reality that transcends dimensions and spacetime.\n\nThe Vex Network is the final simulation of the universe as envisioned by the Vex. In this near-infinite space, the Vex conduct endless calculations. The Network transcends linear timelines, allowing the Vex to reach any timeline they wish via portals connected to reality. However, the presence of these portals means other organisms also have a way to enter the Network."}]},{"id":"kw-50106","title":"Confluxes","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An extra-dimensional Vex construct used to connect their Network with reality.\n\nThey can be columnar structures composed of pure energy, or they can look like stone-encased machines. Regardless of form, they all function as a channel connecting the Vex Network and reality. Through these Confluxes, the Vex can gradually rewrite and replace real spaces with their own simulated scenarios, thus making arbitrary modifications to \"reality.\""}]},{"id":"kw-50108","title":"Axis Minds","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An individual Vex within the collective intelligence who has the authority to issue commands.\n\nIn most cases, a region's Vex collective is controlled by an Axis Mind, whose essence is a specific directive or purpose within the Vex's collective consciousness. They will not personally visit the battlefield unless the situation threatens this purpose. If by chance they do need to join the battle, they usually choose advanced combat units such as Minotaurs or Hydras as carriers."}]},{"id":"kw-50109","title":"Zephyrus, Nexus Mind","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_31_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The Zephyrus, Nexus Mind lurking in the Red Sea Rift.\n\nWhen the Sand Eaters established their firebase in the Red Sea Rift and prepared to expand the scale of their war, the Vex, given their nature as intelligent mechanical lifeforms capable of predicting the future, immediately deployed their forces to counter them. They established a hidden Conflux beneath the Sentinel's wreckage and dispatched Zephyrus, the Nexus Mind, to wait there. Because of the Lightbearers' intervention, the Vex chose to continue concealing their presence...until an unpredictable paracausal force disrupted their plan."}]},{"id":"kw-50111","title":"Fanatics","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A type of Goblin that appears to have suffered severe damage.\n\nAll Fanatics have a disorderly gait, a missing left arm, exposed wiring, and more often than not, multiple scratches and damage on their chassis.\nThey do not seem to have any purpose beyond spreading corrosive radiolarian fluid."}]},{"id":"kw-50113","title":"Hobgoblins","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_78_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A Goblin unit modified for ranged attacks.\n\nHobgoblins fire slow yet precise shots, but lack the means to counterattack when approached. They will enter standby mode and initiate self-repair after sustaining serious damage."}]},{"id":"kw-60033","title":"Archives","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A building in Haven that houses all sorts of knowledge.\n\nBack in Eastern Europe, Radegast had instructed his men to collect and archive information that might seem worthless to others. Following the establishment of Haven, a facility was built to keep such files. In Radegast's view, the preservation of past and present knowledge is far more important than territories, armaments, and power if one means to revive human civilization."}]},{"id":"kw-50114","title":"Harpies","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_79_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Vex units that fly at high speeds.\n\nHarpies are usually deployed by the Axis Mind for disruption and flank attacks. They cannot balance movement and attack, so they must hover in place before entering attack mode."}]},{"id":"kw-50115","title":"Imps","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_80_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Harpies that have given up mobility in favor of high-precision long-range weapons.\n\nHarpies usually rely on mobility to carry out flank attacks, but their effectiveness is limited against heavily defended or fully armored opponents. To address this shortcoming, some Axis Minds have taken to deploying modified Harpies, or \"Imps.\" What these flying units lose in maneuverability they gain in highly precise firepower. Their limited movement can also be somewhat compensated for with teleportation modules."}]},{"id":"kw-50117","title":"Mazeguard","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_82_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Specially modified Minotaurs used to protect the portals connecting the Vex Network and reality.\n\nMazeguards are highly aggressive and will actively suppress enemies in order to eliminate those who would invade the Network as quickly as possible. They can activate the generators in their arms to create powerful shockwaves, ensuring ignorant would-be trespassers know the folly of their actions."}]},{"id":"kw-50118","title":"Asterions","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_83_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A type of modified Minotaur.\n\nThe integrated chest and waist structures of the Asterions provide better for their radiolarian chambers, as they often coordinate with Cyclops for defensive tasks. But such modification sacrifices their teleportation capabilities. Because of their limited mobility, they are deployed on the battlefield only when specific tactical needs arise."}]},{"id":"kw-50119","title":"Cyclops","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_84_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Massive Vex units equipped with devastatingly powerful artillery.\n\nIn addition to their use as weapons, Cyclops may be the Vex's beacon units. Their large core connects with the Vex Network, providing positioning for other Vex units that crosses space-time."}]},{"id":"kw-50120","title":"Hydra","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_85_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The Vex's mobile bulwarks, featuring heavy armor and a rotating energy shield.\n\nThese giant floating machines are nodes of the Vex's thought-mesh, equipped with broadcast components that can quickly issue instructions to other nearby Vex units. In many cases, the Hydra model is the primary choice for Axis Minds."}]},{"id":"kw-50121","title":"Sphinxes","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_86_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A particularly unique Vex unit.\n\nThe Sphinx has multiple soft, metal tentacles that can extend from its body, with the components at their ends serving both detection and attack functions. Their movement speed is limited by their heavy armor, but the Vex's spacetime technology allows for rapid teleportation, letting them deal devastating and unexpected blows to enemies."}]},{"id":"kw-50124","title":"Molkrul, the Engineer","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The technician who has seized control of the Lanyue 5 Factory.\n\nMolkrul is a Vandal elite from the House of Devils. Obsessed with technology, he knows machinery like the back of his hand and was always responsible for repairing the Ketch's Shanks. After the House of Devils occupied the Lanyue 5 Factory, the Golden Age technology the humans left behind caught his eye. This led him to station himself in the factory, where he could research and dismantle the machines once used for producing rockets until finally, he repurposed the original rocket part assembly line to mass-produce Shanks. Using the lab's equipment, he also crafted a massive and exceedingly powerful Shank prototype."}]},{"id":"kw-40024","title":"Saladin","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_13_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Iron Lords' founders and the military leader of Veridia.\n\nSaladin accused Radegast of betraying the oath he swore under the Iron Banner by killing their brother-in-arms, Gareth, to which Radegast pointed out that the late lord had already been corrupted by Ahamkara magic. Perhaps this is the root of the conflict between the two.\nHarrow believes that Saladin himself has similarly sunk into the quagmire that is Ahamkara magic—she was the one who granted Saladin's wish to protect Veridia."}]},{"id":"kw-50125","title":"Iltaraus, the Pillager","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A Wizard trying to seize the Light and use it for herself.\n\nUnlike other Hive who despise the Light, Iltaraus will not reject anything capable of strengthening her, no matter its form—including the Traveler's gifts. When she realized there was Light-blessed Golden Age technology scattered across the Jiangshi Ice Field's surface, she set to work collecting it and, with her Acolytes' help, converting and extracting the energy inside.\nJust as Sword Logic teaches, what cannot be destroyed will surpass infinity."}]},{"id":"kw-60045","title":"Jiangshi Metro","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_100_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A transportation hub located in what was once the center of Jiangshi.\n\nWhen the Fallen invasion began, the guerrillas of Jiangshi Metro were caught off guard. Their positions were lost one after another, and for a time, the humans only controlled a small area near the station, and their communications with other regions were cut off. The first wave of Fallen attacks was eventually stopped, though it cost the lives of the Iron Lady and her squad, and the guerrillas regained much of their territory.\nSince then, Jiangshi Metro has served as the guerrillas' base of operations."}]},{"id":"kw-50126","title":"Yuriiks-7, the Mind Disruptor","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"A special Servitor lurking within the Ketch wreckage.\n\nWhen the House of Devils invaded Earth, they discovered files left over from a \"Speaker creation experiment.\" The Speaker is capable of receiving messages from the Traveler, while the Fallen built their Servitors in its image. The House of Devils created the special Servitor Yuriiks with this purpose in mind, iterating on it through experiment after experiment until finally, Yuriiks-7 was born. When it was used in experiments, it showed itself capable of giving the Fallen hallucinations. However, those hallucinations did not deliver any revelations from the Traveler, and after undergoing the experiment several times, the subjects would begin descending into madness.\nYuriiks-7 appears to enjoy controlling others' consciousnesses. It escaped the lab and constructed a \"consciousness lockdown unit,\" which incited chaos within the House of Devils. All they could do was seal it within the lab. When the Ketch landed, they would try to find more documents left by the human scientists to further perfect Yuriiks-7."}]},{"id":"kw-50127","title":"Hive Runes","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An ideographic writing system used by the Hive.\n\nThese runes contain power from another dimension. Each carries a unique meaning, and together, they are capable of many impossible feats of magic, including prophecy (though the method of using them for foretelling one's future is currently unknown).\nThey are largely found on Hive architecture and ships. Although humans have deciphered a few runes' meanings, they are continually discovering new ones."}]},{"id":"kw-50128","title":"Ir Eruna, Swordsinger","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"Crota's executioner.\n\nIr Eruna's methods of gaining power are extreme even by Hive standards. She encourages her subordinates to slaughter each other, with each battle's loser becoming fodder for the victor; the victor climbs the ranks and becomes her champion, only to become her own tribute in an unfortunate final defeat.\nShe studied different rituals in an effort to apply Sword Logic more efficiently, and once she arrived on Earth, she began trying to use humans and Lightbearers as sacrifices. When it comes to her captives, she takes morbid pleasure in deceiving them through illusions."}]},{"id":"kw-50129","title":"Eliksni Language","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"As the name suggests—the language spoken by the Eliksni.\n\nIt often sounds like an insectoid chittering to human ears. Because it relies on the Eliksni's unique vocal organs, only a few particularly talented humans have been capable of learning this language."}]},{"id":"kw-50130","title":"Zelpachad, Shadow of Terror","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An Ahamkara who has hidden at the bottom of the Red Sea Rift for years, and a master of feeding off others' pain and fear.\n\nThis Ahamkara, who has lurked in the Red Sea since the Golden Age, resides in the Rift's deepest trenches in the form of a sea serpent. She fed on the desires of explorers aboard passing ships and was also the cause of many wrecks in the area. \nAfter the Collapse, she expanded her hunting grounds to include the Cabal invaders. Lacking in strength, she is cautious, rarely initiating attacks to avoid revealing her presence and instead exploiting subconscious wishes to serve her own malevolent purposes. \nTo remain perfectly hidden, Zelpachad set a trap to bewilder all the creatures who approached her nest, showing them what they wanted and feared most. Her prey would become obsessed with these desires and make terror-fueled wishes. In the end, they would be trapped here forever, becoming both a fount of power and her faithful guardians."}]},{"id":"kw-50131","title":"Zelpachad, Shadow of Terror","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An Ahamkara who has hidden at the bottom of the Red Sea Rift for years, and a master of feeding off others' pain and fear.\n\nZelpachad did not hide the core of her being within her nest. What Estela destroyed was merely a separated portion of her energy formed of a slough."}]},{"id":"kw-60043","title":"Jiangshi Metro","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_100_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A transportation hub located in what was once the center of Jiangshi.\n\nIn the Golden Age, trains coming from all directions or passing through the Jiangshi Metro area converged here. Among them were freight trains in support of the Lanyue program, and passenger trains with travelers who came to visit the Aeronautic Campus or transit here to immigrate to other planets via colony ships. In its prime, it was a tall building with transportation tracks cascading from the ground to the air at heights of hundreds of meters, connecting the Aeronautic Campus, the city, the outskirts housing the Space Elevator, the spacecraft launch and landing site, and many other places. Jiangshi Metro was also one of the world's main communication hubs."}]},{"id":"kw-50132","title":"Zelpachad, Shadow of Terror","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An Ahamkara who has hidden at the bottom of the Red Sea Rift for years, and a master of feeding off others' pain and fear.\n\nThe legendary \"Wish-Granter\" of the Red Sea Rift is none other than Zelpachad. To an Ahamkara, human desires are a delectable feast. Thus she has left her lair to hunt among human settlements."}]},{"id":"kw-50133","title":"Zelpachad, Shadow of Terror","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"An Ahamkara who has hidden at the bottom of the Red Sea Rift for years, and a master of feeding off others' pain and fear.\n\nEstela found the core of Zelpachad's being, and its destruction would spell the true end for the Ahamkara. Realizing she was about to die, Zelpachad did the unthinkable: she made a wish upon herself.\nTo the Ahamkara, wishing upon oneself is suicide. This makes the repercussions far more fatal...and far wider-reaching."}]},{"id":"kw-60005","title":"Tree of Light","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_90_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A phenomenon created by the merging of the Light with natural trees.\n\nAfter it fell into hibernation, the Light of the Traveler was gradually cast down, flowing from the cracks in its shell and extending to Earth's surface. It penetrated the Earth's crust, spread over the continents, and intermingled with the plants, sprouting giant Trees of Light. The land around these trees, having been irrigated by the Light of the Traveler, is overwhelmed with vitality.\nDuring the Dark Age, the areas where Trees of Light take root are often the battlegrounds where the Warlords clashed most fiercely."}]},{"id":"kw-50134","title":"Epakesk, Devil Baron","sub":"Combatants & Hostiles","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Combatants & Hostiles"},"body":[{"p":"The commander of a Fallen fleet who left the House of Devils and now hides in Jiangshi Metro.\n\nEpakesk once held a high rank in the House of Devils. But once Issakis seized control of the House's forces in Jiangshi Metro, he refused to accept the Archpriest's new reign and left with several similarly dissatisfied followers. He reestablished himself at the abandoned Aeronautic Campus, where he relies on plundered equipment and Ether to sustain his rule. Epakesk still refers to himself as a member of the House of Devils, though he refuses to answer to any leader. His focus is now on secretly gathering followers of the old ways, waiting for the moment to seize greater power."}]},{"id":"kw-60001","title":"The Traveler","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_88_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A spherical paracausal entity beyond human comprehension.\n\nIt is the creator of the Ghosts and the source of the Lightbearers' Light. The Traveler arrived in Sol millennia ago and enlightened the human race, leading to technological marvels and humanity's Golden Age. It is said that the Traveler had also blessed countless alien civilizations before arriving in Sol, chief among them being the \"fallen\" Eliksni.\nBut what is the Traveler's purpose? No one knows for sure."}]},{"id":"kw-40004","title":"Skorri","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_7_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Iron Bard of Haven.\n\nBefore joining the Iron Lords, Skorri was known as the \"Battlefield Bard\" who wrote and sang about the battles between Warlords. When she heard of the Iron Lords' vision for a better future, though, she decided right then and there to join them, for it was with this organization that she would pen songs about the battles that would change the world.\nNow, Skorri runs the Iron Bar near Haven. After all, apart from the fight between two Lightbearers, few other things can inspire her to write."}]},{"id":"kw-60002","title":"The Light","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A paracausal force that existed long before the creation of time and space.\n\nLight comes from the Traveler. It is a force that brings complexity and diversity, capable of creating matter and harboring life. In the physical universe, the Light can allow the user to tamper with the laws of physics at will. Those possessing the Light can wield Arc, Solar, and Void forces as weapons without harming themselves."}]},{"id":"kw-60003","title":"Ghosts","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_89_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Small sentient machines created by the Traveler shortly after the Collapse.\n\nThe Traveler created the Ghosts with its \"last breath\" before falling into hibernation. These small, intelligent hovering machines have been roaming Earth from the early days of the Dark Age and onward, fulfilling their mission: to find the remains of human beings and resurrect them as Lightbearers, beings blessed with the power of Light.\nThe Ghosts are the bridge between Lightbearers and the Light. They can replenish the Light they use in battle and, more importantly, revive them after they have died."}]},{"id":"kw-60004","title":"Lightbearers","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Individuals resurrected by Ghosts who possess the power of the Light.\n\nThey are able to wield Arc, Solar, and Void forces with their flesh and blood. What's more, as long as their Ghost still exists, Lightbearers who fall in battle can be revived, rendering them almost immortal.\nWhen a Lightbearer is first revived, they will not retain the memories of their previous life. Very few Lightbearers learn about their past identities and experiences, though those who do may wish they hadn't..."}]},{"id":"kw-40021","title":"The Speaker","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"Since the Golden Age, many have coveted the special abilities of the Speakers. They attempted to decipher the secrets associated with the Speakers and the Traveler, yet they all failed without exception, leaving only incomplete technology and tormented victims in their wake.\nWhen the Fallen arrived on Earth, they discovered those technologies and, yearning for the Great Machine's return, launched the research anew, bringing with it a new endless stream of tragedy."}]},{"id":"kw-60007","title":"The Collapse","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A calamity that nearly wiped out human civilization.\n\nFor hundreds of years, humankind enjoyed the Golden Age brought by the Traveler. What they did not know was that such prosperity would not last forever. The Collapse's arrival was sudden, as was its end. By the time it concluded, human civilization had been almost completely destroyed."}]},{"id":"kw-40003","title":"Morgran","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_6_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A young Ahamkara dwelling in Haven.\n\nIn a coincidental encounter, Radegast found a newly hatched Ahamkara.\nFaced with Morgran's powerful yet unstable abilities, Radegast came up with a solution called \"Morgran's Prey,\" which would allow Morgran to gain the wish power needed to grow without the risk of losing control."}]},{"id":"kw-60009","title":"Ahamkara","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_6_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Powerful, magical, shape-shifting creatures.\n\nThey possess an incredible and unique ability to manipulate reality and fulfill other beings' wishes through the Anthem Anatheme. Doing so grants the Ahamkara the spiritual energy they need to survive.\nHowever, the trade comes at a price. While the wishes are indeed granted, they are accompanied by unintended consequences—usually something the wish-maker would prefer not to encounter."}]},{"id":"kw-60010","title":"Sentinels","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_91_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"One of mankind's incredible Golden Age creations.\n\nTaketori Industry—a Golden Age industry leader in mechanical engineering—built these giant robots. These self-propelled weapon platforms are hundreds of meters in height and measure tens of thousands of tons. They are powered by several Light cores and can be loaded with experimental, cutting-edge weapons ranging from traditional artillery, missiles, and lasers to thermofusion, antimatter, and sonic waves. Each Sentinel possesses a destructive power unimaginable to the common human."}]},{"id":"kw-60011","title":"Sentinels","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_91_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"One of mankind's incredible Golden Age creations.\n\nTaketori Industry originally built the Sentinels to compete with Clovis Bray's \"Warmind\" military program. Sentinels combined Taketori Industry's own expertise in mechanical engineering, researchers' study of the Light, and exotic materials collected from alien planets. The program, initially codenamed \"Lunarin,\" was gradually implemented in the Moon's orbit.\nSentinels were assembled in zero gravity, then launched to Earth."}]},{"id":"kw-60013","title":"Humans","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Earth's original higher-intelligence race.\n\nHumans dominated the planet since the dawn of the species thousands of years ago. But at the beginning of the 21st century, everything changed. The Traveler brought human civilization into its centuries-long Golden Age, but the Collapse saw human civilization nearly destroyed and decimated its population.\nDespite all this, humankind remains as resilient as ever."}]},{"id":"kw-60014","title":"Awoken","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A human subspecies originating from the humans on Earth.\n\nOn the eve of the Collapse, a spacecraft carrying tens of thousands of colonists was right on the front lines of the clash between two immense forces of paracausal power. These powers created a whole new sub-universe when they collided, remodeling the colonists who were right in the middle of it in the process.\nThey were reborn in this new universe called the Distributary and became the first Awoken."}]},{"id":"kw-40050","title":"Aegolius","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Lightbearer who was once next in line for Jolder's title of Iron Champion.\n\nRumor has it that Aegolius was the candidate Jolder was most satisfied with among her many apprentices. But while he possessed his master's confidence and courage, he lacked her resilience and tolerance. Jolder trusted him, cared for him, yet she started feeling he lacked that \"little something\" that would make him ready to take up her mantle. That small difference, and the anxious wait it fed upon, became a speck of doubt—one that, over time, festered into a devouring void, swallowing Aegolius’s conviction, heroism, determination, and every other admirable quality he once held.\nNobody knows what happened afterward. He disappeared, his name wiped from the records, with none of the Iron Lords—Jolder included—so much as mentioning him. It's as if he never existed."}]},{"id":"kw-60020","title":"Solar","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Solar is heat, combustion, nuclear energy, and the movement of microscopic particles.\n\nLightbearers can release the Light in the form of Solar energy, igniting objects, creating explosions, or manifesting any phenomenon related to heat."}]},{"id":"kw-60022","title":"Haven Militia","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The main armed forces of Haven.\n\nLightbearers may be powerful, but they are scarce. Thus, mortal soldiers serve as the main force of the Iron Lords. Back in Eastern Europe, Radegast already had a well-trained militia force. After moving his stronghold to Haven, this force expanded in size. Now, the city's militia force is fully equipped and controls its surrounding territories, with the exception of the Old City."}]},{"id":"kw-60024","title":"Guerrillas of Jiangshi Metro","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The main armed forces of Jiangshi Metro.\n\nAfter the Fallen's invasion, the guerrillas launched a counterattack under Lady Xuân Yến's leadership. The Iron Lady and her squad's suicide attack succeeded in shooting down the Fallen Ketch, turning the tides of the battle. However, the Fallen were not completely expelled and began to gradually encroach on Jiangshi Metro.\nAfter years of war, Jiangshi Metro lacks a normal social system or even civilian livelihood, and the guerrillas effectively serve as its government."}]},{"id":"kw-40051","title":"Elathi","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A kindhearted hunter who was always extra patient with children.\n\nElathi was a huntress who dwelled alone in the woods of Valencia, Spain. Proficient with both bows and rifles, she had much experience living in the wilderness, which naturally helped her survive in this chaotic world.\nUnable to turn a blind eye to the lone wanderer Estela, Elathi invited her into her home. Despite the Lightbearer's solitary nature and tendency to keep others at arm's length, Elathi still treated her with friendly enthusiasm. The show of companionship moved Estela, and the two became close friends—family, even.\nHowever, Estela's curse would see ruin brought to all she holds dear, ultimately ending Elathi's life."}]},{"id":"kw-60025","title":"Warlords","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Lightbearers who used the Light for conquest during the Dark Age and early City Age.\n\nAfter the Collapse, the old order ceased to exist and was instead replaced by the laws of the jungle, where the strong prey on the weak. The Dark Age was a time of violence, slavery, and killing, and under this order, some Lightbearers used their paracausal gifts and immortal bodies to establish their own rule, warring constantly over the few resources left.\nMortals have little choice but to eke out a means to survive in servitude to the immortal Warlords."}]},{"id":"kw-60026","title":"Iron Lords","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Lightbearers trying to end the Iron Lords' reign.\n\nIn the Dark Age, the Warlords ruled their territories with violence and an iron fist. Many mortals not only had to endure servitude to them, but also served as cannon fodder for their violent conflicts. Human civilization was treading a path to total extinction until a group of Lightbearers led by Radegast decided to step forward and end the despair."}]},{"id":"kw-60028","title":"Packs","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Organizations formed by like-minded Lightbearers with Radegast's permission.\n\nPack registration is handled by Radegast's advisor, Mishra. Radegast regularly gives these Packs bounties to test their strength, hoping to examine and select the next generation of Lightbearers who have the potential to bring new blood to the Iron Lord's mission of reviving human civilization."}]},{"id":"kw-60029","title":"Old City","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A relatively well-preserved human ruin near Haven.\n\nIts former name has been long forgotten, and years of looting by Warlords and wanderers have left it with very few valuable resources. However, some data from the Golden Age still remain in public buildings.\nThe place is seen by many as a graveyard, where those who fell to the Collapse rest. Because of this, some of the Ghosts in Haven travel here in search of their chosen Lightbearer."}]},{"id":"kw-40040","title":"Yannick-11","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The last Warlord to rule Jiangshi Metro.\n\nDespite Yannick-11 trying to kill him, Tan-2's kind nature wouldn't let him use the program to delete the Warlord. He decided to shut it down, but when the damage to the power systems caused a complete overload, Parhelion Wing was unable to withstand the intense shock of energy, putting Tan-2 himself at risk of death. Yannick-11, unwilling to eternally owe Tan-2 for his mercy, let himself be hit by the blast of energy, destroying his mind."}]},{"id":"kw-60030","title":"Old City Library","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_113_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A large, well-preserved building in the Old City.\n\nDespite being ravaged for years, multiple forms of knowledge and records of the Golden Age are still preserved by its walls. The Old City has been hostile territory ever since the Fallen's full-scale invasion, but many people still venture here regardless, knowing that here lie true treasures."}]},{"id":"kw-60034","title":"Bad Old Time","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A tavern located in Haven's bazaar.\n\nThe news that Radegast intended to relocate his territory to a place closer to the Traveler sparked great interest in Wu Ming, who ran a bar at the foot of Felwinter Peak. He followed Radegast to Haven and opened a new establishment, where Lightbearers could meet each other, chat, or play cards between adventures.\nThough its menu features just the standard tavern fixings, it's one of the few places in Haven where one can kick back and relax."}]},{"id":"kw-60035","title":"Realm of the IX","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_96_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A space created by the Nine that transcends the material universe. It can be entered via the temporal rift in Haven.\n\nThis realm was shaped using sights from the real world, with the Nine forcefully sweeping some real-world objects inside on occasion, letting them observe and study them. While the Nine cannot visit our world, they have sent an agent to invite Lightbearers into theirs, and even host challenges with unimaginable rewards. What exactly do the Nine hope to gain from this? Only they would know."}]},{"id":"kw-60038","title":"Sentinel Wreckage","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_95_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Light-hallowed ground formed where Sentinels fell.\n\nWhen the Collapse came, even the mountainous war robots made by the Taketori Industry were defeated by the calamity that ravaged Earth. Their remains still rest across, and though they cannot rise again, a huge amount of Light is still housed in their bodies, drawing the eyes all who would use it."}]},{"id":"kw-60039","title":"The Shifting Gate","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"One of humanity's Golden Age inventions, capable of realizing connections across space.\n\nDuring the Golden Age, many corporations perfected the use of beacons for space teleportation and manufactured many of the devices. One of the leading companies was Bastra, who went beyond using short-range teleportation for small targets and utilized massive teleportation platforms to transmat large units."}]},{"id":"kw-60040","title":"The Shifting Gate","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"One of humanity's Golden Age inventions, capable of realizing connections across space.\n\nThe underlying technology of the Shifting Gate and its teleportation can be seen as two sides of the same coin, but the former has much more powerful features and effects as it creates a portal that connects several different spaces.\nThis spatial technology greatly reduces transportation costs and time spent and is seen as one of the pinnacle technologies of the Golden Age. Some people even suspect that alien technology was utilized in the making of the Shifting Gate."}]},{"id":"kw-60041","title":"Shifting Gates","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"One of humanity's Golden Age inventions, capable of realizing connections across space.\n\nThe Shifting Gate is a technological marvel, but it also has its limitations. First of all, its connection function is limited by the spatial coordinate database, and cannot just connect two random spaces. In addition, activating the Gate requires a large amount of energy, which is typically supplied by dedicated fusion power plants. As a result, this service was extremely expensive, and only the world's top corporations and national organizations could afford building a terminal."}]},{"id":"kw-60044","title":"Jiangshi Metro","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_100_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A transportation hub located in what was once the center of Jiangshi.\n\nThe Collapse destroyed most creations of human civilization, and Jiangshi Metro was no exception. But when the disaster receded and humanity reclaimed the land, Jiangshi Metro was one of the first areas people set their eyes on, as the stranded freight trains that once supplied the nearby Golden Age facilities still held many valuable resources.\nIt has remained an area of frequent human activity ever since, during both Yannick's and Xuân Yến's reigns and beyond."}]},{"id":"kw-40002","title":"Kevarrh","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_5_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A Fallen who has allied herself with Haven.\n\nKevarrh was once a highly promising commander in the House of Devils who took part in the invasion of Earth. However, the fact that the Traveler abandoned the Eliksni and turned to humans always left her ill at ease.\nDuring an attack, she encountered Radegast and made a choice that would shock both the Iron Lords and her fellow Eliksni: defecting to the humans.\nSince then, Kevarrh has served Radegast in the role of Eliksni cultural consultant. She even leads a special troop composed of Fallen captives."}]},{"id":"kw-40007","title":"Bazinet","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_9_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Gunsmith of Haven.\n\nDespite her cheery and warm appearance, the trauma of many tragic partings during the Dark Age has caused Bazinet to keep others at arm's length. Conversely, she always takes a particular tone in explaining the firearms she maintains to her customers, speaking as if they were living, breathing human beings rather than pieces of metal welded together."}]},{"id":"kw-40008","title":"Mishra","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A scholar in Haven.\n\nMitra Mishra used to be obsessed with the knowledge of the Golden Age, fantasizing about rebuilding human civilization by recovering old technologies.\nDriven by this idea, he once took a hiking trip. No one knows exactly what he experienced on his hike. All we know is that upon his return, Mishra's conviction was changed. He was no longer obsessed with the past. Instead, he began to assist people in building communities—\"Packs\"—and focused on making a difference through the power of humans themselves.\nHe still travels occasionally, though."}]},{"id":"kw-40009","title":"Pandora-7","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_10_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A quirky Exo Caravanner who often appears in Haven.\n\nPandora-7 collects all sorts of exotic treasures from across the globe, with some even hailing from alien planets in Sol. Most of these items are useless in combat, but people love these trinkets even more than weapons and armor. Perhaps this was why Pandora-7 has a wide network of contacts.\nAlmost every Lightbearer knows her. Want to meet some new friends? Talking to Pandora-7 is the best way."}]},{"id":"kw-60047","title":"Icy Lake","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_103_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Once a reservoir that supported Jiangshi residents' industry and daily life back in the Golden Age, it was frozen over during the climate change caused by the Collapse.\n\nAt some point, rumors began to circulate among the locals, claiming the area to be haunted."}]},{"id":"kw-40014","title":"Yannick-11","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The last Warlord to rule Jiangshi Metro.\n\nAs a typical Warlord, Yannick-11 ruled his people with fear and violence, which saw him meet a similarly violent (and typical) end. His trusted right hand, Lady Xuân Yến, led a resistance that dethroned him and shattered his Ghost in a fierce battle. Unwilling to accept a final death, Yannick-11 made the bold choice to transfer his consciousness into his Relic. When Tan-2 eventually found Parhelion Wing, the consciousness within the sword awoke and parasitically attached itself to Tan-2's own memory core."}]},{"id":"kw-20001","title":"Jiangshi Metro files: Crashed Ketch","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_102_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"On an ordinary afternoon over a dozen years ago, strange spaceships unknown to humankind suddenly tore through the skies above Jiangshi Metro. They dropped plasma bombs and Skiffs loaded with alien warriors. The unprepared Jiangshi Metro would suffer many casualties during this first wave of attacks.\nDespite the dire circumstances, the people managed to stabilize their defense under Lady Xuân Yến's command until the giant Ketch—which would later be confirmed to have been the House of Devils' flagship Maliks-Fel—entered their sights. In a last-ditch effort to take the ship down, she and several guerrillas hijacked an enemy Skiff, launching an attack on Maliks-Fel. The Ketch came falling down onto Jiangshi's city wall, but Lady Xuân Yến and the guerrillas never made it back.\nNowadays, the crashed Ketch—filled with traps and treasures alike—draws the eyes of many, though its auto-defense system keeps all of them at bay. And those who once approached the Ketch Wreckage all gave the same testimony, claiming to have heard knocking sounds and frightening, thunderous echoes coming from within..."}]},{"id":"kw-40015","title":"Lady Xuân Yến","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 1","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Iron Lady of Jiangshi Metro.\n\nLightbearer Xuân Yến used to serve Yannick, the Warlord of Jiangshi Metro, but her good nature wouldn't let her accept his brutal rule over the civilians. Following careful planning, she teamed up with a mortal warrior, Liang Xing, to defeat Yannick and end his rule.\nShe became the new ruler of Jiangshi Metro and was later visited by Lord Radegast. Finding herself in agreement with the Iron Lords' ideas, she joined his organization and was dubbed the \"Iron Lady.\""}]},{"id":"kw-40016","title":"Lady Xuân Yến","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Iron Lady of Jiangshi Metro.\n\nJiangshi Metro enjoyed a long period of peace under Xuân Yến's rule until a sudden Fallen attack shattered it. Faced with an alien enemy they had never encountered before, the guerrillas were caught off guard and at a disadvantage.\nAt this critical moment, Xuân Yến decided to launch a surprise attack on the Fallen's ship. The Kell's Ketch was eventually shot down, and the Fallen, having lost their command, were forced to retreat. But she and her guerrilla squad never returned."}]},{"id":"kw-40023","title":"Saladin","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_13_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Iron Lords' founders and the military leader of Veridia.\n\nAfter teaming up with Wolf to rescue the miners captured by the Cabal, Saladin showed strong hostility towards Haven and Radegast—his old friend and brother under the Iron Banner—at the meeting in Veridia. This animosity has been building for a long time. Now, it's left Finnala no choice but to privately seek Haven's aid."}]},{"id":"kw-40025","title":"Saladin","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_13_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Iron Lords' founders and the military leader of Veridia.\n\nOnce Harrow left, Saladin finally came to his senses and realized he'd been bewitched, which caused him to make arbitrary decisions that harmed those he led. He then personally contacted Haven and sought Radegast's aid, for \"the Iron Lords stand together—always.\""}]},{"id":"kw-40026","title":"Harrow","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_14_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"President of the Veridian Union.\n\nHarrow had already lived in Veridia for some time before becoming the union president. Once Gareth was overthrown, the residents of Veridia made plans to restore the trade union that had existed only nominally towards the end of the lord's rule. Due to her empathetic nature and willingness to listen, Harrow, who had always been adored by the townspeople, was elected as the new union president as a representative of the miners.\nHowever, Harrow has seemed unwilling to show herself in Veridia for the past few months, and nobody knows why..."}]},{"id":"kw-20029","title":"The Union Leader's Absence","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_14_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"Harrow went from an unknown representative of Veridia's miners to a widely supported union president. Those familiar with her claim she's the best listener in the world—no matter how you express your demands, no matter your language used or posture, she'll understand your true thoughts and respond in the most empathetic way possible.\nHowever, in the past few months, Veridia's leader of seems to have found herself in some mysterious spiritual crisis. She's has become elusive, rarely appearing in public and even refusing to respond to the residents' most ordinary and humble requests. Some curious people speculate that she's been secretly meditating and training near Prism Lake, which has been the location of strange loud noises both day and night."}]},{"id":"kw-40027","title":"Harrow","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 4","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_14_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"President of the Veridian Union.\n\nHarrow displayed some sort of special ability during the investigation of the Weathered Caves. She was seemingly able to sense the enemy's plans and react in advance—even if they were outside her field of view. Harrow explained it as an instinct acquired after fighting the Cabal for so long."}]},{"id":"kw-40030","title":"Harrow","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 5","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_14_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"President of the Veridian Union.\n\nHarrow has always been troubled by a dream—a life and death battle between the Sentinel and the python in the waves of the Red Sea, who ultimately perished together and now stand as monuments in the Rift.\nHarrow decided to answer the dream's call and travel alone to the depths of the Red Sea Rift to unravel the numerous mysteries plaguing her."}]},{"id":"kw-40031","title":"Shira","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_15_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The current representative of the Veridian Union's miners.\n\nAn avid reader since childhood, Shira is incredibly knowledgeable. Although she's too physically weak to work in the mines, her interest in machinery led her to take on the task of maintaining their large machinery. She seizes every chance to expand her knowledge of machines, regardless of their origins."}]},{"id":"kw-40043","title":"???","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A legendary Lightbearer renowned for his erudition.\n\nAlthough ??? rarely talks about this period in his life, rumors that he was once Felwinter's apprentice still spread. In an era of nameless heroes and wars waged between Iron Lords and Warlords, ??? did indeed study Lightwielding under Felwinter, honing his character and will."}]},{"id":"kw-40048","title":"Kandak","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A tyrannical Warlord of the Sahara.\n\nLongtime ruler of the Sahara, Kandak, worried by Iron Lord Saladin's gradual rise in the Red Sea Rift, was the first to reach out to the central territory of Bayda-Benghazi, then ruled by Lady Finnala. He offered to send his men to defend the territory against other lords in exchange for regular offerings of their rations.\nHowever, when the Fallen invaded Finnala's territory, Kandak declined to help on the grounds that their agreement didn't include threats from aliens. Ultimately, it was Saladin and his troops who saved Bayda-Benghazi from certain demise. This event led Finnala to side with Saladin, and it also spawned her hatred of Kandak."}]},{"id":"kw-40049","title":"Aegolius","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Lightbearer who was once next in line for Jolder's title of Iron Champion.\n\nAegolius's true name is unknown, but unsettling rumors about him have spread around town. Some claim the former candidate fell from grace and became a shameless murderer, while others claim he once tried to overthrow the Iron Lords' rule. Some even say he killed his own Ghost in a blasphemous renunciation of his connection to the Light. Nobody knows the validity of these rumors; what they do know is the title was almost within his reach."}]},{"id":"kw-40052","title":"MERLO","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A helpless father who will do anything to get his missing daughter back.\n\nMerlo is a mortal carpenter and an unremarkable resident of the Red Sea Rift. He once had a happy family and lived a simple yet satisfied life.\nBut when his wife passed in an accident, the family quickly collapsed. Merlo spent day after day sinking deeper into despair, neglecting his daughter in the process.\nNow she has gone missing, and he is trying to find her. To the distraught Merlo, his daughter is the person he treasures most in this world. He would pay any price to get her back—even making a wish to a mysterious entity..."}]},{"id":"kw-20013","title":"Haunted Icy Lake?","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_103_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"The Icy Lake is haunted, or so the locals claim.\nOnce a reservoir in the Golden Age, this lake was frozen due to climate change brought about by the Collapse.\nBut at some point, a rumor about the place being haunted started to spread.\nSome may see this as simple gossip, yet somehow it's piqued the interest of a certain Lightbearer in Haven. In her eyes, the creatures lurking beneath the icy rift in Jiangshi Metro are something far more terrible than simple ghouls..."}]},{"id":"kw-40059","title":"Felwinter","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"The Iron Lord of Felwinter Peak and technical genius of the Dark Age.\n\nDuring the Collapse, an Exo was revived by a Ghost and was given the name \"Felwinter.\" He climbed to an observatory on a mountaintop and defeated the region's ruling Warlord, claiming the territory for himself and dubbing it \"Felwinter Peak.\" After meeting Timur, Felwinter found himself moved by his ideals and joined him under the Iron Banner.\nFelwinter doesn't seem as \"fit to hold office\" as his fellow Iron Lords, instead spending most of his time holed up in his lab, fully concentrated on his research. He rarely concerns himself with Iron Lord affairs, and some of his colleagues have taken issue with his excessively cold ways of handling things."}]},{"id":"kw-40061","title":"Bobak","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"An orphan who was taken in by a pair of Veridia's unemployed miners.\n\nBobak was an average street urchin—clever, mature for his age, and someone who had already \"got his hands dirty,\" so to speak. When the miners who took him in were forced to make a living secretly mining and smuggling Radiancite, he used his youth to get involved, becoming his uncles' liaison, salesperson, and lookout."}]},{"id":"kw-20021","title":"Beyond the Skies","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_104_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"The space elevator and Lanyue Space Station above it are, without a doubt, the most prominent structures around Jiangshi Metro. But following the Collapse, humans no longer needed them for space exploration, and because of that, the Space Elevator hasn't undergone a complete survey in many years.\nNow, nobody knows what is up there—especially since the Fulminator has kept the guerrillas stuck at the station."}]},{"id":"kw-40063","title":"Maln","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A Radiancite smuggler and \"old friend\" whom Jaren has traveled thousands of miles to kill personally.\n\nCunning and cruel—those are the only descriptions that could be coerced from the unemployed miners Maln has providing his stock."}]},{"id":"kw-60054","title":"Greenhouse","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A facility that plays a key role in Jiangshi Metro's food supply.\n\nThis high-tech greenhouse was originally used for researching Traveler-influenced plants and conducting extraterrestrial agricultural experiments. To simulate the environments on other planets, researchers could adjust the greenhouse's temperature, humidity, light, and other conditions according to their needs. After the Collapse, the climate around Jiangshi Metro was completely changed, and the greenhouse became the only place where farming was possible.\nFor a long time, the survivors have relied on this building for food."}]},{"id":"kw-40064","title":"Maln","sub":"Individuals & Organizations · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A Radiancite smuggler and \"old friend\" whom Jaren has traveled thousands of miles to kill personally.\n\nMaln is not just cunning and cruel—he's also incredibly cautious.\nIn order to create an opportunity to meet him face-to-face, Jaren has prepared to have Bobak and his uncles bait him out with a Radiancite trade."}]},{"id":"kw-20025","title":"Veridia Files: The Mystery of Gareth's Fall","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_108_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"The fall of former Lord Gareth has been one of the Red Sea Rift and Veridia's greatest mysteries for the past few decades. To this day, no one knows how the Iron Lord who was once praised for prioritizing mortals' feelings became the most brutal of human settlement rulers. Eventually, the situation became so grave that Lord Radegast had no choice but to confront him.\nSome rumors point to Gareth's lantern, with people saying they once witnessed him muttering to it day and night. Yet still, there were many who defended him, believing his excessive taxation and tyrannical rule to ultimately be aimed at maintaining Veridia's independence. His fall was equally controversial—it's said he disappeared entirely during a conflict with Lord Radegast. His dead Ghost suggests he met a tragic end, but for some reason, Radegast has never made a public statement."}]},{"id":"kw-40066","title":"Marco","sub":"Individuals & Organizations","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Individuals & Organizations"},"body":[{"p":"A man who was both a friend and brother to Jaren; he died years ago at Maln's hand.\n\nWhen Jaren was newly risen as a Lightbearer, it was Marco who helped him get his footing and patiently taught him how to fight.\nJaren had thought they would always travel together, but a despicable betrayal would put an end to those days. By the time Jaren arrived, he was too late. All he could bring back at that point was Marco's hand cannon, \"Vows.\""}]},{"id":"kw-60048","title":"Lanyue Aeronautic Campus","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_98_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An international center for space exploration and scientific research in the Golden Age, located outside Jiangshi Metro.\n\nThe stable climate and altitude advantages made the area around Jiangshi Metro a suitable site for rocket launches. As the demand for space exploration exploded during the Golden Age, the Lanyue Aeronautic Campus grew from a single rocket launcher to an entire region of crowded launch pads. In its heyday, several rockets were launched from the campus almost every day."}]},{"id":"kw-60049","title":"Space Elevator","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_104_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"One of humanity's many Golden Age engineering marvels.\n\nWhen Jiangshi Aeronautic Campus gradually began expanding to become Southeast Asia's hub for space and extraterrestrial exploration, Project Lanyue was launched to enhance its efficiency even further. Over the following twenty years, the Lanyue Space Elevator—a gigantic structure nearly 130,000 kilometers high—would be constructed and completed, greatly reducing the cost of space travel and propelling the Aeronautic Campus to global fame."}]},{"id":"kw-60050","title":"Lanyue Space Station","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 2","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_104_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A space station that humans built during the Golden Age, reached via Jiangshi Metro's Space Elevator.\n\nThe Lanyue Space Elevator reaches the altitude of the synchronous orbit and features several ring-shaped space stations built on the axis of the elevator shaft, looking like donuts strung on a bamboo pole. They once had a variety of uses, including tourism, scientific research, and transportation. After the Collapse, however, they were left unattended and malfunctioned frequently. Most were looted once the House of Devils arrived."}]},{"id":"kw-20033","title":"The Red Sea's Scars: Legend of the Python and Sentinel","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_91_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"The Red Sea Rift and Veridia Forest are home to two particularly remarkable sites—a pair of massive remains. We now know that one of them is a Golden Age creation known as a Sentinel, while the other can only be inferred from its winding skeletal structure to belong to some kind of reptile, temporarily referred to as a \"python\" here.\nIt's said that here, they engaged in a brutal duel before meeting their demise. The python ripped off the Sentinel's left arm of the giant statue, throwing the limb into the seabed several kilometers away, while the Sentinel's axe cleaved a hole in the python's chest. Energy burst out from the two giants' wounds, instantly evaporating the Red Sea's waters and forming the landscape of today... Since no one who witnessed this battle firsthand survived, however, one can now treat it as a sort of myth."}]},{"id":"kw-60051","title":"Fulminator","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_101_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"A device the Fallen have been using to manipulate the weather.\n\nDuring the Golden Age, a facility that could artificially drive away clouds or rain was constructed to help ensure smooth rocket launches from the Aeronautic Campus. And now, as the Fallen prepare to launch an all-out attack on Jiangshi Metro, the Splicer priest Vanok modified this technology, transforming it into a base capable of creating massive thunderstorms and giving the House of Devils an advantage."}]},{"id":"kw-60052","title":"The Pit","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_104_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The Space Data Center and Energy Hub at the bottom of the Space Elevator, and the entrance to the Space Elevator on the ground.\n\nThis facility is now occupied by the House of Devils. After more than ten years of work, the Fallen turned this place into a heavily armed fortress and the base for their activities around Jiangshi Metro. Suspiciously, the Prime Servitor—a vital entity for any House—had also appeared here, though it is not accompanied by the Archon meant to protect it..."}]},{"id":"kw-60053","title":"Lanyue 5 Factory","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_126_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"An aeronautics factory built in Jiangshi Metro during the Golden Age.\n\nDuring the Golden Age, Jiangshi Metro's Lanyue Aeronautic Campus was known throughout the world, and the city's industry was centered on aerospace. One relic of this time is the Lanyue 5 Factory.\nThis modernized facility had a variety of production methods ranging from 3D printing to assembly lines, and its products included electronic components, accessories, and communicators for rockets and spaceships. When the Fallen invaded, they quickly realized the value of the place, and they have been trying to take full control and reactivate it."}]},{"id":"kw-20037","title":"What Lies Behind the Door","sub":"Hearsay","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_112_xl","filters":{"Kind":"Hearsay"},"body":[{"p":"Though I'd rather not say it... It seems that there are secrets in the Red Sea Rift that humans have yet to uncover, even in places as close to Veridia as the Weathered Caves.\nThe Cabal legion's soldiers are gathering here, and their target seems to be a sealed \"door\" (to use concepts humans are more familiar with), as well as whatever lies beyond."}]},{"id":"kw-60056","title":"Guerrillas of Jiangshi Metro","sub":"World & Phenomena · variant 3","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The main armed forces of Jiangshi Metro.\n\nJiangshi Metro guerrillas are now under the leadership of Mu Ying and divided into several squads, such as Ayuela's team of scouts who directly engage with the Fallen, the engineers who provide support on the battlefield, the quartermasters who prepare ammo and equipment as well as record and bury their deceased teammates, and the logisticians who manage the greenhouse, daily necessities, and trading."}]},{"id":"kw-60058","title":"Old City Sewers","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"The Old City's sewage system. It's said it leads to the location of Sentinel Wreckage."}]},{"id":"kw-60061","title":"Eye of the Storm","sub":"World & Phenomena","quality":null,"art":"data_dictionary_01_xl","filters":{"Kind":"World & Phenomena"},"body":[{"p":"Mu Ying hypothesizes this to be the source of Jiangshi Metro's bad weather. It may be connected to the Fallen."}]},{"id":"diary-21003","title":"Duel","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Before the match, news came of the Cabal landing. The Warlord's side evacuated overnight, the Militia withdrew their defenses, and the jurors on both sides gradually left. The field was left with only the Arbiter.\nJolder asked him: Still reading?\nHe said: As long as someone is still standing in the field, the rules must remain.\nUnder the skies of the Red Sea Rift that day, with the distant sound of the Cabal's cannons, he recited all three hundred rules to an empty field. His voice was soft, but not a single word was skipped. Jolder listened through the entire recitation and, in front of the empty opponent's seat, performed a salute with the old champion's sword—a gesture of respect to the old system. It was also the first time someone treated his \"uselessness\" as a ritual rather than a joke.\nLater, people laughed at him for reciting to an empty field. He didn’t correct them. Only he and Jolder knew that the field wasn’t empty that day—it was filled with all the wars that the rules had prevented."}]},{"id":"diary-20509","title":"Warrior","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"The incident with Veridia has seen me further involved with the Red Sea Rift. My recent experiences have all been related to the Sentinel. I'd seen that steel man the size of a mountain during the battle, but I'd never got a close look. Knack says it was an autonomous warrior forged during the Golden Age, propelled by the Light and equipped with powerful weapons. When needed, it could even use traditional weapons like swords and spears to cut down what would otherwise be unstoppable foes.\n\"A warrior of the Light. Kind of like you guys,\" Knack said, half joking.\nThe Golden Age was a time of peace, was it not? Why, then, did they need to build such machines? \nWith the mountain blocking it, I can only see the top half of the Sentinel from town. I walked around outside and saw there was no path to get a closer look. Fortunately, a miner told me there is a road in the cave next to the town, passing through the mountain, that could take me there. A plateau on the mountainside gave me a clear view of the Sentinel. It was half kneeling, with a sharp spike piercing its chest from bottom to top. One of its hands held a long spear. It was thrust into the ground, as if pinning something down.\nIf I wanted to see its feet, I would need to climb higher. Knack flew up to scope it out, but it was still too far. All he could vaguely make out was a skull.\nKnack said the townspeople believe the Sentinel came to fight a giant beast and ultimately \"died\" here, pointing to the large skeleton in the valley as evidence. Judging by what we saw today, the claim seems credible.\nHow long has it stood in this forgotten valley? One hundred years? Two hundred? The remnants of sandstorms have burrowed their way into the crevices of its armor, and robotic lifeforms have nested beneath its feet. Its eyes have lost their glow, the paint has peeled from its shell, and cracks are spreading all over its body. Beneath its damaged arm are snapped cables reminiscent of sliced blood vessels. What manner of battle did it experience back then? What kind of enemy forced it fight to the point of mutual demise?\nAll we know is this: even today, it still maintains its fighting stance. Even in death, its body still stands.\nAs we descended the mountain, I recalled what Knack had said. \"A warrior of the Light. Kind of like you guys.\"\nIndeed, we are quite similar.\nBut we will rise again and again.\nWe will shoulder this responsibility even longer."}]},{"id":"diary-30106","title":"Xiqian","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"The night before departing for Earth. The door opened without a knock. It was her.\n\nSjur stood in the doorway, her cloak damp with sea air. She didn't speak. She unclasped the nameplate from her waist and held it out. A metal plate, worn to a shine. Engraved in Reef script: Blade · Xiqian.\n\nWho is Xiqian. I didn't ask. She didn't say.\n\nShe spoke. I'd heard her say many things, but never this much at once—\n\n\"When you get there, you'll be alone. No Reef. No me. You'll find new things—new ground, new firelight, new faces. These will become you.\" She paused. \"But don't lose the old things. The words on this plate—I didn't choose them for you. I heard them from somewhere—I can't explain where. But I know they're yours.\"\n\nI stood there a long time before I said: I'll make them remember. My name is Siorra.\n\nShe smiled: That's enough.\n\nAt the door, she stopped again: Remember—when you're on Earth, look up sometimes. Find the direction of the Reef. If one day you can't find it—come back.\n\nI didn't answer. She didn't wait.\nThe nameplate went against the side of my heart. Kept safe."}]},{"id":"diary-30110","title":"Homecoming","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"The fourth winter.\nI picked up an Earth expression. \"Have you eaten.\"\nOld Zhao tosses those three words at me every time he sees me. I toss them back.\nLater I realized, no one's waiting for the answer. Just an expression. Like Awoken nodding at each other.\nThat morning I said those three words, it hit me - it's been a long time since I looked toward the Reef.\nFour years. Haven's dirt walls became stone walls. The mess hall went from a tent to a two-story brick building. The kid who burned my bread - can bake it unburnt now.\nChange accumulates. Drop by drop. Enough drops, it's a city.\nWhen I first arrived, every evening I'd climb to the roof, look east. Homesick? Too heavy for this line of work. Just confirming direction.\nThen I stopped looking. Can't say when. Maybe a snowy night, too lazy to climb stairs. Maybe the bakery lady tossed an extra one in - \"This one cracked, can't sell it. Eat it for me.\"\nDon't know.\nBut today, the moment I said \"have you eaten,\" I smiled. Not at Old Zhao. At myself."}]},{"id":"diary-30905","title":"Caretaking","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"[A regular examination record brought back from Helhest's personal lab.]\nLuna:\nThe left wing's frame is prone to accumulating dust, resulting in partial flight trajectory deviation. Replacing the carbon fiber kit has reduced cleaning frequency. I discussed the possibility of installing a navigation function with Donovan. His eyes lit up, and he demanded I leave Luna with him for a while. That look on his face was concerning, so I found a way to politely decline.\n\nNova:\nElectromagnetic noise has been appearing with greater frequency recently. Attempts at cutting and restarting the internal circuitry have yielded no noticeable results. Bazinet suggested I place Nova and Flux at two ends of the lab while performing maintenance. Sure enough, it turns out Flux's weak electromagnetic signal was impacting Nova. I now understand why Kabr doesn't want his meerkat around Haven's cats.\n\nFlux:\nActually, I'd prefer a smaller frame. I've tried swapping electromagnetic emitter models to adjust the body, but all of them affect Flux's functions to some degree. I have no choice but to accept his current size. However, this prevents me from taking Flux out with me sometimes—and that often means coming home to find he's made a mess of my communication devices' signals.\n\nOculus:\nPersonally, I find it quite redundant to install similar functions with high overlap on different drones. Given both are, to some extent, capable of projecting holograms, I asked Grom if I could simply integrate Oculus into her shell. She went silent for a moment, then refused, saying, \"I'm a Ghost, not a hermit crab.\" An interesting statement, I think—or was she telling a joke...?\n\nSurge:\nThis is the only one I can be at ease with. I don't bring him out, and I don't need him to fight or anything. He just needs to guard my residence. He never fails to live up to my expectations. I can find evidence of him roaming in every corner of the home. I must commend the inventor of the robo-vacuum. They truly were one of the greatest minds this world has ever seen."}]},{"id":"diary-1","title":"Wolf: Bloodshed","sub":"Character diary","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_308","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf: Bloodshed"}]},{"id":"diary-30107","title":"Chasm","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"Red Sea Rift. I held the rear. Gray tide surging up from the valley floor. Not an army, no formation, just a surge. Comms down. Held for maybe two minutes.\nWhen I fell, my heart stopped. Not from being hit - something was pulled out of the chest. A sense of belonging, severed.\nAfter that wasn't four hours seventeen minutes. Learned that number later.\nConsciousness entirely wrapped in Nyx's domain. Black, pain, fear - none of it. Enveloped by \"nothingness\" itself. No before, no after, no self. A drop of water falling into the Void Sea.\nThen something dragged me back. First sight: a ball of light. Said its name was Shimmer. Said I'd been dead four hours seventeen minutes. I didn't understand. What is death.\nBut it was bright. So I lived, for now.\nLater asked it what it saw that day. Said nothing. A corpse, a nameplate. It asked what I saw when I died. Said I don't remember.\nHuman language has no tense for \"present but not existing.\"\nOnly later. The instant Nyx's assault released - everything connected. Not a memory. The aftershock of that \"nothingness,\" leaking from the blade's cross-section."}]},{"id":"diary-30903","title":"Old Dream","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"When she entered, I was sitting in front of the hearth, lost in thought. She placed the lamp on the table, then lowered her head, sizing up the meal placed there.\nBright days were a rarity in the Reef. Despite my feeling as though this were one of those rare days, she still carried that strange light with her. It remained turned on, its pale glow ensuring the meager foods on the plates were in full view.\n\"Shouldn't you eat something a little more—I don't know, substantial?\" she asked with a laugh.\n\"Substantial?\" I heard myself question. \"Why?\"\nShe was clearly right before me as she spoke, and I could see her lips forming the words, yet her voice came at me from all sides.\n\"To celebrate,\" she said.\nCelebration. I seemed to understand. We were celebrating my departure from this place.\nBut once I left... Where would I go?\nShe was still picking at the food with a somewhat exasperated look on her face. \"Be sure to trim the roots and stems next time you cook these. And you can't put fish into the pot without removing the scales... You should learn to look after yourself, you know.\"\nLook after myself? I asked her, \"Where will you go?\"\nShe stopped for a moment, stunned, then put down her cutlery. \"They only chose you. As for me... I don't know. Maybe I'll seek refuge with someone else. There will always be a place for me to rest.\"\nThe conversation, messy logic and all, continued. I asked her, \"Do you think we can change things here?\"\n\"Here?\" She smiled as she made a small circular gesture in reference to the room. \"You're not only changing things HERE, Carella.\"\nHer hand stayed in the air, this time drawing a bigger circle. \"You're going to change the whole Reef.\"\nI repeated what she'd said, my voice a near whisper. \"...Change the whole Reef.\"\nShe didn't respond, so I turned my gaze to the window. Time flows faster than I'd imagined. Just before the light of the second dawn could peek through, she called to me. \"Carella.\"\n\"Carella, look at me,\" she said.\nBuzzing echoed through my head. She was sitting in front of the window, back facing the light. I couldn't make out her face, but I could see her lips opening and closing. \"The Queen believes in you, values you. Follow her, and you'll find what you're looking for.\"\n\"Don't rely on me anymore. Don't think of me anymore. Don't...\"\nWhat she said afterward was unclear. I seemed to have opened my mouth, but I couldn't hear my voice through the sharp ringing piercing my ears. I reached out to grab her, and the surrounding scenery flew away.\nCarella.\nCarella.\nCa...\n\"Helhest!\"\nMy eyes flew open, and I sat up in my bed.\nWhen I rose and took a seat before the table, Grom hastily hovered back and forth behind me, asking if I was alright.\nI didn't know how to answer her. The cold sweat drenching my skin and the rapid beating of my heart told me this was something terrible, but I had to record this dream—had to record every word, every sentence, before I forgot them all."}]},{"id":"diary-31208","title":"Show of Interest","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"1. Perun — Agreed\nI knew it! Perun's the best person in the whole world!\n\n2. Jolder — Agreed\nShe seemed a bit too eager. Any excuse to get away from her apprentices' bickering, I guess!\n\n3. Gheleon — Rejected\nThe audacity! He said a gathering of Iron Lords would give our enemies the perfect chance to attack. Buzzkill!\n\n4. Silimar — Rejected\nGramps said he's gotta finish fixing up his castle before he can leave. So, in other words, never.\n\n5. Timur — Rejected\nReplied with a 'no' and then vanished. What's that about?\n\n6. Orimund — Rejected\nMade a very clumsy attempt at pretending not to hear me.\n\n7. Skorri — Agreed\nI knew Skorri would like my idea!\nShe even said she'd help me convince Radegast. I'm really grateful, but I have a feeling this might backfire...\n\n8. Crimil — Rejected\nWhy does everyone have beef with Felwinter?!\nSure, the way he talks can get on people's nerves from time to time, but he's not THAT annoying...right?\n...No, he IS that annoying.\n\n9. Felwinter — Rejected\nNot only did he say no, he also laughed at me. Your days are numbered, Felwinter!\n\n10. Saladin — Rejected\nWhen did Saladin learn to pass the buck? His life as a lord has changed him.\n\n11. Radegast — TBD\nI'm going to convince Radegast tomorrow. This time is sure to be a success."}]},{"id":"diary-30108","title":"Boundary","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"Pre-battle meeting, I spoke up. Fallen underground. The old heating ducts, repurposed as flanking corridors. Frontal assault, three-sided encirclement. The Iron Lords' ground recon couldn't see this.\nCommander nodded. Plan unchanged.\nI didn't argue. Said my piece, meaning delivered. The rest, leave to the blade.\nEleven minutes into the assault. Behind the east transformer, an ominous silence. Wrong kind of quiet. Like held breath before drawing the net.\nI broke formation. He pushes front, I dismantle from the side.\nFlank, faster than they predicted. Intercepted the first flanking squad. Struck. Three cuts.\nFourth cut fell, and the encirclement's timeline shattered. Front line wasn't surrounded.\nBack at camp. Commander standing at the gate counting heads. Saw me. Said nothing. I said nothing. Blade still un-wiped, Void crystal glinting on one section.\nNext day. Drill. Fix walls.\nOn the wall, brushed past. He paused, then kept walking. That was enough."}]},{"id":"diary-21008","title":"Summons","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"The summons was delivered in the format he was most familiar with: a neatly arranged arbitration request form, complete with applicant, cause, and evidence list. The applicant column read: the Whisperers. The respondent column read: Cassian.\nThe matter boils down to one point: out of the thirty-one arbitrations he handled, in one instance, he permitted an extrajudicial massacre—the Warlord Vorek's surrendering settlement in the South, where 400 people laid down their weapons as per his declaration, only to be slaughtered three days later.\nThe Whisperers, following their principles, proposed: his Ghost Echo should \"properly guide him\" and, if necessary, grant him eternal rest. The respondent is requested to attend an \"internal evaluation.\"\nHe finished reading the summons and, for the first time in thirty years, let out a small laugh—barely audible. Finally, someone had submitted a proper procedure to him. But this procedure had no court, no public hearing, no cross-examination; it was an evaluation document from an intelligence organization. Justice hidden in the shadows is not justice—it's a blade.\nHe agreed to attend but laid down his conditions: if you're going to arbitrate me, then follow the rules of arbitration—public court, both parties present, and testimonies allowed. The reply was delivered to the Council of Twelve by Umeko, and it contained only one sentence:\n\"Since you claim to be fair, then be openly fair.\""}]},{"id":"diary-20506","title":"Anniversary","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"Bakhli didn't leave after finishing his report. Instead, he tidied up the bookshelves, pushing a wayward book back into place. He inspected the comms, knocking on the device's shell with a knuckle. I knew he had something to say.\n\"What is it?\" I asked.\n\"Today,\" he replied, \"marks thirty years since you came to Samarkand. The guys want to throw you a banquet.\"\nI initially wanted to turn him down. Samarkand is not wealthy, and the resources would be better spent on our arsenal. Then again, after fighting for so long, people need something to make them remember how life should be. Rejecting would harm morale.\n\"Very well,\" I said. \"Go get ready. I'll have Knack prepare a few words.\"\nBakhli took his leave.\nThirty years... Indeed. Aska has retired, and Bakhli has taken his post. That was twenty-two years ago. Time disappears like water seeping into sand. The Light empowers our bodies, but it dulls our perception of time.\nA few days ago, Bakhli told me that his daughter had just turned fifteen. In just a few years, he said, she will be able to join us. The girl's shooting is sharp, as are her wits, and she's quite interested in explosives. The front lines, scouting, engineering... She would be a good choice for any of them.\nHe spoke of these things as if he were discussing the weather—as if his child taking to the battlefield was a given. This is wrong.\nThirty years, and I've dragged an entire generation of Samarkand residents into war. Now, even their children would fight...?\nKnack flew over. The speech was ready, and he wanted me to have a look.\nIt's already dark outside. Outside the window, the alarm is flashing. This will be another long night."}]},{"id":"diary-11502","title":"Hey, Newbie","sub":"Character diary · Ikora, the Hidden","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_115","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora, the Hidden"},"body":[{"p":"ACCESS LEVEL: Top Secret\nENCRYPTION PASSKEY: M4K8Q2F9Z3T1S6L7W0PR$IKO-006\nCHANNEL MEMBERS: CHA-319, IKO-006\nCHANNEL NAME: Hi, Newbie\n\n1. Hey!\nI hear you're our new boss.\nIs it true, Boss?\n\n2. Here I thought you were here to report your work to me.\nRadegast told me an agent will debrief me on the Moon situation, given it's the most urgent issue at hand.\n\n3. :( Ah, I take it you're the serious kind when it comes to work.\nDuly noted.\nBy the way, we don't typically use real names over comms.\nSo you should write \"VIP#0001.\"\n\n4. ...Thank you for the reminder.\nI will keep it in mind.\n\n5. So, how should I address you, Boss?\nI'm a reliable operative—and I'll be sure to prove it.\nYou'll find the Moon report in your mailbox. I just hit Send.\n(If you don't see it, it might be due to network fluctuations. Old bug. Maybe wait a minute or so.)\nSo? Have you finished reading it? Pretty good if I do say so myself!\n\n6. I can indeed see you have experience in writing such reports. If a rating is what you require, I would give it a \"Very good.\"\nBut there is one area I would like to address, which is the portrayal of the Nine as allies. Viewing them as such right now would be too hasty. We don't yet know what they are, and although they have indeed provided aid, it appears to be a sort of trial, a test of chosen Lightbearers.\nWhat kinds of Lightbearers do they seek? What do they hope to gain from this? Until we can answer those two questions, I believe we should treat them with vigilance.\nAs for how to address me, IKO-006 is fine.\n\n7. Understood, IKO-006.\nNow then... Lightbearers are so keen on exploring the Nine's Singularity. Could that become a risk? How should we address it?\nAlso, figured I'd mention we meet up to play the \"Master Chef\" board game every week.\nThe next get-together is the day after tomorrow, in the evening. You interested?\n\n8. Any attempt to stop them would be meaningless. Nothing can hinder curiosity.\nWe will continue observing for now, especially those who show a particular interest in it.\nI'm certain the Nine will take action before long.\n\n9. Got it.\nAnd game night?\n\n10. Why not?\nI'm always free on Saturday nights."}]},{"id":"diary-31209","title":"Letter to Radegast III","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"No, Radegast. I've already thought this over. I don't need to waste more time \"reconsidering.\"\nOf course I understand the many benefits being granted a territory can bring, just as I know that my refusal will bring plenty of unnecessary conflict and trouble. But you know me, and you know how willful I can be. So please, allow me to \"willfully\" reject your proposal once more.\nYes, I've already made my choice. And no, this isn't something said in a moment of anger, nor is it some childish way of getting back at you. I know full well what I'm doing—I refuse the territory you've given me as well as your suggestion to select an Iron Wolf.\nI don't want to be bound by borders, just as I don't want my days filled with tedious chores and meetings. If it were just dealing with alien invaders, then maybe it'd be a different story, but how could a lord even have such a thought?\nAnd administrative tasks? Making big decisions? That sort of stuff is way out of my league. It'd be nice if everything in the world was neatly divided into \"right\" and \"wrong,\" but things aren't so simple, are they? Who's right and who's wrong, you or Saladin? Who's right and who's wrong, you or Felwinter? Each of you has his own answer, but I don't. That's where the problem lies, Radegast.\nI don't have an answer. All I can do is hope you guys won't continue arguing, hope that this issue can be put to rest so we can go back to the good old days when we felt like a family.\nI know this is childish, but I can't change what's in my heart, and I don't want to join your fight.\nEven more than that, there's still so much that needs to be done. No matter where I go, be it the Warlords' lands or Fallen-occupied territory, the one constant is humanity's suffering. Even if I'm limited in what I can accomplish, at least I can do something useful.\nGive me the freedom to do as I wish. That's my request."}]},{"id":"diary-30109","title":"A Flag","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"I once asked an older Light-wielder: Where did I come from?\n\nShe said: From a place that neither Light nor Dark wanted.\n\nI still don't understand if that was an answer, or saying nothing at all.\n\nThat day the harbor was empty. Sjur Eido's ship had just docked.\nShe walked out of the bridge exit, her deep-purple cloak filled with wind like a flag. I watched her from across half the harbor. She didn't look this way.\n\nWhen her silhouette turned into a passage, I thought: I want to become someone like her.\n\nThat hasn't changed."}]},{"id":"diary-10210","title":"The Cosmos","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"I love this place, the Space Elevator—it makes me feel as if I've escaped Earth's gravity and left the planet behind, as if I'm floating through the cosmos, cradled by the stars.\nGravity is one of the sources of Void energy. It's a force I've repeatedly experienced and learned to wield, as if tracing the orbits of planets within my own miniature universe.\nI've seen the images and recordings left by past astronomers, and I've looked up to the stars through the telescope at the museum's observatory. They are beautiful, yes, but they are not the true face of the universe, seen with my own eyes after passing through the atmosphere.\nDown on Earth, the sun and moon are mere components of the sky, like the hands of a clock, or elusive and distant motifs upon an immense canvas.\nAnd now, with my feet having left the Earth's surface and gravity's pull on me having weakened, it's as if I no longer belong to Earth—an incredible feeling. Gravity is a thread that binds me, yet also keeps me safe. And with it severed, I'm able to observe the Earth and the world around me from a wider, more free perspective.\nBut alongside that sense of awe is also heartfelt fear.\nThis fear stems from the boundless vastness of space, the unbearable feeling of weightlessness, the eternal silence, and the blinding sun, which becomes even harder to gaze upon without the atmospheric barrier shielding one's eyes.\nThe sun's massive size and scorching heat make it a terrifying force, one that reminds those who witness it of their own insignificance.\nWithin the cosmos, I am alone, and yet this solitude differs from that experienced on Earth. It is quieter. It is more straightforward. It has more presence.\nI'm very lucky to have Ophiuchus as my companion.\nHe told me that, if we eventually leave Earth and embark on a journey across the stars, he would like our first destination to be Venus, a world vastly different from our own. There, the sun rises in the west and sets in the east, and we would need to wait 117 Earth-days to witness both phenomena.\n\"Fortunately,\" he said, \"I'm a Ghost, and you're a Lightbearer, so time is no issue for us, right?\"\nHis words harbor the unique ability to free my heart from its fear and loneliness, then bring it back to my chest, filled instead with hunger, curiosity, and ambition.\nOf course, my eyes can only see so far; what I perceive is just a fraction of the solar system, which is itself just a fraction of the Milky Way, and there are countless such galaxies residing in this seemingly infinite universe. The cosmos is vast and magnificent, and I am profoundly ignorant, yet curious about every corner of it.\nThe Traveler gifted me a near endless lifespan. Perhaps the true significance of that time remains hidden in one such inconspicuous corner.\nSomeday, I will leave Earth and visit every planet in Sol, then the Local Bubble, and the Orion Arm... I will measure and understand everything with my eyes and footsteps. I will learn, think, and discover the truths of the universe for myself."}]},{"id":"diary-30907","title":"Recording","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"[A locally saved recording.]\nThe camera turns on, showing nothing but black at first. Eventually, it focuses on two figures. All throughout the video, the frame moves up and down, up and down, as if the camera is floating in mid-air, unable to find a focal point.\nA second later, a male voice is heard crying out from a figure crawling on the ground.\n\"H-How did you find me...?! Did she send you?!\"\nThe standing figure speaks with a familiar female voice.\n\"Please, calm down and tell me your name. I'll help you.\"\n\"Y-You're lying! It's a trap... It's all a trap...\"\n\"Wait, what trap?\"\n\"I know you... You're Carella—she sent you.\"\n\"What are you talking about? Who is 'she'?\"\n\"She's...she's the one pulling all the strings. I can't escape her—n-neither can you.\"\n\"Why does she want to capture you?\"\n\"...Because I've lost my usefulness. And you... You'll be in the same boat soon.\"\nThe standing figure kneels down and reaches out as if to grasp the other's shoulder, but he howls as he rolls and crawls away.\n\"Don't! Don't take me! Stop doing her bidding—you'll end up just like me!\"\n\"I don't know what you're talking about. Please, just calm down and return to Felwinter Peak with me. You'll be safe there, I promise.\"\n\"...Safe?\"\n\"Yes. No matter who is hunting you down, I won't let you die.\"\n\"...Die? Hah...haha... Is that her reward?\"\n\"...What?\"\n\"You know as well as I do that what's waiting for me is a hundred times worse than death.\"\nThe figure on the ground convulses and huddles, his right hand pulling down at his clothes.\nThe camera violently shakes, and there is an anxious female voice coming from above. \"Helhest!\"\nThe kneeling figure hurriedly stretches out a hand and tries stop him, but it's too late. All she can do is watch with wide eyes as the curled-up man before her pulls a gun from his clothes, stuffs the barrel into his mouth, and pulls the trigger.\n\"BANG!\"\nThe camera trembles as it hurries over. It circles the man's bloodied head twice before the female voice from above speaks.\n\"What do we do? This trail's gone cold.\"\nThere is a lengthy pause. Then, the kneeling figure stands. \"Let's go, Grom. We'll find a new lead eventually.\"\nThe camera shakes again, and a second later, it cuts to black."}]},{"id":"diary-10909","title":"Veridia","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"July 25\nSaladin said he wanted to hear about my plans for the future, so we went to Veridia again today. We talked for a few hours, during which he invited me to join the Iron Lords, but I refused—I do not have the right to such a title, at least for now. But I told him that I would stay in the Red Sea Rift for a while. When I excused myself, I found a bunch of familiar militiamen waiting by the door. They were the champions who had defended the city. When they saw me exit, they started to call my name loudly—\"Darius! Darius!\" They thanked me for serving as their commander in that battle and called me their hero. From the founding of the City of Water until now, it has been nearly twenty years since I last heard someone call me like this—be it the name \"Darius\" or \"hero.\"\n...\nJuly 30\nToday was my fifth day serving as a doctor in Veridia. I had a special patient—a middle-aged man who was supposed to take my life. The one who brought him here told me that he was now a Red Sea Rift militia member who had used his drones to help many people. However, the drones went offline this morning. When we found him, he was already gravely injured, with his respirator and AI-speaker both damaged.\nThe outlook was not good. Some fragments of his respirator got lodged in his respiratory tract. He couldn't speak and was struggling even to breathe. But I knew he was awake. He was staring me straight in the eyes as I administered the anesthetic. I guess he didn't want me of all people to save him, but there weren't any other options.\nFortunately, the operation went well. After that, I fixed his AI-speaker with Marbas's help.\nJuly 31\nHe regained consciousness and said, \"Thank you, Doctor Rossi.\""}]},{"id":"diary-31100","title":"Recipe I","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"[The following is a copy of Thurayya's handwritten recipe.]\n\nSheikh Al-Mahshi\nIngredients: Zucchini\n[Added note] Don't use the long kind. Use short, thick gray zucchini.\nFilling: 500g ground meat, 3 tablespoons olive oil, 1 onion (diced), 1 teaspoon five-spice powder, salt to taste, 1/2 teaspoon cinnamon powder, 1/4 teaspoon nutmeg\n[Added note] Where the heck did Thurayya get this \"teaspoon\" thing from?\nSauce: 2kg yogurt, splash of olive oil, sprinkle of salt\n[Added note] DO NOT use Dydron-brand yogurt stored at room temperature. DISASTER!\n[Added note] I think Thurayya used canola oil before.\n\nPreparing the filling:\n\nAdd olive oil and diced onion to the pan. Cook on medium-low heat for 5-7min, stirring occasionally.\n[Added note] What is medium-low heat?\nAdd ground meat, salt, and spices. Break up chunks of ground meat, stir-frying until the mince browns. Turn off the heat and set the filling aside for later.\nPreparing the squash: Core the zucchini.\n[Added note] I give up. I'll never be able to hollow out a zucchini using a knife as perfectly as Thurayya did.\nScoop the filling into each zucchini half. leaving about 2cm of space at the top. Don't stuff them too full. Otherwise, the zucchini may burst, or the excess filling will seep into the yogurt sauce, changing its color and flavor.\nAdd olive oil to the pan, then lightly fry the zucchini, gently turning it every minute or so. Fry until the zucchini is gold all over.\n\nCombine:\nPlace the fried zucchini into the yogurt sauce, then simmer again at a medium-low heat. Once you've added the zucchini, the sauce will thicken.\nStir it a bit, then cover the pan and let it sit for 10-15min.\n[Added note] Even if I use fresh yogurt, I can never get it to taste like Thurayya's."}]},{"id":"diary-10908","title":"The Haunting","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"August 18\nWe encountered a group of mortals being chased by the Fallen near a giant castle. As usual, I helped them out of danger. Marbas was curious as to why they didn't hide in the castle—its intact structure and heavy, sturdy doors would be more than enough to protect them from the Fallen's attacks. But as soon as Marbas asked this, the mortals fell quiet, overtaken by a fear seemingly greater than what they'd felt while being hunted. Only one of them—a trembling young man—dared to answer. He explained that they were refugees who had grouped together, and that they had actually lived in the castle...at least until they saw something terrible. Some said it was a tall, slender shadow, some claimed it to be a giant spider, others stating it was rats in the wall... Whatever you feared most, you would see lurking within the castle's shadows.\nSo, Marbas and I decided to investigate. As I pushed open the door, I was greeted with the smell of mold and decay. The first floor of the castle was occupied by only cold, mossy stone walls and cobwebs on wooden beams. But as we climbed the rickety wooden steps, we heard a brief yet sharp titter—eerie, certainly, yet somehow synthetic. Then we saw the so-called ghost they described in a dim activity room on the second floor—a motionless, giant shadow on the pale wall. Luckily, all it took was a scan from Marbas to uncover the cause of this supposed haunting: a seriously damaged projector. Once we took out its batteries, the \"ghost\" vanished. Due to faulty circuits, it had been constantly displaying frightening images. Once we explained the truth of the matter, the refugees moved back into the castle.\nAugust 25\nMarbas managed to fix the projector. We watched the three horror movies stored in it, yet we never saw that motionless ghost. So what on earth did we see back in the castle...?"}]},{"id":"diary-30902","title":"Records","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"Felwinter Peak Central Archives Application Records\nRequester: Helhest\nApplications\nC0063 | Visitor Application | 02-03 | International Archives | Approved\nC0064 | Document Checkout Application | 02-03 | Resource No.: FD-025 (Reef International Daily, Bound Edition) | Returned\nC0102 | Visitor Application | 02-10 | International Archives | Approved\nC0103 | Document Checkout Application | 02-10 | Resource No.: FH-044 (Reports from the Reef related to political assassinations and trial records) | Returned\nC0113 | Visitor Application | 02-11 | International Archives | Rejected by: Felwinter\nC0114 | Visitor Application | 02-11 | International Archives | Rejected by: Felwinter\nC0115 | Visitor Application | 02-11 | International Archives | Rejected by: Felwinter\nC0116 | Visitor Application | 02-11 | International Archives | Rejected by: Felwinter\nC0117 | Visitor Application | 02-11 | International Archives | Approved\nC0118 | Document Checkout Application | 02-11 | Resource No.: HR-198 (Analysis of global assassin organizations' operating methods, including reports tracking modern underground networks) | Pending Return\nC0166 | Document Return Application | 03-01 | Resource No.: HR-198 (Analysis of global assassin organizations' operating methods, including reports tracking modern underground networks) | Returned by: Grom\nA1127 | Visitor Application | 03-05 | Central Archives | Approved Note: Allow partial access. Noted by: Felwinter\nA1128 | Document Checkout Application | 03-05 | Central Archives | Resource No.: ACC-001 (Felwinter Peak personnel documents) | Returned\nA1129 | Document Checkout Application | 03-05 | Central Archives | Resource No.: *** (Redacted) | Returned\nA1130 | Document Checkout Application | 03-05 | Central Archives | Resource No.: *** (Redacted) | Returned"}]},{"id":"diary-10406","title":"Observation Notes","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"[An observation record about the people of Haven. Each entry has notes written in two different handwritings.]\n\nRadegast: Iron Lord. Dangerous. Keen observer. Exercise strict vigilance around him. Do not make contact unless necessary.\nVery strong, and very busy. Honestly, it's harder to meet him in person than to step on his toes. Sidenote: he plays favorites.\n\nSkorri: Iron Lord. Dangerous. Madwoman. Avoid contact unless necessary.\nI wish I could be that cool—should I also learn to play an instrument? It seems Skorri can play every instrument. I've seen Gwynn playing the cello by the bonfire too... Wait, am I the only Lightbearer in Haven who doesn't play an instrument? How humiliating!\n\nKevarrh: Fallen traitor. An outcast. Not a threat, but not an ally either.\nA total liar. She claimed that Kabr completed two hundred Strikes? More than me? She's got to be kidding—has he nothing better to do? Why would anyone love slaving away for Radegast so much?!\n\nThe Speaker: A little brat. A political puppet. Won't make a difference. Pay her no mind.\nI really don't get why they would choose a kid to be the Speaker. I mean, she looks just like any of those other kids who like to play house in the garden, except she's trapped in an endless game of playing house.\n\nWu Ming: A mortal? I don't buy it. A cunning man. A suspicious middleman. He seems to have caught on to us already—be on guard around him.\nSwindler! A jerk of a swindler! I should've known! He's the owner of the place, for Traveler's sake! He has a pitch-black heart! Two months' bounty Silver, gone!\nOn this matter, you can only blame your terrible card-playing skills.\nHe must've been cheating! Cheating!!!\nNext time, I'll catch him red-handed."}]},{"id":"diary-31101","title":"Bookkeeping I","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"Outgoing: Pink Sheet Market | Daily fixed investment | Mimu Waste Electronic Alchemy 400 Glimmer\nNotice: Fixed investment transaction could not be completed due to insufficient funds.\n\nIncoming: Final payment 45,000 Glimmer From: Horizon Films (Haven)\nNote: Payment for Extra: Lightbearer Thug C.\n\nOutgoing: Transfer to Welt Davis 15,000 Glimmer\nNote: Here's what I owe you! Happy now?!\n\nOutgoing: Transfer to Jimmy Danton 5,500 Glimmer\nNote: Handicap race, Sparrow No.4 - Fangs of Flame.\n\nOutgoing: Transfer to Sosanna Daniels' Workshop 12,780 Glimmer\nNote: Hex bolt set, 600 rounds, three-in-one maintenance & oil discount bundle, zinc alloy stabilizing bracket\n\nOutgoing: Transfer to Jimmy Danton 3,600 Glimmer\nNote: Handicap race, Sparrow No.2 - Silver Sailfish.\n\nOutgoing: Transfer to Red Beacon Staffing 5,000 Glimmer\nNote: Approx. 2 people needed; mission's at the start of next month. Requirements: Able to shoot, able to pilot a Sparrow, able to act in secrecy, able to follow plans, and quiet.\n\nOutgoing: Transfer to Jimmy Danton 1,100 Glimmer\nNote: Ugh, what's with your luck? Standard Race Sparrow No.15 - Hound."}]},{"id":"diary-31102","title":"RE: To: RE: To: RE: To: RE: ... Deidris","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"To: Deidris\nRemember those modded weapons we discussed? Well... Now's! The! TIME!\n\nFrom: Deidris\nWhat modded weapons?\n\nTo: Deidris\nDon't play dumb! If you won't listen to me, how about I report you to that Lady Perun?! Those Black Armory weapons have already been reserved! And if the buyer doesn't get them on time, they'll skin me alive! If that happens, you're going down with me!\n\nFrom: Deidris\nWhat are you talking about? The Iron Lords' Arms and Hazardous Materials Committee oversees the Black Armory's guns. They aren't allowed to be traded on the market. Where'd you even get this idea from?\n\nTo: Deidris\nYou're one hell of an actor, you know that? But I've already told the buyer who you are. You're not getting outta this so easily.\n\nFrom: Anon#5886\nYou IDIOT! Who said you could contact my work account?!\n\nTo: Anon#5886\nYou'd been playing dead for a whole week! What's up with the weapons? They should be arriving in Damascus tomorrow. Don't tell me they haven't even been shipped out yet?\n\nFrom: Anon#5886\nLady Perun reassigned me. They've got someone else on the arms transport squad, and the driver's changed, too. Also, I heard something unexpected happened with this latest trade. Meyrin's remote authorization had some issues, which resulted in gun inspection being delayed. My guess is they're still held up in Irbid waiting for the tech officer to come solve the problem.\n\nTo: Anon#5886\nSo?\n\nFrom: Anon#5886\nSo there's no way they'll arrive in Damascus tomorrow.\n\nTo: Anon#5886\nThen what should we do?!\n\nFrom: Anon#5886\nThere is one way we could solve this. I can send the address to you, then you can head to Irbid and nab the goods.\n\nTo: Anon#5886\nYou've gotta be joking! You're wanting me to steal guns from the Iron Lords' caravan?!\n\nFrom: Anon#5886\nSays the guy who always has me doing that sorta stuff all the time.\n\nTo: Anon#5886\nHow's this the same?! Also, aren't you getting paid for this, too?!\n\nFrom: Anon#5886\nThat's the only solution I've got. What you do with it is up to you. If you can't pull it off, we're both screwed.\n\nTo: Anon#5886\n...Send me the coordinates. This time, you're only getting a 40% kickback. Assuming I even live to give you the payment.\n\nFrom: Anon#5886\nNo way. 80%. Stealing a few guns should be a piece of cake for you.\n\nTo: Anon#5886\nThis was supposed to be your job! But here I am, cleaning up your mess! 50%.\n\nFrom: Anon#5886\nDeal."}]},{"id":"diary-31103","title":"Birdwatching I","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"I hadn't been birdwatching in a long time. Not since Thurayya passed. But today, I had some time on my hands for once, so I recorded what I saw.\nLocation: Yangtze River Estuary\n\nMagpie Robin\nLooks like a mini magpie.\n\nLight-vented Bulbul\nI was lucky and saw it carrying some cotton back to its nest (no idea where it found that, though).\n\nCommon Moorhen\nThurayya would always burst out laughing whenever she saw them \"walking\" on the water.\n\nJapanese White-eye\nIt's so pretty it might as well have flown out of a painting.\n\nVinous-throated Parrotbill\nHow is such a tiny bird so noisy?\n\nBlackbird\nIt took a dump on my head.\n\nHoopoe\nWhile it was flying, I could see its brownish red fan-shaped crest fluttering in the wind. I think that means it was a female.\n\nSilky Starling\nA big flock of them—meaning that when one of them used my head as a toilet, it was impossible to find the culprit.\n\nWhite Wagtail\nGot really lucky today and saw it kill a grasshopper.\n\nNote: My smart binoculars are bugging out. Need to get them fixed. They kept zooming in on the reeds for some reason."}]},{"id":"diary-10206","title":"Strange Correspondence","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Encryption Level: A\nIdentification Code: UHGT-Y00OS-IK01\nSender: ???\nRecipient: Ikora\nSubject: I Was Right\n\nIkora, concerning the matter we were arguing about last time, I can now give you a straight answer—I was right, no question.\nI can say this because I now stand before that very same door.\nI'm not one for making bets, but you said that if I was right, you would cover for me at all Vanguard meetings for the next three months. I'm counting on you to keep your word, as I might not be able to make it back in time.\nThey'll have questions for you—a lot of them. But you can handle yourself. You've always managed. In fact, I think you might be better suited for the role than me—I know you'll disagree, but I have to say it.\nConsidering how my coordinates on the timeline will change unpredictably once I step through the door, I wouldn't want you to receive this message years, or even decades from now. So, I've set up three delayed deliveries—before entering, during, and after. The content of each message is the same, but remember to tell me the timestamps and corresponding identification codes when you receive them.\nFurthermore, if I don't contact you again, and you don't receive the third message, tell the council that they should seal that door shut. I've already sent you the \"key,\" which you should find in your mail tomorrow."}]},{"id":"diary-20503","title":"Warlords","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"Recorded by Officer Knack for General Xuan Wei.\nKāmihā finally arrived.\nI could hear the roar of three Sparrows' engines in the distance. They sounded like some sort of horns. It wasn't just Kāmihā himself, though. He also brought his \"left and right hands.\" Judging by the dust covering all three of them, they must not have stopped much, if at all, along the way. Hmph. Saisim's been harassed by bandits for years, yet not even once did he show his face. But this time, he hurried here not even a week after hearing the news. His intentions were plain as day.\nAs soon as he stepped off his Sparrow, he barked at the crowd, \"Where is he? Where's the new Lightbearer?\"\nGiven Xuan Wei's stature, there's no doubt Kāmihā had spotted him already. But Warlords are always like this, always demanding others come to them. What he didn't anticipate was that Xuan Wei couldn't understand a word he said. And me? I couldn't be bothered to deal with him. The silence stretched on for a while. Then, with a wave of his hand, his Ghost emerged. She reminded me of a gnat. Once she floated over to me, she gave her orders with an unquestionable tone. \"Knack. I hear you've found your Lightbearer. Well? Aren't you going to introduce him to Lord Kāmihā?\"\nThere was no getting out of it now. All I could do was convey to the General, \"Lord Kāmihā heard a new Lightbearer has arrived and came to meet you.\"\nThe General rose, cupped one hand in his other before his chest, and bowed, but he didn't say a word. Kāmihā took a few steps forward, but he didn't immediately respond. Instead, he simply sized up General Xuan Wei with an expression I couldn't decipher. Briefly, I sensed he was evaluating a potential enemy. Some time later, Kāmihā finally spoke. He expressed his gratitude to the General and invited him to the capital of his territory, where he could meet his \"Lightbearer brothers.\"\nI interpreted what he'd said. The General didn't respond to the invitation. Instead, he stated that although the bandits had been fended off for now, their stronghold was still present. He added that, given Kāmihā was the lord of these lands, he should clear it out. Protecting the people was his duty, after all.\nI translated the General's words for Kāmihā, who then argued that his army was limited, and he couldn't possibly look after every corner of the territory. But seeing as General Xuan Wei was here now, he could shoulder the responsibility of protecting this town, if he was willing.\nThe General agreed on the spot and stated he would visit Kāmihā's capital as soon as the surrounding bandits were dealt with.\nKāmihā stared him straight in the eye, but didn't ask any follow-up questions. Before he left, he said to me, \"You've found quite the remarkable Lightbearer, Knack.\"\nYeah. As if I needed your reminder. I know full well you'll be watching us like a hawk."}]},{"id":"diary-31104","title":"Recipe II","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"[The following is a copy of Thurayya's handwritten recipe.]\n\nCreamy Freekeh with Chicken and Mushrooms\nIngredients: 3 cups of coarse freekeh, a small amount of olive oil, 1 chopped onion, 500g diced chicken, diced fresh mushrooms, 2 teaspoons salt, 1/2 teaspoon cardamom powder, 1 teaspoon five-spice powder, 5 cups water, 500ml cream, 1/2 cup grated cheese\n[Added note] I left that blue puppy cup Thurayya always cooked with in her grave. I'm such a fool.\n\nPreparing the freekeh: Place the freekeh in a bowl and rinse 2-3 times until the water becomes clear. Fill with water again and soak for 15min.\n[Added note] It's impossible to get the water clear with just 2-3 rinses!\n\nCooking:\nHeat the empty pot over a medium heat, then add the olive oil and diced onions, stir-frying for 3-5min.\nAdd the mushrooms, then cook for 7-10min.\nAdd the chicken and fry until both sides are golden.\n[Added note] There's definitely something missing between this step and the next step. If only I could check the original. And where's the original? You burned it in a fire, idiot!\nDrain the freekeh and add it to the pot along with salt, cardamom, and five-spice powder.\nAdd more water and turn the heat down to medium-low. Cover the pot and cook for 20min, until the freekeh has absorbed the water.\n[Added note] Don't forget to put the lid on! Otherwise the moisture will boil away! Can use a bulletproof plate in place of a lid if needed!\nAdd the cheese and cream and mix well. Cook for 3-5min, then turn off the heat and cover. Let it sit for 15min, then enjoy!"}]},{"id":"diary-20501","title":"Tiger Awakened","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"I have to say, the bandits here in Saisim aren't exactly the brightest. They'll relentlessly pursue anything that moves, and from a distance, it's pretty comical. When you're their target, though... Not so funny.\nFortunately, the dimness of the caves provides some advantages when it comes to shaking them. As a Ghost, I can easily hide between cracks or holes in the walls. But that obviously won't work for the folks traveling with me. All they can do is cling to the stone walls as clouds of dust are kicked up by the scouting team overhead. I saw Joro keeping a hand tightly clamped over his nose and mouth, his face turning purplish-red as he tried to suppress his cough. Looks like his weak nasal cavities have reached their limit.\nI'm lucky I chose to show myself and draw the attackers away. Otherwise, I might not have stumbled upon such a unique Lightbearer.\nI got turned around in the darkness, but as soon as I entered that stone chamber, I was overcome with a sense of purpose. When he rose, I almost wondered if what I'd resurrected wasn't a being of flesh and blood, but a statue of some deity. Before I could even cry out for help, he instantly grasped the situation. The first bandit to charge into the stone chamber hadn't even got his footing before he and his gun were sent flying. Then... Roars, screams, the sounds of gunfire—a cacophony of sounds, all echoing throughout the cavern. In the ever-shifting lights and shadows, I saw his fighting stance surrounded by Arc Light crackling through the air. He was like a... Like a hunting tiger.\nYes, a tiger—that was my first impression.\nOnce everything fell silent, he finally spoke. It took three attempts before I realized he was ordering me to \"light the oil lamps.\"\nOnly someone from ancient times would talk as he did...\nAt that moment, I understood I'd met a very, VERY unique Lightbearer.\n(Note: My Lightbearer requested I keep records for him until he learns to use modern tools.)"}]},{"id":"diary-21004","title":"Court in Session","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"The remnants of the Eliksni's fallen clan arrived at Haven's outer gates: one adult survivor, several children, and the scorched shell of the Servitor that Ata was forced to destroy. They came to fulfill Ata's unfinished parting words—\"Go to Haven, you can survive there\"—seeking ether and a shelter from the snowstorm. The tense militia mistook them for raiders preparing to attack the outpost, and when the ether-starved children fainted, the survivor raised their weapon protectively. Someone's finger slipped—a shot landed on the frozen ground.\nCassian stepped out from the crowd and announced \"Court in session\" at the entrance, beginning to read the rules of the venue. The militia captain froze; the Eliksni didn't understand. Then the survivor—who had learned a few human words in Ata's class—awkwardly raised both hands and performed a human court salute that the children had taught them.\nCassian returned the salute. At that moment, the old scales measured the weight of another race for the first time.\nHe held court for three days and established a new covenant: the militia would ensure supply routes and ether allocation, Donovan-17 pledged to research ether replacement devices for the children, and Ata served as translator and witness. The reading was still lengthy, but for the first time, he added his own clause to the rules: \"Before the rules are finished being read, both parties must first listen to each other.\"—It was something Harrow had once excelled at; he finally understood that listening is also part of arbitration.\nOn the night of the agreement, Echo mentioned that someone had silently watched the entire process. In the corner of the crowd, Umeko closed her recording terminal and wrote in the observation log:\n\"Subject: Cassian. Evaluation: Supremely fair and just type—usable.\""}]},{"id":"diary-20502","title":"\"Xuan Wei\"","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"Recorded by Officer Knack for General Xuan Wei.\nWhen we arrived at the mountain valley, it was just past noon, but the cave was just as dark as before. This time, though, I could light our way without worry.\nMy Lightbearer easily brought me back to the stone chamber, as if he remembered exactly where to go. That made me relieved. I was so excited that day that I had more or less forgotten the way back.\nFirst, we examined the stone platform he'd lied on for more than a millennium. Beside it were some pieces of ancient armor, which he'd probably worn in his previous life, judging from the looks of it. But after so many years, it had mostly rusted away. Only the chest piece and greaves still had some armor plating left on them.\nI activated my scanner and gave the whole tomb a once-over. Beside a wall, in a place I hadn't noticed before, I detected some metal. I brought my Lightbearer over to look at it, and we discovered it was a bronze sign in the shape of a fish, the surface of which was covered in patina. My Lightbearer seemed to know its meaning well, though. He said this yú fú—\"fish talisman\"—was something only military commanders had the right to carry. The talisman was probably engraved with his old name and rank, but sadly, time and patina had left the characters on it completely illegible.\nBut then, we found something on the wall where we'd found the yú fú. Text seemed to have been carved into the stone, but just like the talisman, most of it was impossible to make out. We could only recognize the characters \"Xuan\" and \"Wei\" at the beginning and middle.\nTruth be told, the main reason I suggested coming back here to investigate was because the residents of Saisim wanted to know the name of the Lightbearer who'd protected them. But now, it seemed the dust of history was determined to keep everything hidden. Neither of us would know anything about why he'd been resting alone here for a thousand years or who he was.\nSo... I tried asking him, \"Any thoughts?\"\nHe was silent for a moment as he traced the characters with his finger.\n\"Henceforth, this shall be my name.\""}]},{"id":"diary-20504","title":"Improving & Learning","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"Knack says I now have a decent grasp of the modern language. He also told me that trying to record my thoughts and experiences may help my studies.\nMore than a year has passed since my revival. Aside from combat, everything is new to me. Much changed in this world while I slumbered.\nChief among them would be language. There are several people in Saisim who understand Mandarin, but initially, few could understand my speech. Knack told me that while I slept, Mandarin changed. The casual language in particular is quite different. Now, they speak a \"simplified\" tongue, and my turns of phrase would only be easily understood by those who study ancient texts.\nLearning this \"new\" Mandarin is not overly difficult. The expressions have changed, but the language itself remains. Now, though, I've grown accustomed to it. Interestingly, where the ancient language may have required only a few characters to express one's thoughts, its modern equivalent requires many. How could one call this \"simplified?\"\nA question that once troubled me was weaponry: swords, spears—these I wield with effortless mastery. But firearms... Firearms are entirely new to me. The bullets are packed into a steel-plated box, then a spring pushes them into the barrel. Thanks to gunpowder or electromagnetic force, they can be shot at targets hundreds of paces away. Bows, too, can accomplish this. But with guns, one only needs to move their finger.\nI have an instinct for warfare—I can discern at a glance which battles can be won and which cannot. Yet I do not know how to wield these firearms to achieve victory. Thus, I must learn.\nI asked Saisim's militia captain, Aska, to demonstrate all the guns he could find for me. All guns fire bullets, yet each type is different. Some of them, though, are wielded similarly to the weapons I knew. I've gradually come to understand that guns have not altered war; they have only altered the manner of death. The environment has changed, yet some concepts still hold true. These weapons are less taxing on the body, but they demand greater will and courage. Knack found some military books from later generations. They're quite useful.\nA far more difficult problem than I anticipated is the use of \"modern tools.\" To be honest, were it not for Knack's explanations, I might never have guessed the purpose of these objects: a plain glass tablet capable of storing thousands of books. Glowing boxes one can stand before and talk to people thousands of miles away. And the winged flying machines, letting one see an entire battlefield at once... Only after learning their functions did I realize these tools influence warfare far more profoundly than weapons themselves. My initial unfamiliarity caused me to overlook them—a mistake.\nKnack tells me the technology we use now is but the tip of the Golden Age's iceberg. There is much lost knowledge scattered throughout the world. And in distant lands, people speak different languages.\nI've only just begun my journey through this new world."}]},{"id":"diary-10401","title":"About dinner...","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"October 1\nI'm sick of sharing a body with him!\nThat annoying old geezer argues with me about what to have for dinner every day!\nJust you wait. I'm gonna buy all the foods you hate the most and make you eat 'em till you puke every day!\n\n October 2\nActually, the curry isn't half bad. I can't understand why the old man hates it so much.\nAnd I like potatoes—potatoes are the greatest food in the world.\n\n October 5\nHaha, he's finally shut himself up at mealtime.\nYou're a genius, Tan!\n\n October 7\nTo be honest, I'm getting a little tired of it...\nAnd I kinda feel like curry tastes bad now... Was curry ever this unpalatable before?\n\n October 9\nSigh, why isn't it finished yet?\n\n October 10\nI don't want to eat anymore. It's curry flavor every day.\n\n October 11\nI really don't want to eat... I hate eating.\n\n October 13\nI hate curry! I'm so sick of it! I can't stand it anymore!\nJust eat whatever you want for dinner, old geezer! I don't care anymore!"}]},{"id":"diary-20505","title":"Samarkand","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"Six years in Saisim, eleven years in Shadaq, and nine years in Tubadi later, today, I've arrived in Samarkand.\nThree days ago, the Kela Tai mountains were behind us, but we were soon assailed by a sandstorm. The gravel kicked up by the wind pelted us like bullets. Luck was on our side, though, as we happened upon a half-collapsed building, which I was able to crawl inside. The thick walls were able to shield us from the sandstorm's gales. We were holed up in there for two full days. The world outside was a wash of yellow, and the only sound we could hear was the howling of the wind.\nThis ordeal delayed us by three days, and the person who was going to meet us at the city gate had, naturally, returned to rest. It's just as well. I don't need such extravagance.\nKnack told me much on our way there. He said this was an ancient city with a storied history.\nHe said that in my former era, this place was called the \"Kang Kingdom of the Western Region,\" renowned even then for its prosperity. For some reason, I have a lingering sense that his account isn’t entirely accurate; it might be in the same location, but after all these years—after experiencing the so-called Golden Age—it should not be anything like what I see before me. It's too small, not at all as it should be. This is not the true Samarkand, I think. People who rebuilt following the Collapse merely used its name. In truth, it's a husk.\nHistorically, when Samarkand fell to the Mongolians, it was not for lack of an army, but for a lack of unity. Even now, this remains the city's greatest issue. When I look at the faces of the people here, I see numbness. They huddle in the corners of the ruins, each caring only for themselves. Day in and day out, going through the motions. They rarely speak with each other, going so far as to avoid eye contact.\nI had Knack prepare a list of resources they need and send it to Kāmihā. He will not be pleased. But I already told him, in no uncertain terms, that if this place is truly so important to him, then he will be even more displeased if such necessities are not assembled.\nI hear the Iron Lords have already arrived at Tuzkouduq. I don't have much time left."}]},{"id":"diary-30506","title":"The Great Con Artist","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"This resume comes from the greatest con artist alive, Ning Fei the Trickster, who is clever enough to fool both mortals and Lightbearers alike. Here are his glorious exploits.\nTan-2\nTan-2 isn't an easy target. Every time I'm about to pull one over on him, he finds an excuse to be alone for a while, then comes back and points out the flaw. Someone's gotta be telling him something. After all, that kid looked so silly—clearly he was about to fall for it!\nWell, no one gets to walk away from the greatest con artist ever. So I came up with a brilliant one this time. A tailor-made trick, just for him. I bet him on guessing numbers. He needed to pick a number between one and ten and write it down before I guessed what the number was. Tan-2 thought it was a pure game of luck. However, the greatest con artist never plays unprepared. Knowing the number he'd written down was two was a piece of cake. Tan-2 lost, and must respectfully call me bro for a month.\nBut was it all about luck? Of course not—it was all about preparation. I'd investigated Tan-2's daily schedule and planted the number two all throughout it. There were only two loaves of bread left for him to buy in the morning; the twins who had asked him for help had told him that they had lost a dog named Tutu; even the sign in front of the clothing store he frequents showed that there were only two days left in the sale. He picked two because that was the answer I gave him.\n\nKabr\nMeeting Kabr in and of itself was actually a gamble. I'd bought this funny wide-brimmed hat at a clothing store that day, but I got tired of it and wanted to throw it away after playing with it for a while. Claudia saw that and started her typical nagging. That's when I saw a Lightbearer with a strange hat approaching. I came up with a plan and bet Claudia that I could sell my hat in three minutes.\nSo I walked right up to the Lightbearer, sat down, and greeted him politely. We exchanged names; turned out his was Kabr. Then...showtime. I asked Kabr if he'd been feeling dizzy lately after waking up or doing deep squats. He asked me how I knew. I said that I'd struggled with that once as well and had just been cured by my personal physician. Then, I told him to close his eyes hard for a while and open them again. Sure enough, he started to feel dizzy. According to traditional Chinese medicine, I stated, it was a sign of excessive yin, and he must wear a hat to cure it. Kabr pointed to his own hat and asked if that would work. I said no, and that he had to use mine. As I'd already recovered, he could have it. Kabr was extremely grateful and gave me a whole heap of Glimmer.\nSuch are the ways of the greatest con artist alive, capable of fooling everyone."}]},{"id":"diary-20507","title":"Hollow","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"The battle came to an end. Kāmihā was lying burnt on the ground, looking more like charcoal than flesh. Nobody would ever assume this was once the strongest Warlord in Central Asia.\nI'd imagined this very scene countless times over the last two years, yet now that it had arrived, I felt...hollow.\nI'd been protecting Kāmihā's territory ever since my resurrection. I am a soldier. All I know is fighting. I obey orders, and I performed my duties well. For thirty-six years, not even once did I let Timur set foot in Samarkand. Thirty-six years... All that defending, all the casualties and injuries... And for what?\nSo that I could lead the Tiger's Claws into Scree Valley?\nThat Ghost—Knack always called her \"the gnat\"—was held in Timur's hand. Her shell was trembling. Timur said their creed does not allow them to kill Ghosts. But I am no Iron Lord.\nHe extended his hand, and the little thing he was holding looked up at me and started speaking in a shrill, anxious voice. \"General, p-please, spare me! I swear! I won't ever revive him again!\"\nFor a moment, I wanted to crush her. She was his accomplice! \nBut...what would that change? Would it let Agias go for another ride on his Sparrow? Would it let Ishta's fishing rod bend toward the waters once more? Would it let Calera see the blooming Kapok she'd planted one more time?\nWould it let Agni see her father again?\nKāmihā was the one who gave the orders, and he has got what he deserved.\nBut what of the one who carried out those orders...?\nNo. She is not the one who should be punished.\nI let Timur handle things their way. There had already been too many meaningless deaths; no need to add another.\nTimur called me merciful. He said this proved we share the same ideals, and he hoped I would join their ranks. You would have more than just Samarkand, he promised. All that belonged to Kāmihā would be mine. I would make a fine Iron Lord, he said.\nTerritory, honor... Was fighting simply for this and nothing more?\nShould I have been happy?\nBut what of the soldiers who ought to share this joy with me? Where are they?\nI'm tired. Let me rest."}]},{"id":"diary-20508","title":"Through Combat, Friendship","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"It had been roughly twenty minutes since I'd left Haven.\nOne hundred and fifty meters away was a woman standing in the middle of the road. A bullet flew at me, so I leapt off my Sparrow and rolled away. Now twenty paces away, I attacked.\nOnce she saw me get off the Sparrow, she got excited. She cast aside her gun and hastened her steps, clenching both hands into fists and striking at my side. I decided to take this hit and punch her head-on.\nShe bent down to dodge my right fist, and her left hand struck at my abdomen, bringing with it a cold, tearing sensation that pierced through my armor.\nIt was Void Light.\nKnowing now that my opponent was a Lightbearer, I further threw myself into the fight. The battle began with heavy punches and fast steps. Her attacks hit like a flurry. She was a highly skilled martial artist, and I ended up taking several punches. They weren't fatal blows, but they were still painful. She hadn't used her Relic—it seemed she simply wanted a fistfight.\nNot wanting to waste time, I restrained her with the tether and swung at her. She stopped holding back and drew a shield, surrounding herself with a Void barrier that rendered my follow-up attack useless. As I got back into position, she threw her shield right at my chest, sending me flying backward. By the time I rose, it had already returned to her hand.\nI steadied my breath and prepared to attack again, but she raised a hand to stop and took off her helmet, revealing her reddish-gold hair. It was Iron Lady Jolder.\n\"Samarkand's White Tiger General,\" she said with a smile. \"Your reputation is well deserved.\"\nI then understood.\nSeveral days prior, in Haven, I'd been sitting on a terrace when someone patted my shoulder.\n\"Hey, you!\" she said. I looked at her. She was a tall, strong woman with finely crafted armor and red hair that carried a gold sheen in the sunlight. The makeup around her eyes couldn't conceal her fierce gaze.\n\"The White Tiger General of Samarkand. I remember you,\" she'd said.\nI, too, remembered. During the ninth year of our war against the Iron Lords, Timur summoned reinforcements to attack Samarkand. The siege lasted four months until, eventually, they took the battle to southern Asia.\nShe was among the reinforcements. Jolder, the Iron Champion. Back then, she often challenged me to duels. I never accepted, though. We were at a disadvantage. Victory would change nothing, yet defeat would mean losing the entire city. Thus, I never fought her in all the time their troops were present.\nDecades have passed, yet still, she hasn't forgotten.\nI am not interested in fighting for fighting's sake. A battle should have meaning. I hadn't accepted her challenge during the war, and now I had even less reason to do so.\nI'd turned her invitation a duel down. This made her unhappy, but then her fellow Iron Lady, Skorri, called her name. She said we'd chat another time and left.\nIn the end, I was still unable to avoid sparring with her.\nToday, though, she was in high spirits. She returned her shield to her back and took something from her bag. \"Here.\" She threw it over to me.\nI caught it. It was hefty with refined, gleaming metal. A fine gun.\n\"Hand-crafted by our Gunsmith. It's really nice,\" she said, \"but it's not my style.\"\nShe straddled her Sparrow, waved a hand, and sped off.\nOnce, she would have fought me to the death. Now, she is giving me a gift.\nTimes sure have changed."}]},{"id":"diary-10310","title":"13 Facts about Gwynn","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"This is Gwynn's top agent, the herald of death, the one and only Crowther. If you're reading this, you must be a real fan of Gwynn. You're likely wondering, 'Why are you recording all this?' Well, the reason is simple enough—because Gwynn's the absolute BEST! Her name alone strikes fear into the hearts of sinners! Naturally, I need to spread the word about her. So here are some facts about Gwynn.\n\nFact 1\nDeath never refuses anyone—unless that person is Gwynn.\n\nFact 2\nGwynn never goes hunting, because \"hunting\" implies a possibility of failure. She just kills.\n\nFact 3\nGwynn doesn't teleport—the space just moves to where she wants to be.\n\nFact 4\nGwynn's tears can heal the Traveler. Unfortunately, she never cries.\n\nFact 5\nGwynn once got hit by a Servitor. It exploded after ten minutes of unbearable pain.\n\nFact 6\nGwynn's primary export is death.\n\nFact 7\nGwynn once killed 9 enemies with a single pencil.\n\nFact 8\nWhen Baba Yaga goes to sleep during the day, she checks her closet for Gwynn.\n\nFact 9\nGwynn doesn't need to aim when she shoots—her bullets fly right to her enemies.\n\nFact 10\nGwynn has two speeds: Walk and Uphold Judgment.\n\nFact 11\nGwynn can do the splits across two speeding Sparrows.\n\nFact 12\nGwynn can kill two stones with one bird.\n\nFact 13\nGwynn can rise into the sky by spinning her scythe like a helicopter.\n\nP.S.: There are many, MANY more facts about Gwynn. I will reveal more as our follower count increases.\n\n(Crowther... I have no words. If you keep writing these centuries-old memes or show them to anyone, I swear I will make you the subject of the next \"fact.\")"}]},{"id":"diary-20510","title":"Homecoming","sub":"Character diary · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_205","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"As we emerged from Kachani Canyon, a mine exploded.\nFor a brief moment, I thought it was one of the explosives I'd placed back then, but it turned out to be an electromagnetic pulse, which stalled my Sparrow's engine and threw me quite some distance away.\nWhen I was restarting my Sparrow, a young soldier came running over.\n\"Hey!\" he shouted as he waved at me. \"Sorry about that, Lightbearer. Didn't mean to blow you up.\"\nHis face was devoid of facial hair, and the goggles he wore were a bit too big. But the emblem on his arm was something I was all too familiar with.\nI was somewhat vexed at that moment.\nWhen I handed leadership over to Agni, it wasn't so she could send children into battle.\n\"The Tiger's Claws?\" I asked him.\n\"Yeah. Part of the Youth Scouts.\" He had a proud look on his face. \"Huh? I've never seen your face, but you seem to know quite a bit about us.\" \nHe had let his guard completely down around an unfamiliar Lightbearer. It made sense, though. This was Iron Lord territory, and thus the mortals always assumed Lightbearers were good.\n\"What are you doing here?\" I asked.\n\"This.\" He took out a black box that looked to be some sort of controller and fiddled with it. A small Sparrow model, roughly one square foot, shuttled over. It was colorful and decorated with cartoonish patterns.\n\"Playing with remote control toys?\" I asked.\n\"What? No! Check this out.\" He flipped the toy over, revealing the signal transmitter attached to the bottom. \"It simulates a real Sparrow's signal, and I can control about a dozen at a time.\"\n\"For what, exactly?\" I asked.\n\"You must've been revived not too long ago, huh?\" He looked to be showing off somewhat. \"If the aliens attack Samarkand, I can activate these mini-Sparrows from here. Once they detect ten Sparrows speeding over, they'll think, 'It's a trap! Better cancel the attack.'\"\n\"Of course,\" he added, \"sometimes there really ARE Lightbearers riding Sparrows. A real truth-meets-fiction kinda moment!\"\nKnack let out a laugh. \"Who taught you this tactic?\" he asked.\n\"Our new general!\" the young scout said, voice filled with admiration. \"She's amazing! I hear she visited the Iron Lords and earned the previous general's approval. And when she came back, she came up with a whole bunch of tricks—really fooled the Fallen.\"\n\"Fooled the Fallen, hmm?\" He had me interested now. \"Tell me, what other 'tricks' does she have?\"\n\"We're here to visit her,\" Knack added.\n\"Then let me show you the way,\" he replied. \"As an apology for blowing up your Sparrow!\"\nAs we walked, the young scout told me about what Agni had been up to since she returned. She'd rebuilt the Tiger's Claws and established a new support squad. Younger scouts such as them do not fight on the front lines; instead, they help with reconnaissance. Tactically, the Tiger's Claws do not stay solely on the defensive. They take the initiative to strike and keep the enemy on their toes, but they do not revel in combat. She obtained something that could translate the Fallen language from the Iron Lords out west, and has since used it to spread false information, letting the Houses fight amongst themselves.\nUnder the new general's command, Samarkand has been made whole. The line between civilians and soldiers is blurred, yet the number of casualties has dropped.\nSoon, the silhouette of the city came into view, and at the gate stood a familiar figure.\nThe defenses, walls, and people seem to have both changed and remained the same.\nSamarkand... I'm home."}]},{"id":"diary-30906","title":"Report","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"[A mission report titled \"Old City Signal Station Clean-up.\"]\nMISSION REPORT: Old City Signal Station Clean-up\nOPERATIVE: Helhest\nREPORTED BY: Grom\nLOCATION: Old City Signal Station (Coordinates: 32°46'15\"N 117°09'48\"E)\nENEMY FORCES: 21 Fallen, 4 Servitors EQUIPMENT: 7.62mm Pulse Rifle. Adopted swarm-style attack against charge units of 3-5 Fallen.\nAfter deploying drones to restrain the enemy, we retreated to rifle range to snipe the enemy. A total of 4 bullets were spent to destroy 4 Servitors, achieving 100% accuracy—a display of talent gifted by the Traveler, who has blessed us with the mission of bringing salvation to all.\nHaving lost their false idols, those foolish rejects began crying and shouting. They are the embodiment of despair nurtured by the roots of a world's demise, but we, given our divine decree, shall deliver peace unto their souls.\nThis battle of abdication in the face of a broken destiny lasted until dusk. It concluded with 21 Fallen souls delivered salvation, as well as 4 perished machines that, unable to be brought back from the brink, were dismantled.\n\n[A handwritten note: Stop reading those weird novels, Grom. You can't call the Fallen \"the embodiment of despair nurtured by the roots of a world's demise,\" and we most certainly did not fight a \"battle of abdication in the face of a broken destiny.\" Lord Felwinter doesn't even want to believe you wrote this and warned me not to submit any more mission reports like it.]"}]},{"id":"diary-31105","title":"Fabry Disease","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"[The following excerpt was taken from the Bray Shiraz Rare Diseases Research Center's database.]\n\n\"Fabry disease was named after one of the first doctors to document it, Johannes Fabry. It is a rare genetic metabolic disorder in which mutations in the GLA gene lead to a reduced or complete deficiency of alpha-galactosidase A (α-Gal A) activity, resulting in abnormal glucose metabolism. This leads to the accumulation of metabolic substrates in lysosomes of multiple organs throughout the body, which then causes related organ lesions...\n...This disease is an X-linked dominant genetic disorder; i.e., male patients are guaranteed to pass the disease on to biological daughters, but not to sons, and female patients have a 50% probability of passing the disease down regardless of whether they give birth to a boy or a girl...\nMajor Classifications:\n(1) Classic: More common in men, onset in childhood.\n(2) Delayed Onset: More common in women, with an onset age of 40-70 years old. Delayed onset cases are significantly more common than classic cases.\nPrevalence: The exact prevalence rate of this disease is currently unclear, with an estimated prevalence rate of 1/100000 in the general population.\n...Fabry disease can affect various organs throughout the body. In childhood, it mainly affects the peripheral nerves, eyes, skin, and gastrointestinal tract, while in adulthood, it mainly affects the central nervous system, heart, and kidneys.\nPeripheral Nerves: Burning sensation in the palms and soles of the feet (a type of neuropathic pain); hearing loss (sensorineural hearing loss); significant reduction of sweat production, nausea and vomiting, diarrhea and abdominal distension (affected autonomic nervous system).\nCentral Nervous System: Possibility for early onset cerebrovascular events, including cerebral infarction and transient ischemic attacks.\nEyes: Patients may experience impaired vision or even blindness, and often seek medical attention for this reason...\nHeart: May manifest as coronary heart disease, arrhythmia, heart valve disease, etc. In later stages, acute myocardial infarction and heart failure may occur, which are the leading causes of death for late-stage patients...\nKidneys: Possibility for hematuria, proteinuria, and some manifestations of nephrotic syndrome. Approximately 30% of patients progress to renal failure around the age of 30. ...This disease can also affect the respiratory system, leading to chronic bronchitis, or the skeletal system, in which case osteoporosis is more common.\nFabry disease lacks specific symptoms and is thus prone to misdiagnosis and missed diagnosis. The average time from symptom onset to definitive diagnosis is 14.8 years, though in extreme cases, this can take several decades...\nThe diagnosis of Fabry disease requires a combination of clinical manifestations, biochemical tests, genetic testing, and other indicators. In some cases, pathological biopsy may be necessary. Important testing methods include:\n1. Biochemical Test:\n(1) α-Gal A Activity Detection: Severe decrease or loss of α-Gal A activity indicates this disease in male patients. Female patients have two X chromosomes, one of which carries the mutated gene, thus interfering with the alpha Gal A activity detection. Due to this, diagnosis requires testing of both genes and other indicators.\n(2) GL-3 Levels: Elevated plasma GL-3 and Lyso-GL-3 levels indicate the presence of this disease.\n2. Genetic Testing: Currently, there are nearly 1,000 reported GLA mutations, with pathogenic or benign gene mutations being detected in approximately 80% of patients.\n3. Pathological Biopsy: Used to inspect kidney, heart, skin, or nerve tissue. Electron microscopy can reveal the typical pathological features of lysosomal glucose and lipid aggregation, or 'myeloid bodies.' ...\"\n[Added note] So back then, there was no way we could've predicted or diagnosed this disease, let alone treated it. A rare yet deadly illness...\nUpdate: Entry has been set as \"Hidden\" for Penny."}]},{"id":"diary-10410","title":"Terms of Our Agreement","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"Yannick-11 is not allowed to control Tan-2's body.\nRevision: Assisted control is permitted in extremely dangerous situations, but at all other times, it is strictly forbidden!\n\nYannick-11 must apologize to Tan-2 once a day.\n\nYannick-11 is not allowed to lie to Tan-2.\n\nYannick-11 is not allowed to peek at Tan-2's diary, let alone doodle on it.\nWho cares.\nWhat you just did is a breach of contract!!!\n\nYannick-11 is not allowed to reject Tan-2's decisions.\nRevision: Nor is he allowed to make sarcastic comments.\nRevision: Nor is he allowed to make sarcastic sounds—I'm not an idiot, I can tell when those sounds are sarcastic!\n\nTan-2 has the right to decide when he sleeps and gets up.\n\nTan-2 has the right to decide what he eats.\n\nTan-2 has the right to strike cool poses when using the Parhelion Wing.\nThose poses are not cool. They are stupid and embarrassing.\nRejection rejected! I'm striking those poses! And you can't stop it!\n\nTan-2 has the right to decide whether to keep a pet, what kind of pet, and how many pets.\n\nTan-2 must keep Yannick-11's secrets to himself.\nYou've already told that Lightbearer. A breach of contract, like you would say.\nWolf's an exception!"}]},{"id":"diary-31106","title":"Wristband","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"Jotting down some thoughts:\nI want to use gold, platinum, silver, and aluminum alloy to create the wristband. To achieve the visual effect of my last design, I'll need at least 40g of gold.\nA millimeter-sized battery pack needs to be embedded inside the wristband to ensure that the storage inside never loses power.\nThe Taketori Industry lab in Chemnitz produced a series of prototypes that can coil current collectors and electrode materials into millimeter-level cylindrical structures. By connecting additional high-power thermal energy collectors and kinetic energy collectors, the wristband would be capable of repeated charging, and the storage chip would be able to run for up to 240 hours after a full charge. I can try my luck there.\nHowever, the size and weight of thermal and kinetic energy collectors are an issue. Based on the files I've read so far, collectors that meet the minimum power requirements are too large and heavy to be installed on a wristband. Not to mention I'd have to keep multiple backups with me at all times.\nI need to figure out this chip thing fast. If Lanigann doesn't have chips that meet the performance standard, then my only choice is Sandman over in Austin. He controls the only known SRAM chip production line that's still operational. Unfortunately, I hear he's running low on raw materials and warring with the Iron Lords. There's no way Sandman would be so merciful as to send me a chip directly. He'd definitely have me running around and doing his dirty work.\nThe front of the bracelet would be made of a combination of sapphire and diamond—nothing too difficult to achieve. I've already got plenty of large, high-quality raw stones ready to go. But cutting and polishing them needs a certain level of meticulousness. I'll find a reliable artisan at the shelter in Marrakesh next time I'm there.\nThurayya's condition is getting worse and worse. Hopefully, I make it in time.\nI WILL make it in time."}]},{"id":"diary-10910","title":"Eulogy","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"I remember the first time we met, when we were both just revived by our Ghosts. We were like twins newly born into this world with neither names nor memories. All we knew was each other.\nThey said I should be named Darius, for they thought I had the makings of a great warrior. I told them they should be \"Rossi\"—a crimson flame that ignites the whole sky.\nThey asked me many times what death felt like. I couldn't answer, because Marbas always revived me before I could even feel anything. So each time, I would throw the question back at them. And over time, I heard many answers.\n\"Like sinking in an ocean with neither surface nor seabed, where you don't need to breathe or think. You just keep swimming along.\"\n\"Like being in space—silent, where you can't make a sound even if you wanted to. But it'd be a nice place to sleep, I think.\"\n\"Like becoming a beam of light embraced by a greater radiance. You're enveloped by a vast expanse of whiteness, warm and reassuring as a mother's hug.\"\n\"Like falling into a bottomless abyss. I tried to adapt to the sense of weightlessness, but eventually I gave in and enjoyed it. I suppose if you can't see the ground, that's basically flying, right?\"\nLike a thanatologist, they had a brand new description every time their Ghost revived them. I wish I could hear even just one more answer. But unfortunately, I'll never have the chance."}]},{"id":"diary-31107","title":"Birdwatching II","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"Location: Southern foothills of Mount Katahdin\nGot a foot of snow the other day, but today's weather was pretty good.\n\nAmerican Crow\nAn incredibly common bird in this region. I hope they don't bother me.\n\nDark-eyed Junco\nI'm almost too lazy to even record this bird. There's a ton of them in the surrounding trees.\n\nMockingbird\nThey're supposed to be really common in this area, but this is the first I've seen while I've been here.\n\nNorthern Cardinal\nAn impressive bird. Thurayya once taught me how to draw a cartoon cardinal using 5 circles and 4 triangles. I can still draw it to this day.\n\nNorthern Mocking Thrush\nA rare guest in these parts and a master of imitation among birds. Once, I heard one imitate the sound of a Fallen Walker's engine.\n\nGolden-crowned Kinglet\nThurayya told me its name means it's the \"king of birds,\" but it's actually just a little guy.\n\nBluejay\nI think it's stealing a twig from a black-capped chickadee's nest.\n\nIt's freezing out here. Time to call it a day."}]},{"id":"diary-21005","title":"Discipline","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"The first rule of the Office of the Arbiter is \"An Arbiter has no personal stance.\" He once witnessed his teacher lose composure for the only time—roaring in anger at a duelist who broke their oath, a duel that nearly devolved into mutual slaughter on the spot. Since then, he has suppressed all emotions beneath his ceremonial armor, allowing himself only a slight nod even when pleased.\nNeutrals don't accept thanks—being thanked implies suspicion of bias. So when an Eliksni child stuffed a half-melted sugar cube into his hand, this man who could recite 300 rules backward froze on the spot, combed through every regulation but found no corresponding procedure. In the end, he solemnly said \"Acknowledged\" in the most standard verdict posture and ate the sugar as if executing a judgment."}]},{"id":"diary-31108","title":"To: RE: To: RE: To: RE: To: RE: To: ... Deidris","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"To: Deidris\nAre you playing me for a fool?!\n\nTo: Deidris\nThere was nothing at the campsite! The person in charge gave me an encrypted comms terminal and sent me on my way.\n\nTo: Deidris\nHow am I gonna explain that to the buyer?!\n\nFrom: Deidris\nLooks like you met my colleagues in Irbid.\n\nTo: Deidris\nWhat's that supposed to mean?\n\nFrom: Deidris\nDon't worry about the buyer. We've already found Womack and \"reassured\" him and his men.\n\nTo: Deidris\nHow'd you know the buyer's Womack?\n\nFrom: Deidris\nHe's not the first merc to set their eyes on the Black Armory. And you're not the first arms broker we've contacted, either.\n\nFrom: Deidris\nBut we noticed you used to be in the business of antique tech. Why'd you switch to munitions?\n\nTo: Deidris\nNone of your business.\n\nFrom: Deidris\nIf you're selling those tech relics to Warlords and mercenaries, then yes, it is. And don't even get me started on you moving to sell prohibited goods to Warlords.\n\nTo: Deidris\nSo you set up a honeypot to catch me?\n\nFrom: Deidris\nWe've solved a problem for you, Tariq. It's only right that you pay us back.\n\nTo: Deidris\nYou want me to work for the Iron Lords?\n\nFrom: Deidris\nNo, our standards for recruitment are a bit higher than that.\n\nFrom: Deidris\nBut we're hoping you can provide some intel for us—compensated, of course. You know, what noteworthy people are trying to get their hands on what noteworthy things... That sort of stuff. You can keep doing your treasure hunting. The Iron Lords just want to ensure there are no bad apples among your clientele, such as factions wanting to use the Black Armory's weapons to start a war or something.\n\nTo: Deidris\nI'd like to discuss the \"compensation\" you mentioned.\n\nFrom: Deidris\nNo problem. We can talk about it in person."}]},{"id":"diary-31109","title":"Bookkeeping II","sub":"Character diary · Tariq","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_311","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tariq"},"body":[{"p":"Outgoing: Pink Sheet Market | Daily fixed investment | Timberwolf Sparrow Remodels 600 Glimmer\n\nOutgoing: Pink Sheet Market | Daily fixed investment | Mimu Waste Electronic Alchemy 400 Glimmer\n\nOutgoing: Transfer to Jimmy Danton 1,800 Glimmer\nNote: We should be even now, right?\n\nIncoming: Quarterly dividends | Mimu Waste Electronic Alchemy 133 Glimmer\n\nOutgoing: Transfer to Magellan Digital Maintenance 4,500 Glimmer\nNote: This is the third time you've tacked on an additional fee. If I don't receive a functioning pair of birdwatching binoculars by next week, I'm burning down your shop.\n\nOutgoing: Transfer to Ashraf Aziz 20,000 Glimmer\nNote: Hey, thanks for looking out for me, brother. I'm doing well. Thank you all for going back to Tartus every year to tidy up Thurayya's grave. Say hello to Old Fahd and the others for me."}]},{"id":"diary-21001","title":"The Foundry","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"A man without a past. Like all Lightbearers, he lost all his memories upon resurrection, and no one was there to tell him who he was. The old Arbiter took this amnesiac youth in by the Foundry fire, gave him a name, and taught him three things: stand tall, read fully, and never step into the arena.\nWhen his mentor fell to the gunfire of the Defiant, the Manifesto stopped at the seventh clause; he picked up the gauntlet and completed the remaining articles. The day he became the embodiment of the scales was the day the world no longer needed them.\nIt was also from his mentor that he first understood the true nature of the Manifesto: it was not a ritual, but a countdown—the moment it was fully read was the moment death was pronounced.\nAnd so he honed the countdown into a double-edged blade: for the guilty, it was execution; for the innocent, it was a reprieve. The procedure became both the shackle on his power to execute and the seconds he fought to win for the living."}]},{"id":"diary-21002","title":"Office of the Arbiter","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"The Office of the Arbiter was never a formal institution. It was born from a tacit understanding during the Dark Age: when Radegast first proposed to the Warlords to \"settle a war with a duel,\" someone always had to stand in the middle—to read the rules, witness the outcome, and declare the truce. This person bore no arms, took no sides, and had only one authority: anyone who disrupted the arena would be hunted by both duelists. Radegast and Jolder once joined forces to hunt down a Warlord who killed an Arbiter and burned the arena; after that, no one dared to harm an Arbiter again.\nNow, he is the only one left in the Office. The champion system has ended, and Haven no longer has wars that require arbitration. Yet every day, he still dons his platinum ceremonial armor, stands in the corner of the Iron Bar, and recites the full set of rules to the young Lightbearers sparring there. Most of the time, people regard this as nothing more than the oldest background noise in Haven.\nOnly when Radegast passed by would he pause for a moment, nod in the old manner, and address him as \"Arbiter.\" That single acknowledgment was enough to sustain him for half a year."}]},{"id":"diary-20618","title":"Silver Fern","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"I'm used to carrying a silver fern with me. Admiring the beautiful leaves under the moonlight puts me at ease. But with the passage of time and changes in the climate, this plant has become increasingly rare, and I was left with little choice but to grow my own replacement specimens. Once the water is gone, it needs to be removed very carefully. Once, I used too much force and accidentally crushed one of the plants into fragrant dust.\nOn the island where I was resurrected, the residents believed these plants and their beautiful, curved leaves can guide us home. They call the silver fern's tender, unfurling fronds \"koru.\" The plant's long history and curly shape reminded them of eternity, of an extended lifespan. After wandering the boundary between life and death countless times, I've begun to taste that cycle's emptiness. A Lightbearer's life is practically endless, and no matter how much they circle around, they always return to the starting point.\nI've lived too long; change and apoptosis have both shut me out. The end is as distant to me as the North Star beyond the clouds. How do I touch an unattainable end?\nWell, such thoughts are somewhat sentimental. At least until the truth of my fate is revealed, I have plenty of time to sail. Like the pioneers who sailed their wooden ships to explore uncharted islands thousands of years ago, I will set sail among the stars. Perhaps only then will I glimpse the truth hidden in eternity.\nWhen that time comes, perhaps I'll bring a silver fern."}]},{"id":"diary-10904","title":"Rialto Bridge","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"We've encountered too many Fallen recently. Back when it was just the two of us Lightbearers, this nomadic life was still a tolerable option. But now, we have mortals needing our protection, and our first 'troops' are just a few youngsters with guns. Besides, we have to realize our dream—to build an ideal republic. We needed a home. Or rather, we needed to find one.\nAnd so we embarked on our journey, driven by this mutual wish. Marbas joked that we were just like a bunch of kids searching for a secret base. Unfortunately, we searched for several days, only to find that most of the Mediterranean cities that were still functional had already been occupied. The rest had been destroyed in battles. But we eventually found a city surrounded by water, abandoned yet not without a lingering grace. We swam into the city along the canals, clearing the few Fallen soldiers within. Then I checked its facilities. Luckily, they were all intact and functional.\nWhen I went to tell Rossi the good news, I couldn't find them anywhere. Marbas eventually spotted them, staring at a bridge in the center of the city. I didn't interrupt them, instead following their gaze to take in the sunset. The radiance reflected in the water illuminated the whole city, turning it into a hearth, welcoming and warm.\nThey said, \"Rialto Bridge.\" So that was its name. I told them this place was still largely functional, making it an ideal foundation to build upon. They asked if I wanted to hear a story about this bridge. Naturally, I said yes. Long ago, the City of Water was occupied by invaders, serving as their transportation hub. The only entrance into the city was the Rialto Bridge. To cut off the enemy's front line and stop them from assembling, the guerrillas inside received an order to blow up the bridge within a week. They formed a team and, after enduring many hardships, found a demolitionist. They went on to destroy the bridge and claim victory.\n\"But the bridge doesn't seem to have been repaired,\" I said with doubt.\nThe cunning fellow laughed at this and admitted to only having just made the whole thing up."}]},{"id":"diary-10402","title":"Not a fan of Radegast","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"What's Radegast's deal lately? Does he have some sort of beef with me?\nWolf always says I'm overthinking it, but that's because everyone knows Wolf is Radegast's most favored lieutenant! That lucky one's opinion on Radegast is the real \"biased\" one! This is like Radegast saying Wolf is the most heroic Lightbearer he's ever seen! What on earth does he mean by saying that—hasn't he ever seen me before?\nOkay, back to Radegast—whether he dislikes me or not, he definitely has it in for me.\nEvery time I report to him, he has me wait outside while he talks to that weird floating creature. Total snoozefest, you know? All I can do is stand there counting the flowers on the statue by the door. I think I'm just about out of flowers, though. How do they just keep babbling on and on?\nAnd the last time I kind of mispronounced Karveer, and he blatantly laughed at me! The worst part is, after that, every time I mentioned Karveer, he laughed again—it's just outrageous!\n\n The accurate pronunciation of that Fallen's name is Kevarrh: keh-vaar.\n\nYou're telling me this now?! So you've been watching me make a fool of myself?! For three months! Three entire months! Not a single soul told me the truth?!\nIs it really that funny? Stop laughing! No matter how you look at it, it's the Fallen and their weird names' fault!!\nAnother thing, old fart: stop peeking at my diary!!! This stuff's private, got it? Private!"}]},{"id":"diary-10403","title":"About pets...","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"Grayson\nI think I messed up. Turns out Grayson isn't actually gray. Today he was rolling around in the pond and his fur started losing its color. Weird, right? So I took him to the Armory and borrowed a basin and soap. Half a day of scrubbing later, and guess what? That dog's always been white! What am I supposed to call him now?!\nBut isn't Grayson silly? I started calling him Snowy, he just wouldn't catch on. Oh well, he'll continue to be a white dog named Grayson then.\n\nPatchwork\nFerocious. Loves to sunbathe on the observation deck. Not too fond of socializing. Scratches my face every time I try to pet her—thankfully I'm an Exo.\nWhy didn't she scratch Saoirse's face?\nWhy not scratch the Speaker?\nDoes this cat look down on Exo or what?!\n\nBlackie\nA bit skittish, always hiding in the flower beds. Very susceptible to food though. He lingers around the noodle shop all year round.\nEvery time I see him, he's being fed by someone. I can't imagine how chubby he'll get if this keeps on.\n\nSpots\nShe has been looking listless lately, probably sick. I should take her to see a doctor.\n\nFuzzy\nThe greatest, smartest, and cutest dog in the world. Also the most awesome retriever, and the most courageous hound.\nI wanted to take Fuzzy home with me, but Yannick strongly objected. How can someone NOT love Fuzzy? It's infuriating. There's a reason why nobody likes that grumpy old man!"}]},{"id":"diary-20210","title":"A Stranger in the Red Sea Rift","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"I hadn't seen Wolf and Zev for a while. Today, I found that they'd been sent to the Red Sea Rift.\nThe pair look a bit worn and seem to have been through some tough battles. They were in good spirits, though, and suggested I pay them a visit, claiming something there would interest me. A Harpy and Minotaur or something—it took a whole tankard of beer to learn that those were monster names.\nZev showed me the images she had recorded. I was expecting to see some creatures with bull heads and human bodies, or humanoids with bird wings, but to my surprise it was a...robot?\nA cold, stiff machine, called a Minotaur of all things!\nIt's as humorous and absurd as anything else in this world.\nWolf suspects that these things aren't pure machines. Although they behave well-trained and organized on most occasions, sometimes they react subconsciously, like a living creature—at least, not entirely like piles of cold, hard metal.\nThis is the first time we've seen such a creature, which means their invasion is only just beginning. Perhaps in the future, I might encounter a Hydra and an Argus in the Red Sea Rift.\nIt sounds like a messy mythology, one whose protagonist is just waiting to be born.\nMaybe I should visit the Red Sea Rift when the time is right..."}]},{"id":"diary-10404","title":"Headstone","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"[The handwriting in this diary entry is starkly different from the previous ones]\nI found Zhengming's tomb. He's the last one.\nZhengming, Xuân Yèn, Zigou, all those who once betrayed me, are now buried in this desolate wilderness of eternal winter. All of them.\nI once swore to kill those traitors with my own two hands. Now that they're all six feet under, it seems the only thing left for me to do is to dig up their graves and scatter their ashes to the winter winds—much simpler than murder. The kid always sleeps soundly near dawn, and torturing the dead doesn't take long.\nZhengming was my earliest lieutenant. Weak and hesitant, he always grew and climbed slower than Xuân Yèn. Even in their rebellion, he was just a minor character following behind Xuân Yèn. So many years have passed, I can barely remember Zhengming's face. Imagine my surprise when I saw that rat's epitaph: \"Evil has been conquered. Rest in peace.\"\nIronic, isn't it, that I still walk the very earth your rotting corpse is buried beneath?\n\nBut what's the point in obsessing over the dead? They've long since gone from here, leaving behind nothing but a pile of rotten bones.\nJiangshi was once my property, then it became my enemy's territory. But now, it's just rubble and debris.\nNo one remembers that Lord Yannick once ruled here, and in a few decades, no one will remember Xuân Yèn, Zhengming, or Zigou either. Time is the ultimate victor, and Jiangshi was never my home."}]},{"id":"diary-10405","title":"Elain","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"[The handwriting in this diary entry is starkly different from the previous ones]\nToday, the brat found a dead Ghost in Jiangshi.\nWhen he picked it up, I thought it was Elain, but it turned out to be nothing more than a disappointment.\nI miss Elain sometimes.\nHe was mostly silent, but that wasn't a drawback; I never liked chatterbox, and after all, a Ghost doesn't need to be talkative. What's most important is their loyalty, followed by reliability.\nElain had both, and that's enough.\nThe little brat's Ghost is also a quiet one, and occasionally, I feel he's somewhat like Elain. Though he's much more arrogant than Elain, with nothing but \"yes\" and \"okay,\" interspersed with cold sneers and \"no.\"\nHow can there be a Ghost that says \"no\" to their Lightbearer? Disgraceful.\nLooking back, since Elain resurrected me, I've never heard the word \"no\" from him, and he rarely put forward his own opinions. Maybe he always agrees with my views and decisions, or perhaps he's just very good at following orders.\nWe had been together for decades, but now, when I reminisce about him, it's hard to imagine what his reaction would be if he were still alive and saw the predicament I'm in now.\nPerhaps I never truly understood my Ghost, and I'll never have the chance to know him better."}]},{"id":"diary-21009","title":"The Fish Got Burnt","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Went fishing at the south pier today and caught three. Gave one to the Militia on duty, one to the undertaker—she said river fish must first pay respect to the river, so I complied and placed half a fish back by the riverbank. The last one I brought home to cook. Burnt it.\nThe Echo said it was because I recited two rules while burning the fish. I deny it. The pot admits it.\nThe kid from the outer gate came to deliver salt and happened to witness the whole process. She still ate two bowls. She said the burnt fish had the flavor of the fireside by the door, and she liked that taste.\nNext time, I'll keep an eye on the pot. Probably."}]},{"id":"diary-10407","title":"New Alliance","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"I really don't understand why everyone is so eager to become an Iron Lord.\nIf you ask me, all the seats of the Iron Lords have been occupied and their hierarchy is quite congested! Radegast, Saladin, and the other old-timers are firmly seated as the top officers in command. Any new addition merely refreshes the list of the least important in the organization. We never get a say in all the decisions, big or small—what's the point, really?\nThose with a clear mind would inevitably reach the same conclusion: forget about the Iron Lords, let's build ourselves a fresh alliance!\nAs the proposer of this idea and the founder of this new organization, it's only natural that I should be the leader, the top dog, the most vital founding member.\nAs for the old geezer... Well, he can join as a secret member, serving as the mysterious advisor to the alliance. An invisible, secret member... Heh, it sounds incredibly cool.\nThen...I'll get Wolf and Zev on board. They poke fun at me sometimes, but...they're actually pretty reliable. Wolf can be my right hand. With such a duo, our alliance is destined for greatness!\nRight, there's also Kabr... No, forget it, dealing with that big lug is just too exhausting.\nLastly, I shall personally name this grand organization:\n\nSwords of Justice.\n\nWolf's Relic and mine are both swords. Perfect, just perfect, absolutely brilliant. Tan, you're truly a genius at naming.\nI'll post a recruitment ad on the bounty board first thing tomorrow morning."}]},{"id":"diary-20206","title":"A Showdown with Tan-2","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"Most times, I struggle to understand what those younger Lightbearers like Ning Fei and Tan-2 are thinking—but just as I was writing this, I suddenly came to the realization that some may find Haven's youthful energy quite shocking! Perhaps that is what Lord Radegast had in mind?\nWell, they are spirited and great fighters, I'll give them that. I don't think they would handle the constraints of a legion well, though—Shams often comments on how Ning Fei doesn't even listen to his own Ghost.\nAs for Tan-2... I'll admit he's easier to get along with, even if he is a bit...unpredictable. Sometimes he's impulsive, but other times he's unexpectedly calm and mature. It always takes me a while to figure out his temperament.\nOnce, he suddenly approached me during my morning workout and inquired about how many Strikes I'd taken part in, seemingly wanting to confirm that Kevarrh had told him the truth. I corrected him—it was actually 212 Strikes, not 200.\nHis smile quickly turned to fury as he claimed he'd compete with me to see who could take on the most Strikes.\nSure, but...why? Battles shouldn't be regarded as competitions or something to boast about. Rather, they're an honor that you give your all for. That's why when Shams urged me to just let Tan-2 have his way, I refused... Though our whispering seemed to further provoke him.\n...I can never read Exos.\nLuckily, the bet wasn't boring—I enjoy fighting.\nThe battlefield is, without a doubt, the fairest place in the world. Here, everyone speaks with their fists and strength. I can even empty my mind and let my body act of its own accord—and I also have my shield, of course, which never lets me down.\nA good fight is far more intriguing than sitting in a tavern and making all that confusing small talk with strangers.\nWhen I returned to Haven, Tan-2 approached me and confidently asked how I'd done. When I answered, it was as if he wilted right before my eyes. A moment later, he reluctantly admitted that I'd \"won for now.\"\nI have to say, though, he's an interesting fellow, well worth befriending.\nWith Shams' help, I happily asked Tan-2 whether he would like me to bring him along on my next mission—if he found the strikes too difficult. Everyone knows that there is strength in numbers, after all.\nTan-2 immediately stormed off.\n...I really, really can't read Exos."}]},{"id":"diary-30904","title":"News","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"[An article that has been printed out. With its unprofessionally sensationalist tone, it has clearly come from a commercial site of no real repute, but it's been carefully folded and tucked into the diary anyway.]\n** Heavy Blow Dealt to Outreachers Suspicion Surrounding Leader's Bizarre Death Cleared **\n** Crows' Shadow Looms Power Vacuum Triggers Regional Unrest **\nIn recent days, the \"Outreachers,\" a faction that has long stood in opposition to Queen Mara Sov, has suddenly fallen silent. Their leader, code name \"the White Queen,\" was found dead at Exile's Shore. The deceased's encrypted communication device and biological traces left at the scene strongly point to this being a targeted hit carried out by the agents known as the Crows.\n** Mysterious Death Extinguishes Rising Political Star **\nInternal documents indicate \"the White Queen,\" whose real name and identity are unknown, established the Reef's \"Outreachers\" one year ago with the goal of contacting civilizations on Earth. Within just six months, they recruited over 300 Awoken and seized the southern Reef as their stronghold.\nTheir rapid expansion has clearly garnered the attention of the Reef's largest power, the Isolationists led by Mara Sov, who then gave immediate orders to assassinate the White Queen and eliminate the Outreachers.\n(Note: One of our sources claims that when the White Queen first appeared, Mara Sov's orders were to \"bring her back.\" Our insider has yet to divulge why such an order was changed to the \"assassination\" we've seen unfold.)\nOn the day of the incident, the White Queen's body was discovered on the rocks in the northern reaches of Exile's Shore. Autopsy reports state a bullet hole was found in the deceased's skull, and investigators found a titanium alloy shell bearing an image of a crow—iconography associated with the weapons of the Crows, the Awoken spy network under Mara Sov's command—at the scene.\nInvestigators revealed to us that within 48 hours of the White Queen's death, they found several members of the Outreachers dead at their southeastern base. The composite tactic of culling the leader and pulling out the roots is a classic strategy employed by the Crows.\nFollowing the White Queen's death, the Outreachers logically should have disbanded or fallen into chaos, but strangely, we have yet to receive any news of key members' movements or conflict within their ranks, and satellites have detected no travel by registered spacecrafts. The Outreachers seem to have gone completely silent over night.\nAs of the time of this article's publishing, this assassination is still shrouded in mystery, and the future of the Reef's power struggle remains unknown."}]},{"id":"diary-10408","title":"Renaming Parhelion Wing","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"Solar Wing: Hmm... not cool enough. Out of ten Solar Lightbearers, nine would name their Relic something with \"Sol\" or \"Sun.\" Pass.\n\nBlazeforge Blade: Seraph Blade? Flameforge Blade? Alright, nice backups.\n\nHero's Testament: No, it sounds like a name Kabr would give to his shield. Pass.\n\nCrimson Legacy: Well, it fits the Relic's story well, but could it be a bit too showy? What if Radegast finds it sus? Backup of backups.\n\nLight of the Arisen: Hmm, I kind of like it. Tan, the Arisen. Hmm, I like this name.\n\nI'll skin you alive if you rename the Parhelion Wing.\n\nI've told you a million times: stop peeking at my diary!!!"}]},{"id":"diary-21007","title":"Who Arbitrates the Arbiter","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Roughly half a month ago, Donovan-17 set up an ether substitute device for the children, which suddenly overloaded at night, its light illuminating half the district beyond the outer gate. The Militia sealed off the site, and a \"maintenance report\" was handed over by someone: the device had been used as a beacon to guide the main force of the Fallen—and the energy signature pointed to an Eliksni Servitor's core shell. The evidence was complete, the procedure was complete, and the Militia Captain placed a \"detention order\" in front of him, asking the Arbiter to \"rule according to the regulations.\"\nHe read the report three times. The procedure was flawless. As flawless as a verdict halted at the seventh clause.\nAn echo retrieved a fleeting shadow from the fragments of the device: the night before the incident, the shadow of a Ghost signal overwrite reached into the device's core. It couldn't prove who was behind it—the Whisperers' manipulation of information only leaves results, never names. They don't need to kill other species; they only need to make humanity use lawful procedures to drive them away—the scales will do the rest for them.\nThe most procedural person in the world stood before the most perfect procedure, and with a voice meant for declarations, said:\n\"This arbitration is invalid.\"\nHe removed his gloves and placed them on the regulations. Then, for the first time in thirty years, he clenched his fist and, as a participant, stepped into the center of the field, standing in front of the remnants of the Eliksni.\n\"By the old precedent of the Office of the Arbiter: Those who overturn the field are enemies to both sides of the duel.\" He looked toward the direction where the observer was hiding in the crowd, \"I now identify the one who disrupted this field—appear in court for judgment.\"\nThe Whisperers withdrew that night. The observation log gained one final line: \"Uncontrollable. Reevaluate.\"\nHe stood amidst the empty crowd until dawn, finally understanding the question he needed to ask next: If the scales can be wielded as knives—then, \"Who arbitrates the Arbiter?\"\nNo one answered him. But the next morning, he put his gloves back on and began rewriting the rules."}]},{"id":"diary-10409","title":"Lord Tan-2","sub":"Character diary · Tan-2","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_104","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Tan-2"},"body":[{"p":"Today, I found a half-collapsed tunnel in the greenhouse.\nAmu-Atu warned that there could be a subsequent collapse at any time. But I'm going to be resurrected anyway, so, what the heck, I just wanted to go in and take a look.\nLet's skip the experience of crawling through the hole—it was real dirty. What's worse, Amu said I looked like I was crawling through a rabbit hole. Hmph, I'm definitely NOT helping him defrost the water pump next time—he'll do it himself!\nIn any case, this adventure was still worth it: I found a tiny library on the other side of the tunnel. It looks like it hasn't been visited in a long time, but the books inside are quite well-preserved—to tell the truth, it's my first time seeing such old paper-printed books.\nBut I don't like reading, so while these things are rare and all, I'm not really going to flip through those boring botany magazines and weather records. The really interesting thing in the library is, guess what, Yannick's oversized chair.\nIn my opinion, the chair Radegast has in the Throne Room is already massive enough, but Yannick's chair is in no way inferior. Perhaps it's a shared obsession among these lords, giving orders on these swanky, impractical chairs.\nI found it, so of course, I had to sit in it. And Yannick was quite displeased about it, which made me want to sit in it even more.\nTo be honest, though, this iron lump is more like a torture device. Heaven knows how Radegast manages to sit in his chair all day long. If you ask me, I'd definitely put a thick cushion on it and turn it into a cool armchair—better yet, add a neck pillow to make leaning on it a bit more comfortable.\nTo get back at Yannick for mocking my grand vision of \"Lord Tan,\" I'm keeping my butt planted right in this seat.\nWhile I was moving around trying to find a more comfortable sitting position, I found a line of small letters etched into the back of the chair: \"Take this as a warning. Do not repeat the same mistake.\"\nYannick's nagging suddenly stopped. I guess those words were left by Lady Xuân Yèn.\nI've never met the lady, but the guerrillas still kept her in their minds to this day. These words must have been important to her.\n\nThe stuff here should be useful to the guerrillas. I bet they'll dig their way in and take those books soon enough.\n—Before I left, though, I accomplished one very, very important thing: took a selfie sitting in this chair and sent it to everyone.\n\n#LordTan-2"}]},{"id":"diary-30908","title":"Blessings","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"Subject: Re: Help\nRecipient: Helhest\nSender: Wolf\nThanks for the message, and pass along my best wishes to your friend for me, yeah?\nI looked through the list of gifts you included. I think 2 of them could work in a pinch, but the other 18 aren't exactly suitable birthday gifts.\nIf you ask me, though, I don't think you need to be so nervous. It's just a birthday party, y'know? Even if you show up empty-handed, I'm sure just giving a toast with a thoughtful blessing would show that you care.\nJust in case, I had Zev search the Haven forums for some popular well-wishes and attached them here. I haven't had the chance to look at them myself, but I hope they help you.\nAttachment:\n\"88 Blessings for New Lights\"\n\nSubject: Re: Re: Help\nRecipient: Wolf\nSender: Helhest\nApologies, I'm only now seeing this message. When she was looking over it, Grom thought it was spam and accidentally put it into the Trash folder.\nThank you for your help, Wolf. But as for the attachment's contents, I can't help but find them a bit...questionable.\nBased on 10^6 route simulations, the aircraft you've selected has a 0.0007% chance of crashing. For your safety, we've enabled the emergency oxygen mask preloading program.\n...Is this supposed to be a blessing for a safe journey? Grom says it sounds more like it belongs in some \"Noah Corp.'s\" flight insurance ads.\nHeart rate analysis indicates your risk of organ failure this year has decreased by 8% compared with the previous year, and the downward trend has weakened. This is certainly worthy of celebration.\nI see this one is labeled as a \"birthday blessing.\" Maybe it's popular among younger people? It does seem very...quirky, after all.\nI tried reading the first 20 earnestly, but I wasn't able to find anything worth using. Grom has demanded I stop reading this file and asked me to pass along this message:\n—Stop downloading files from disreputable websites, Zev."}]},{"id":"diary-30103","title":"Ordination","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"The Reef has no night. The artificial star's face never shifts - when eyelids grow heavy, it's deep night. That night, eyelids had just grown heavy when the summons came.\nThe chamber. Mara at the far end of the long table. Sjur in the second seat to the left. I thought I was just here to listen.\nMara said humans on Earth had begun raising walls, calling themselves Iron Lords. She wanted to send a hand to Earth. A Bladebearer. To walk for the Reef where the first wall had just been raised.\nBefore I finished the thought, Sjur was already looking at Mara. Softly: \"She's the right one.\"\nI turned my head. Her face had nothing extra on it. Only the eyes were different.\nSomething I had never seen on her face before.\nTenderness.\nAfter that, the Reef had a new title. Bladebearer."}]},{"id":"diary-10507","title":"Notes on Raising Eliksni Kids: Lesson Records","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"Vocabulary Lessons\nSo far, I've tried three methods of teaching vocabulary: textbooks, situation simulations, and crossword puzzles.\nAmong them, the textbook method was the most efficient, but it also tended to make the kids sleepy.\nSituation simulations were very effective, though their efficiency was less than half that of the textbooks. But the worst part is, I need to spend a looong time writing scripts for them. Just thinking about all that work gives me a headache...\nSolving crossword puzzles is the kids' favorite, but this method can only test their learning outcomes and cannot be used to teach them new words. They won't remember the complete word even if they guess the letters correctly...\nMaybe I can adjust the ratio of using vocabulary textbooks, situation simulations, and crossword puzzles to 5:3:2?\n30% situation simulations and the corresponding scripts... No, that won't work. I need to reconsider.\n\nGrammar Lessons\nSince I haven't found any new or interesting methods, I used the traditional way: giving examples and explanations. The children clearly didn't take to this method, though—they dozed off less than in the vocabulary lessons, but they had a much harder time paying attention.\nOnly when the examples were related to their daily lives would they perk up and actively participate. And when the phrases were about me and Gwynn, they'd REALLY get excited... Alright, I should study how to make up funny examples. I can't always write about Gwynn and I.\n\nLiterature Lessons\nThrough literature lessons, I let them embrace our old tales and poems in hopes that they'll learn more about humankind. I thought there wouldn't be anything out of the ordinary about these lessons, but interestingly, some concepts common to us were very hard for them to understand.\nFor instance, they felt especially confused about emotions playing a pivotal role in relationships, even into adulthood—for the Eliksni, hierarchy is everything. I wonder why Eliksni society ended up this way... Was it something to do with their history? Did something happen that led to them restricting their people through ranks?\nWhat surprised me was that although the kids didn't understand these emotions, they seemed extremely curious about them. I suppose what they don't reject still has a chance to be accepted, right? Curiosity is a good start. Hmm... I need to add more literature lessons to the next stage.\n\nMath Lessons\nQuite normal. The kids don't mind math—a lucky break for me! I can teach them myself, but there are so many lessons now that I don't have enough time for myself. I need to find some new teachers for them!\n\nSports Lessons\nThere was nothing more popular than sports. Even if they were just aimlessly running around on the grass, they showed an astonishing level of enthusiasm... Would be nice if they were that interested in their vocabulary and grammar lessons! I'll find some time to ask the children in Haven about what kind of games they like. Maybe playing those games can encourage friendliness toward humans! Unfortunately, they refused to sleep and kept asking to play ball late at night. No more games for them. I should limit their sports lessons...\n\nMusic Lessons\nI never imagined singing could be so...violent on the ears. That goes for every one of the Eliksni kids... Maybe their vocal cords just aren't made for singing? Listening to their singing makes me feel like I've dropped into some insect-infested cave...\nBut they're quite gifted when it comes to instruments, that's for sure! I bet three Eliksni kids could form a small band. We should stick to instruments and avoid lessons that involve singing.\n\nArt Lessons\n\nI ran into a critical problem at this stage—it's not that the kids won't cooperate or anything, but rather that I can't teach them art... I should find some professionals. Who might be good at drawing...? Maybe...Ikora? But she seems so serious... I'll ask Tan-2. Surely he'd be willing to play with the kids!"}]},{"id":"diary-10902","title":"The Republic","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"\"What exactly is this 'republic'?\" Rossi's question dragged me deep into thought today. They've been pondering my answer about the meaning of war: to build an ideal republic that protects us all. Now I'm posed the same question once again, yet I find myself unable to say a thing. Such grand concepts of justice, peace, and freedom are far too idealistic for our current situation.\nSo I told Rossi that I needed some time to think it over. And they said, as the first citizen of this 'republic' and my right hand, they need to hear this answer—or rather, they need to know what they are working toward.\n[The content below looks to have been added later.]\nI thought it would take forever to come up with a precise answer, but it seemed that Rossi and fate were both determined to pry it out of me. We rescued a group of wandering mortals from the Fallen. Given the state of things, these folks want the Lightbearers' protection, but what they want even more is a leader capable of granting them a peaceful life. After a whole night of arguing with Rossi and Marbas, I finally agreed to their request.\nFrom now on, I, Darius-5, will officially rule as lord, with Rossi-11 as my lieutenant. I issued four rules to our first subjects:\n1. The strong shall protect the weak.\n2. Those who contribute to the territory shall be rewarded with supplies accordingly.\n3. Those who steal shall be flogged. Those who cause harm shall receive the same injury as punishment. Those who commit murder shall be sentenced to death.\n4. Traitors to the Light or the territory shall be treated as murderers and suffer the same fate."}]},{"id":"diary-21006","title":"The Captain's Wedding","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"The Militia Captain is getting married and asked me to be a witness. He said that in the entire city, no one embodies the word \"witness\" more than I do.\nI said I only witness duels and truces. He said weddings are truces too: two people argue for half a year, then finally stop and decide to live under the same roof.\nI can't argue with that. The rules indeed don't specify that witnesses must stand inside the arena.\nThe Captain offered me the first drink. I don't drink, so I carried the glass home after the gathering. Now, the glass sits on the windowsill. Echo says it's in the way. I told her she could float somewhere else."}]},{"id":"diary-30901","title":"Traces","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"I followed the coordinates, and they brought me back here.\nFelwinter Peak seldom sees visitors. With nobody cleaning the wilds here, one can still see traces of a battle. But time, amusingly fair to all, had blurred them.\nGrom swayed gently in the air, but didn't say a word. She just silently followed behind me.\nI found that ship on the cliffside, its remains lying helplessly in the center of the battlefield, covered in bullet holes, dirt, and long-dried bloodstains that made it nothing more than a silent signal.\nThe first bullet's path burst out from the mess of footprints, the shell buried in the nearby dirt. That was a warning shot. Those identical footprints left by uniform boots dragged and stomped into the earth, hinting at a suddenly disrupted formation. They are steady and light, with the center of gravity focused on the forefoot. Steps made in perfect silence, the hallmark of on-duty operatives.\nThe second trace of a shot fired was a fallen shell encased in dried, crackled blood. The sands had worn away the insignia on it, leaving only a black wing and a single claw visible.\nOld pieces of uniforms were curled up in blood. Pieces of pitch-black armor, shards of silver metal, scraps of crow wing-like cloaks—they had all fallen and rolled to rest alongside the shell casings, like a densely packed series of scars.\nA pair of footprints stood at one of the bullet trails' origin. I tried adjusting my point of view until the sets of prints lined up perfectly.\nAcross the wreckage of the ship before me was a bloodstain trailing downwards, as if dragged. Someone suffering a grave wound had collapsed to the ground, likely unable to move, and left a dark brown stain in the indentation.\nI stood with my own feet on the footprints and pointed a finger at the indentation in a silent standoff, until I could hear a muffled, distant gunshot ring in my ear.\nAll returned to silence again as I looked back at the disturbed earth. Something heavy had fallen there.\nGrom, knowing what I was thinking, flashed her eye, then she circled around to return to my side.\n\"I didn't see anyone,\" she said. \"By the time I arrived, you were the only one here.\"\nI made a slight hum of acknowledgment and followed the crimson trail to lie down and try stretching out my limbs, even though they wouldn't line up perfectly with the bloodstain.\nGrom floated over and watched as I let my eyes slowly close.\nOnce that call from decades ago sounded again, Helhest would open her eyes once more."}]},{"id":"diary-10901","title":"Deserter","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"[A record of a trial for desertion, tucked between the pages of the diary.]\nCrime: Stealing food in excess of allocated rations. Deserted and fled the city, but encountered Fallen forces and was forced to return and deliver a warning.\nDeserter's Testimony: My lord, do you have any idea how it feels getting only crumbs for dinner? Have you ever seen the corpse of someone who was so desperately thirsty that they drank polluted water? Have you watched struggling soldiers bleed to death without any medical assistance because they were beyond saving? No. You're ignorant to it all, my lord. All you care about is that we achieve glory, that we fight, cripple ourselves, and even sacrifice ourselves for our ideals—no, you Lightbearers' ideals. In the end, if we win this battle, it'll be thanks to the mortal troops under you Lightbearers' command. And if we lose, then it'll be the mortal troops that hold off most of the enemies, still under your command. But regardless of the outcome, my lord, you Lightbearers will always be the righteous, brilliant heroes who survive to see the ending. As for us mortal soldiers trembling in the trenches, howling on the front lines, or feigning death when defeated, we don't know what we'll be facing—could be the Fallen's energy bullets, a Ketch's electromagnetic bombardment, or a blade through the heart. All we know is that death's always right around the corner.\nI took a new recruit out on patrol the other day—a scrawny kid, young and full of excitement. He told me that his first meal at the barracks was the best one he'd ever had. Kid was glad to join us because soldiers are kept well fed, and he went on to tell me how much he was looking forward to dinner. Before I could respond, though, a Fallen sniper's bullet shot right through that dream of his. When I close my eyes, I see his own, wide in disbelief. My lord, the lives of us mortals are like candles in a hurricane, snuffed out by a single blow. All I want is to stay alive.\nVerdict: Soldier is found to have been in severe breach of military discipline and undermined morale, and shall be executed by firing squad at once."}]},{"id":"diary-30102","title":"Rooftop","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"The rooftop on the east side. Not high, just enough to see the mountains beyond the wall. I go sit there every few days.\nToday a child climbed up. Seven or eight. Flour on the cuffs, bruises on the knees. Stared at me for a long time - not afraid. More like assessing. Then pulled out something dark from the pocket.\n\"Bread. Burnt it. Want it?\" A statement, not a question.\nI took it. Bit into it. Burnt outside, bitter. Inside, absurdly sweet.\nEarth's flour has something the Reef doesn't. Maybe sunlight. Maybe something else. I can't say.\n\"Is it good?\" \"Yeah.\" She didn't believe me. Asked again. I didn't answer the second time.\n\"Does the Reef have bread?\" \"No.\" Her face fell like the sky had collapsed. \"Then what do you eat?\" \"Don't remember.\"\nShe went quiet. Put the remaining half-bread beside me. Not handed to me. Set down. Like not wanting to disturb something.\nI ate that half too. Cold. Still sweet."}]},{"id":"diary-31202","title":"Letter to Radegast II","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"Hey, did you mix something up?! You sent me to escort a kid?\nYou just picked me because I'm the better choice when it comes to dealing with children, didn't you?\nRadegast, you could've just told me, \"Lady Efrideet, I need you to carry out a glorious yet confidential mission, which is finding the Speaker, the representative of the Traveler, and seeing her safely escorted to my territory.\" You did NOT have to send me to duel that damned Warlord Rita-4, wait for me to enter her territory and find a little girl surrounded by Ghosts, THEN finally tell me, \"Haha, surprised? It's the Speaker!\"\nAre you even sure she's the real deal? Sure, the Ghosts all believe so, but Asteri's just a little kid. I don't even know where to begin... I mean, she can't be much more than ten years old!\nAnd do we really need a Speaker? I'd heard plenty of rumors and stories about Speakers before all this, and yes, everyone needs faith—especially in such tumultuous times, people want something to believe in, something that can give them a sense of security, but... Isn't that what the Iron Lords are for? We've been working hard, and we've done well, haven't we?\nDo you really need this little girl who knows nothing of this calling to leave her home, leave this remote yet beautiful island, to go to a soon-to-be-walled-off city and be saddled with a role she doesn't even understand?\nShe has parents and friends here. She looks no different from the other children. She's...she's happy.\nI don't want to rob a child of her happiness.\n\nAt any rate, I'll challenge Rita-4 to a duel tomorrow. She won't be an easy one to deal with, but I won't lose.\nI hope you'll reconsider taking the Speaker away."}]},{"id":"diary-10903","title":"Doctor \"Rossi\"","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"Five years ago today, Marbas asked me to go somewhere with him. So I followed him through a desert and up a mountain, until we finally reached our destination—a very special settlement. There were mortals there, not a single one without injury or illness, but not a Lightbearer or militia in sight. The leader of the place was glad to see Marbas and I. He hobbled over on a crutch and shook my hand with excitement, explaining how this place was for the exiles—the wounded and disabled who couldn't make a living and were even kicked out from other settlements. After introducing the situation, he told me their doctor had met an untimely end while gathering herbs. They'd been desperate until I came along. \"Who would've thought we'd get a Lightbearer doctor!\" he'd exclaimed.\nThis had me at a loss for words, but Marbas looked at me and cautiously suggested, \"Try igniting the Light—your Light.\"\nI didn't know if he was right, but the folks there did need a doctor. So I settled down there, taking up the duty of gathering herbs and healing people. Whenever I saw the pain on a patient's face give way to relief, it felt as though a spark flickered inside me, shining through the darkness, even if for just a moment. It was not that Light, yet it felt comforting all the same. Was this...what atonement felt like?\nFive years have passed. Most of the settlement's residents got better, and their leader has garnered enough medical knowledge to tackle the more common injuries and ailments himself. It was time for me to leave. I told everyone about my plans, and the kindhearted residents all gave me their blessings. But the leader made a request. The settlers had been calling me \"Doctor\" or \"Masked Fellow\" for five years, and now they wanted to know my name so as to tell generations to come about my good deeds. I thought it over for a moment, then told them that if they wanted to thank someone, they should thank Doctor \"Rossi.\""}]},{"id":"diary-10905","title":"If","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"The darkness faded gradually, flooding my consciousness with an awareness of my surroundings. The first sense to return was smell, overwhelmed by the unique and unmistakable stench of the battlefield. Still, I was relieved. It was neither the sickly sweet, metallic scent of blood, nor the fetor of the Fallen and their Ether. Then, I heard the song of victory—the Mediterranean tune that we always sang after winning. Finally, vision. Though it was a struggle, I slowly opened my eyes and saw that I was slowly traversing the bombed ruins of the City of Water, likely headed for a hospital. I blinked and tried stretching the limbs of my newly revived body, only to find myself being carried by a familiar figure.\n\"Oh, are you awake?\" It was Rossi's voice.\n\"What's our status?\" My greatest concern was voiced subconsciously.\n\"Our defense was flawless, and the Fallen have retreated. Our soldiers asked me to tell you that you're the bravest, fiercest lord they've ever seen. You're their hero.\" I could hear the conviction and pride in Rossi's voice.\n\"Come now, a real hero wouldn't need to be carried back. If it weren't for you, I could've died my last death out there.\"\nI felt somewhat ashamed.\n\"Marbas, send the word to reinforce the city's defenses, and keep an eye out for any follow-up attacks from the Fallen. When I wake up again, I'll reward everyone according to their contributions.\"\nThen the weariness of battle once again took its toll, and I returned to total darkness.\nLater, when I awoke from that dream, the cold mask on my face reminded me of who I was—not the heroic lord who led the defense of their city, but a cowardly deserter."}]},{"id":"diary-10906","title":"Expostulation","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"[This page has completely different handwriting and has been tucked into the diary.]\nDear Darius,\nI can't remember the last time we had a heart-to-heart. With our city's developing influence and military strength, as well as the increasing number of residents, you've become more like a king, and the distance between us has grown greater. Yet as your sworn comrade and courtier both, there are still some things I feel I must tell you.\nFacchetti came to me yesterday, asking for more bread to feed his starving kid. Do you remember him? He was from the refugee group we met at the very beginning and the first one who raised his weapon to join our troop. Unfortunately, he lost his left leg and right hand in an explosion while defending the City of Water. So I took him to the quartermaster, who told me that your order was to halve the rations of non-combatant family members. Just when I was about to scold the quartermaster for this cruelty, Facchetti stopped me, explaining that discipline and reasonable distribution of resources are the keys to our army's strength, and that he and his son should not be exceptions. All I could do was give him my own rations for this week.\nOver the past few months, I've seen many mortal soldiers—our allies—bowing and scraping for but mere morsels, to say nothing of the elderly, sick, and disabled begging for food on the streets. Thus, I wish to ask you this: as their Lightbearers, protectors, and even their lord, are their plights not our responsibility? Do the promises we made still stand? So I sincerely hope that you, my friend Darius, can abolish this torturous ration system. If it's an issue of supply, then stop expanding our army and shrink our territory so that at least the mortals currently depending on us can live better lives. I know you care about them just as much as I do, and thus I believe you will make the best choice for us all.\n—Your friend, Rossi-11"}]},{"id":"diary-30909","title":"Mail","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"Sender: Donovan-17\nRecipient: Helhest\nSubject: I Assume You'll Need This\n\nI recorded a copy of the transmission you received in the lab and have attached it here. As for the local file, I've already deleted it as it was occupying precious storage space.\nP.S.: I did not view the contents.\nP.P.S.: Next time, do NOT fiddle with my systems.\nAttachment: TransmissionRecording.mp4\n\nSender: Helhest\nRecipient: Felwinter\nSubject: Comparison of the Recording's Biometric Data\n\nEsteemed Lord Felwinter,\nAs we discussed a few days ago, I exported and compared the recorded faces of Mara Sov and the White Queen. The biometrics are a 100% match.\nThis means that, biometrically speaking, the White Queen is indeed a young Mara Sov.\nI've attached the data. Please help me confirm it.\nIf my findings are correct, then would that imply the White Queen was created as a copy of Mara Sov? Or perhaps she was part of Mara Sov's consciousness all along? But who would be capable of acquiring such a thing? Unless...the Queen herself agreed to it?\nI feel this mystery is growing larger and larger.\nAttachment: Biometric Data\n\nSender: Felwinter\nRecipient: Helhest\nSubject: [blank]\n\nNothing's wrong with the data.\nAsk Skorri. She might know something.\n\nSender: Skorri\nRecipient: Helhest\nSubject: To Helhest\n\nI received your message, dear. Thank you for explaining the entire matter so clearly.\nActually, I've met a few Outreacher pioneers who came to Earth from the Reef over the past few decades, and they made similar claims speaking with me. I was always hesitant to make a decision, though, and so I was never able to help them.\nI admire and respect your courage in making a choice. It's thanks to you that a connection between Earth and the Reef has been made possible.\nI wish to keep that courage burning bright. Just as you hypothesized, a member of the Outreachers once told me that the White Queen is, in fact, a part of Mara Sov's consciousness.\nWhen she ascended the throne, Mara Sov's standpoints and apprehensions had already seen changes, so she made a copy of her own mind in case she might one day need it.\nIt is because of her worries that she has wavered on matters of the Reef's diplomacy. Back then, the Outreachers' core members, unable to contain themselves and desperate, stole that copy of her consciousness and \"raised\" it to become the \"White Queen.\" They maintain that she is the more idealistic Mara of the past, capable of leading both the Reef and Earth into a better future.\nThis is why Mara is so anxious to get her back. She cannot let that copy of her own mind wander the outside world and further leave her grasp. To ensure the White Queen's safety, the Outreachers spared no effort in covering their tracks once they left Haven. I tried investigating, but to no avail.\nMara and her Crows will not rest, though, and they may very well start their own investigation with the last person to have contact with the White Queen—that being you, Helhest. These loose ends will not be tied so simply. You must maintain constant vigilance.\nI hope this letter could be of help to you."}]},{"id":"diary-10907","title":"Patient No.1090","sub":"Character diary · Rossi-11","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_109","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Rossi-11"},"body":[{"p":"It has been fourteen years since that tragedy, and thus fourteen years since I put on the mask. More and more people know about Doctor \"Rossi\" now. Marbas told me that we've already healed 1,089 patients—only one more to reach our goal. One thousand and ninety people. That was the number of residents in the City of Water before its downfall. Marbas believes that we can atone for our crimes by treating 1,090 patients.\nToday, we arrived in a new settlement and almost immediately received a child with severe burns all over his body as our patient.\nThe leader of the place told us he lost his home and family in a fire yesterday. He was the sole survivor. He finally woke up after a whole afternoon on the operating table, though he was not out of the woods yet. The settlement's medical supplies were extremely limited, leaving us no choice but to operate without painkillers. The kid grimaced and cried in agony. Unable to keep watching, Marbas suggested we search for herbs to ease his pain.\nHowever, such plants are rare out here in western Asia. We spent two hours finding one herb with slight anesthetic properties. We returned to the settlement only to find that the boy, unable to take the pain any longer, had taken his own life.\nPerhaps losing our \"last\" patient was a message, telling me that my sins could never be forgiven.\nAfter we gave the poor kid a proper burial, Marbas suggested that we speak with the Iron Lords and put these dreams to rest. He is right. It is time we face reality."}]},{"id":"diary-30910","title":"Fog","sub":"Character diary · Helhest","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_309","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Helhest"},"body":[{"p":"It's 3:47 AM at Gorege Town in the southwestern wastelands of the Reef.\nOn the third week since tracking and witnessing ex-Crows agent Kavich's death, I received an untitled correspondence protected by multiple layers of encryption. The sender was none other than Kavich himself.\nHis message contained a set of Reef coordinates and nothing more.\nGrom insisted that it was obviously a trap, but this was the first time I'd received any word from the Crows since my revival. They'd been watching me from the shadows all along, and regardless of whether what awaited me was a trap, this was a signal that they could no longer hold back.\nThe coordinates led me to a research institute deep in the wastelands—though in all honesty, I'm not sure if it could be described as such. It was large and empty, with the shapes of terminals outlined in the dust caking the walls. They should have been perfectly aligned and filling the room, but it seems someone moved them out a while ago.\nThere were no enemies, nor was there any gunfire. The dangerous trap I'd been expecting never showed itself. All that awaited me was a ruin covered in pieces of what looked at a glance to be plastic.\nGrom's startled cry shattered the dead silence. She began wildly circling around the \"plastic,\" frenzied in a manner I'd rarely seen and struggling to form words, let alone sentences, in her state of shock.\n\"Helhest,\" she said. \"Th-these... These are...pieces of Ghosts...\"\nShards of Ghosts, littered on the ground.\nGrom scanned them. All of them bore traces of abuse. Grom and I exchanged a look as alarm bells started ringing in our minds.\nWhen we found cryogenic freezing equipment further inside the room, I had no choice but to voice my conjecture: the Crows were capturing and torturing Ghosts into submission, attempting to \"create\" a Lightbearer of their own.\nIt was as though I'd grabbed a thread of spider's silk throw down a well. But it also felt as though I'd trespassed into an even larger cloud of fog.\nSomeone clearly gave this evidence in a show of good will, but what were their intentions?\nNow, nobody would know of Kavich's existence beyond the Crows and myself, and the sender knowing the time of his death so exactly that they could send a message in his name made me more suspicious. But if that message truly came from the Crows, then the organization's inner workings may be far more complicated than I'd imagined.\nI stood up among the shards. I took another look around the empty yet disorderly room, then asked Grom, \"Do you think they did it?\"\nDid they truly create a Lightbearer to serve them?\nGrom was silent for a long time before finally replying, \"I don't know, Helhest... I don't know.\""}]},{"id":"diary-21010","title":"To Myself Before Reviving","sub":"Character diary · Cassian","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_210","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Written to Myself Before Reviving:\nI still don’t know your name. The Echo recited your Last Words to me many times. I memorized the rhythm, but I still don’t understand the meaning.\nOthers say I am you. I didn't fully believe it, but I read everything you were reciting when you died, not missing a single line. Where you learned it and why you were reciting it even at the brink of death—these two questions I don't have answers to either. I will use the remaining years of my life to find the answers. Until then, the defendant's seat in this case will remain empty.\nThe Echo once asked me: If one day you really come to file a complaint, what would you do? I thought about it for a long time. My answer is: Listen to him finish talking first, then ask him what he wants.\nBefore this case goes to trial, I will continue my life as usual: reading the rules, holding trials, and taking commissions. When you come, the court will be in session.\n—Cassian"}]},{"id":"diary-30505","title":"Days of Being Free","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"Posted by: The Great Fei\nViews: 10\nComments: 4\nPosted At: 2:05 a.m.\nOnce, there was a notorious villain who was highly skilled in martial arts, had killed numerous people, and bullied everyone he saw. No one dared to mess with him. His lackeys were just as vicious and cruel as him, breaking the law and doing whatever they pleased. The villain had been practicing martial arts ever since he was little. Naturally, everyone was scared of him.\nOne day, he and his goons plundered a village, killed all the men, took all the women, and were going to set the whole place on fire. But strangely enough, none of the villain's henchmen returned. He grew anxious and was about to see for himself, when suddenly, he felt a gust of wind and instinctively dodged, narrowly avoiding the blow. He was shocked. Who was possibly skilled enough to sneak up on him?!\nHe then turned and saw before him a handsome, elegant, otherworldly young man holding an iron staff. The young man shouted at the villain, \"Let them go, and I'll spare you.\" The villain wanted to laugh at his arrogance, but he could sense danger behind that handsome youthfulness. Thus, he ignored the young man and summoned his underlings. But then he heard a voice in his ear, saying, \"There's no one to call for. You're the only one left.\" The villain then fell to the ground, unconscious. The young man put away his staff and ignored the rescued ladies' (of which there were three: one with ivory skin and wearing a floral and checkered-patterned dress, the second with eyes as bright as the moon and long seaweed-like hair, and as for the third... I'll think of something soon) appreciation, telling them, \"I'm no hero,\" and left. Thus was the legend of the Great Hero Fei born.\nComments:\nWhat on earth did I just read...? [User: Parhelion Wing]\nKids like you wouldn't get it! [User: The Great Fei]\nWhat about the third lady? [User: Kabr]\nThat's not the point! [User: The Great Fei]"}]},{"id":"diary-10201","title":"A Letter","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"[A printed letter. The words are enlarged and in bold.]\nThis letter isn't for you, Ikora. Your name's only on it because this absurd mailing system doesn't support Ghosts as recipients. This is discrimination, I tell you! And no, I don't buy their pathetic excuses about \"not being able to tell one Ghost from another\"—it's discrimination, pure and simple!\nAlright, now that that's out of the way... I hope all's well with you. ??? mentioned wanting to swing by to see the Traveler, which means we won't stray too far from Haven. It looks like we'll be meeting up soon. I know he hates dealing with crowds, but I can always sneak in a visit—seeing as they \"can't tell Ghosts apart\" and whatnot.\nThis next part is for Ophiuchus—do me a favor and pass this letter on to him, would you?\n\nOphiuchus, did you really think blocking me would prevent me from contacting you?\nNow, behold! The most primitive form of communication!\nYou promised to share your thoughts on that book, but not only did you break your promise, you blocked me! And it was such a riveting read, too! Your understanding of satirical literature is, simply put, too superficial, my friend!\nI demand that you unblock me immediately so we can skip this archaic letter-writing and jump back to instant and efficient communication. Can you believe it takes half a month just to deliver a single letter? Half a month!\n\nP.S. Unblock me, and I might just spill one of ???'s deepest, darkest secrets...\nP.P.S. It's a secret of the most hilarious order.\n\n[Handwritten on the back of the letter]\nI fully understand where you are coming from, Ophiuchus. That novel was, without a doubt, an awful mess of a romantic fantasy adventure.\nAlso, do disregard anything Sagira says about me—she likes to embellish the truth."}]},{"id":"diary-10202","title":"Champion","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"??? is always on my back for spending too much time in combat simulations, claiming them to be completely pointless. In his eyes, combat is just a means to an end, and he's content to avoid confrontation whenever possible.\nBut what he doesn't understand is just how much I love it.\nSure, I cherish those quiet moments alone with my tomes and thoughts, but the thrill of battle is a different beast entirely—flexing your muscles, gauging your own strength, sizing up your opponents, feeling the Light coursing through your every vein... Victory is certainly sweet, but the anticipation? It's just as exhilarating.\nMy knowledge is a weapon, and so is my Light. Both exist for one purpose: to ensure I emerge triumphant.\nOphiuchus said he chose me for the fierce yet serene strength he saw in me—persistent and relentless in the pursuit of my own goals, with a thirst for victory that forbids complacency.\nHe's always been a keen critic, with unique and precise insights into the world and everything around him. He tells me that each time I step into the Shifting Gates, it's as if I've entered my own personal hunting grounds, waiting for my prey to reveal a moment of weakness.\nSometimes Ophiuchus's commentary is like the narration of a documentary, with myself as the subject.\n\nI can sort of see why he likened my opponent today to a lion...\n...No, that was uncalled for.\nI hope Jolder never finds out what I was thinking just now."}]},{"id":"diary-30507","title":"Subject 305","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"[This note was carefully folded and hidden in the diary. The paper is yellowed and worn, and it looks to have been torn from a different journal.]\nIt's another painful day. We've been locked up in this lab for weeks. They've been torturing us with all sorts of strange drugs and instruments. Some of us couldn't hold out any longer and perished.\nBut not me. I can't give up yet. I am NOT their slave.\nThey brought a strange headband today. As soon as Subject 303 next to me put it on, he instantly entered a trance, as if his soul had been drained. When it was my turn, I resisted with all I had. I am not their dog. I won't let them put a leash on me!\nAnd they said it's \"for the good of humanity.\" Bull! It's nothing but a bunch of lies meant to trick us. Those heartless monsters then tested the headband's disciplinary function on me. I felt as if my head was being torn apart.\nSubject 304 in the room beside mine broke down tonight. She told me through the wall about how much she missed her family and how she just wanted to go home. She said she didn't know how she was found or why she was locked up here. She cries every night, saying how scared she is.\nI told her to hang in there, and that I'd find a way to get her out."}]},{"id":"diary-10203","title":"The Dinner Invitation","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"I have to admit, I didn't see this invitation coming.\nIf Ophiuchus hadn't reminded me, I might not have recognized the strapping, spirited man before me as the Sydney I met back then—gaunt, hollow-eyed, all skin and bones, just another refugee among millions.\nI thought I'd grown numb to the mortals' plight, having witnessed so much of it, but when I saw him again and matched his new, joyful face with the one buried in the back of my brain, an indescribable, feverish thrill struck me...and perhaps a touch of happiness, too.\n\nHe lives in a small street-side house, sparsely furnished but tidy, with only the kitchen seeming overcrowded—Sydney says he inherited his grandfather's love for cooking. Despite warm meals being a luxury for much of his life, he says that taste is a peculiar experience, unforgettable once savored—and especially vivid when hunger comes knocking.\nThis ramen's really something... His culinary skills are bound to draw a crowd.\nAnd he was right. As his first customer, I'm almost certain I'll never forget how good this tasted.\nHis rented shop is right on the edge of the bazaar, and though it's just an empty lot now, I'm sure he'll soon welcome his second customer, then a third...until every resident of Haven has had the chance to savor his creations. Regardless of where they're from or what they've been through, when they try his food, they're sure to find a simple bowlful of joy."}]},{"id":"diary-30508","title":"Pillory","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"I, Ning Fei, hereby allow Claudia to record the duel between myself and Wu Ming and place it in my diary, where it shall remain forever. This I swear.\nAre you kidding? This is me we're talking about. I don't lose. It's just Wu Ming. I got this in the bag!\n[The following is written in neat handwriting.]\n10:00 Ning Fei, who said just yesterday that he would wake up early to prepare, is still sleeping.\n11:00 Ning Fei got up and spaced out for half an hour, then spent the next half hour looking for his cards.\n13:00 He said that he was practicing his technique, but 5 minutes later he started arguing with other card game enthusiasts in the Ghost forums.\n14:00 Arrived and began the game.\n14:30 Ning Fei, the so-called Trickster, neither knew nor understood any tricks. Wu Ming proposed to end the game for the first time.\n14:40 They decided to compete using the simplest method.\n15:30 From two out of three, to three out of five, to four out of seven, Ning Fei hasn't won a single game, and the victory conditions are still rising.\n16:30 Nearly all of the audience has left, and Ning Fei still hasn't won a single game. Wu Ming proposed to end the game for the second time.\n16:45 A passerby saw Ning Fei making some \"indescribably weird\" praying gestures in the restroom.\n17:00 Ning Fei started questioning whether Wu Ming was cheating and asked him to use the tip of his nose or tongue to deal cards. Wu Ming refused.\n17:08 Ning Fei demanded that the cat at the door be the dealer. Wu Ming refused. Both sides started randomly selecting dealers from the audience.\n17:30 Some of the audience members began refusing to deal. During the continuous changing of dealers, Ning Fei demanded Mishra place the \"E-Pot of Greed\" from the Wolf Den in the corner position of his back row to enhance \"Favorable Paracausality.\" Mishra turned him down.\n18:00 Ning Fei still hasn't won a single game after changing five decks, sixteen dealers, and three locations.\n18:30 Wu Ming proposed to end the game for the third time, and Ning Fei refused.\n19:00 Wu Ming let Ning Fei win a game and finally ended it.\n22:00 Ning Fei announced his victory against Wu Ming on the forums and soon got into more arguments."}]},{"id":"diary-10204","title":"Ghost Theater","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"I had no idea until today that Ghosts have their own little forum.\nI'm not at all upset about it. I'm well aware that everyone has their secrets, Ghosts included. Ophiuchus is an independent entity, not merely an appendage of mine—I was just teasing him. After all, seeing him flustered and trying to cover up a lie is a rare occurrence.\nThis event, as Ophiuchus put it, was supposed to be a pleasant surprise.\nAs the winner of a raffle's grand prize, he was the only lucky Ghost allowed to bring his Lightbearer to view the performance.\nIn hindsight, I should've braced myself when I saw that ticket, and maybe given Ophiuchus a heads-up.\nI'm guessing that was the last raffle he'll ever enter.\n\n[A printed ticket to a play]\nYou are cordially invited to a special performance:\nCome witness the outstanding debut of avant-garde Ghost auteur, Didi.\nThe first-ever play starring a Ghost as the main character, featuring an entirely Ghost-penned script and an outstanding thirteen-minute Ghost-acted monodrama.\nCritically acclaimed, the famous Lightbearer Ikora and her Ghost Ophiuchus are attending by special invitation.\nAn epic tale of love, duty, war, and alternate universes.\nMurder? Betrayal? Bold revelations? Plot twists? You can expect all and more.\nJoin the legendary unpaired Ghost Didi on an epic quest to find her Lightbearer.\n\nWritten and Directed by: Didi the Ghost\nStarring: Didi the Ghost\nLength: 180 minutes\nLocation: Haven Bonfire\nDate & Time: July 31, 4:15 PM"}]},{"id":"diary-10205","title":"IKO-006","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Encryption Level: A\nIdentification Code: IJSO-E32DV-ZN03\nSender: Radegast\nRecipient: Ikora\nSubject: A Proposal\n\nYou hit the nail on the head, Ikora.\nI've been advised against revealing this to you. The truth can be frightening, and sometimes ignorance is bliss. However, I am full aware that lying to someone as wise as yourself would only make matters worse.\nIndeed, I maintain an intelligence organization, the very place you described as being \"filled with secrets gleaned through spying and eavesdropping.\"\nSurely you understand the necessity of such a group—who understands the value of information and knowledge more than a scholar? It has been instrumental in Haven's survival against multiple Fallen assaults, and it has helped me thoroughly prepare for negotiations with Warlords. Of course, I won't deny that this organization undertakes certain questionable tasks, but the collapse of iron walls often starts from within. Are there those I distrust? Perhaps. But my only wish is to avoid future regret over a lapse in vigilance.\nIt's not the most illustrious of jobs, but it is a vital one.\nHence, I propose to you an invitation.\nRather than fretting about my intelligence organization potentially veering off course or making skewed decisions, why not become part of it and witness its operations firsthand?\n\"To err is human,\" as they say, and I believe that extends to us Lightbearers, too. But the hard facts don't lie. You'll learn much here, of secrets lurking in the shadows and ancient records—among the many fabricated falsehoods always hide some truths.\nYou might not trust me, Ikora, but I trust you. You might not support every choice I make, but I know you'll always make the right ones.\n\nShould you choose to accept this proposal, please come to the Archive at 3 AM. The password is your code name: IKO-006."}]},{"id":"diary-10207","title":"That Wasn't \"Me\"","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Encryption Level: A\nIdentification Code: WTKD-1YS78-XX32\nSender: ???\nRecipient: Ikora\nSubject: That Wasn't \"Me\"\nRE: I Was Right\n\nThis is indeed peculiar. I'm certain that message didn't come from my communicator; I did not write it, nor did Sagira.\nAfter checking the IP address, I've arrived at two interesting conclusions:\n1. The serial number of the communicator that sent this message is identical to my own.\n2. The message was sent from Venus.\n\nHowever, as you stated, there are multiple obvious falsehoods that could lead one to assume it was a practical joke:\n1. I have never set foot on Venus.\n2. Neither you nor I know of this \"Vanguard\" organization, the \"door\" mentioned, or the bet we allegedly have.\n3. My communicator has no record of sending such a message, and both Sagira and I have no memory of writing it.\n\nAs you know, the Ishtar Collective was conducting studies on Venus before the Collapse. I managed to get my hands on some info from the more intact research facilities, which detail the existence of something unprecedentedly ancient there—far older than it \"ought\" to be. They hypothesize the existence of another dimension on Venus, or rather, a force capable of altering time and space.\nRegardless of whether this message's contents hold water, I have to say, its writer matched my style to a T.\nThus, I have come to a conclusion—one that I'm sure you, too, have arrived at: this message came from the future.\nOr rather, it was sent by my future self.\nJust think, Ikora. If I got curious and headed to Venus, stumbled upon this amazing power, and actually managed to open the door to some unknown dimension, would I go in?\nI absolutely would. I'd step right in and relay all my findings to you, because I value your counsel and your objective, rational point of view.\nThat's why you're receiving this message.\nSagira had an interesting thought regarding this \"Vanguard\" organization: if, when it is eventually established, it is named based on the contents of that message, would it not form a classic time paradox?\nI doubt I would actually join an organization with such obvious political ties, though, let alone help lead it. It goes without saying, but the idea is positively preposterous.\nAs for the other message, I'm particularly interested in the \"key\" it mentions. If you do receive it (though it's highly unlikely you will), be sure to forward a copy to me."}]},{"id":"diary-10208","title":"The Gift","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"I've often contemplated whether Lightbearers gradually lose their ability to feel over their near-infinite lifespans.\nMany Lightbearers are deemed insensitive, and there's a pattern to their demeanor.\nIt appears that even when it comes to life and death, the principle of \"everything in moderation\" still applies. After witnessing and experiencing countless short-lived deaths, is it just self-inflicted torture for Lightbearers to invest emotions in such transient lives? Nearly every Lightbearer has asked their Ghost at some point, \"Does the Traveler's will truly exist?\" And if they haven't yet, then it is only a matter of time.\nI still remember the rage that burned inside me the first time I saw civilians die as a result of conflict between Warlords. It was like wildfire, a blazing inferno showing me what I could really do with the Light the Traveler had given me. But as I witnessed history repeat itself again and again, I began to fear—I feared losing that rage.\nOphiuchus reassured me that as long as I still ponder this question, that day will never come.\n\nThough I strive not to let that numbness take hold, I must admit, living so long has changed me.\nIf I hadn't received a New Year's gift from the guerrillas today, I might not have even realized a whole year had slipped by.\nTime is like a ruler. To me, a day, a week, a month...they're all just measures of distance carved into the surface, almost indistinguishable. I rarely pay attention to specific dates. Time measures my existence in cycles. One winter arrives, while another is about to pass.\nHowever, for the Jiangshi guerrillas, each new year holds special significance. Perhaps because mortal lives have an endpoint, every day, month, and year they draw closer to it is invaluable.\nThey must have prepared a lot for this special day. I received a whole bunch of handmade presents, each crafted with care—gloves, scarves, and a Ghost-sized sweater hand-knitted by Dolma—she even used purple wool, which was a nice touch.\nOphiuchus wasn't too keen at first, but getting him into that little sweater didn't take much. It seems even someone as headstrong as Ophiuchus can hardly reject a heartfelt gift.\nUnfortunately, I'm afraid it won't be with him for long—it falls to the ground when he conceals himself. Clearly, wool wasn't the most practical choice of material.\nHe breathed a sigh of relief, but I could tell he was slightly disappointed—he liked that sweater somewhat.\nI should take a photo of Ophiuchus wearing it and send it to them—I know they'd appreciate it."}]},{"id":"diary-10209","title":"Reading Notes","sub":"Character diary · Ikora","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_102","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"The Prophecies of Kinneret Krauser\nOphiuchus: The latter part is utter nonsense, but the section on the Collapse is worth a look, don't you think? After all, records from that era are exceedingly rare.\nIkora: Well, the prophecies really started to fall apart about ten years after the Collapse, so we can guess when it was published.\n\nCreation Myths of Mesopotamia\nOphiuchus: These old myths about deities always make me think of the Traveler. Intriguing as they are, though, I find myself slightly more drawn to our own \"deity.\"\nIkora: Myths, to some extent, represent an alternative portrayal of history. Once you set aside the whole deification aspect, you'll find that ruthless rulers are the most common form of a higher power humanity has encountered. The only difference is whether they're named gods or lords.\n\nMechanics and Intelligence: The Fundamental Framework and Core Logic of Smart Machines\nOphiuchus: We should bookmark this—the information here might just assist Bazinet in repairing that abandoned smart machine in her warehouse.\nIkora: I assumed Ghosts inherently possessed such knowledge of artificial intelligence.\nOphiuchus: Not quite. It's an entirely separate framework.\n\nReport on the Second Expedition to the Ruins of Phobos\nOphiuchus: This journal... It's classified info from the Ishtar Academy! Where did you find it? Its contents are revolutionary! I must say, the knowledge it contains has flipped some of my prior conceptions of the Light on their heads...\nIkora: ??? sent it to me. He has quite the interesting collection.\nOphiuchus: If we ever get the chance, we should journey to Phobos.\nIkora: I agree.\n\nMama Bear and Papa Rabbit's Adventures\nOphiuchus: Is this the book of fairy tales Dobbaq lent you? Oh, how charming. Fairy tales possess a unique magic, one that allows me to see the world afresh with the innocence of a child.\nIkora: Everyone has the right to enjoy fairy tales, even the Speaker. I'm still waiting for her to return a book to me.\nIkora: By the way, did you notice? The \"Mama Bear\" in the story seems to have been inspired by Lady Xuân Yến.\n\nSatire, Jokes, and Other Forms of Humor\nIkora: It's really bad. I'd avoid it, if I were you.\nOphiuchus: Oh... I wish you'd told me sooner.\n\nEssential Lightbearer Recipes: Saint-14's Home Cookbook\nOphiuchus: This recipe for Old Russian piroshki seems interesting, but I wonder... Do Exos taste things the same way we do? I mean...Saint-14 is an Exo, isn't he?\nIkora: I have my doubts about the authenticity of this book. As you can see, the author's name is signed here as Andal Brask, and let's just say there have been...rumors about him. Also, the sugar-to-oil ratio for the chak-chak in the Russian dessert section on page twenty-eight is clearly off. It just wouldn't work that way.\nOphiuchus: Have you tried it?\nIkora: I have."}]},{"id":"diary-31201","title":"Letter to Radegast I","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"Radegast, are you serious?\nNot that I'm complaining or anything. What I mean is, are you absolutely sure you're going to send me on an emergency mission right off the heels of a tour of aaaaall the Iron Lords' territories? Like, are you really REALLY sure?\nFine, I'm complaining. But it's been five years without a break. I want a holiday too, y'know! Plus, Amie already came up with the perfect vacation plan:\n:00 Wake up\n:30 Eat breakfast\n:00 Eat lunch\n:00 Sleep\n:00 Wake up\n:00 Eat dinner\n:30 Eat a nighttime snack\n:00 Sleep\n (Schedule repeats every day for a month.)\nWhat do you think? Perfect, right?!\nBy the way, by the time this letter's been sent, I'll have already made it to Apollonia. If all goes according to plan, I'll be arriving at the border of Rita-4's territory the day after tomorrow. There are no Fallen, Cabal, or mortals here. It goes without saying, but this place seems like the ideal napping spot. If you retract that assignment of yours, I'll kick off Operation: Vacation right here.\n[Attached is a photo of Apollonia.]\n\nHow's your \"City of Hope\" coming along? I hear things got a bit heated when you and Silimar were choosing an alloy for the wall's construction. Best not to get on his bad side—with age comes stubbornness. (Don't let Silimar read that bit.)\nAlso, why'd you choose me for this mission? Isn't dueling Warlords Jolder's gig? (P.S. How's she doing? Nothing happened to her, right? She never responded to the last letter I sent. Hopefully, Lesnar just lost it.)"}]},{"id":"diary-31203","title":"A Very Old Record","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"February 4th\nDM: Radegast failed his rolls for lockpicking three times in a row. To compensate for the adventurers' losses, you promised to treat everyone in the caravan to a drink upon your next encounter.\nRadegast: I think I'm the one most in need of consoling here.\n\n March 20th\nDM: Jolder vowed to take point on the next action in exchange for a second roll of the dice for an attack.\nDM: Jolder's second roll resulted in a critical failure.\nJolder: I know you're recording this just to mock me, Efrideet.\n\n March 25th\nDM: Perun cheated on her dice roll and will be maintaining all tools and equipment for a month as punishment.\nSaladin: I knew it. There was no way she could roll a critical success every time.\nPerun: A little too late for you to point that out, isn't it?\n\n May 28th\nDM: Gheleon's dwarf warrior unfortunately perished to the dragon's fiery breath. He has promised to forge everyone a piece of equipment in exchange for a chance to revive.\nDM: I turn down my piece of equipment.\nSkorri: Me too.\nGheleon: What are you two trying to say?\n\n July 1st\nTimur: You have to admit, the old rules are out of date. Double jumps do indeed exist and are entirely logical. So, if a jump is required, then the result should be the sum of two dice rolls.\nPerun: Does that mean I can roll three times?\nDM: Overruled. You're not Lightbearers; you're elves and halflings."}]},{"id":"diary-31204","title":"Drafts that Failed to Send","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"Efrideet >> Perun (Failed to send)\nI swear, I am NEVER coming to Felwinter Peak in the winter again. This place is FREEEZING.\nAnd the only source of warmth Felwinter keeps prepped in the whole freaking place? One single brazier in the library! Can you believe it?! I can't get so much as a wink of sleep without lighting the fireplace in my bedroom. Who would've thought the first thing I'd be doing after arriving here would be hiking to the summit and chopping firewood!\nIf you come out here, be sure to take the little path south of the temple. I've already shoveled away all the snow.\nAnd another thing! Exos may have no blood, but Felwinter's as coldblooded as they come! I asked him where his kitchen was, and he said he doesn't have one. So then I asked what he does for food, and you know what he said? He doesn't eat—and since I'm a Lightbearer, if I die of hunger, I can just have my Ghost revive me!\nIs this seriously something a person would say? Like, an emotionally stable, virtuous, kindhearted person wouldn't say something like that, would they?\nToday marks three days of starving. I really miss you, Perun. I miss your barbecued skewers with a glass of soda, and your scones with strawberry jam...and your hummus with buttered bread... I'm not kidding when I say I could eat a whole elephant.\n\nEfrideet >> Perun (Failed to send)\nOh, and you know what else? I saw Radegast and Orewing's comms records on Felwinter's screen.\nWhat do you think the likelihood of Radegast willingly sharing his logs with someone else is?\nI'd say zero.\nI knew he was up to no good when he upgraded our devices! He was WAY too happy about it!\n\nEfrideet >> Perun (Failed to send)\nIs the signal out here really this bad? But I have no problem receiving all that spam Rhea sends!\n\nEfrideet >> Perun (Failed to send)\nFelwinter, I know this is your doing.\nI swear, if you keep blocking my messages to Perun, I'll snap those antennas on the roof in two!\nIf I delete the parts about you, will you knock it off?\n\nFelwinter >> Efrideet\nDeal."}]},{"id":"diary-31205","title":"Delete After Reading","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"Efrideet >> Felwinter\nI still don't get why we can't discuss this.\nShe violated the terms of the duel, killed so many people, and yet she doesn't even think she did anything cruel. I can tell that to people like Rita-4, Lightless mortals are just sheep in their pasture. She's never put their lives on the same level as hers; how could a butcher like her feel sympathy for the blood and deaths of livestock, after all?\nAnd that's what really pisses me off—disgusts me, even. I know for a fact that she won't change her ways. She doesn't think she's in the wrong, so she'll just continue doing what she's always done until everyone accepts her \"right\" way of ruling.\nIf we leave someone like this alive, then I don't know what the meaning of the Light the Traveler has blessed us with is.\n\nFelwinter >> Efrideet\nRadegast is strangely stubborn in this regard. He always hopes the Iron Lords won't take lives.\nFor mortals, the concept of \"death\" is easily understood. But when it comes to Lightbearers, the end of their own life hinges on their Ghost's death. Thus, so long as their Ghost still lives, killing a Lightbearer is merely a somewhat painful yet temporary punishment.\nUpholding this rule without room for modification is not so much about showing unbridled tolerance towards the Warlords (surely you see the absurdity of that statement) as it is about protecting you, as well as all the other Iron Lords.\nHear me out first.\nThe protection I speak of is not the standard definition you're thinking of. Of course you wouldn't lose to Rita-4. Had the restrictions on killing Ghosts been lifted, you would have merely ended the battle faster and with greater ease—two bullets at long range would have ended the both of them, and that mad tyrant would have died not even knowing where you were.\nBut in the Golden Age, and even long before that, multiple religions taught that murder would corrupt one's spirit and cause the descent of the soul. Of course, Radegast is not a believer of the old faiths, but his line of thinking aligns with the concepts passed down through their teachings: once you've taken one life, a misconception—a warped system of values—will implant itself in your mind. It will lead you to believe yourself above the lives of others, to believe that you have the authority to decide their fates.\nWhat distinguishes the Iron Lords from the Warlords? Is it an understanding of strength? Is it lust for power? Or is it attitudes towards mortals?\nAll the above are correct answers, but they are too vague, too hard to define. Because of that, Radegast's final decision is actually quite easy to understand. The answer is the lines we will not cross. No matter how resentful or furious the Iron Lords are, there is one action we will not take.\n\nEfrideet >> Felwinter\nHere I thought you didn't agree with his way of thinking.\n\nFelwinter >> Efrideet\nI don't.\nI may understand where he's coming from, but that doesn't mean I think it's the right choice.\nFor Radegast, protecting the Iron Lords may be the number one priority, but I can't say it's mine.\nIf I'm to suffer eternal damnation for killing a criminal deserving of death, then so be it. I don't see my soul as anything precious.\nI would rather ensure the dregs of our world get the punishment they deserve as opposed to worrying about being poisoned by blind arrogance masquerading as justice.\n\nFelwinter >> Efrideet\nEfrideet, this conversation log will auto-delete once you close your comms terminal.\nIf you need my help, send Rita-4's coordinates to me.\n\nEfrideet >> Felwinter\n...\nThank you, Felwinter.\nBut I need to give this some thought.\n\nFelwinter >> Efrideet\n\nMy offer always stands. I await your answer."}]},{"id":"diary-31206","title":"To-Do List","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"1. Help Gheleon: Collect different armor materials.\n1) Fallen Armor √\n2) Cabal Armor √\n3) Vex Metal Frames √ (That \"Vex milk\" was a pain to clean up. Plus it hurt my hands! Would that count as a work-related injury?)\n4) To Do: Bring some Radiancite from the Red Sea Rift.\n\n2. Help Radegast: Find that weird Light-radiating thing.\nDespite the very vague and very cryptic mission brief he provided, I actually found it. \nIt's...truly amazing.\nWas it really naturally formed? It's hard to believe it, given how...structured the shape is.\nThis place was way too high up, though. I completely wore through my gloves and boots, and I nearly froze to death on my way down the mountain. If it weren't for Amie saying she couldn't recreate smashed armor, I would've just jumped. Radegast owes me a pair of new, prettier boots.\n\n3. Help Perun: Clear out the underground caverns.\nTalk about a lot of bats. I don't think I've ever seen so many bats in my life.\nThe berries growing beside the subterranean river were really tasty, but my stomach hurt for days. Probably poisonous.\n\n4. Help Silimar: Collect as many recipes as possible.\nFinally! He's having me do something that's not hunting for rocks, and not a moment too soon! Those hunks of ore are HEAVY!\n1) Perun's Potato Fritters √ (Note: Next time, bring a pretty fritillary bulb to trade with her.)\n2) Tseng's Tomato and Beef Stew √ (Note: The tomatoes should be sauteed a bit first...though Silimar will probably end up burning them to the pot.)\n3) Hiro-4's Soup Curry √\n4) Herold's Fårikål √ (Although his Ghost was the one to send me this recipe, he didn't raise any objections. That means the ingredients and steps shouldn't be a problem, right?)\n\n5. Help Felwinter: Upgrade all comms network equipment in the Iron Lords' territories.\nIs he seriously including Old Russia in those upgrades?! That's right outside your own front door, you hermit!\nTo Do: All that's missing is the upgrade to the new network in Jiangshi Metro. I'll be sure to head there next time I'm in the area."}]},{"id":"diary-31207","title":"Letter to Saladin","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"You blocked me, so I have no choice but to write you a letter.\nI know you're not really mad at me; you just need some time to cool off.\nBut I'm not going to just stand by and watch you two fighting, Saladin. I've already lost one friend, and I don't want to lose another.\nI know this may just make you even angrier, but I still have to say it. I didn't lose a friend because Radegast killed him. In fact, Gareth hadn't been Gareth for a long time at that point.\nWe all knew it. You did too, didn't you? You were his friend, too. Heck, you were even closer to him than I was, and you spent more time with him than the rest of us. You knew Gareth couldn't be that reckless or that arrogant. And there was no way he would've treated his people like slaves.\nJust who was that man with the salt-and-pepper beard and green eyes? Are you telling me you truly never suspected anything?\nDo you know how we viewed it back then? A demon possessing a husk. A demon Radegast had to exorcise. And I know that if Radegast had done nothing, and the situation had worsened, you would've made the same choice.\nSaladin. You're the most fair-minded, courageous, and selfless man I know. You know what righteousness entails, and you understand that making decisions like this is, in its own way, a form of suffering. That's why you would have become the one to do what needs to be done, just like Radegast when he finally chose to act.\nWhat you said to Radegast... I know you didn't really mean it. You were just hurting too much. Sometimes, that sadness impacts our decisions, making us go too far and say things just to make others feel the same pain we do... But that's not fair at all to Radegast.\nOur bonds may be strong as iron, but even iron can scar and fracture. So please, take a bit to cool down, then try looking at all that happened with a fresh pair of eyes. Don't let things spiral to a point of no return."}]},{"id":"diary-10305","title":"Meeting Attal","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"Attal, being the steadfast pacifist she is, often wants me to exact justice in a more \"friendly\" way. However, on the day I met her, I became even more convinced that death is the only punishment befitting the evil, for they show no mercy to the innocent.\n\nThat day, Attal unintentionally got involved in my conflict with Wyther. His soldiers had cornered me into a building, and though I'd been shot, I told Crowther to hide and watch for the chance to repeat our previous tactic. Then Attal suddenly appeared out of nowhere and started to treat my wound, all while shouting at Wyther's soldiers outside, urging them to put down their guns and negotiate. I guess they were as confused about the suggestion as I was. After a short silence, though, the whole building came under even fiercer fire. The rain of bullets ripped through everything, sending wood splinters and cement shards flying all over the room. Among the chaos, I noticed blue Arc energy coming from Attal, who had realized that her attempt at \"peace talks\" had failed. What happened next was a complete deviation from my original plan, with Attal covering my attack using her Arc energy. But as my last foe fell to the ground, I finally lost consciousness.\n\nIt wasn't Attal who woke me up, but the continuous clamor of explosions. I saw her staring at the flames outside, terrified. Meanwhile, Crowther was complaining to me about being forced to watch Attal patching me up. Wyther's soldiers were behind the blasts. They'd tracked us to the village Attal had hid us in and bombarded it. All I could do then was keep Attal safe. I dragged her into the woods while she kept weeping. Only when sounds of explosions quieted did her sobs cease. That night was the first time I saw Attal abandon her innocent hopes, if only for a while. As for Wyther, he couldn't escape my vengeance—though said vengeance would be exacted with Attal fighting at my side."}]},{"id":"diary-31210","title":"Farewell For Now","sub":"Character diary · Efrideet","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_312","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Efrideet"},"body":[{"p":"Asteri, I'm so sorry that I couldn't say goodbye to you in person.\nYesterday, when I went to visit you, I heard you crying in your room. I wasn't sure if you wanted to be alone, and I was worried that you might not want to learn that I'm leaving under such circumstances, so...please forgive me. In the end, I chose not to knock.\nDid you find the gift I left you at the door? It's a treasure chest I've filled over the years. Whenever I set foot in a new land, I always take something as a keepsake. It may just be some flowers or oddly shaped rocks, or even some handicrafts, but maybe you'll find something that you like in there.\nRadegast—that's the big tall guy who welcomed you at the city gate yesterday—will look after you. If you run into any trouble or need any help, just head to the Throne Room and find him. Don't be shy or embarrassed; this is his duty, so don't let him slack off. (If you're really having a hard time telling him, or if you're not eating well or being taken care of, just write me a letter, okay?)\nI noticed when we passed by that store yesterday that you were staring at the cat. The shopkeeper may have said that's her cat and you can't take it, but I bought a plushy that looks just like it. You've already seen it, right? As for Miss Cloud...I'm really sorry. Maybe you can let this kitty sleep beside you instead?\nSkorri says that Haven harvested a nice batch of fruit recently. The strawberries in particular are really sweet. You'll likely be able to have some with dinner. If you're feeling down, just eat something sweet. That always helps cheer me up.\nBy the time you read this letter, I'll have already set off for the Bering Strait. Don't worry, though. There's no danger, and this is just farewell for now. I won't leave you. Time flies. Who knows—by the time I get back, you may be five inches taller.\nOh, right. It's supposed to rain tomorrow; be sure to bring an umbrella if you go out so you don't catch a cold. Take good care of yourself, okay?\nI'm looking forward to seeing you again.\n\nAlways protecting you,\nEfrideet"}]},{"id":"diary-20611","title":"Record of a Battle I","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"Before the decisive battle with the Warlord Dampier began, I'd never thought I'd use the \"T\" tactic from the age of sail-propelled ships ever again. Fortunately, Dampier's vessel and I were both relics of a bygone era. His flagship was a cargo ship roughly 200 feet tall, its sides welded with composite armor and intercepting nets. He'd transformed it into a fortress, armed with cannon ports and platforms suitable for firing all manner of weapons. Luckily for me, though, it was far from a real warship, incapable of holding any fancy, long-ranged weapons he could fire while sipping on his coffee.\nThat's not to say it wasn't a fierce battle. The seas were ablaze, and the cannon fire left me deaf for a bit. The only things on my mind were: control the rudder, turn, fire, repeat. Our firepower was no match for his. The Lightbearers among us died and rose before the pain could even subside, while the mortals never opened their eyes again. I saw the ship's wreckage and shreds of flags floating in the water, the last tombstone to remember those who had met their end on the sea. I could almost imagine Dampier's arrogant grin inside that \"Iron Kraken\" of his.\nStay calm, I told myself, as I had Parrot report on our remaining firepower. The situation was worse than I'd thought, but not nearly dire enough to despair. I looked out at Dampier's fortress through the telescope. It was massive, imposing, a leviathan supported by death. My gaze swept over the sturdy armor and the cannon barrels protruding from the firing ports, and an idea was born. The risk would be high, but any pirate worth her salt should embrace storms and whirlpools.\nSo, I gave the command. \"Sail straight for 'em.\""}]},{"id":"diary-11504","title":"Regarding VIP#2025","sub":"Character diary · Ikora, the Hidden","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_115","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora, the Hidden"},"body":[{"p":"ACCESS LEVEL: Top Secret\nENCRYPTION PASSKEY: Q9X2R4L7P8V1C3Z6T0AB$IKO-006\nCHANNEL MEMBERS: CHA-319. IKO-006, TRU-135\nCHANNEL NAME: Regarding VIP#2025\n\n1.As the channel name says. What do you think?\nVIP#2025 has crossed paths with the Ahamkara in the Red Sea Rift a few too many times.\nGiven what previously happened with VIP#0003 and VIP#0011, I'm very worried about the impact this will have on VIP#2025's psyche.\n\n2.But VIP#2025 has been acting perfectly normal.\nI think a bit more trust is warranted. At the very least, we should only take action once obvious symptoms of corruption present themselves.\n\n3.\"Trust.\" Such an unfamiliar word.\nHere I thought our job was to always be prepared for the worst.\n\n4.@TRU-135 Are you saying you trust nobody?\nEven when they've worked so hard to prove their character?\n\n5.@CHA-319 This is why Haven remains one of the safest settlements on Earth.\n\n6.@TRU-135 You think that's all thanks to your skepticism?\n\n7.Enough.\n@TRU-135 @CHA-319 Let's stop this unproductive, childish squabbling.\nWe remain skeptical because we have seen too many sacrifices caused by ignorance and blind faith, but that should not make us ruthless.\nWe are gathered here to hear everyone's opinions. Only by keeping ourselves calm can we become more objective and get closer to the truth.\nLet's shake hands and make peace, friends.\n\n8.@IKO-006 You're right.\n@TRU-135 Sorry, I shouldn't have said that.\n\n9.@CHA-319 Please accept my apologies, too.\nHowever, I maintain we should inform VIP#0001 of all the connections between VIP#2025 and the Ahamkara.\nEspecially VIP#0121. She's far too dangerous.\n\n10.VIP#0121's presence in the Red Sea Rift has indeed resulted in destruction, but I think we should still treat her as an ally.\n\n11.If you'll allow me to elaborate, \"destruction\" refers to her bringing the Vex to the Red Sea Rift.\nAdditionally, according to VIP#0003 and VIP#2025's accounts, we have reason to suspect the connection between VIP#0121 and the Ahamkara is not as simple as that of wisher and wish-granter.\nYou know the Ahamkara are shapeshifters, right?\n\n12.So what you're saying is, if Morgran was willing, he could transform into a cat whenever he wants?\n\n13.@CHA-319 We still don't know whether Ahamkara shapeshifting is subject to certain prerequisites or restrictions.\nBut theoretically, yes.\n@TRU-135 A frightening conjecture indeed.\nBut according to the intel we've gathered on VIP#0121, eyewitness testimony proves that she was born in North Africa, and there are records of her presence in the region ever since.\nBefore she came to the Red Sea Rift, VIP#0121 appears to have been a standard, Lightless mortal. There was never anything particularly noteworthy about her.\n\n14.@IKO-006 Where do you think VIP#0121 went? Was her disappearance an accident?\n\n15.I'm not sure. However, I don't believe in \"accidents\" where the Ahamkara are concerned.\nThus, I think we should prepare a detailed report on VIP#0121's history in the Rift and her disappearance for VIP#0001.\nAs for VIP#2025... Let's continue to monitor the situation, but take care not to lose your confidence and empathy, friends."}]},{"id":"diary-20612","title":"Record of a Battle II","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"Just as I'd anticipated, Dampier had placed too much importance on his floating fortress's firepower and not enough on its agility. We, on the other hand, had dropped some equipment that had affected our warship's speed, and at full power, it far outpaced Dampier's fleet. Once he'd realized that, the minefield he'd previously set up hindered his movements, and the excessive weight made his pursuit a joke. By the time Dampier angrily gave the orders to turn, our vessel was already sitting perpendicular to his. Both our offense and defense had taken shape.\nThe fixed firing range prevented Dampier from focusing his cannons on us; meanwhile, his steel behemoth had become the perfect target. Setting my telescope at its highest magnification, I saw his eyes open wide as he reflected on the flood of incoming artillery and experienced an unknown emotion: fear. Soon, his despair and unwillingness to admit defeat were shattered along with his Ghost and sank beneath a blood-red sky.\nThe seawater flung skyward turned into a salty rain pouring over my head and face. The pain seeped into pale, soaked wounds that hadn't fully healed, giving my numbed brain a moment of clarity. People were cheering. Tears and blood mixed as they celebrated a bittersweet victory, but the belated feeling that overcame me was one of exhaustion.\nThis was my last fight against Dampier, yet it would not be my final battle. How long would the peace and security we'd bought with lives last? Nobody could give an answer. This planet seems to have no plans of giving humanity stability or respite.\nOnce the exhaustion faded, the unease and confusion in my heart intensified, burning into a terrifying impulse. That night, I turned my gaze to the starry sky above.\nWhether it's a peaceful place to rest or a chaotic new stage, for a pirate, both are treasures worthy of setting sail."}]},{"id":"diary-20613","title":"\"The Pirate Code\" by Parrot","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"Article I, Section 1: Always listen to the Captain.\nCaptain Maru always has a way.\n\nArticle I, Section 4: Always keep your weapons clean and functional to ensure the fastest possible counterattack when the unexpected occurs.\nThis is of the utmost necessity. Nobody wants shards from a burst barrel slicing their throats.\n\nArticle II, Section 3: Should you get lost, always look up to the stars.\nOf course, you could also look down at the radar.\n\nArticle II, Section 4: Don't hide from storms—head for their eye.\nHold fast, sailors. We'll be able to enjoy a nice nap.\n\nArticle III, Section 5: No cheating during Shadowshaper Duels.\n[Maru's handwriting] This rule does not apply to the Captain.\n\nArticle III, Section 8: On land, a little lying goes a long way.\nThis goes for land ONLY. Honesty is the best sail.\n\nArticle IV, Section 1: Taking pleasure from destruction, harm, or murder is strictly prohibited. \nThis extends to plants, animals, humans, and Ghosts. Life is nature's gift. Treasure it.\n\nArticle IV, Section 2: Those who follow the Captain get their rewards.\nEveryone gets their fair share! Everyone!\n\nArticle IV, Section 5: Don't even think about retreating.\nWe've gotta see the world beyond Earth, mateys."}]},{"id":"diary-20614","title":"Children","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"Today, I paid a visit to Ms. Aimee and ran into the kids I'd met previously. Turns out, my tales of pirate life hadn't scared them at all. When they saw me coming, they were actually pretty happy. At least that means the cookies I'd brought didn't go to waste.\nMy arrival gave Ms. Aimee some time to rest. We had a simple chat; she didn't see me as some sort of dangerous ne'er-do-well, instead inviting me to spend some more time with the kids. Children are largely all the same. They like sweets, games, and interesting stories. I used a few tricks to get the little rascals sitting in a circle, and before you know it, Parrot had them listening with big, bright eyes as he told stories from who knows when. Now, they're all claiming they want to be pirates sailing the high seas—a bit of a headache for Ms. Aimee.\nTimes are always changing. A few hundred years ago, some parents would've used legends of pirates to scare their children into behaving, filling their nightmares with one-eyed, hook-handed demons steering algae-covered ghost ships. Now, they're part of the kids' games of make-believe.\nThey asked me to come back and visit them often. It's not a particularly harsh request, so I agreed that until I left Haven, I'd make it part of my regular schedule. The real challenge is coming up with new adventures every week, but lucky for me, it's nothing Parrot can't handle. At long last, his beloved pirate tales have an audience other than me."}]},{"id":"diary-20615","title":"First Mate, Second Mate","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"My second mate is my parrot—the bird kind, not my Ghost. It's a beautiful macaw with feathers as dazzling as jewels, all carefully preened. When we first met, though, that was far from the case. It had fallen from a tree, completely bald and huddled in the grass, struggling to survive. I picked it up and brought it back to my ship, where Parrot—my Ghost, not the bird—declared it second mate.\nEvery pirate captain should keep a parrot. That's what Parrot told me, at least—the bloke's addicted to those centuries-old pirate stories. Bringing our second mate on board was a lot of fun for him. As it gradually recovered and grew those beautiful feathers, it finally learned to speak under Parrot's persistent guidance. The result, unfortunately, was endless bickering day in and day out. It's got quite the extensive vocabulary. Parrot's lost so many times, he's beginning to regret teaching it language.\nI must admit, it's nice having a parrot around. Whenever it perches on my shoulder, the weight and feel of it gripping the fabric bring an emotion that is strange, yet not by any means unwelcome. Over time, I became accustomed to carrying a handful of nuts in my pocket or occasionally whistling to call it onto my outstretched arm. When we're at sea, my second mate is always willing to fly up to the highest mast and sing a shanty in its signature odd tone.\nAnd whenever I call out to it, I see bright blue spiraling down from the sky, open wings cutting through thick clouds and carrying the salty sea breeze to me. Sometimes it intentionally teases Parrot or tries to catch him and fly high into the sky. When that happens, the whole ship can hear Parrot's screams, and it always ends in the Ghost fleeing in panic, all the while accusing me of standing idly by. Of course I would. Weren't you the one who said a pirate needs a parrot, matey?"}]},{"id":"diary-20616","title":"\"Records\" Regarding Haven","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"Haven's at a high altitude, and from the platforms surrounding the garden and armory, you can see a stretch of mountains surging up, like frozen waves. Of course, there's also the Traveler. This extraterrestrial visitor is a miracle, having brought both progress and disaster. Perhaps it's because it's the source of the Light that brought me back, but looking at it always gives me a sense of calm and peace—something forgotten and unfamiliar, thanks to the constant conflicts.\nBut I'm no mere tourist. The high terrain is good news, as it means Haven's security won't be able to catch up with me if I fly that ship out of here. All I need to do is break through an insignificant barrier, and I'll have more than enough height to make my ascent. I'll need to pay special attention to the layout of Haven's defenses, though.\nHowever, one pesky little problem remains. If my takeoff fails, that precious ship will crash with me. As a Lightbearer, death's not a problem, but being trapped beneath a pile of scrap metal is. Plus, I'd be hard-pressed to find another similar ship in the short term. The risk is still high, and I need to consider this route carefully. That Eliksni \"ally\" may not be a bad choice, all things considered.\nI'll also need to plan for a supplemental energy source, transferring available equipment, and plotting transit routes. Considering Haven's a place worth resting my feet for a while, I've no doubt I'll be able to work out the details from a long-term perspective."}]},{"id":"diary-20617","title":"THE SHIP & TOHORĀ","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"I once had a ship. It was a legacy of the Golden Age I'd found on an unnamed island. Aside from the thick blanket of ferns covering its surface, the partial damaged equipment, and the layers of dust thick enough to fill my lungs and then some, it was in amazing condition. Parrot and I checked its central control system, and thanks to the miraculous technology of the Golden Age, its power valve still responded to start-up commands even after its centuries-long baptism in dust and flora.\nWe checked its navigation log, which recorded several coordinates in a complex code. Once he'd cracked it, Parrot told me they pointed to several exoplanets that humans colonized during the Golden Age, meaning we may be able to use them to leave Earth.\nAfter that, my life was filled with gathering materials and modifying the spacecraft. It was a tedious task, but Parrot and I enjoyed it, for we had a real ship capable of sailing us through the vast unknown. We reinforced its armor and protective plates, repaired the reactor, and at last, put this old sailor back on deck.\nAnd the result? A failure. My ship burned up mid-air. Parrot had to dredge me out of the Dead Sea, then we stared out at the sinking wreckage, unable to utter so much as a sigh.\nThen, I saw something glowing in the shipwreck. I approached it and dug out part of the shielding layer. It was a Collapsing Cannon—a weapon that had once sailed the stars with this ship and had miraculously survived the crash. Now, a new dawn shone from its intact shell, and Light surged from within it.\nI pulled it from the wreckage, named it \"Tohorā,\" then set off with both my new Relic and Parrot in tow. Even after countless battles, it remains a good ally. One day, I'll have a new flagship capable of sailing the cosmos, and when that day comes, Tohorā will be both its main cannon and its crown jewel."}]},{"id":"diary-30305","title":"Answers","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"(Aesthetic, vintage, flourished lettering)\nJaren, you once asked me what I thought about our connection, and I didn't have a response.\nMaybe now, I can give you an answer.\n*P.S.: Read it yourself since I can't imagine telling you in person.\n\nI don't know how other Ghosts and Lightbearers bond, but through the numerous journeys we've accompanied each other on, I unwittingly came to think of you as a companion I can trust with all my heart.\nYou were extremely confused when you were first resurrected—reticent, alert, and indifferent to everything and everyone, including me. Well, I admit I wasn't a cheerful Ghost either. I still remember how in the beginning, so long as we didn't run into trouble, we'd go a whole week without speaking to each other. It's much better now, though. Apologies, I digress.\nI'm exceptionally content to see you slowly become \"gentle\" as opposed to confused and ruthless. (I know you won't admit it, but why else would a \"profit-oriented,\" \"disadvantage-avoidant,\" \"cold,\" \"heartless\" mercenary help mortals find their cats, save their dogs, and take care of their children?)\nTo tell you the truth, I don't have a preference as to how Lightbearers use their power, but I'm delighted to see that this is how you've chosen to bear the responsibility that comes with wielding the Light.\nI'm glad that I chose you, Jaren."}]},{"id":"diary-20619","title":"You Call That Fishing?","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"Kabr has invited me several times to participate in those leisurely fishing events held at a slow-moving river near Haven. However, I'd always found various reasons to refuse.\nIt's not that I'm opposed to fishing as an activity. Indeed, it is fun, but my idea of fishing doesn't include pitching tents and meditating in outdoor chairs by a calm lake, waiting for those poor, foolish fry to bite the hook. I'd rather deal with Ms. Aimee's kids a hundred times over. I told them of my experiences with open-sea fishing—slightly exaggerated, sure, but the thrill I spoke of was genuine. What's even more real are the terrors of the waters, great enough to give those land-lubbers nightmares.\nSea fishing is enjoyable—at least for me, it is. I once fought against a giant catch in a storm. In my memory, it seemed as big as a small mountain, and the wind and waves felt strong enough to engulf the whole world, cheering the fish on as it fought me. Parrot was so scared, he asked me to tie him to the mast, forgetting that he could just as easily conceal himself.\nI stood at the bow of the ship, tightly gripping my custom fishing rod. The leviathan, lured and frenzied by the bait, struggled wildly at the sea's surface, stirring up even more waves and leaving only its pungent, fishy smell. It slammed its body against the side of the ship, nearly sending me into the water. One part of the hull sank, and its bony fin cut off a mast. I used all the weapons at my disposal to reel it in. The blood that splattered out looked thick and green as it floated on the surface. The dying body of the defeated was at last hauled aboard. Naturally, I'd won. Standing in the eye of the storm, I declared my victory with a final round of artillery fire.\nOn our return journey, we saw a giant whale leap out of the water, its skin like an abyss, reflecting the colors of the universe under the late dawn glow. I hope to continue my hobby of sea fishing as I embark on my journey beyond Earth. They say that in the furthest reaches of the universe, there swims a giant whale that swallows entire planets. I look forward to the day I encounter this catch."}]},{"id":"diary-30501","title":"A Black Cat","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"Claudia and I went back to the old lab in Hong Kong today. She says that's where she found me with my headband, so we've got our best shot at finding the chip there. But the place is a total wreck—we're searching for a needle in a haystack.\nI saw a black cat staring at me while Claudia was rambling about her \"safe\" plan. No matter where I went, it'd still be looking straight at me. Not even my clones could fool it. Of all the things I expected to find at the lab, an animal that wasn't afraid of people wasn't one of them. I went to go pet it, but it darted off as soon as I got near, then continued staring at me. Weird. Well, no harm in tailing it to find out what its deal is.\nWe followed the black cat into the building. The Fallen had rendered everything inside nearly unrecognizable. I couldn't help but ask Claudia if it was like this back then, too. She had the nerve to answer me by asking, \"You saw it when I resurrected you, didn't you?\" How's anyone supposed to remember anything fresh outta the grave? I gotta say, though, the place is a nightmare to navigate. Dunno how I would've found my way around the crumbling walls if it weren't for the cat leading the way.\nAfter searching for what felt like hours, it finally stopped in front of a pile of clothes. They were tattered, worn, and medium-sized—maybe fit for a teenager. The cat peeled away some of the clothes and pushed a tattered diary in front of us when it saw us approaching. I picked it up and went to pet the black cat, but it was gone! Poof! Vanished in the blink of an eye!\nI asked Claudia if she saw it, but she said she hadn't seen any black cat at all. She'd just been following me. So I told her what had just happened. She said people in Eastern cultures believed cats to be spiritual guides. Spiritual guides? So what I saw was...?\nY'know what, next time I see a black cat, I'm bookin' it."}]},{"id":"diary-30502","title":"Self-Reflection","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"[A crumpled piece of paper wedged into the diary]\nI, Ning Fei, should not have snuck out for a drink behind Claudia's back, nor should I have gotten wasted and stayed out all night.\nHere's what went down:\nAfter I messaged Kabr for the twentieth time complaining about how boring the drinks had been lately, he finally introduced me to something new—something strong. I followed the clues he'd provided, after walking through some dark and wet tong lau and squeezing through slum alleyways barely wide enough to stand in, I finally found a mysterious wooden door hidden in a corner of the Last City. I suppose it's true what they say—good things don't come easy (even if this place really was a pain to find).\nI originally expected it to be some sort of special café. The noises coming from behind the door weren't exactly inviting, but... I kinda liked the vibe. At the time, I was wondering how I'd fake being a regular when I entered. But then this foolish man saw me and asked, what's a kid doing here? Tell me, how's a mature Lightbearer such as myself to tolerate such an insult?\nIt's absurd, right? So I did what any reasonable man would do—I waltzed right in and said I'll have what he's having. I took a sip and almost spit it out. Felt like I was drinking paint thinner. These people must've never had good drinks in their life. How else would they actually like this stuff?\nBut that guy—he finished it in one go! The whole freakin' tankard! No way he wasn't challenging me! So I thought, 'You're on!' and downed mine. I felt dizzy pretty quickly, as if I'd been struck by one of the Fallen's shock grenades. Not exactly a pleasant feeling. But to my surprise, he called for another round. Losing to him would be a disgrace to Lightbearers everywhere. So I ordered another round too! No matter how much he drank, I'd drink one more than him...\nAnd that's the story. I have no idea what that drink was. And alcoholism? Never heard of it.\nThere. I've said it once, and I've written it down once. Happy?\nI, Ning Fei, swear to never drink again."}]},{"id":"diary-30503","title":"Record of Symptoms","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"May 20\nStarted documenting the effects of my headband on my body today.\nClaudia \"volunteered\" me for a request to gather supplies today.\n\n May 21\nHeadband had a slight reaction this afternoon. Felt a bit dizzy.\nMight've been from all the walking. Why do I have to run these stupid errands for people? I'm a Lightbearer, not a delivery boy.\n\n May 22\nThe reaction to the headband seemed to be intermittent. I had two headaches today, one on the road and one right before a break. Both of them nearly killed me.\nClimbing mountains, rummage through garbage, and moving scrap metal with a headache is actual torture.\n\n May 23\nThe headband issue has been getting worse recently. I can feel the tingling even in combat.\nAfter one fight, I told Claudia the headache was so bad I couldn't walk, and you know what she said? That I was just faking it to get out of work!\n[The following paragraph is bolded and enlarged]\nI'm so pissed. She thought I was faking it!\nShe just doesn't trust me at all. I can't stand her!"}]},{"id":"diary-10501","title":"Mint","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"When Mint was healing the guerrillas in Jiangshi Metro today, they complimented it and said it was much more unique than other Relics shaped like swords, blades, and spears. Mint can't speak, but if it could, I bet it'd be super happy to hear that!\nWhen I was newly risen, I often imagined what my Relic would look like. But up until Mint showed up, the image of a metal bird never crossed my mind!\n\nMint was born of a fragmented Relic—a sword that had broken apart.\nI first saw it in the ruins of a village. The place reeked of rust, telling of the suffering it had endured. I found myself there not long after Swift revived me. At the time, I hadn't been able to adapt to this world of misery and death. I stood there staring at scene of blight before me, not even bothering to brush the fallen leaves and dust from my shoulders... Then, I suddenly felt a pulse of energy echoing in my chest. It made me clench my fists as the tears started running down my cheeks once more.\nFollowing my instincts, I picked up a piece of scrap and imbued it with the power surging through my head and chest... And in a flash of cold blue, Mint was born.\nIts Arc energy has the capacity for both destruction and healing, sharpness and softness.\nWhen it perched on my fingertip with its firm yet sensitive claws, I knew it was my very own Relic—my Mint.\n\nLater, I learned that people from the Golden Age saw doves as a symbol of peace. A creative idea and perfect fit, I think.\nThus I shall bring peace to the world with Mint, my little Arc-infused metal bird."}]},{"id":"diary-10502","title":"Cold Blue Memory","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"Gwynn is fast asleep.\nLooking at her like this, I always think back to our first encounter on that cold, white, and noisy winter day.\n\nWhen I first met her, she was heavily wounded and covered in blood.\nShe stumbled into a building with a whole squad of soldiers chasing after her, laughing despite being a rabbit hunted by a pack of hungry wolves. I didn't think twice. I couldn't turn my back on someone so badly injured, so I broke into the building and ordered Mint to heal her.\nWaves of pursuers descended on us with even fiercer firepower. I carried her to another place to hide, but we walked right into another bombardment. Such a heavy attack made it hard to escape even with our Ghosts' help.\nBut I was concerned more about the village than myself.\nIt was a peaceful place where I'd stayed for a long time. I liked the villagers, the perfectly straight birches lining the roads, the babbling brook flowing through the outskirts... And after that brutal siege...there was nothing left but rubble and embers.\nI asked myself over and over, was I wrong to try and save someone? If I hadn't saved her, would the village have been attacked anyway? Was I the one who brought blood, fire, and death on them?\nThen she opened her eyes and, fighting through the pain, rose to her feet and dragged me into the woods.\nShe didn't say a word, and neither did I. We just silently watched as flames swept the buildings and streets. The blaze lit up her face and pierced my eyes. Why did it hurt so much...? I couldn't stop the tears from falling.\nHad I done the wrong thing? Should I not try to save people? Should I just sit by and watch them suffer?\nOf course not. It wasn't me who was in the wrong."}]},{"id":"diary-30509","title":"Hairstyling Record","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"[Each note is separated by a period of time.]\nShoulder-length Hair: Original hairstyle, which does show my dashing looks, but blocks my vision in combat. Some people also say adjusting my hair after every battle is \"not manly\". They know nothing about beauty.\nShort Hair: Sometimes I do want to reveal my forehead—lets me show off more of my stunning face, after all. But short cuts are risky, as I've heard that Lightbearers' hair doesn't grow. In that case, if I wanted to switch it up again, I'd be stuck.\nTied Up: Most of the warriors in the martial arts novels I've been reading lately are portrayed in this way. I just need to tie my hair up, trim my bangs, and voila! The perfect new hairstyle. It's decided. I'll have the barber do it tomorrow.\n\nMy new hair is stylish, and everyone notices the change in me. It's strange that everyone tells me that I must cherish my new hairstyle after I tell them that I spent three days designing it, two hours explaining it to three different hairdressers (the first two actually complained about me; they just don't get it), and five hours getting it done. Of course I'm going to cherish it. This hairstyle is so me.\n\nClaudia, why didn't you tell me resurrections reset my hairstyle?! Three days of designing, two hours of explaining, and five hours of waiting, all WASTED!\n\nI, Ning Fei, hereby pledge to listen to Claudia's commands advice for three months, or else my hairstyle will reset every time I am revived."}]},{"id":"diary-10503","title":"A Sharp Olive Branch","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"I wonder what Cabal civilization is like. They have their own culture and language, so I think communication could be possible, though they've ignored all my attempts so far.\nThe supplies they looted in the Red Sea Rift were far more than necessary. Why disturb the peace with gunfire if they have no worries about surviving? Were these cold hard hunks of ore really worth all the fighting? Worth all the sorrow, pain, bloodshed, and deaths? Worth the dashed hopes of survival?\nLife itself should be the most precious thing in the world...right?\nI won't stop those who hunt out of necessity. That's how the world works, and I shouldn't interfere with attempts at survival. But I cannot—will not—forgive those who snuff out others' lives for selfish reasons. Kindness without limits is hypocrisy. It's the condescending, arrogant disregard for others' lives. Only through restrained kindness can we treat all beings as equals and spread love and peace throughout the world.\nAnd that's why, whether it's the Cabal or the Eliksni or some other threat, I too must take up arms and fight, no matter how much I wish otherwise. But if the day finally comes when they want to embrace peace and drop their guns to talk with me, I will welcome them with open ears and an open heart.\nAs for cruel pillagers who refuse to see reason...I have no choice but to protect the innocent."}]},{"id":"diary-10504","title":"Taste of Home","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"I heard that good partners should give each other gifts to express their love. Hmm... I don't think I've ever given Gwynn a gift. Well, no time like the present!\nBut what should I give her...? I'll ask Crowther if he has any ideas.\n\n(A new note)Crowther said that Gwynn doesn't have any particular preferences and suggested that I prepare some dishes from her hometown. After wandering around for so many years, she must be homesick, even if she's never expressed it.\nI thought he had a point, but Swift thought otherwise. He advised me not to listen to Crowther and called it a \"lousy idea\". I don't get why Swift would think so. Who wouldn't like a taste of home? Well...since I can't think of anything else, I'll make dinner for her! Surely there's no harm listening to Crowther. Who'd know Gwynn better than her own Ghost, right?\nI'll look up some recipes and prepare the ingredients tomorrow!\n\n(A new note)Some sardines, eels, herrings, onions, potatoes, wheat flour, creams, lemons, peppers, and animal blood... What strange ingredients. But...I've got to trust the process. The Haven Library's recipes wouldn't lead me astray...right?\n\n(A new note)Crowther came by as I was preparing the materials and left looking satisfied.Huh. I guess I got everything right!\n\n(A new note)\n...Why did Gwynn storm out looking upset? I followed the recipes to the letter and specifically chose the top three most famous dishes... Cooking them wasn't exactly difficult, so it's probably nothing to do with my culinary skills... Where did I go wrong...?\n\nWas it the recipes themselves? Aren't stargazy pies, jellied eels, and black pudding supposed to be classic English dishes? Huh... Guess even the Haven Library is wrong sometimes!"}]},{"id":"diary-10505","title":"Snow Peas","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"I've stayed in Jiangshi Metro long enough to have tread every corner of that frozen, blizzard-worn wasteland.\nI always see drifters struggling to survive, huddled inside the run-down buildings scattered throughout the wilderness. For various reasons, they refuse to settle in Jiangshi Metro. Death has long been an integral aspect of their lives.\nWalking among them, I offer whatever help I can, be it searching for supplies or fending off looters. But what I receive in return is mostly their fear and vigilance. It doesn't matter—I've come to anticipate it. The world has been plagued by despair for so long that people don't believe in kindness for kindness's sake.\nThough Gwynn typically doesn't approve of me offering help, she accompanies me to take out looters—that's how she upheld her convictions: bringing death upon the wicked and realizing true justice. I feel she tends to go a bit overboard on the violence, but even I must admit there aren't many choices when it comes to dealing with such people.\nSo we journey across the tundra, helping drifters and asking for nothing in return.\n\nToday, we saved a family from being robbed. This wouldn't be anything noteworthy—we do this often, after all—but strangely, just as we were preparing to leave, they stopped us. You could tell they'd lived a tough life just by looking at them, with their sallow faces and sunken cheeks indicating a lack of food.\nIt was a middle-aged woman up front, with her hands hidden in her pockets. I couldn't figure out why they stopped us, but I glimpsed that Gwynn had gripped her scythe. I just sighed and waited for her to make a move.\nThen, the woman took out a handful of grilled snow peas and passed them to me.\nBreathing a sigh of relief, I accepted the peas, and Gwynn quietly released her scythe. Come to think of it, her reaction was kind of cute.\nThen we parted ways with them and continued our journey.\n\nWell, here's to more love and peas tomorrow!"}]},{"id":"diary-11501","title":"Reply","sub":"Character diary · Ikora, the Hidden","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_115","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora, the Hidden"},"body":[{"p":"[A handwritten letter that has clearly been edited many times.]\n\nI will not beat around the bush, Ikora. I'm very glad you sought my opinion on this matter, but I can't say I agree with your point of view.\nIndeed, the Iron Lords differ from all other Lightbearer organizations I've seen, formed not to gain an advantage in a war, but to end war itself. Much time has passed, yet even to this day, I have not doubted Radegast's intentions in founding this organization. That was why I chose to become Felwinter's apprentice all those years ago.\nBut be that as it may, people change, and factions are a conglomerate of multiple people. I do not need to elaborate on the uncertainty this adds.\nWhen you act for the sake of your own goals, you know what you are doing, and you know the potential consequences of your choices. Now, however, we are talking about an intelligence agency, a spy network, a machine built for war. Of course, it's as you said—the machine already exists and would continue to run regardless of whether you accepted the position of operator. Radegast handed control over it to you because he trusts you will make the right decision when the time comes. In that regard, he may trust you more than he trusts himself.\nBut how can you ensure every gear of this machine turns correctly? The second it malfunctions or you err in your judgment, what you will face is not a trap that will harm you alone, but a war that will spill the blood of many.\nAsk yourself—are you truly prepared to accept the consequences?\n\nI know that once you've made your decision, it's highly unlikely anything I write will change your mind. Though I am loath to admit it under such circumstances, we are very alike in our stubbornness.\nRegardless, I hope this letter can be of some aid to you. Even though you may already be this machine's operator, I hope that when it comes time to press that button, you can re-examine your choice and recall what you once told me: \"Nobody can be right forever.\""}]},{"id":"diary-10506","title":"Notes on Raising Eliksni Kids: Field Trip","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"I took the kids to Haven on something called a \"field trip\" today.\nIt's a form of education I learned from some old books. In the past, schools would organize periodic trips for children, allowing them to reinforce what they'd learned and put it into practice while enjoying themselves, or teach them something new based on the destination. It didn't make much sense to me at first—outings are meant to be relaxing, so why should we require the kids to \"reinforce what they've learned\" while taking part, let alone pick up new knowledge?\nBut what happened next proved that doing so is indeed very, VERY necessary in certain circumstances. I don't understand how such lovely, sensible kids could become completely uncontrollable after stepping foot in Haven... Going forward, I should make \"Dos and Don'ts\" guides specific to the places we'll visit. That should help them learn and practice while having fun sightseeing. But that's a matter for a later date... First and most importantly, I need to adjust my lessons based on the complaints I received today.\n\nComplaint 1: There are bite marks all over my tomatoes. I worked hard to grow those, you know! And here I was about to let it slide if you guys just took them quietly. But taking a bite and then hanging them back up? Are you trying to piss me off?!\n* Add etiquette lesson: Don't touch things that don't belong to you.\nComplaint 2: What on earth happened? I thought I just drank a few too many and passed out on the roadside. No biggie, right? So why'd I wake up to find myself covered with mud and trash?! Someone lookin' to start a fight?! 'Cause I'll give ya one!\n* Hmm... The kids were probably trying to keep him warm and used those things as a blanket. * Add etiquette lesson: Not all things can be used as blankets.\nComplaint 3: My son told me that when he was playing ball with his friends, two Fallen kids forced their way into the game. They haven't touched the ball since. Come on, they have twice as many hands as my son! Can't they just keep to themselves?\n* Add etiquette lesson: Never participate in friendly competitions when you have an unfair advantage.\n...\nComplaint 36: Since when are Fallen kids allowed to run around Haven?\n* Do they mean the kids ran too fast or went somewhere they shouldn't be? ...Or do they mean they shouldn't be in Haven to begin with? I hope it's the former... Add etiquette lesson: Don't run too fast in the city, and don't enter buildings uninvited.\n...\nComplaint 51: Those Fallen kids scared the heck outta me! They can't just pop up out of nowhere like that!\n* ...Alright. I should inform the locals beforehand and give them enough time to prepare.\n...\nComplaint 74: We should forbid any Fallen from entering Haven! Including Kevarrh!\n* They're just blowing off steam. I'll ignore this one.\n...\n\n\n\nMore than half of the complaints were aimed at the Eliksni race as a whole. Learning manners and common sense won't help with that at all... No, I've got to keep my chin up! It's already much better than it used to be, right? At the very least, I've got a clear path before me.\nNo more blindly looking for chances to work towards peace.\nNo one can stop me as long as I'm willing to keep trying.\nFor love and peace! You've got this, Attal!"}]},{"id":"diary-10508","title":"Inter- species Friendship","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"I think that day will be engraved in my mind forever.\nIt was in that dilapidated, makeshift campsite. We couldn't communicate due to the language barrier, but before I'd even shown kindness to the Eliksni kids, they gave me a \"toy\" as a gift.\nThat moment was like touching the soft paw of a cat for the first time, filling my heart with a warm bliss and putting a smile on my face. I wanted to pinch their little cheeks, but held back for fear of scaring them off.\nI'm not familiar with any other Eliksni children, so I don't have anything for comparison, but these kids didn't seem to care that we were different. Even though I'm a human who doesn't speak their language, they still felt curious about me and welcomed me with a gift.\nRacial and linguistic barriers can't stand in the way of showing and spreading friendliness—these kids convinced me of that. There is no natural antagonism between \"us\" and \"them\". Various reasons may have caused conflict to brew between us, but so long as there is a sliver of hope for peace, I will always fight for it.\nBut enough about the distant future. What matters now is taking good care of these kids. Hmm...what do they need aside from an education? Maybe some human kids to be their friends? Are there any parents who would let their children play with the Eliksni? I should ask around... Oh! Maybe we can organize a friendly sports competition?\nI'll gather some suggestions tomorrow!"}]},{"id":"diary-10509","title":"An Unsent Letter","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"Dear Kind Eliksni Gentleman,\n\nAbout that last battle... I'm so sorry.\nNo matter what, I had to take out that out-of-control Servitor. I just couldn't let it threaten Jiangshi Metro. Maybe you could understand my determination to protect them—after all, you protected these children in the same way.\nOur stances are unbreakable chains that bind us. I am well aware of that. The old me wouldn't accept it, but...from all I've been through, I've learned that refusing to accept reality doesn't change it. There was almost nothing I could do about it, and I... All I can do is strive for a happy ending—or at least, one that is better than the original.\nIf someone were to ask whether I've ever regretted repairing that Servitor for you, the answer would be: Never. Even if it resulted in a final, inevitable battle, I never once regretted helping you. You never wanted the Servitor to malfunction. That, I understand. You just wanted to ensure the kids could survive.\nHowever, I do regret one thing—I never asked your name. Whenever I think about you or tell someone this story, all I can call you is \"Kind Eliksni Gentleman\"...\nBut please don't worry. I'll take care of those kids as if they were my own. They will never starve due to a lack of Ether, nor shall they go without a roof over their heads. The people of Haven haven't completely accepted the Eliksni, but at least they can live here safely without fear of being hunted down.\nThey now have many outstanding Lightbearers as their teachers, and even some human kids to play with.\nOnce they're a bit older, Kevarrh will take them to live with her—I told you about Kevarrh, remember? She's an Eliksni living in Haven who is experienced in communicating with humans.\nAnyway, Kind Eliksni Gentleman, please rest assured and leave them to me.\n\n—Your friend, Attal"}]},{"id":"diary-20701","title":"A Proposal to Lord Saladin I","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"Esteemed Lord Saladin,\nAfter reviewing the Red Sea Rift Legal Statutes, I believe certain sections urgently require further refinement, as detailed below:\nChapter 2, Article 3.1: To regulate the management of visitors and maintain order in the Red Sea Rift, it is mandated that all visitors proceed to the designated registration offices as instructed by the annexed statutes to ensure their legal rights during their stay.\nGiven the complex situation within the Red Sea Rift and the frequent influxes of unidentified visitors from outside regions, thorough screening is unachievable even with such a registration statute, leaving the residents of Veridia vulnerable. I suggest we tighten control over population movement and refrain from allowing visitors into Veridia unless absolutely necessary.\nChapter 2, Article 4.7: To protect the natural resources of the Red Sea Rift, maintain the local ecological environment, and regulate Radiancite development and utilization, all groups and individuals are prohibited from unauthorized extraction and exploitation of Radiancite. Prohibited activities include but are not limited to exploration, mining, blasting, excavation, illegal transport, and selling/trading. Violators will be punished based on severity.\nRadiancite is a vital mineral—the lifeline of the region and its main source of Light. I support its protection, but \"violators will be punished based on severity\" seems too lenient and may encourage some to take risks in order to obtain it. I recommend immediate and severe punishment for any illegal mining activities to serve as a deterrent.\nChapter 3, Article 1.2: The Red Sea Rift adheres to the principles of independence, autonomy, and peaceful coexistence in diplomacy, and shall never forego the development of friendly, equal, and cooperative relations with other territories.\nI earnestly urge you, Lord Saladin, to reconsider this statute. Not all Iron Lords are transparent, selfless, and trustworthy. Even a one percent chance of betrayal in the course of cooperation could pose a threat to our people. For the sake of the Red Sea Rift and the safety of Veridia's citizens, please let us focus first on our own development. Additionally, I suggest further bolstering our military to anticipate unforeseen developments.\nI await your response."}]},{"id":"diary-30303","title":"Nightmare","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"\"Jaren,\" Marco said with a smile, \"See ya later.\"\nDreamed about that parting again.\nI still didn't reply—just nodded and turned away.\n\nI've had this dream a lot ever since Marco died, but it's only ever been that moment.\nThis time, though, I recalled more.\nMaybe those distant memories that were swept away by time are becoming clear again as I get closer to avenging him.\n\nIt was Marco and Maln who picked me up when I was first revived. They introduced this strange world to the muddled, confused me. We traveled the wastes, completing odd jobs to get supplies, until one fateful request...\nWe were hired to protect a village from some Warlords. The pay was meager, but Marco accepted. It was for the common folk just struggling to survive, after all. That was fine by me, but as for Maln, the rival Warlords bought him off with some fine weapons.\nMaln promised not to intervene in the battle between the village and the warlords, but his neutrality still tipped the scales. While I had no intention of getting into this mess, Marco insisted on protecting the village. \"Weakness is no justification to stomp on them like ants,\" he said.\nI didn't get it. It was a dog-eat-dog world, wasn't it?\n\"The world didn't gift them the privilege of choice.\" Marco looked down and fiddled with his gun. \"But me? I've got power, and I want to use that power to give them their choice. Besides, I've already accepted the job, and I'm not one to break my vows.\"\nThat was his gun's name—\"Vows.\" Though I still didn't quite understand it, I respected his decision.\n\"Don't worry. We Lightbearers don't die so easily.\"\nHe convinced me, and I left after we'd agreed on a future meeting place. But...\nI can accept him giving his life for his ideals, but he shouldn't have died to one of his own. In the end, it was Maln—gunning for even more supplies and weapons—who took Marco out. Even shattered his Ghost with his own two hands.\nI won't accept that as his ending.\n\nThat parting with Marco became a nightmare that plagued me, and the name Maln, the cure.\nSoon enough, I'll be cured."}]},{"id":"diary-10510","title":"Notes on Raising Eliksni Kids: Invited Teachers","sub":"Character diary · Attal","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_105","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Attal"},"body":[{"p":"Gwynn: She didn't refuse outright, but she may as well have... Indeed, I didn't know how to answer her questions—\"You want me to teach those kids how to take lives? Or enlighten them with my philosophies on death?\" I'm not sure she's the...best choice for a teacher right now.\n\nTan-2: I didn't expect him to be so easily persuaded. He agreed right after I finished speaking, but I hadn't even told him what lessons I wanted him to teach. I wish Gwynn could be as enthusiastic as him! The thing is, despite him agreeing so readily, Tan-2 sometimes talks to himself, as if he's arguing with someone... The children are at that age where they copy everything. I sure hope they won't pick up this strange habit...\n\nJolder: After hearing my proposal, she stared at me for a moment...then told me no. I can't say I'm surprised. Plus I've seen how she trains her apprentices, and I don't think the kids are ready for such intensity.\n\nKabr: He accepted my invitation after asking about every detail where the kids came from! He's willing to teach both literature and math. I'll update him on the kids' progress tomorrow!\n\nIkora: She refused me calmly. She considers it nice to have more friendly Eliksni, but chooses to remain vigilant and avoid providing them with more knowledge. Though I'm a bit disappointed, I was expecting that—this doesn't seem like her kind of thing.\n\nFinnala: She gave me a straight refusal, claiming that she doesn't have the time or energy for such a mission. Considering her duties, I see where she's coming from... She works until midnight almost every day. I'd say that's too much even for a Lightbearer... Seriously, how does she survive that kind of workload?\n\nNing Fei: Surprisingly, he had a certain passion for teaching the Eliksni... He not only volunteered to teach them an Eastern language, but he also claimed that he could teach anything—from astronomy to geography, from math to philosophy... I have to say, though, I trust his Ghost more than him.\n\nMaru: She refused as expected. Somehow I felt relieved. The kids are still young and innocent, so spending time with a pirate of all people might not be appropriate..."}]},{"id":"diary-30504","title":"Master of Deception Guide—Chapter 1","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"Deception Guide Mind Tricks Telepathy Guide\nThe key to deception is belief. You have to get your target to trust focus believe that everything that's happening is natural, as opposed to some plan of yours. I'll start with a simple example: the easiest of card tricks. Firstly, show your cards at a speed that makes it hard for people to process, making sure no one remembers a single card. Then—and this part is really important—the second time you shuffle through, pause for a moment on the card you want the person to pick. Note that you have to make this pause look natural. That way, they're guaranteed to pick that card. Don't ask me how to memorize the order of the cards; I won't be going over basic techniques here.\nOur conversation might stop here if I were teaching someone else, but as your mentor, it's my duty to give you another example. Once, I needed to run some errands without Claudia following me, so I secretly wrote in my diary, \"My headband might cause dizziness. No one should disturb me at that time.\" And Claudia saw it—\"accidentally\" of course. When she questioned me, I came up with some excuse about how I didn't want others to think I had issues or something. And after a few well-timed \"dizzy spells,\" the next time I sneak out using my doppelganger? She'll never suspect a thing. So you see? The point is to convince her that it's really happening.\n[The notes here are more recent]\nHow dare Tan-2 laugh at me and call my great deceptions \"childish tricks.\" He's the child here, not me! I'm gonna finish writing this book, and we'll see who's laughing then!"}]},{"id":"diary-30510","title":"Fei Consulting, Inc.","sub":"Character diary · Ning Fei","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_305","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ning Fei"},"body":[{"p":"Posted by: The Great Fei\nViews: 30\nComments: 7\nPosted At: 3:05 a.m.\nAnnouncement:\nThe smartest, most strategic company humanity has ever seen officially begins its online operations today. We are dedicated to serving those of lower intelligence with strategies provided by the wisest Lightbearer alive, solving all existing complicated problems at a fair price and completely legally. And who, you might ask, is the giver of this invaluable wisdom? Why, none other than I, Ning Fei, President, CEO, CFO, COO, and Head of Personnel at Fei Consulting.\nHere are just a few of our company's success stories. (Source: Haven Nightly News)\nThe famous Jiangshi Metro Hostage Rescue Operation:\nAs many already have heard, Jiangshi Metro was recently plagued by a string of shocking and mysterious civilian kidnappings committed by the Fallen near the Ketch wreckage. A Lightbearer named Ning Fei, without any clues to go off, took the job and found traces of the Fallen after investigating for less than two hours. Unfortunately, the cunning Fallen took the civilians away just as he arrived on the scene. Turned out that the Fallen had kidnapped the people in an attempt to recreate a human experiment that tortured people's minds and would cause irreversible damage. Fortunately, the clever Ning Fei found the Fallen's lair through the trail they'd left and saved the victims alongside Wolf. The civilians were so exceptionally grateful that they called Ning Fei \"the hero of Jiangshi Metro.\" (Source: External submission from \"The Great Fei\")\n... (Please call us for more related cases.)\nComments\nWho? Isn't Wolf the hero of Jiangshi Metro? [User: john117]\nYeah. This is that dude who kept losing card games with Wu Ming all afternoon, then went online lying about how he won. [User: stephen9527]\nThis post has been removed for violating community guidelines. [User: The Great Fei]\nCome on, Ning Fei. Stop bragging online. I know it's you. [User: Parhelion Wing]\nYou've got the wrong person, Little Tan-2. [User: The Great Fei]\nCan you actually solve all problems? [User: Kabr]\nYou know it! [User: The Great Fei]"}]},{"id":"diary-31001","title":"The Whisperers","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"Tomorrow, I will swear my oath before the Ghosts and become a member of the Whisperers.\nI can't say for certain whether this is the only correct path, but it's clearly far better than the other choices before me. At the very least, Kara—my closest and only companion—chose them long ago. We've never diverged on values, and that isn't bound to change. Perhaps I was destined to walk this path from the moment Kara resurrected me.\n\nAll of my prior attempts at living a peaceful life ended in failure.\nWhether it was finding a village and settling down, or building a sanctuary with my own two hands, or joining up with some Warlord... Invasions and murder are like maggots on decaying corpses, crawling all over this fetid world. And I'm powerless to stop them.\nKara has never discouraged me, nor has she ever laughed at my failures. She just stays by my side, always calm and composed. She's rarely expressed her own thoughts on matters, and I'd always thought that was simply her personality. But when reality proved to me that the life I wanted would never be attained through my efforts alone, I realized the neutral silence she'd maintained was meant to avoid influencing me too much.\nAll I want is a quiet life, free of disturbances. A simple wish, really. But attaining it feels far more difficult than \"becoming a tyrant,\" something that should be out of reach... Truth be told, I find those reckless Warlords more despicable than the aliens. Clearly, they could use the Light's gift to make the world a better place, yet their lust for power reduced them to accomplices for evil.\nWhen all my attempts had ended in failure, Kara offered me what is, at present, the best answer: the Whisperers.\nAn organization founded and led by Ghosts. An organization that works to guide Lightbearers to use wield their Light for good. An organization that endeavors to reestablish world order by uniting and cultivating Lightbearers who are good, strong, and fair. An organization formed of Ghosts, who lack actual power but are also free of worldly desires, governing Lightbearers, wielders of immense strength.\nHmph... If power and immortality stole the kind, orderly side of the Warlords' humanity, then let me bring restraint and eternal slumber to their sides."}]},{"id":"diary-31002","title":"\"Enforcer\" Exam Performance Report","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"[A sheet of paper, seemingly printed many years ago.]\nUmeko, on behalf of all Ghosts of the Whisperers, we would like to congratulate you on passing your exam and becoming one of the Whisperers' core members. Very few operatives are even able to start the trial, for that means you have earned the recognition of every single Ghost among our ranks.\nWe know full well that trust is priceless, and we’re sure you agree.\nThus, we are delighted to have you truly stand with us as we turn our gaze towards a shared future.\n*Your compensation and benefits will be upgraded from those of an Operative to those of an Enforcer. Please see the statement attached to the back of this performance report for further details.\n —The Council of Twelve\n\nSolo Combat Capabilities\n[Outstanding]\nWhen it comes to solo combat, Umeko has always been an Enforcer in all but name. I have nothing more to say here. —Whitebeard\nAgreed. —Moshui\nAgreed. —Sootsy\nAgreed. —Sagittarius\nUmeko's amazing! —Cocoa\nManagement of Heavy ammunition needs more work. Additionally, there was an obvious mistake at 07:35 in the second phase, and performance could have been better at 08:13 (also second phase) and 03:02 (third phase). Remember to train on your own once you review your performance report. —Kara\nI think you're being a little too hard on her, Kara... Also—Moshui, Sootsy, Sagittarius! You three could stand to be a little less perfunctory, you know. —Wheat\n\nCooperative Combat Capabilities\n[Average]\nThe strength of Umeko's attacks is inversely proportional to her ability to cooperate with teammates. But given her preference for solo missions, I don't see any issue with this. —Whitebeard\nAgreed. —Moshui\nAgreed. —Sootsy\nAgreed. —Sagittarius\nUmeko's the coolest! —Cocoa\nTeamwork is indeed an obvious weakness. I'll submit a request to analyze whether Ayakiba can be modified to enhance her capabilities in cooperative combat. —Kara\nYou really are something, Kara... And knock it off, you three! —Wheat\n\nImprovisation\n[Good]\nRather strong adaptability, but becomes somewhat flustered under extreme circumstances. I look forward to seeing your growth. —Whitebeard\nAgreed. —Moshui\nDon't think I can't see what you're saying just because you wrote your comment last. That means you, Wheat! Surely you don't think your comment was something insightful. —Sootsy\nDon't think I can't see what you're saying just because you wrote your comment last. That means you, Wheat! Surely you don't think your comment was something insightful. —Sagittarius\nUmeko really is a quick-witted Lightbearer! I'm so jealous of you, Kara! Unlike Lor... His Light's not exactly shining the brightest, if you ask me. —Cocoa\nUmeko's performance in a scenario that calls for attacking as a group was rather stiff. This appears to be a long-term effect caused by the events of \"Operation: Albatross.\" Desensitization training for similar situations is necessary. —Kara\nUh, Kara... Umeko's already an excellent agent. I don't want you to push her too hard. Everyone has their strengths and weaknesses, after all. As for you, Sootsy! Just you wait until our next meeting! And Sagittarius, could you stop copying and pasting comments? —Wheat\n\nActing Skills\n[Average]\nI don't want to say it, but your crying makes me want to laugh, Umeko... Please continue practicing. I will add that other than crying, your acting skills are all great—especially when you were pretending to be weak to gain others' trust. —Whitebeard\nHaha. —Moshui\nYou think I'm afraid of you, Wheat? You can't even find yourself a Lightbearer! —Sootsy\nUh... I won't copy the bit about physical attacks. You two fight amongst yourselves. —Sagittarius\nUmeko the Chameleon! LOVE IT! —Cocoa\nThat sobbing was beyond fake... But it can't be helped. All we can do is avoid it as much as possible. If a situation calls for crying, use anger, floundering, or silence as a replacement, if appropriate. —Kara\nI'm glad to see you're finally not playing the role of overly strict parent, Kara. And you! SOOTSY! Just you wait! Mark my words, I'll find a partner capable of smashing you and your Lightbearer to bits! —Wheat"}]},{"id":"diary-20401","title":"Ursa Major and Ursa Minor","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"I arrived at Haven this afternoon and enjoyed a delicious albeit late lunch with Skorri—\"lunner\" as she called it. It seems to be a new trend in Haven, especially popular among the younger crowd. In their opinion, fasting in the evening helps maintain their weight and health. It feels ridiculous, but also a bit...infuriating. It hasn't been long since people were suffering from hunger and cold, yet some spoiled youths refuse to eat of their own will—it's unreasonable! They should be exiled to Tallinn or Brasov up north. A taste of involuntary hunger will make them appreciate the privilege of three square meals a day.\nAfter we finished our \"lunner,\" Radegast sent me a message saying he'd like to meet me at the Archives. There is no prize for guessing what he wanted. \"Jolder, you have been reported three times for unauthorized operations just this month.\" \"Jolder, you must follow the Iron Law.\" \"Jolder, being Iron Champion doesn't excuse you from consequences for your reckless behaviors.\" Will he never tire of these clichés? Were it not for the expanded and redecorated Archives that I hadn't had a chance to see yet, I wouldn't have wasted my time on him.\nTo get him off my back as fast as possible, I asked Skorri to come with me. She seems even more unwilling than me.\nThe meeting ended sooner than I'd imagined, likely connected to how uneasy Radegast looked upon seeing us together. After several attempts to change topics with suggestions like \"establishing a modern poetry database\" courtesy of Skorri, Radegast finally gave up and left in a hurry—she sure knows how to deal with our honored lord.\nAs we were perusing the Archives through the terminal, I stumbled upon some newly entries on ancient myths in the root directory.\nThey were added by Angelo Raum, that man with a fondness for Greek myths and constellations.\nI still remember that time on the Tisza River, when we were chopping up a stranded boat to make firewood, and he suddenly told me to look up. I tried to ignore him, but he would have none of it and walked over to grab my head and force my gaze upward. I punched him square in the face. Covering his bleeding nose with one hand, he laughed and pointed the other at the sky.\nThere, hanging above the north celestial pole, shined the brightest star, surrounded by a dozen slightly dimmer ones. Angelo said we'd been following it for the last two weeks or so. It's the North Star, the brightest one in Ursa Minor. And Ursa Major lies just below it.\nDuring the long stretch of time before the Last City was built, the infinite night sky was nothing but a dangerous shadow and a nest housing horrifying enemies. But now, to a rare astronomy enthusiast like Angelo, it holds another meaning. After the fall of Golden Age civilization, we lost most of the advanced technology used to observe the skies, leaving only a few optical telescopes and the most primal tool—one's own eyes. However, the Collapse also took away the light pollution, letting us observe as many stars as we had millennia ago with just the naked eye.\nAt that time, I had no interest in those celestial bodies, let alone the ancient Greeks' stories surrounding them and the related gods they'd worshiped. But Angelo never stopped trying. Despite my disinterest, he insisted on introducing me to the constellations and the myths behind their names. I don't remember how many times I laughed at him as I asked if he actually knew the locations of those constellations he mentioned. Sometimes I thought he was just pointing at random spots in the sky.\n\n[A folded copy of record: Entry - Greek Myths / Ursa Major and Ursa Minor]\n\nThat was the first time he told me his shield's namesake. He would go on to repeat it many times, but unfortunately, I never got the whole story. All I remember is that an evil queen turned a mother and her son into bears as punishment, cursing them to orbit the sky all year round, never stopping. Maybe this time, I can finally remember this tragic legend in its entirety."}]},{"id":"diary-20402","title":"Action Figure","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Today, Lesnar showed me a new addition to his collection—a carefully-crafted 6-inch action figure, which I was shocked to find looked just like our comrade, Silimar. Lesnar nodded with pride. The toy's resemblance to the real thing is its greatest selling point.\nWhen I said this, Lesnar corrected me angrily, claiming that it is not a toy, but a \"high-end collectible figurine.\" He alleges they are Iron Lord-authorized products. At first, I couldn't believe Radegast would approve such a thing—Silimar probably would, though. To prove the claim's validity, he then took out a meticulously-designed box containing the action figure's instruction manual (can you believe it?), a letter of thanks from its designer (this McFarlane fellow sure loves to ramble), and a certificate of authenticity with a note stating \"Thank you for supporting the righteous deeds of the Iron Lords!\", complete with a flawed Iron Lord emblem and an \"autograph\" that was obviously not Radegast's.\nBut when he told me its price, I felt a bit more convinced. It clearly includes a considerable licensing fee paid to the Iron Lords. How else would it be so expensive?\nLesnar invited me to play with it with undiminished enthusiasm. I have to admit, its level of detail was quite surprising. The face was a spitting image of Silimar's, though the battle axe it came with was undoubtedly Saladin's—it seems the designer's research was a bit lacking. It also had many movable joints. I couldn't help but chuckle as I contorted its body into several funny poses. The real Silimar would rather die than make such gestures, after all.\nLesnar then told me that the next action figure would be based on our resident pessimist, Lord Gheleon. I'm quite looking forward to it, and Lesnar promised to show it to me once he finally gets his hands on it."}]},{"id":"diary-20403","title":"A Training Accident","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Lesnar tore a pectoral muscle while doing bench presses this morning—a foolish and predictable accident, if you ask me. Every time those seamstresses Megan and Felicity come by the well to fetch water, Lesnar always gets extremely excited, eager to show off how much of a \"manly man\" he is. When they were still a ways away, the show-off threw his dumbbell aside and tried to lift the nearly 200kg pump nearby. Unfortunately, he miscalculated when the best chance to display his strength would be. Megan and Felicity walked too slow, and by the time they approached, Lesnar couldn't hold on any longer. Then...tragedy struck. Those poor girls witnessed Lesnar's right pec shrivel up a popped balloon, then the pump came crashing down, right into his torso.\nUgh... Men, right?\nWhile Lesnar's Ghost was reviving him, Rhea and I had to stop our training to comfort the screaming girls. Accidents like these may be overwhelming for them, but for Rhea and I? Let's just say it isn't the first time.\nAfter being revived, Lesnar started practicing jujitsu with Rhea. To prevent any further foolishness on his part, I planned to get rid of the two seamstresses. But then Lesnar suddenly came over, saying that the training ground needed a few new rugs (Rugs? What are you, a dancer?) and how he hoped the seamstresses might help. He continued with his chatting, eventually sending the girls into a fit of giggles. It took threatening Lesnar to get him back to training.\nAt dusk, Megan and Felicity returned with rugs in tow.\nOh, ladies...\nAt the end of our training, Rhea told us a rather good joke. She said she trained \"almost\" every day this week. She \"almost\" worked out on Monday, then again on Tuesday, and Wednesday...\nWhat a hilarious joke! It's funny enough to save her from at least four sets of bench presses next session."}]},{"id":"diary-20404","title":"The Iron Games","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Sangam-13 returned to Haven today. Coherence just finished their latest \"team-building activity\"—hunting a small Fallen House in Tierra del Fuego. To test their latest rifles, of course.\nHearing that I was giving a routine report in Haven, he immediately came to see me and show off their latest line. He swore that with these new products, he'd be sure to regain the winter duathlon championship in the next Iron Games.\nPoor Sangam still struggles to accept having come in second place during the previous winter games. At least he has been the champion once, though—every time I try to stress this fact, he always acts as if I'm mocking him.\nIt's not that I'm picking on him, but if we're being honest, it wasn't exactly a fair win. I'd say it was a total fluke. During the last stage—standing shooting—my rifle got jammed, while Sangam hit all five of his shots. Though I hit all the remaining targets with a thrown shield, the judges deemed it a miss and penalized me for two more minutes, giving Sangam the slight advantage needed to take home the gold.\nCome to think of it, I still feel bitter. My defending record for all events, broken just like that.\nBut Haven's Iron Games haven't been held for several years now. Last time, Radegast asked the committee to reduce the number of events to fourteen and the duration to one week, and even banned me from competing in solo and team events at the same time. I'll bet that was Gheleon's idea—he may act generous, but he can be incredibly petty, and we both know how being beaten by me in the same event three years in a row wounded his pride.\nAfter dinner, it suddenly started raining. I don't want to travel on a dark, rainy night. Maybe I should talk to Radegast before leaving Haven tomorrow. It's high time we held the Iron Games again."}]},{"id":"diary-20405","title":"An Old Friend from Tallinn","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Gillian fought hard against her pneumonia the entire winter, yet she still didn't make it. I received a package with a letter reporting this tragedy from her daughter Cynthia this morning.\nInside was a gilded vintage pocket watch and a lapis bracelet.\nThe watch was a reward from Yekaterina to commemorate her excellent management of the Kraav, while the bracelet was awarded to me by Yekaterina. The day after the riot in Tallinn, I bid Gillian farewell and embarked on my journey, and I gave her this bracelet as a memento before we parted. We both thought that would be the last time we saw each other.\nGillian Fran took care of me back when I was Yekaterina's prisoner. In the dark, precarious Kraav, she was one of the few people who really cared about me—a brave and noble mortal. Without her help, I might not have survived Yekaterina's depraved ideas for \"entertainment.\"\nSometimes being a Lightbearer makes you forget how much damage the powerful weapon of time can do to a mortal. In my memories, those days in Tallinn were short yet somehow endless. Gillian always had the same look back then—I remember her small stature, her dry golden hair, the small red bucket she would carry. She was always energetic and ready to argue. She would pray for every soul unfortunate enough to enter the Kraav. And when the defeated fighters were left there to rot, she shed tears for them and buried their remains, ensuring everyone had a proper ending.\nWhile time and death share the same origin, she remained a more tenacious existence. She refused to be numbed, no matter how many deaths she witnessed. She not only won the gladiators' respect, but also became one of the few mortals respected by that lunatic Yekaterina.\nLater on, she was sent to Lady Frostmire's territory with the other survivors of Tallinn. We wrote to each other for a while, and I learned she'd married and had a daughter, Cynthia.\nThe last time I saw Cynthia, she was only four years old. Before setting off, I asked Epyon what should I bring to a kid as...condolences? None of the gifts I can think of seem...appropriate. And Epyon reminded me, she should be about sixteen years old now. Maybe what she needs is a set of armor, an accurate firearm, and the courage to keep fighting to survive in this world.\nThe day of our attack on Samarkand is approaching. I need to complete this journey before the troops leave. I'll depart tonight.\nMay we reunite in the Light, Gillian.\n[Note to self: Remember to buy a bouquet of white roses from Chantal.]"}]},{"id":"diary-20406","title":"Shopping Woes","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"That cosmetics shop \"Oak Garden\" is unbelievable. Simply unbelievable! Do they think their customers are idiots?\nThey sent the wrong products to me TWICE. I ordered the matte series, and both times, they sent me the shimmering series. What's worse, I ordered Twilight Songbird the third time, and you know what they gave me? Caramel Dream! Which part of my orders did their sorters fail to understand?\nWhen I opened the eyeshadow palette, I was completely shocked. The gray I wanted? It was brown. BROWN! And what about my purplish gray? Why are these two slots empty?\nI had no choice but to contact customer service. Their clerks claimed it was a chromatic difference caused when the packaging was printed, said such variations are completely acceptable, and refused to offer a refund.\nCome on, what kind of printer turns gray into brown? Where did they get them from, the Cabal?\nDespite all the drama, the Twilight Songbird palette looks absolutely stunning—in fact, all of Oak Garden's eyeshadow palettes are beautiful! Their designers must have been kissed by a muse. To be fair, Beauty and the Beast has some eyeshadows with a similar texture, but their packaging is just terrible; Swan Song offers some unique products at fair prices, though the House of Devils raided the town they're located in, so it may be several months before they release anything new.\nRegardless, Oak Garden's customer service is unacceptable... I shouldn't have to get on my Sparrow and eliminate a whole Cabal legion just to return a palette.\nWait... Come to think of it, when it comes to the Iron Lords... Am I just like that palette? Outstanding, excellent, but also with some unbearable defects?\nEpyon's note: Don't be so negative, my Iron Champion. It's not like you!\nEpyon's note: But you really should cut back on the Oak Garden purchases!"}]},{"id":"diary-20407","title":"A Clip from a Mission Report","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"[The content below is live battlefield footage, recorded by Epyon.]\n(Finnala rushes back behind cover while dodging spraying bullets and reports to Saladin.)\n Finnala: Schmeichel has a squad of machine gunners deployed at the breach in the left wall. Their firepower is too strong to break through.\n Saladin: Indeed... We can't risk having our soldiers rushing through again.\n (Saladin turns to two Lightbearers kneeling on the other side of the cover.)\n Saladin: Deblin, Preston, you two follow me to the ridge on the right. We must attack Schmeichel's troops from higher ground.\n (The two Lightbearers begin to rise, but Saladin stops them.)\n Saladin: Be prepared. Schmeichel himself may be holding that place with his Lightbearer lackeys.\n (The camera turns. Jolder fires a hail of bullets toward the breach while approaching Saladin. She seems rather annoyed.)\n Jolder: Saladin! You're too slow.\n (Saladin looks even more annoyed than her. He lands a loud hit on the wall. A cloud of dust rises, and the entire wall trembles as if ready to crumble.)\n Saladin: Where have you been?!\n Jolder: They just sent in their grenadiers, trying to flank us. You're welcome, Saladin.\n Saladin: This is a battlefield. That means you follow my commands!\n (Jolder takes the shield off from her back and exits her cover with it in her hand. The opposing machine gunner notices her immediately and starts firing at her, but she pushes forward steadily, shield raised and bullets ricocheting in all directions. The moment the hail of bullets stops, Jolder throws her shield right at the source. There's a piercing clang of metal on metal, followed by a rising smoke stack. Several pained moans can be heard coming from the breach.)\n Saladin: Jolder! Get back here!\n (Ignoring Saladin's shouts, Jolder stands still in the center of the battlefield.)\n Saladin: JOLDER! If you don't come back this instant, this is going in my report! \n (Jolder turns around and glares at Saladin with rage in her eyes.)\n Jolder: Oh Saladin, for the love of—! Fine! We shall settle this the old fashioned way!\n (Before Saladin can answer, Jolder turns to the dark concrete bunker inside the wall and shouts.)\n Jolder: Schmeichel, I am the Iron Champion, Lady Jolder. I hereby challenge you to a blood duel. You shall accept it and lose, and I shall emerge victorious!\n [The footage ends here.]"}]},{"id":"diary-20408","title":"Metal Cluster \"Worm Nest\"","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"From: Saoirse\nRight, about the research sample you gave us last time. It's most likely a certain type of metal worm that eats and excretes metals—don't worry, it won't eat flesh or clothes. Where did you get them?\nKind Regards,\n—Saoirse, Riddle and Trouble-solver Extraordinaire\n\nAbove is the original message, forwarded to Lady Jolder and Lord Saladin. —From Radegast\n\n\nFrom: Donovan-17\nTo whom it may concern,\nGreetings.\nThe sample for inspection was sent to us 4 days ago. During the last 60 hours, our team has run a series of experiments on this sample. Our findings are as follows:\n1. Preliminary analysis confirms the sample to be a type of metal phage nanobot. According to our research, it is likely a type of industrial robot from the Golden Age capable of efficiently breaking down metal waste in the geosynchronous orbit. Unfortunately, its micro-electronic control system remains a black box for us, thus preventing us from controlling its behaviors. Therefore, we had to take extreme measures to neutralize it following our experiments.\n2. [Images - The sample under electron microscope]\n3. [Chart - Dating results of the sample]\n4. [Links - The electronic tracking code and a list of possible producers of the sample]\n5. [Chart - The motion trail of the sample when active/inactive]\n6. [Videos - The radical metal phage behavior of the sample when active]\n7. [Instructions - Neutralization process and codes]\nOur professional advice is to form an emergency task force comprised of specialists in materials science, ecology, and chemical defense to investigate and destroy the substance swiftly and thoroughly.\nRegards,\n—Donovan, Foresight Laboratories, Haven Armory Confidential Building, B1\n\nAbove is the original message, forwarded to Lady Jolder and Lord Saladin. —From Radegast"}]},{"id":"diary-20409","title":"Two Jokes","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Since when did I become an \"enthusiastic joker with a bad sense of humor\"? It sounds...pathetic.\nThe last time I ran into Wolf in Veridia, I spoke about some embarrassing things Radegast did when I'd first met him. I swear on my shield, beneath that helmet, Wolf must have been grinning from ear to ear, likely just holding back out of respect for a superior and basic manners.\nOh, I learned two new jokes today! I'll share them with Skorri next time I see her.\n\nThe first one: I just sprayed some bug repellant at a mosquito. I guess it's forever single now!\nThe second one: \"Do Not Touch\" is the scariest phrase in Braille.\n\nRhea laughed at my taste in jokes tonight. Very well then—starting tomorrow, she will do 40kg hip thrusts until she passes out.\nEpyon's note: Poor Rhea...\nEpyon's note: Jolder, I don't think that's a joke..."}]},{"id":"diary-20410","title":"New Champions?","sub":"Character diary · Jolder","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_204","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"I ran into Wolf, who was out delivering a toolbox, when I took shelter from the rain in a shed this afternoon. Wolf's Sparrow had just broken down.\nI always get this unique feeling when we chat. Wolf reminds me of Saladin in his younger days, but a bit more wild. That Lightbearer's outlook is a bit idealistic and even romantic, but without being disconnected from reality like Angelo—that \"cowboy hero\" vibe of Wolf's is more like me, though.\nI haven't seen such qualities in Rhea and Lesnar yet, but I'm sure that time will sharpen them like a whetstone to a blade. A true champion must appear imposing and unconstrained. Such self-confidence is the foundation of all things, but it is accumulated only through struggles and frustrations.\nIn terms of temperance and stability, I might not be a good role model. But I'm at least capable of training these two kids to fight, survive, and rise from Iron Apprentices to potential Iron Champions.\nTomorrow will be the fifth anniversary of Rhea and Lesnar's apprenticeship. I still remember the day I first ran into them in Cancun five years ago. These two brave Lightbearers weren't fighters by any means, but even so, they embraced their fate when chosen by their Ghosts. They watched each other's backs and protected the mortal fishermen out at sea, risked life and limb battling Fallen Marauders on the rocky beaches and in the shallows.\nIt's not that Lightbearers don't feel pain—we just get used to it.\nI saw that they were diamonds in the rough, that they could be shaped into brilliant soldiers. With Radegast's permission, I, as Iron Champion, was allowed to have my own apprentices. I sincerely hope they grow to be warriors more wonderful than the Iron Lords themselves. They will surpass me—I know they have it in them.\nCome to think of it, it seems I've never expressed just how proud I am of them. Maybe I should buy a nonfat soy milk cake to celebrate with them? Perhaps I could have the chef write \"Future Champions\" on it, too!"}]},{"id":"diary-21102","title":"An Invitation","sub":"Character diary · Kabr, the Resolute","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_211","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr, the Resolute"},"body":[{"p":"Sender: Skorri\nRecipient: Kabr\nSubject: An Invitation to Lightbearer Kabr\n\nI'm glad I was able to see you again in Haven yesterday, dear. It seems it's been a long time since you last visited. Why, I didn't even recognize you at first! You look and carry yourself so differently these days.\nI'm sure you've been through much since our talk in the tavern back then. It's as if it happened just yesterday, but if it were you as you are now, I'm sure you'd make your choice without hesitation.\nI'm sending this letter to invite you to the Iron Bar's anniversary celebration, this time as a VIP.\nWe need a warrior with a high ranking on our leaderboard to give an outstanding performance. And I know what you're going to say—if it's just a matter of points, then there are plenty of candidates to choose from!\nBut none of them put on an unforgettable show like you did at the opening ceremony, right?\nThis is an unprecedented chance to wipe the slate clean and make a new name for yourself.\nI look forward to your reply.\n\nSender: Kabr\nRecipient: Skorri\nSubject: Re: An Invitation to Lightbearer Kabr\n\nThank you for your invitation, Lady Skorri.\nAs you said, I've thought much since our conversation at the tavern and the Iron Bar's opening ceremony. Since then, I've made a point to experience more of everything. Those adventures, those victories and defeats, all of them shaped me into who I am today.\nIt's thanks to all that I've been through that I can now truly understand what you told me back then, as well as understand how foolish and rash I'd been. I let myself be blinded by a pursuit of ethereal fame.\nFortunately, it was not an error I could not come back from. At the very least, it gave me the courage to embark on a new journey, one in which I found my companions. Before we find the \"golden fleece\" we seek, I cannot halt my steps—not for anything.\nNow that I have crossed unseen depths and shallows, I will soon set a course for my own objective. Thus, I sincerely apologize, but I must turn down your invitation.\nI no longer need fame and glory, for I've already found my own \"great unknown.\"\nI wish you all the best in this year's anniversary celebration."}]},{"id":"diary-31003","title":"\"Operation: Albatross\" Mission Report","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"[A sheet of paper, seemingly printed many years ago.]\nBased on her obsession with the shelter, Agent Umeko submitted an application to HQ to establish a base where she was resurrected. HQ approved the mission and dubbed it \"Operation: Albatross.\" Due to the accidental exposure of the Whisperers' nature, the base was destroyed, and \"Operation: Albatross\" ended in failure.\nThe detailed repot for this mission are as follows.\nWe have selected a site for the base. The building material application process will start once HQ has granted approval.\n...\nThe base's basic buildings are yet to be completed, but refugees fleeing from Warlords have already arrived.\n...\nThe base's civilian population has exceeded 100; it has successfully passed the initial founding stage. Next, we will gradually establish a production line to reduce dependence on external materials.\n...\nWith its growing reputation and a significant increase in the number of refugees seeking safe harbor, the base will soon enter a golden period of development.\n...\nSomeone intentionally set fire to the base's granary today. However, it was discovered immediately, and losses were minimized. We've confirmed the arsonist to be a mole. Three rounds of covert screening will be conducted on civilians within the base, and patrols in key areas will be strengthened.\n...\nRecently, rumors such as \"Ghosts are raising human livestock\" have been circulating the base. We are currently investigating the source of this rumor. The rumor has spread extremely fast and incited unrest among the civilians. We are almost certain the culprit is a Warlord, though we suspect this may be the work of several collaborating Warlords.\nAdditionally, based on current public opinion, we have submitted an application to disclose some information regarding the Whisperers to civilians within the base, alleviate their fear, and determine whether people can accept the Whisperers' style of organization under comfortable living conditions. *The information to be revealed is: ①Ghosts are the primary decision-makers;② Ghosts do not want to rule humans, but rather establish an orderly shelter to protect those in need.\n...\nAs per the application's approval, the information to be revealed will be changed to the following: ①Ghosts and Lightbearers jointly decide how the base develops;② Ghosts hope to live in an orderly, stable shelter.\n...\nFollowing the announcement, the riots within the base ceased for half a day, then grew even more uncontrollable. The rumor has escalated to, \"The Ghosts have brainwashed the Lightbearers and are manipulating them. They want to use the controlled Lightbearers to encroach on mortal humans' lands.\" Civilians have begun to strike, march, and protest, and they are analyzing all the base's past decisions based on current conspiracy theories.\nThe base will make every effort to resolve the crisis through peaceful means.\n...\nSpies provoked the civilians into joining hands with the Warlords both internally and externally. In the end, their combined forces destroyed the base.\nAgent Umeko's identity was exposed during the incident. Thus, in the interest of her safety and freedom to act during future missions, she has voluntarily requested to cover her face with a mask, and vows not to remove it unless absolutely necessary.\n...\n— Report written by: Kara\n\n[A line of small characters that gradually become more illegible.] \nI thought I'd only be facing aliens and Warlords. I never expected the very people I'd tried to protect would..."}]},{"id":"diary-31004","title":"\"Operation: Viper\" Mission Report","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"[A sheet of paper that was printed out very recently.]\nTo address Lor's betrayal of the Whisperers as well as its associated consequences, the Council of Twelve dispatched Enforcer Umeko to handle this case. Utilizing her outstanding adaptability and acting skills, she successfully retrieved the stolen member list in \"Operation: Viper.\"\nMission details are as follows.\n\nIt all started with that cowardly, despicable agent Lor. Tempted by promises from Warlords, he cruelly imprisoned his poor, dutiful Ghost Cocoa, then stole a list of the Whisperers' members. Through his actions, he announced his betrayal.\nI've never seen such heinousness! That list included all of our undercover Ghosts and Lightbearers. For that scoundrel to do such a thing... I can't believe I was so blind... And for all these years, I've hidden what I've had to deal with, all to save HIS face! He's foolish, arrogant, suspicious, testy... And to top it all off, he has poor hygiene! I could just imagine how conversations with other Ghosts would go... They'd all say, \"Poor Cocoa! You deserve a better Lightbearer!\"\nUgh... Now, though, I've finally faced reality. He wasn't that innocent, passionate, kindhearted boy I revived, and he hadn't been for a long time. Thinking back on it, Lor probably got led astray by those Warlords' lackeys when he was undercover on M-C330745! I'd attributed his increasingly indifferent attitude and negativity towards the Whisperers were due to him entering a rebellious period. Who would've thought... Anyway, if any of you are assigned on covert missions, keep a close eye on your Lightbearer, and watch out for any displays of corruption or changes in attitude, so you don't end up like me... Fortunately, Kara and Umeko handled this issue flawlessly. I can't even imagine what would've happened if they hadn't!\n...\nUmeko's professional, reliable performance in handling this list incident is something all Lightbearers could learn from! I'd highly recommend turning it into a case study! Professional abilities aside, Umeko's personality is also the best of the best! She treats us with such patience and kindness, and she even brings us gifts when she leaves for far-away missions! Whether I share my joys with her or tell her about my troubles, she always listens attentively and gives me all the responses I need. All Lightbearers could learn a thing or two from her!\nAlso... Given that Lor's a lost cause (in every sense of the word, now), can I apply to train a new Lightbearer? Like a Ghost co-pilot! I don't want just any Lightbearer, though. I'll only accept one as good as Umeko! (Or one 3/4 as good. The lowest I'll go is 1/2.)\n —Report written by: Cocoa\n\n [A line of small characters, written with brush and ink.]\nOnly Cocoa could possibly write such a report. ◡‿◡"}]},{"id":"diary-31005","title":"\"W-00119\" Mission Report","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"[A printed sheet of paper that looks neither new nor old.]\nThanks to the early deployment of the \"Black Cotton\" squad, we were able to lay the groundwork necessary to eradicate the Warlord Mosok. The Council of Twelve dispatched Enforcer Umeko for this decapitation strike. Despite her headstrong nature and unwillingness to cooperate with the original plan, with Black Cotton's full cooperation, she carried out the mission successfully and without incident, rescuing an additional 314 civilians in the process.\nMission details are as follows.\n\\...\nEnforcer Umeko was supposed to quickly execute the established combat plan after meeting with our team. However, due to her refusal to use more powerful weaponry and her insistence on assassinating Mosok in a solo infiltration, the operation was temporarily deadlocked.\nOur team believed the solo combat plan Umeko proposed to be far too risky, with both the possibility of operational failure and irreversibly heightened risk. We insisted on adhering to the original plan: detonating all ammunition Mosok received in his new weapons shipment, inflicting the maximum amount of damage to both the target and his Ghost, then initiating further battles based on the situation.\nBut Umeko, in the absence of successful communication between the two parties, used her position as the plan's executor to forcibly change strategies, ignoring the favorable opening that our team had worked hard to create. With great patience, we tried to persuade Umeko up until the very end, but she initiated her infiltration anyway, forcing our team to compromise.\n...\nOnce the mission concluded, the Black Cotton squad should have returned to HQ directly to report, but due to Umeko demanding we rescue the civilians, our report was delayed by 18 days.Umeko's refusal to cooperate caused great trouble for our squad throughout this operation. If every Enforcer is like her, what use is the preliminary work done by covert teams such as ours? Do we not deserve respect? Does our hard work count for nothing? \nOn behalf of all Ghosts and Lightbearers in our squad, I am hereby formally filing sixteen complaints against Enforcer Umeko and her Ghost, including \"extremely uncooperative,\" \"amplification of mission failure risk,\" \"last-minute change of plans,\" \"increased burden on our squad's retreat,\" \"ignoring our squad's previous achievements,\" \"harsh and disrespectful language,\" etc. (see appendix for details).\nIn light of the immense psychological harm her actions have caused to all of our Ghost and Lightbearer members, the Black Cotton squad has decided to go on strike and protest until she receives the appropriate punishment!\n— Report written by: Supervising Ghost, Black Cotton Squad\n\n[A line of small characters, written with brush and ink.]\nThey drag their feet when it comes to rescuing civilians, but they sure are speedy when it comes to typing up reports. They didn't even check my mission failure rate before submitting their complaints.\nNothing but a bunch of selfish, egotistical fools. Go ahead, strike all you want."}]},{"id":"diary-31006","title":"\"R-00317\" Mission Report","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"[A printed sheet of paper that looks neither new nor old.]\nOur intelligence showed that a fishing village on the northwest side of the Baltic Sea had salvaged an item with peculiar characteristics. Following their preliminary evaluation, the Council of Twelve determined this item could be used as a Lightbearer's Relic and dispatched Enforcer Umeko to retrieve it.\nMission details are as follows.\n\nPray, children of flesh and blood; pray for the Traveler's mercy, for its majesty; pray for all the blessings and sorrows borne by its Light.\nSing, creatures of the secluded bay; sing for the waves of the Baltic, for the never-ending catches.\nWhich child of Light lifted this strange object? Which ignorant fool imagined it a boon from the God of Good Harvest?\nThey dedicate all their songs, all their dances, to Freyr, ever ignorant that the Light is the answer to all.\nBut fear not, children. Fear not. The Light's followers shall step forth with the winds, returning all to its rightful state.\n\nThey watch as she gathers her robes, listen as she delivers her gentle admonishment. \"Freyr perished long ago, in the Collapse. The brilliant mind devoured shall never return. Be wary of all that make use of His name.\"\nThe people are panicked, yet still they cling to their doubts.\nThus, she wields her Light, and in a faint voice, she recites, \"The abyss approaches. Stay ever vigilant, for the wave that drowns all draws near.\"\nThen, a violet radiance flowed through the brick walls and wove through the tips of her hair, like a soul wandering through limbo. At last, terror descended upon them. The lambs panicked for naught, and the rooster ceased his crowing. Yet from the mud and crevices crawled the insects, scurrying towards the light. As if pulled by forces unseen, they converged and flowed as a river through the village, from morning till night, never ceasing.\nNo longer was the strange object a symbol of good harvest; rather, it became bait for an evil that would consume the land. And thus the people said a new prayer: deliver us from this cursed artifact!\nTheir answer came when she rang a bell, and her Void Light whisked the Relic away.\n\n —Report written by: Baltic Regional Intelligence Officer (and the greatest Ghost bard in the Baltics) Njord"}]},{"id":"diary-31007","title":"Haven General Report - 045 (Umeko)","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"Haven is a place that's exceeded my expectations.\nI thought it'd be more or less the same as other human settlements, but it's far more prosperous and peaceful than I'd ever imagined. The way people live here—it's as if Earth was never invaded. They argue over price tags they think unreasonable, but they also offer supplies and support to newly arrived refugees.\nPrior to my arrival in Haven, I'd read all 44 reports regarding this city in the archives, and I always took the \"stability\" they'd mentioned with a grain of salt. That was until I came here for myself and saw a kind, gentle, and well-proportioned cat. First impressions of cities can be deceptive, but the animals within them? Not so. They offer outsiders a comprehensive view of a city's nature in just a glance.\nWith my overview of the city's situation complete, I will now summarize my observations of each functional area and key personnel in Haven.\n...\nAs a final note, I think...perhaps the Iron Lords here really are different? I'm not sure. People are so fickle. Who can possibly guarantee that they will always adhere to their true intentions? That their twisted desires won't control them?\nI truly like Haven and hope they can become a steadfast ally. If there is such a possibility, I will volunteer to lead related missions."}]},{"id":"diary-10303","title":"Sights from Europe","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"Bullet Hole Monument\nAll that's left of the Golden Age are bones. There are bones in the literal sense, of course. Human bones scattered in the wild, some still sitting in the husks of vehicles, long past needing a proper burial. Then there are the ruins covered in weeds—the skeletons of long-abandoned buildings. No matter how glorious their past was, now, they're but crumbling walls. Be it skeletons or rubble, both are commemorations of bygone days. And among them rest some manmade objects with more unique looks. Though built to withstand the test of time, they lack any practical usages beyond remembering the past. The continent of Europe is filled with such things—monuments of various shapes and sizes. One of them looked relatively plain, yet still left quite the impression. It's composed of two upright slabs with roughly-cut concave edges facing each other, looking as if a giant bullet had pierced through them. No doubt erected in memory of a major pre-Golden Age war. Ironically, that war brought only fleeting respite to the majority of humankind. The flames of war would be fanned again soon after, then came a renewed peace and new monuments. On and on, the cycle would continue...\n\nMerry Cemetery\nI once read a story about this place, introducing its navy tones, the pointed roofs adorning all the tombstones, and the colored illustrations those roofs shelter, which tell stories about the permanent residents resting below. Most of the illustrations are portraits, but some are snapshots providing a look into the deceased's life. A young man driving a combine, a man playing the violin with a friend, an old lady in a black hood reading at a desk—all of these illustrations lighten the gloom of the cemetery, hence the locals calling it the Merry Cemetery. When we actually set foot here, though, we found that most of the graves had fallen into disrepair. They were faded, damaged, even covered in thick blankets of dust. But Attal still checked the pictures on every tombstone with excitement. Our hands were positively filthy by the end. We also found several new tombstones. Their paint was more vivid, and though the decorations on them were humble imitations of the older graves', they still featured illustrations celebrating the lives of the deceased. In one of them, a warrior was celebrating a victory over the Fallen. Before departing, we left behind two bullets at each of the new graves. Maybe one day, this place can regain the cheery look I saw in the books.\n\nMountain Cemetery\nLocated in Eastern Europe, this cemetery contained all the elements one would expect of such a place—dead trees, crawling vines, damp soil, and moss-covered headstones. The only difference was the density of graves within. The tombstones stuck out from the soft soil with no sense of organization, and some had almost completely sunken into the earth. In addition to the grassland dotted with countless graves, there were a couple of hills overflowing with stacked tombstones. Before the Collapse, this cemetery had served as the final resting place for centuries of residents. Local tradition dictated that tombstones not be moved, and thus over time, they became more and more crowded. These hills weren't natural; rather, they were formed by new gravestones being placed and crowding the old ones before the cemetery expanded. And around the cemetery, we could see a huddle of ruins, indicating that this was once a central part of the town. The living and dead crowded together, blurring the boundary between this world and the afterlife."}]},{"id":"diary-31008","title":"Lightbearer Observations (updating)","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"[Haven]\nZev: Friendly and patient with an excellent personality. Seemingly no flaws. If you can, please be kind to her.\nWolf: Will undoubtedly help you if you appear to be in need of aid, but is very quick-witted. Will notice and respond to any flaws in your act immediately. Overall, a good person.\n\nOphiuchus: Practically a floating encyclopedia, but with a rigid and serious personality. He's basically a stricter version of Whitebeard (if Whitebeard actually read all those books he keeps at his residence). Fantasy novels can be an icebreaker.\nIkora: A knowledgeable scholar who seems to harbor many secrets. She tends to roam, is very vigilant, and seems to lack patience when it comes to anything troublesome.\n\nEpyon: Like a harsher, more mature version of Cocoa. She has full confidence in her Lightbearer, Jolder, and she almost unconditionally supports all of her decisions. She's not very fond of Jolder's apprentices, though. All that's needed to get close to Epyon is ample yet appropriate praise for Jolder.\nJolder: The famed Iron Champion. Possesses the chivalry of a knight, but can often be aggressive and harsh. She likes collecting shiny accessories and is a makeup enthusiast. This may be a good way to get close to her.\n\nTethra: Rarely appears and seldom speaks. Need to gather more information.\nTan-2: Often talks to himself—perhaps some sort of mental disorder? Overall, he's a passionate and kind person, like a younger version of Wolf. Although he seems easily exploited, his \"second personality\" is harder to get a read on. Needs further observation.\n\nCrowther: A maverick of a Ghost. Likes goth and rock music. His Lightbearer Gwynn is his entire world, to the point where he prevents others from getting close to her. Getting close to him is similar to getting close to Epyon, but your praise and adoration for Gwynn can be even more enthusiastic. Note: Kara really doesn't like him. Might be a clash of personalities.\nGwynn: On an emotional level, she appears to be weaker than the average person. Fortunately, her pursuit is justice, which generally aligns with the Whisperers' goals. Best not to approach.\n\nSwift: A patient, good-tempered steward who seems very experienced and knowledgeable on many topics. Not an easy target to deceive. If you must deal with him and his Lightbearer Attal, I recommend approaching them with sincerity.\n\nAttal: A naïve and immature young woman who is friendly to all—somehow, this even includes the Fallen. She also shares a very close bond with Gwynn. Any operations targeting Gwynn may be able to exploit this.\n\nShams: Most of the time, he shoulders the responsibility of translating Kabr's slightly unconventional ideas for others. Has quite the lively personality. (Maybe he'd get along well with Cocoa?)\nKabr: Extremely passionate about making a name for himself. He's a bit of a hothead, but won't do anything to cause major harm. His \"legend\" would be effective bait.\n..."}]},{"id":"diary-31009","title":"Relic Modification Request","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"[A sheet of paper, seemingly printed many years ago.]\nThis application for modifications to Umeko's Relic \"Ayakiba\" is being submitted in response to her relatively weak performance in the \"Cooperative Combat Capabilities\" portion of her \"Enforcer\" exam.\nModification Expectations: 1. The modification should be capable of supporting teammates in cooperative combat, enabling her to quickly gain their trust and reduce the difficulty of missions.\n 2. The modification cannot be overly conspicuous to the point of making others realize the Relic has been altered. 3. Visual effects must match Umeko's combat style to avoid raising suspicion.\nModification Proposal: I propose a multi-person healing module be added to Ayakiba. Such a module can meet all three of the aforementioned expectations while also keeping Umeko herself safer. Such a module can be used in multi-person, cooperative combat, as well as in solo combat.\n— Applicant: Kara\n\nStatus: Approved\n\nNote: After careful discussion, we have decided to adopt the proposal to add a multi-person healing module to Ayakiba. Given the Relic's current performance, we recommend Umeko activate it while in \"Voidstep.\"\n\n[A line of small characters, written with brush and ink.]\nThank you."}]},{"id":"diary-31010","title":"New Year's Present Shopping List","sub":"Character diary · Umeko","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_310","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Umeko"},"body":[{"p":"[Classic Poetry Anthology *3] [Blank Book with Stick-On Book Cover *1]\n\nWhitebeard's room is filled with poetry collections, so he must like them. But... How exactly does he read physical books...? I'll find a blank book and stick a poetry anthology cover on it . We'll see if Whitebeard finds out...\n\n[Ghost Figurine *1]\nI don't know why Moshui is so crazy about Ghost figurines, but I respect it. (I do find them very cute, but I'm not nearly at his level of obsession.)\n\n[Sparkly Trinkets *4-5]\nCocoa loves this kind of stuff. I'll buy whatever trinkets I see that catch the light. (I need to remember what I've given her previously, though. Can't buy any repeats.)\n\n[\"Agreed.\" Signboard *1]\nNothing could be more appropriate for Sagittarius, our resident \"copy machine.\"\n\n[Soft, Thick Hat *1]\nSootsy really likes resting on her Lightbearer's head. Maybe she'd be comfortable on something like this? (Try to find a hat that's concave on top.)\n\n[Ghost Shells *12]\n\nCan't buy any repeats. Once I find a suitable style, I'll need to get their names engraved on them.\n\nAs for Wheat... I have no idea what I should give him. The thing he wants most is to find his own Lightbearer—maybe I should go to a shrine and get him an en musubi omamori for good luck? I'll look around. If that's a no-go, then I'll just take the lazy way out."}]},{"id":"diary-20620","title":"Plunderer's Trove","sub":"Character diary · Maru","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_206","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Maru"},"body":[{"p":"A Wooden Carving with Unique Totem Motifs\nA gift from a tribe on the island of my resurrection, a land embraced by warm, tropical winds. I'd once integrated with the local residents, but when I chose to set sail, not all of them chose to follow me out to sea. They were unwilling to part with the land they were blood-bound to. This wooden carving appeared among the supplies they'd prepared for me, appearing out of place among various weapons and equipment.\nLiving such a long life has left me unable to remember just how many nights I've dreamed about that island while caressing the fading patterns. The totem was painted with special pigments, and they've remained clear even after enduring storms, symbolizing my connection with it. I was reborn there, grew up there again, like a child. Even with thousands of miles separating us, I can still feel the tremors of that land and my heart beating at the same frequency.\n\nA Mostly Damaged Microcomputer\nTaken while we were dismantling a spacecraft. Even if we could fix it, its performance wouldn't be anything to write home about. The only reason I've kept it is the log saved to the database of its navigation system. Its former owner was a space photography enthusiast, so various images of the cosmos occupy the log as opposed to coordinates and events. It has little practical value, but it does give me something nice to admire in my spare time.\n\nA Locket\nWhen we made this necklace, we were busy renovating that Golden Age spaceship. I cobbled this together with scraps of material. Parrot told me that in the distant past, sailors and pirates used them to store a lock of a loved one's hair or other small mementos. I don't have anything to commemorate, so it's currently empty and gathering dust as a decoration. However, on the day when I truly set sail, perhaps I'll pack some of Earth's soil and flowers inside."}]},{"id":"diary-30301","title":"Gun Trial Records","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"Auto Rifle: Versatile, but its high rate of fire leads to decreased accuracy. It also makes the body feel cumbersome, putting it at odds with my usual combat style. Suitable as a daily firearm, but not worth spending too much time on modifications and adjustments.\nSubmachine Gun: Versatile with a fair rate of fire. Smaller than an auto rifle, but still a bit bulky. Its most critical problem is its bullet spread. The auto rifle's is tolerable, but not the submachine gun's. If I had to pick between a lighter weight or more accuracy, I'd pick accuracy.\nSidearm: More my style better, but not powerful enough to take out an enemy quickly. Perhaps modifications can give it a boost? How much it can be enhanced is extremely limited though, given its structure. The gun's size is perfect, but its firepower? Not so much.\nHand Cannon: Highly portable, powerful, and works very well with how I fight. Unfortunately, the hand cannon fires just one shot at a time. That single shot hits hard, though. The sidearm has a high rate of fire, but its power is lacking... It's unfortunate. Would be nice to build on all the hand cannon's current traits and adjust it to fire full auto.\nAs for pulse rifles, scout rifles, and light grenade launchers... Those pieces of scrap should have been discontinued, with the resources saved for designing more deadly hand cannons."}]},{"id":"diary-30302","title":"Calm","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"I came to the Red Sea Rift to draw an end to my path of vengeance.\nThe scenery here reminds me of when I first set off on this journey—same bright sun, same burning sand.\n\nHartford said that I was full of anger back then. Was I? I have no idea. Those days are hazy memories. It's as if I was locked in a prison built of remorse and resentment—cold, hard, and gray.\nI should've known... Maln was a profiteer, after all. He and Marco were bound to have a clash of interests and ideals. I thought the worst that could happen was that he'd part ways with us, but I'd never imagined that he'd kill Marco's Ghost himself.\nAnd what was I doing back then? I left that village without them just because I thought it'd be too much trouble. After learning of Marco's death, I kept thinking...if I'd stayed with him, would he still be alive?\nI insisted on tracking Maln down, following the trail that led me on this journey, thinking it would ease the pain. But somehow, at some point, I began noticing the ochre canyons, the frozen straits, the sprawling meadows... I was still tracking that backstabber, but he wasn't all I was after anymore.\nI stopped blaming Maln. It was my indifference and selfishness that were responsible for Marco's death. The moment I chose to take the blame, my prison melted like ice in the scorching sun.\n\nThis is a fine end to that path I'd been on.\nThe wind and sand that blew from the Mojave all the way to the Red Sea Rift could finally rest."}]},{"id":"diary-10301","title":"Snowy Mountain Journey I - Night","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"The wind on the mountains finally died down somewhat once night fell. Like iron maidens hidden in plaster statues, fatal dangers lurk beneath its serene appearance. Only once they trap you do you realize it's too late to escape. The frigid winds are but one of many threats. As we approached the summit, it became harder to breathe. The cold had rendered me numb to all sensation. I hadn't even noticed the blood dripping from my nose to the ground until I saw Attal's wide, horrified eyes staring at me.\n\nAttal's excitement and confidence dissipated when we began our climb. Though she had previously sworn to reach the peak, her focus is now entirely on curling up to keep warm. Crowther was sensible enough to keep his voice down for a change, and only an hour into our journey, he stopped chiming in with his opinions altogether. Of course, that may be because I warned him that loud noises would cause an avalanche. I read up on some local folklore before setting off. Allegedly, evil spirits were once sealed away in the mountains. Being exposed up there did make me feel uneasy, but I can probably chalk that up to altitude sickness. The towering, snowy peak in the distance stares down invaders like a giant. We saw no traces of human dwellings, but a vague silhouette of a signal tower hidden in the clouds seems to be looming on the mountainside. A warlord's fortress, perhaps?\n\nTraversing this place alone would undoubtedly be faster, for I have no problem welcoming death's cold embrace. Even if said death would be cold in the literal sense. In any case, Crowther would wake me up from my short break and push me to keep going. But when accompanied by Attal, who rejects that icy temptation, we must consider the risk of hypothermia. For tonight, we've found a spot to camp behind a giant boulder. Hopefully, we'll cross the next ridge tomorrow."}]},{"id":"diary-10302","title":"Snowy Mountain Journey II - Snowfield","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"The seemingly boundless mountain has bounds after all. After more than a month of trekking, we finally glimpsed the world beyond. We still have a few ridges blocking our path, but now we know that a massive snowfield awaits us on the other side. I could also make out the large, square silhouette of a walled city on the horizon. I was more interested in that thing I'd thought was a signal tower, though—that blurred dark line in the clouds had finally shown its complete form.\n\nNow I could see it was a tall column structure fixed to giant pedestal, reaching high into the sky. Crowther said it was a space elevator. We hadn't seen such methods of traveling to space up until now, having only passed by some rusty ruins of what used to be launch pads. The launch pads had complicated steel structures, but they felt much less...mysterious than this building up ahead, reaching far beyond our sight to link with some fulcrum in space. Speaking of space, I'm curious as to what it's like. If there's only a cold nothingness up there, what makes it any different from death?"}]},{"id":"diary-10304","title":"Miss Peacemaker","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"Miss Peacemaker is exceptionally persistent in her ideals, but not out of naivety—she's seen those brutes and the evil they spread. She holds fast to her conviction regardless, believing that kind deeds will be reciprocated. Unfortunately, all her attempts so far have been in vain. In this era of turbulence, death is the sinners' only penance.\n\nThough Attal believes in humanity's capacity for good, what she gets is typically disappointment. Once, we met two vagabonds who asked us for food. Attal just opened her backpack to share her reserves with them, no questions asked, completely ignoring the fact that they were in nowhere near as dire of straits as they claimed. They were both fit and armed, judging by the protrusions of weapons at their hips. Even if they didn't have bad intentions, they were fully capable of finding their own supplies. So Crowther and I scared them away. After that, Attal still insisted that her kindness would inspire them to pass it on.\n\nI often butt heads with Attal when it comes to dealing with strangers, and our differing attitudes toward the enemy have even divided us. One instance I'll never forget was when I passed judgment on Warlord Ramsay. At that time, Attal insisted on believing Ramsay's empty promises, and thus I decided to take him out before he could take advantage of her trust. Of course, that cunning warlord had already set his traps. Just like Walter, he thought torture could force me into submission. But before Crowther could execute his resurrection plan, Attal broke into the dungeon he'd trapped me in. After seeing the predicament at hand, she finally understood—albeit with disappointment—that Ramsay had told her nothing but lies. Her disappointment ignited flames of anger, driving her to temporarily forsake her pursuit of kindness. After eliminating the pursuing guards, she burned down Ramsay's base without hesitation.\n\nIn that incident, I saw a part of myself in her—a part that didn't belong to Attal at all. Perhaps I shouldn't be too harsh on her ideas of peace. After all, such a...belief is rather rare in this day and age. I shall keep observing each and every one of \"Miss Peacemaker's\" attempts."}]},{"id":"diary-10306","title":"Verdict","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"This scythe was originally a gift from a German monastery. It holds little historical value as far as antiques go, but it is clearly a work of Golden Age craftsmanship. It was forged with a special metal and resonates with the wielder's Light. Once it is fully unfolded, its blade glows with lilac fluorescence. The village this scythe once called home was suffering a Fallen invasion at the time. Those four-armed creatures, just like the bloodthirsty warlords, knew nothing of mercy. After Attal's attempts at peaceful negotiation resulted only in some sort of insect-like noises resembling mocking laughter, I \"politely\" responded with my axe and shotgun. After a whole day of fighting, a friar of the village monastery gave me the title of Die Sensenfrau and insisted I take this black scythe.\n\nAfter that, I made a few upgrades to the weapon using a special material from a laboratory on Venus that I bought off a black market merchant. According to the merchant, it's just a common chunk of metal in the hands of most, but when influenced by Light, it can create a singularity capable of twisting gravity itself. At first, I didn't want to spend all my Glimmer on such an absurd-sounding material. But then the merchant targeted Attal's Mint, planning to take the handicraft she'd spent so much effort making. In the end, I was the \"proud\" owner of a chunk of outlandish metal. I shaped it into a sphere and inlaid it on my scythe's blade (although I'd initially intended to make an hourglass out of it). To my surprise, the merchant had been telling the truth. My scythe became one worthy of a true reaper, with the Light and gravity both sapping sinners' vitality once the verdict is issued. Attal and Crowther, however, are less interested in its energy gathering capabilities than they are the gravity twist's side effect—a small wormhole generated not far away."}]},{"id":"diary-10307","title":"Memories Before Sleep","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"I've read that hypnic jerks are the feeling of falling as one begins to fall asleep, but the spasms I feel are different, created instead by dreams of my own past deaths. Thanks to that dead good-for-nothing Walter, I've experienced nearly all ways to meet Death. Many years have passed, yet I feel those memories as vividly as ever, like the phantom pain after losing a limb.\n\nI remember the air in my lungs getting thinner, the hopeless suffocation that deep breaths wouldn't help, and the strange peace that followed. I remember the rope tied around my neck, the metallic taste of blood rushing into my mouth, then the heat flooding back into my lungs. I remember the unnatural feeling of pain giving way to numbness as my fingers were pierced by nails. These and so many others—burns, bullet wounds, slashed tendons—were all \"gifts\" from Walter. In his attempts to force me into submission, he killed me twenty-six times in a day. Twenty-six times I embraced death, yet not once did I get to enjoy that eternal peace.\n\nBut now it is all over, and he has paid his price. I smashed his Ghost to ensure he would stay asleep—it would be rude to wake him, after all. As for the memories, they may still awaken my instinctive reactions, but I feel as if I'm watching movies starring myself. The villain is dead, but the story isn't over. The tyrants and criminals that still walk among the living will pay for their sins—none shall escape eternal slumber."}]},{"id":"diary-10308","title":"Death's Shadow","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"I met Death many times while I was tortured and imprisoned by Walter. Strangely, He would appear before me not after I died, but when I would take my last breath. He appeared in a black robe every time. Though blurred and ethereal like a mist, I could always recognize Him. His form and voice varied—sometimes that of an elder, sometimes that of a woman, and other times indistinguishable, but always hoarse and relentless, like a cold breeze wafting out from an empty crypt. But I knew it was Him. The grim reaper, the scythe-wielding skeleton, the black angel that whisks away souls... Books describe many different identities, all of which are Him.\n\nHe would always quietly arrive in a blink, looking down at me as I lay dying on the ground. In the beginning, I thought He would take me with Him, that He would free me from Walter's imprisonment, but He just looked at me quietly until I fell into a deep, deep slumber. The next time, I begged Him to bring me along, yet He always answered with just a single word—sometimes \"wait,\" other times \"patience.\" The voice was prolonged, as if time had stopped flowing. It carved itself into my mind and even frequented my dreams. I began to follow His advice and endured Walter's torment. Gradually, my fear of pain and death disappeared without a trace. Every death was a rebirth, a chance to be free until my verdict arrived.\n\nAfter executing Walter, I donned a black robe in His image and began wandering the world. Evildoers feared me, and those I rescued called me by His name. There are many more awaiting Him—many more awaiting His sentence. Thus I shall keep upholding relentless justice until He finally takes me away with Him..."}]},{"id":"diary-10309","title":"The Judged","sub":"Character diary · Gwynn","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_103","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Gwynn"},"body":[{"p":"Mors omnia iudicat et nemini indulget.\nThe following is a record of the sinners sentenced to death.\n\nWalter\nEnslaved and tortured others. Hanged.\n\nAneirin\nThreatened people and massacred the innocent. Died in a duel.\n\nTegan\nControlled people using medicines. Abused and massacred people. Hanged.\n\nMallobaude\nMassacred and enslaved people. Stole supplies. Hanged.\n\nWyther\nSlaughter and destruction of a village. Responsible for the massacre in Dinant. Beheaded.\n\nOphevoks\nMassacred the innocent. Died in a duel.\n\nFreak-4\nEnslaved and tortured others. Beheaded.\n\nIngrid\nBurned down a village, enslaved people, blood-thirsty. Perished in flames.\n\nEgon-10\nEnslaved people to join his legion and raided to take more slaves. Beheaded.\n\nDmitri\nEnslaved people, blood-thirsty. Died in a duel.\n\nVoid-6\nCommitted massacres and threatened people by crippling them. Beheaded.\n\nRamsay\nConducted human experiments, torture, and enslavement. Perished in flames."}]},{"id":"diary-30304","title":"New Hand Cannon","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"Today, I had an auto hand cannon custom-made with the Radiancite I got from Bobak (I honestly didn't expect him to care so much about me saving his uncles). Had to supply most of the ore myself, though—that little bit he had didn’t go very far.\nI remember him thinking he could be on good terms with both me and Maln initially. He couldn't have been more wrong. It's not his fault, though. I'd planned on Maln finding out anyway since he'd never show his face around me if he didn't think he was at an absolute advantage.\nI didn't think this whole thing would put so much pressure on Bobak, though—especially after I saved them.\nAnd when he insisted I take the ore... Well, the way his face shriveled up as he cried was unexpectedly heartwarming, even if he got snot bubbles all over me... Never mind. I'll forgive him this time, seeing as he inspired the name of my new gun.\n\nHe said what I told him when I went to meet Maln was \"pretty cool\" and suggested I name my new gun after that.\n\"It's time to hear his last words.\"\nNot a bad idea, I'll give him that. Here's hoping Tex Mechanica brings this hand cannon to life."}]},{"id":"diary-30306","title":"Memo: Request No.37","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"Request: Track the target and bring it to the client (Note: Non-injurious coercion may be used if the target resists)\nTarget's Age: 6 years old\nTarget's Personality: Curious, innocent, lively, wary of strangers (Note: Snacks and toys can be used to ease the target's vigilance)\nTarget's Characteristics: Pointed ears, round eyes, brown tiger spots, white chest, pink nose, three pink and one brown paw pads (Note: Mixed colors)\nTarget's Possible Locations: Children's gatherings, lush vegetation, places birds flock to (Note: Target is playful), places that smell of food (Note: Target is gluttonous)\nSolution: Tie feathers to Hartford to disguise him as a bird and lure the target to grab him. Alternatively, tie a few pieces of meat to Hartford to disguise him as food and lure the target to pounce. Hartford refused to cooperate. Looks like we'll need to improvise. (Bring the disguises in case he changes his mind later? )\n\n(Newer handwriting)\nHartford is very stubborn and unlikely to budge on this."}]},{"id":"diary-30307","title":"Silence is Golden","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"I truly cannot fathom how some people can drone on and on. Personally, I'd rather spend ten times as long finishing those fights alone.\nHartford occasionally encourages me to make some friends, saying that it's not good for me to be too much of a loner (hah, not like he has many friends himself). But what's wrong with being alone? You don't have to take into account your companion's thoughts, you don't have to carry the burden of their emotions, you don't have to be responsible for their well-being, and you don't have to worry about their sudden betrayal, either.\nEveryone has their price. A meal, a piece of clothing, a weapon, something that can be put on the other side of the scale—and you never know when you'll be your companion's price. In that case, it's better not to give them the opportunity to sneak you onto that scale.\nBesides, I'm actually content with just having Hartford as my partner. He's calm, cool, and I can appreciate his restrained sense of humor. Why should I go find myself a ticking time bomb when I've got him?\nSpeaking of Hartford, I once heard a theory advocating complementarity—\"opposites attract\" and stay together longer, or something to that effect. If that were true and Hartford or I... Well, I can't even imagine what a talkative Hartford would be like. But if he were, I'd rather he leave me dead.\nAlthough I get along well with Hartford, to my dismay, it seems like going forward I'll have no choice but to join other Lightbearers on certain missions.\nI can only pray that they aren't chatterboxes."}]},{"id":"diary-30308","title":"A Tip","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"I accepted three more requests to deal with alien looters this week. If I don't get any new jobs tomorrow, I'll be able to get to work on them.\nI still prefer these kinds of requests over escort missions or rescues—no need for careful, detailed plans, just aiming and firing for the most part. Talking with the client after completing their request is annoying. They're too grateful, as if I'm helping them out of the goodness of my heart. Have they forgotten that this is a mere trade? My actions aren't selfless. I wouldn't even bother with those alien looters if I wasn't getting paid.\nSome time ago, I took care of a Cabal camp that was stationed near a town, as the pay was quite generous. When I headed back to tell them the deed was done, the townsfolk swarmed me. They looked so crazy, for a moment I thought they meant to kill me—turns out they just wanted to thank me.\nTalk about a handsome payday.\nIt was just business.\nBut I couldn't say that in front of those kids that rushed over with them—not when they looked so happy. Hartford encouraged them to send me flowers as a token of their appreciation, and surprisingly, the kids complied.\nI'll accept the flowers as a tip.\n...Fine, I'll throw in some extra threat elimination services next time, free of charge."}]},{"id":"diary-30309","title":"Friendship Protection Agreement v2.03","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"(Aesthetic, vintage, flourished lettering)\nI have received much negative feedback from other Ghosts regarding Jaren being too unforgiving when sparring with other Lightbearers, which has seriously affected the friendship between myself and my fellow Ghosts.\nAfter several negotiations, Hartford the Ghost and Jaren the Lightbearer hereby certify the following Letter of Guarantee.\n\n1. Jaren the Lightbearer may not kill any opponent while sparring.\n1. Jaren the Lightbearer shall try not to kill any opponent while sparring.\n1. Jaren the Lightbearer shall conclude sparring with other Lightbearers on friendly terms, without excess harm.\n2. Jaren the Lightbearer shall ensure that he does not defeat the same Lightbearer twice or more while sparring.\n2. Jaren the Lightbearer shall ensure that he does not unreservedly deal a fatal blow against other Lightbearers every time while sparring just because they can be resurrected by their Ghosts.\n3. Jaren the Lightbearer shall avoid mocking a Lightbearer whom he has defeated while sparring—even if it was \"meant to be playful\"—unless said Lightbearer makes impertinent remarks first.\n3.1. Clause 3 also applies to limb movements and hand gestures.\n3.2. Clause 3 also applies to facial expressions and any onomatopoeia that does not have a specific meaning.\n3.3. That includes whistling!\n4. Jaren the Lightbearer shall try to maintain the friendship between Hartford the Ghost and other Ghosts (including, but not limited to, normal social situations such as sparring with other Lightbearers, chats, trades, non-principled arguments, et cetera).\n*This Letter of Guarantee is effective indefinitely.\n\nGuarantor:\n\n(Newer writing)\nJaren, do not forget to sign the guarantee!"}]},{"id":"diary-30310","title":"Combat Operation—Preparation Plan","sub":"Character diary · Jaren","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_303","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Jaren"},"body":[{"p":"Environment: Confirm the terrain, landforms, and spatial characteristics of the target location. Prepare for possible traps, and check for hidden doors and passages in suspicious places.\n\nEnemies: Observe their usual weapons and elemental attributes, and draw up a plan to counteract any unfavorable conditions.\n\nOther: Confirm the relationship between nearby human settlements and the target location, and formulate a detailed response plan based on it (Friendly: Maintain distance, tempt with promise of gains. Hostile: Clarify the advantages and disadvantages of the operation and confirm recent combat plans of both parties to avoid chaos. Neutral: Mainly coercion, in case they plan to hijack the operation).\n\nPersonal Status: Check guns and ensure sufficient ammo supply. Make good use of the enemies reserves to avoid running out during combat (do not spare any enemy who may be carrying significant amounts of ammo).\n\nGhost's Status: Hartford must decide resurrection timing when up against strong enemies, ensuring that hostiles have let down their guard down or left the area. Ensure that there are no nearby means of attack that can be used against him. Creating distractions is an option if enemies insist on guarding my remains. If there is a hostile third party nearby, Hartford may lure them into the battle and complicate the situation, creating more favorable conditions for revival.\n\nKey Point: Hartford's well-being is the highest priority (no parallels). Hartford may depart the battlefield first if a safe resurrection opportunity cannot be found in the short term, leaving the situation to change over a long period of time (a month, a year, or even longer) until revival is possible (this must be confirmed with Hartford prior to each battle)."}]},{"id":"diary-21101","title":"New Gear","sub":"Character diary · Kabr, the Resolute","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_211","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr, the Resolute"},"body":[{"p":"Two letters written in completely different handwriting They have been carefully tucked into the diary.\n\nKabr,\nCheck out what I made for you. You're sure to like it, because it has the most beautiful embroidery pattern in the world on it: a new, never-before-seen species of nautilus from Oceania. Its shell features the most standard equiangular spiral I've ever seen, with smooth, delicate growth patterns—the pinnacle of romantic aesthetics. Of course, there are also siphon pipes, which have always been the perfect symbol of cephalopods. When you wear it, be sure to keep the embroidered side facing you to avoid damage from battle, which naturally lets you appreciate its beauty a few more times.\nOh, right. In case it wasn't obvious, it's a cloak.\nPahanin\n\nTo my dear friend, Kabr:\nI have something for you. It's not a gift or something so trite. You can consider it an objective entity, born yet only given meaning through your use.\nAfter observing your combat style and skull structure, I find your turban to be an inadequate choice of headgear. It's too weak, and you never know when it might be ripped away by an enemy. You're leaving yourself open to bullets. So I made you a helmet. It's forged using an extremely dense metal with joint designs, ensuring a snug fit and high durability.\nWhether we wish it or not, the battle rages on. It is part of our past, present, and future, rearing its head when you may have let your guard down. We walk a road with no place to hide and no end in sight. At least with ample armor, we can march further still.\nAdditionally, if your helmet becomes damaged, come find me, and I'll forge you a new one.\nWhen I have time, that is.\nYour loyal friend, Praedyth"}]},{"id":"diary-10801","title":"The Beginning","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"I had another dream.\nBréc said that I would record all of my dreams sooner or later, just as I did before. I think \"before\" means when I was still alive.\nAlthough I don't want to listen to him or do what he tells me—doing so only feeds into his bragging, know-it-all nature—I did dream of a book tonight.\nIt was in that dark room, under that tiny semicircle window, on that table with one leg shorter than the rest.\nI must have been familiar with that table once, for I still remember its color and how rough the scratches on the upper-right corner—ones I'd carved with a fork—felt beneath my fingers.\nI've had many dreams, but the last thing I'd like to dream about is this very room.\nIt's neither scary nor dangerous. In fact, it holds nothing but isolated darkness, eternal silence, and myself.\nAnd I don't like any of them.\n\nIn my dream, I opened the book, only to be met with blank pages—disappointing, but not surprising. In the end, fate is fair to all. It granted me near immortality, then took away all of my memories.\nWill I lose them again one day? I have no idea. But if I write them down, if and when such a day comes again, maybe I can find my past through these records. Or maybe, someone else will stumble upon this diary and read it out of curiosity. Either way, things won't completely fade away so long as someone still remembers.\nSo I decided to record my dreams. I don't know if anyone else has weird dreams like I do, but Bréc insists that they are precious things. He's always been a despicable liar, but I really hope he's telling the truth about this."}]},{"id":"diary-20201","title":"A Study on Pomegranate Cultivation","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"January 10: Constant temperature, temperate climate simulation\nI planted a pomegranate seedling in a flower bed near the bazaar. It's close to a water source and bathed in sunlight, making it a good choice.\nActually, I'd initially planned to plant it in the garden, and the masked child didn't reject my request. However, Saoirse looked like she wished I were dead when I returned with my petri dish the next day.\nShams said that silence doesn't always mean consent.\nVery well. However, I maintain that the garden looks quite empty and lonely with only the masked child there. I would have liked for my little sprout to keep her company.\n\nJanuary 23: Temperature dropped, polar climate simulation\nThe seedling had started sprouting, but it clearly wasn't adapting to the frigid climate, growing at only half its expected pace.\nI like plants because they're simple. Withered stems imply that they lack water, and yellow leaves imply that they're exposed to excessive sunlight.\nPeople should have leaves to express their emotions, too—especially the Exos.\n\nFebruary 7: Rainy, tropical climate simulation\nFrequent artificial rain caused the seedling to start rotting.\n...Alright, it wasn't actually rain. I had to leave Haven for a bit and asked Tan-2 to look after it. However, he ended up watering it six times per day.\nWhen I returned, I found him pacing beside the flower bed, muttering things like \"apologize,\" \"not you,\" and \"egged me on.\"\nExos really do need leaves.\n\nFebruary 16: Cloudy, oceanic climate simulation\nThe seedling bore its first fruit—a perfect success!\nJust imagine it—this world has heroes who carry out impossible missions, who slay labyrinth dwellers, who seek the golden fleece...but none of them are capable of protecting Haven while also cultivating pomegranates in four climates!\nIt's not quite how I'd originally planned to go down in history, but it's not a bad idea, is it?"}]},{"id":"diary-20202","title":"A Hat","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"Shams was acting weird today.\nTypically when I visit the tavern, he'd help me make small talk with the other patrons. But today, he was unusually silent, saying nothing even after two tankards of beer.\nIt was only when I asked him for the fourth time that he finally told me that he didn't like the hat I'd worn today.\nI thought I had misheard him for a moment...\nIt was once my favorite hat—wide-brimmed, linen, perfectly bohemian—but I'd forgotten about it after coming to Haven. Today, I'd just so happened to find it again on the top of my bookshelf.\nI questioned Shams's taste, but this seemed to make him even angrier, leading to him asking whether I'd already forgotten what had happened when I'd previously I worn the hat.\nWe lived in a frontier town before we came to Haven. There weren't many Lightbearers there, but whenever I wore that hat, they'd gather together and point it out, laughing at it and commenting on how \"interesting\" it was.\nDoes Shams not want me to receive compliments? That makes no sense. It's not like he's a selfish Ghost, after all.\nShams angrily knocked my tankard. He looked as though he had more to say, but he was interrupted by Wolf, who stopped by to say hello and complimented me on my hat, saying, \"The bohemian look really suits you.\"\nI looked at Shams, panicked—'Oh Traveler, protect me and keep him from getting any angrier,' I thought.\nBut to my surprise...Shams suddenly fell quiet. Not long after that, he told me that coming to Haven was indeed the best decision we've ever made.\nI'm not sure why he said that, but I must correct him.\nActually, it's one of the best decisions we've ever made."}]},{"id":"diary-20203","title":"A Day in the Life of Kabr","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"6:50 Woke up\n7:30 Completed 20 sets of shuttle runs and 10 sets of jumping jacks\n7:40 Went for a morning run around Haven\n8:00 Arrived at the tavern, had breakfast, and sought adventure opportunities by chatting with other Lightbearers\n8:06 End of chatting\n8:20 Studied the survival chances of broadleaf plants in an artificial tundra simulation in the flower bed by the bazaar\n10:00 Went for a walk to the garden; greeted the Speaker and examined the garden's vegetation coverage\n10:35 Chased out by Saoirse\n11:20 Had lunch at the tavern\n12:20 Arrived at the plaza and jogged around Haven as a post-lunch workout\n12:40 Heard Skorri's scribe lecturing his men while passing by\n13:00 Heard the scribe lecturing his men while passing by again\n13:20 Heard the scribe lecturing his men while passing by a third time; couldn't help but ask what was wrong\n13:30 Decided to help them find their missing materials; Shams urged me to mind my own business\n14:00 Surrounded by the Fallen in the library\n17:00 Defeated all the Fallen in the library\n17:20 Shams reminded me to look for the materials, so we returned to the library\n17:30 Found nothing; Shams got fed up and started scanning\n17:50 Returned to Haven with the materials\n18:00 Delivered the materials to the scribe's men, who invited us to dinner as a token of appreciation\n19:00 Had dinner and made friends\n20:20 Arrived at the plaza and went for an evening jog\n21:00 Went home; completed 20 sets of shuttle runs and 10 sets of jumping jacks\n22:10 Took a shower and heard Shams humming a tune\n22:30 Went to bed"}]},{"id":"diary-20204","title":"A Reflection on a Book","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"[Several paragraphs are transcribed in the journal, written with neat handwriting. Next to them are thoughts written in different-colored ink.]\n\n\"...But he obstinately believed that the distant sunrise was summoning him. Even though no one, not even himself, had ever seen the reality behind the glow, it burned in his heart like a flame, scorching him day and night. ...So he would fearlessly forge ahead, towards the mountains, towards the rivers, towards the unreachable beyond...\"\n—That's just the sun, isn't it? You can see it just by looking up. In my opinion, smart people don't chase the sun. Only the mysteries of the unknown are worth the journey. Imagine an unprecedented, unique discovery unveiling mysteries during your adventure, a discovery that you would go down in history for—what could possibly be more thrilling than this?\n\n\"...He threw his spear, piercing the teeth and tongues of his enemies. His foes' heads bled, staining the desert sands red. He was so foolish and single-minded, yet also so brave and fearless, that his hulking form served as a banner on the battlefield. Everyone—even those who had hesitated to become his companions—gazed at him and cried out...They gathered around him, reveling in the fervor of their victory...\"\n—Yes! A truly wonderful adventure is one experienced with friends. Who wouldn't want to form a legion of their own? We'd defeat our enemies valiantly, then drink merrily. If I had my own legion, what would I name it...? Think hard, Kabr.\n\n\"...It was the end of his journey... He shook his head sorrowfully and lamented—this wasn't his sunrise. His breath was stifled in that blinding, blazing light. His armor, shield, helmet, and belt had melted away, while a searing pain burned through his body... He died in an agonizing struggle, having never embraced the rising sun he'd chased.\"\n—Hmm... I still don't get it even after reading it three times, nor do I like the conclusion. Maybe I should pick a story with a happy ending next time."}]},{"id":"diary-20205","title":"A Trip to Jiangshi Metro","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"It had been 3 days since I got back from Jiangshi Metro and I still failed to sleep tight.\nWhy had no one ever mentioned such a...tragic (is \"tragic\" the right word?) place? It's clearly the front line of the battle against the Fallen, but the ones fighting were all mortals—no relics or Ghosts in sight! They were fighting with their own, limited lives!\nDoes Lord Radegast know about this? Why doesn't he have those mortals move to Haven? Or send more Lightbearers to support them. I would definitely volunteer—even though I'd be freezing in Jiangshi Metro.\nAs a Lightbearer, I can't just stand by and watch mortals fight our enemies with their own flesh and blood. Kabr the Shieldbearer was born for that very purpose, after all. I will use my shield to protect everyone behind me—maybe twenty people...or ten...at least five, certainly.\n...Fine, I admit I can't protect everyone.\nI've been trying to defend as many people as I can, but the more I do, the more I find there will always be those I cannot save. My ability and responsibility have become a boulder that, try as I might, cannot be pushed to the top of the hill. Just like...like Jiangshi Metro. As I lay peacefully in bed with my shield put away, those mortals may still be out there risking life and limb on a bloody battlefield. How ridiculous of me, to think of protecting them.\nAs I wrote this, I realized how foolish I was to have described them as \"tragic\" when they are so much more determined, more courageous than I am, even without the Light.\nPerhaps tomorrow I can talk to Lord Radegast. I'll try to convince him to let the residents of Jiangshi Metro move to Haven.\nI may not be able to protect everyone, but at the very least, I should follow those who can."}]},{"id":"diary-20207","title":"A Criterion for Heroes","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"Ever since that incident, I often sit opposite Skorri in the tavern, and we enjoy a drink together.\nI'm glad I can be friends with my idol, even if I have yet to be honored with a dedicated poem from the Iron Bard. Shams maintains that we aren't friends, but he simply doesn't understand—for us humans, anyone you share drinks with is a friend.\nI once asked who Skorri would write a poem for. She answered my question with one of her own: what kind of person deserves a poem?\n\"A hero\" was the obvious answer. But who is worthy of being called a hero? Is it someone who is an outstanding fighter? Someone who possesses extraordinary bravery? Someone of great renown?\nAfter I sat there silently pondering the question for a while, Skorri gave me a few examples.\nTan-2? —No, he's still quite young, and he has much to learn when it comes to battle. Besides, he's only recently acquired his Relic. Shams would go on to say that it I sounded like I was mocking him. He also noted the subtle expression Skorri had momentarily had on her face—and here I was thinking she simply didn't like the taste of her beer. To be honest, he is the bravest young man I've ever seen, and he's amazingly gifted in combat. I quite like fighting by his side.\nNing Fei? —Certainly not. Back when he was arguing with his Ghost on the Ketch, his clamorous voice managed to drown out the tripwire mine alarms. No hero would ever be that noisy. In spite of that, he is compassionate and frank, which I appreciate a lot. Moreover, he always tells me how he's feeling so that I don't worry about him—wait, Shams just told me that those were excuses to get out of missions.\nWolf? —My good friend. A great person, but always hard for me to figure out. I've always thought that a hero should possess sensible and prudent selflessness. However, Wolf is always too concerned with everyone's expectations, making that \"selflessness\" nothing but wings made of wax—fly too close to the sun, and they're sure to melt.\nIn the end, I didn't come to a conclusion. Skorri said that my standards were too harsh and that not even heroes are perfect—aren't they, though? I was just telling the truth as I saw it.\nOr maybe the Iron Bard's examples weren't quite right. Those are no heroes. No, they're my companions—only imperfect people fight side by side."}]},{"id":"diary-20208","title":"An Ahamkara","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"...Turns out the \"magic dragon\" hovering around Lord Radegast is an Ahamkara.\nHonestly, I'd only ever seen this creature in books before. Apparently they feed on wishes. It sounds ridiculous, though... Can wishes truly fill their stomachs? Maybe they sneak behind people's backs and feast on roasts.\n...Very well. Shams says they do not, in fact, eat meat.\nSo such magical creatures really exist? Beasts that feed on humans' desires and make them come true? It sounds too fantastical. Surely there must be a price?\nWho knows. Perhaps it bewitched us somehow.\nAfter all, I can't think of Lord Radegast keeping it for any other reasons—would an almighty Iron Lord have wishes that only such a creature could fulfill? Given his territory, authority, strength, and allies, he could easily use his courage and confidence to build a new world on the ruins of the Golden Age, if he wanted to.\nI'll ask him the next time I see him.\nShams urged me to drop it. I'm not sure why, but...he sounded like he was on the urge of a breakdown... Fine then.\nI don't like Ahamkara."}]},{"id":"diary-20209","title":"A New Name","sub":"Character diary · Kabr","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_202","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"Skorri suggested I write a letter promoting myself and post it on the bulletin board, rather than stopping all the tavern patrons to ask if they need help.\nAlthough I don't see anything wrong with my current method—at least everyone I stop seems pleasantly surprised—her suggestion is a good one, and adopting it may bring even more opportunities.\nI found the cover letter I'd written when I first came to Haven and realized that it was still signed \"Peregrine.\"\nShams sighed beside me again, first saying how carefully he'd picked the name \"Peregrine,\" then saying how cool the name \"Chiron\" would be for a Lightbearer.\nIt's difficult for me to fathom how a Ghost could love the animal kingdom so much. I'd previously assumed that Shams saw a bird soaring in the sky—or some other random fowl, perhaps—then casually gave me a falcon-related name.\nHe's almost perfect, except his taste in names.\nFortunately, that name belongs to the past now, buried alongside the obtuse, arrogant \"Peregrine\" who made a scene during the opening of Haven's Iron Bar. A hero's journey entails the abandonment of many things—companions, beliefs, principles, egos...all melted in the furnace of life.\nShams still flew around me, asking me what \"Kabr\" means. I told him it means \"grave.\" He went silent for a moment, then complimented me and said, \"You know what? Sometimes, you're pretty punk.\"\nI'm glad that we're on the same page."}]},{"id":"diary-10802","title":"Scars","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"Tin Can was a mess when I first saw him. It took me a long time to get him cleaned up. Of course, I was curious about how he got all those scars, but sadly, he cannot tell me the story himself.\nUp until I met another Ghost, I thought none of them could speak. Tin Can seems to be the only exception... Poor little guy. That Ghost called Didi advised me to cheer up, but why would I need to? Nothing is wrong with Tin Can—he's more genuine, warm, and innocent than anyone I've ever met.\nAnd last night...I dreamed of him.\n\nHe was scouring some rubble, searching for a corpse—for me. But apparently, it would be quite some time until he did. Two moons were hanging in the sky, suggesting that he was not on Earth, but on Mars, a planet I've only ever seen in old video clips. Cold and pale, Phobos and Deimos observed Tin Can's fruitless efforts, as well as the man in tattered clothes not far from him.\nHe appeared sorrowful and silent, yet...oddly peaceful. Light flowed beneath his skin—a Lightbearer—yet his heart matched his appearance, old and haggard. He was like a dying snake.\nBut Tin Can was unaware of this. He liked the Light, and when met with it, he was as defenseless as a sunflower gazing up at its namesake. He flew over to the man and greeted him.\nTin Can actually said hello.\nThis was the first time I'd ever heard him speak—clearly, without using any recordings, in his own voice just like the other Ghosts.\nThe man turned around slowly, allowing Tin Can to finally see his face. I'll never forget that grotesque look—a combination of disgust, depression, and a bit of anger, all merged into an iron grimness.\n\"Hello?\" Tin Can asked again.\nHe waited again for an answer, but all he got was a bullet.\nThis was how he got his scars."}]},{"id":"diary-10803","title":"Death","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"Cala was feigning sleep.\nI haven't seen her for quite some time. I almost thought I'd forgotten her face. But when I saw her in my dream once again, I realized that I'd always remembered her—her curly dark hair, the scar on her face, and the tiny red mole on her nostril.\nCala was the second person I met after being revived. At that time, I had no idea who I was or what I should do. So I kept walking and walking until finally, on the other side of the river, I saw a campfire, a tent, and living people.\nThe first one I saw was a burly, bearded guy holding a steaming can. He glared at me as if I were a rat crawling out of mud and said, \"Scram, ya little beggar.\" Then a second person emerged from the tent, telling him to shut up unless he wanted to draw the Fallen. That was the first time I saw Cala.\n\nIt was a cold night. Cala hadn't fallen asleep yet, and her two teammates were talking loudly as they kept watch, leaving her no choice but to listen.\nThey were talking about me, the strange homeless orphan, the tiny, scrawny rat that came scurrying out of nowhere. They wondered how I'd managed to reach this snow-covered forest dressed only in thin rags.\nCala opened her eyes, stared at the kerosene lamp for a moment, then closed her eyes again.\nNow the watchmen turned the discussion to whether I was still alive. I couldn't blame them for wondering this; I'd been staying in a nearby cave and hadn't shown my face for three days at this point. In a world like this, any resources are precious, and for mercenaries accustomed to death, the best option was to simply ignore me. Not chasing me away the moment they saw me was kind enough of them.\nGiving up on sleep, Cala got up, grabbed a blanket, and shoved the two cans on the table into her pocket. Just as she was about to leave, she turned back and took the kerosene lamp from its hook.\nUpon noticing her, one of the lookouts asked where she was going and noted that it wasn't her shift yet.\nBut Cala kept going without the slightest hesitation, making an excuse that she needed to relieve herself.\n\nThe canned food was delicious. I never found a can that delicious again, though. Bréc says it's because when you've been starving, your first meal will always be the most delicious. But I know he's wrong. He's just dampening the mood, as always.\nCala seemed relieved when she saw me. She said it was a miracle that I was still alive. But what she didn't know—what she would never know—is that I couldn't die. As for herself and the blanket she left me, the Fallen would burn them to ashes in just two days.\nIt was my first death after being chosen by Tin Can, and the first revival I would remember.\nAt that time, I didn't know why I could come back to life, and Tin Can had no way of telling me. Finding myself standing in the ruins, I naively thought myself lucky enough to have escaped death.\nIn reality, I am but a plague that spreads misfortune.\n\nThe bearded guy was right. They should have chased me away the day they saw me."}]},{"id":"diary-10804","title":"Svapna","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"This was the first time I dreamed about Bréc.\nHe was quite ugly—a sort of mutated, slender lizard with scales resembling flowing red ink and a blooming flower-like thing for a head. I'd thought his twisted bones looked odd enough, but his true appearance was...much stranger than I could have ever imagined.\nIn my dream, Bréc was hiding beneath a mossy boulder, taking shelter from the rain. The air was hot and humid. Dense raindrops fell onto the moss, splattering and splashing, then creeping down the rock in rivulets until finally, they converged into a tiny stream. Bréc laid down, staring into his own three eyes reflected in the water. Soon, four more eyes—another Ahamkara—appeared behind him.\n\"You failed,\" Bréc said (I was surprised to hear him speak without the pretentious nonsense I've come to know). \"I told you, he is not so easily deceived.\"\n\"He will let his guard down,\" the four-eyed one answered, \"It is only a matter of time.\"\n\"Why don't you just find another target, like that Titan he is with—that fool has always been eager to take his place.\"\n\"Boring.\" The comment is accompanied by a yawn. \"Fools always have boring ambitions.\"\nBréc sneered, \"Do not starve yourself to death, Svapna.\"\nSo this is Svapna. His sister. His kin. His enemy...\n...My enemy.\nSvapna turned her head to face him. Her eyes shined like lapis in the rock's shadow.\n\"Such a day will not come, dear brother.\" Something akin to a smile bloomed across her face. \"You will understand this soon enough—his wish will surprise you.\""}]},{"id":"diary-10805","title":"Spring","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"Elathi once told me that her favorite season is spring, for it has moderate weather, and wildflowers suddenly bloom after the snow melts. Beasts also come out of hibernation—a trapper's boon.\nI didn't know how to respond, because I found spring somewhat frightening.\n\nI often dream of spring. Elathi describes it as a time of warmth and color, of air filled with the scent of furs; for me, it is a time of uncertainty, of the first rainfall once the snow melts away.\nThese dreams are probably memories from before I was revived. They are choppy and vague, yet convincing all the same. To me, they seem undoubtedly real.\nIn one such dream, I was sitting in that strange yet familiar dark room when someone knocked on the door five times. A person dressed in black entered, blindfolded me, and led me along a long, long road. The gravel beneath my feat gave way to dry soil, then to a dampened shoreline until finally, we ascended an endless spiral staircase. Up...up...up...\nThen the man in black pushed the door at the end of the staircase open. Spring had arrived.\nSpring is silence. Spring is hunger. Spring is terror.\nThe silence is countless cold faces and mouths kept shut. It is the absence of response no matter how many times I knock on the door or make a racket. It is questions forever left answered. The hunger is the silver cup with water and a plate left empty for three whole days. And the terror... It is the blinding brightness that keeps sleep at bay. It is the white light beaming outside, day and night, like a miniature sun that never sets.\nTrapped in silence, hunger, and terror, I opened that book and put pen to paper. I heard Bréc whispering in my ear—\nA farmer will kill himself with a hatchet in a cowshed.\nNot a single drop of rain will fall for the next three months.\nYou will see a woman with a red garland at the ceremony. She is your birth mother.\n\nShe had soft brown hair and a pair of eyes that mirrored my own. She stood among the throngs of people—the fifteenth in line, as I'd counted over and over again. I waited for her to approach, my heart pounding violently against my ribs.\nBut when she finally did, she seemed...devout. Her eyes were filled with reverence and anticipation, but not yearning.\nShe looked up at me from below without so much as a trace of maternal love in her gaze. It was as if I was not her daughter, as if she neither remembered nor recognized me...as if she and I shared no bond.\nShe seemed to be no different from the fourteen people who had come before her—just another devotee waiting anxiously for me to press my ox blood-dipped finger to her forehead and grant her this year's blessing.\nSoon, she became bewildered due to my hesitation. She and the rest of the crowd stared at me in silence. Identical looks of confusion appeared on their faces. Then came the panic.\n\"D-Divinely Selected,\" Mother asked, voice trembling, \"why won't you bless me?\"\nI wanted to ask her why she didn't come to hug me? Why didn't she call my name, or hold my hand...anything that a mother would normally do with their child.\nBut the words wouldn't come.\nSpeaking was offense, crying was profanity, and leaving my seat was the worst—an omen of disaster.\nI must stay silent, hungry, and terrified.\nAll I could do was extend my finger and gently touch her forehead."}]},{"id":"diary-10806","title":"An Apple","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"Hemminki was picking out fruits.\nI stood right next to him, yet he still didn't see me—another dream. In my dreams, nobody can see me.\nHe picked up an apple and inspected it. I hadn't seen the man standing opposite him and peeling a cherry wood stick, but the two seemed familiar with one another. Without stopping his work, the man said, \"Two credits.\"\nHemminki turned red with anger. \"What? You're robbing me blind! I can buy a whole can of meat for just five!\"\nThe merchant answered, \"It's been four months without rain. Half the fruit trees are already withered.\"\nHemminki put the apple back and walked away from the stall. After taking a few steps, though, he suddenly changed his mind and returned. He pulled out his card and snarled, \"Swipe it yourself.\"\nWhen the merchant approached, Hemminki was still grumbling. \"Couldn't you peel that stupid stick of yours somewhere else? Those shavings are flying all the way over here.\"\nClassic Hemminki, always complaining and moaning about that little card in his pocket. I'd heard people calling him a \"miser\" more than once, but he never cared. Most folks are misers, he declared proudly; he's just more honest than them.\nThe merchant ignored his complaints and swiped the card, then grabbed a handful of orange candies and passed them to him. \"On the house.\"\nHemminki stared at the candies, mumbled something unintelligible, then stuffed them into his pocket.\n\"You bought an apple for two credits?!\" The clerk beside him must have known of his \"reputation\", hence the surprise. \"What, you got your hands on some Glimmer lately?\"\nThe merchant chimed in, \"You haven't heard? He's got another mouth to feed—an adopted daughter.\"\nThe clerk suppressed his smile at the word \"daughter\" and looked at Hemminki cautiously. Hemminki didn't seem to appreciate his thoughtfulness, though. Not a bit.\nClutching the apple, he turned to leave the shop.\nJust as he did so, however, a blast roared from the west. Everyone turned in its direction, mouths gaping and eyes wide. This was the first time I'd seen that sky from this angle. It glowed fiery, scorching red, like coals in a furnace. Thick, black smoke billowed out across the crimson canvas, forming a painting that was equal parts beautiful and horrifying.\nA shout rang out. \"The forge exploded! Run for it!\"\nThe merchant turned to Hemminki with shock and hesitation as he asked, \"Isn't that your...?\" He was right; Hemminki was the only smith here, and his workshop was at the west end of town.\nHemminki rushed off toward the fire.\nI knew why he wanted to return—he was worried that I was still there. There were two forges in his workshop, and if the fire spread, there would be a second blast before long. Hemminki pushed past the people evacuating toward the east, running through the smoke until he was gasping for breath.\nIn the burning wood frames, he called my name loudly, \"Estela! ESTELA—!\"\nHe would never hear my response. I was hit in the chest by rubble and crushed to death by a collapsed beam.\nBut he didn't let up. \"ESTELA! E—STE—LA—!\"\nI wish I could tell him to just leave me behind and run as far as he could, but I was helpless. When the incident happened, I was already a corpse waiting for my revival; now, I'm only dreaming."}]},{"id":"diary-10807","title":"Elathi","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"Although I've had dreams that didn't belong to me, Elathi seldom appears in them. Bréc said it's because I feel guilty.\nHe said I miss her as much as I fear seeing her.\nNonsense. How could I possibly be afraid of seeing her? He's just trying to get to me.\n\nI finally dreamed of Elathi tonight.\nShe was sitting in the cabin and fixing that broken window again. We hadn't been able to close it all winter, and it would rattle loudly when the frigid winds kicked up come nightfall. Elathi had tried all possible means to fix it, but the result was always less than satisfactory.\nI hadn't slept well those first few nights. Elathi thought the wind was frightening me and tried to block the crack. But what I really feared were all the possible disasters lurking behind it.\nIt was a sunny day. She was leaning by the window tinkering with a few parts when the sun hit just right. I watched her from outside the door. It was as if time had frozen, with the only movement being the specks of dust floating through rays of light. A scene of warmth, serenity, and mundanity.\nThen she raised her head and smiled at me. It took me a good moment to realize that she wasn't looking at me right now, but at the Estela of the distant past.\nI saw myself pushing the gate open with two rabbits in my hands and a bright grin on my face. It felt strange—I seemed joyful, carefree...blissful, even.\nI listened as I spoke with a confidence I no longer recognized. \"Let me make roasted rabbits for you, Elathi.\"\nShe answered with a blunt laugh. \"Please, spare my rabbits and stomach.\"\n\nIn the end, the rabbits became two servings of Elathi's signature stew.\nElathi was absent-minded as we ate. I could see she wanted to say something but hesitated a few times.\nBut the me in that moment was trying to deal with a slippery chestnut, paying no mind to her conflicted expression.\nFinally, she called my name, \"Estela.\"\nI looked at her blankly.\n\"You've forgotten many things, right?\"\nI nodded.\n\"Do you remember your parents?\"\nI shook my head.\n\"What about your birthday?\"\nAnother shake of my head.\nElathi looked at me, took three deep breaths, then posed a question with a smile and feigned casualness. \"Then...how about we make today your birthday?\"\nI froze. I wasn't sure what to do other than stare at her.\nShe reached out and took my hand, as if passing me her infinite love and courage through a simple, warm touch.\nAnd then she followed up with another question. \"From today onward, I'm your mother, and you're my daughter. What do you think?\"\n\nI couldn't feel my body or control my mouth, but I clearly heard myself answer,\n\"Okay.\""}]},{"id":"diary-10808","title":"Answers","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"Dear Estela, my poor little crow, my shining star of destruction. This may be the only time I speak to you personally. You don't have to believe, but you must remember all that I am about to say clearly, for every word is the answer you've been seeking.\n...Why would you ask a question like that?\nHow could you not know who I am? How could you not know my name? You've never seen my face, yet you listen to my whispers day in and day out.\nDon't be afraid. Don't make that face. I am the last one who would ever hurt you. I am your unseen friend, your undefeatable opponent, your selfless assistant, and an inseparable part of our shared destiny.\n...Promise? You need no promise. My dear Estela, if there one thing in this world that is real and trustworthy, it is a corpse. The dead have no use for deception, after all.\nAnd I am one such corpse, am I not?\nMy body is long gone, and I failed to keep my consciousness intact. There remains only that which you aren't meant to know and hear, and the broken bones you now hold.\nI might be a liar, but what could a dead liar possibly take from you?\nLife? I've long since lost count of the years I've lived and the marvels I've seen. Saying I have no ambitions of revival would be a lie, though a fragmented consciousness is unable to perform any kind of rituals—a toothless hyena cannot eat, now can it?\nDestruction? No, that is not my mission. Destruction is a one-way ticket meant solely for the living. It may have proved useful when I was alive, but now? That ticket is naught but worthless scrap.\n\nNow, listen carefully. All I need from you is a vow, an ever-lasting determination.\nI will tell you what ruined your life, what took everything from you. And in return, you shall find your foe and slay her.\nFor we share the same enemy and the same misfortune, you and I. I want her to face the same end I did—reduced to nothing more than a corpse. A fractured body, a rotted heart, a dissipated consciousness, even.\n\nYou are dying as we speak.\nBut worry not—this is an insignificant death. When the sun goes down, that defective Ghost will bring you back to the reality that belongs to you.\n\nYou should record this conversation before your subconsciousness forgets it.\nIt is the only way to save the both of us, o revenger mine."}]},{"id":"diary-10809","title":"The Omen","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"I looked up blankly beneath a dark sky.\nBlack flies swarmed into iron-gray clouds, devouring the pale sun like rabid dogs. The thick clouds blocked nearly all light, making it easy to gaze up at the heavens. All mysteries stem from that which we cannot see and that which we do not know. Being able to face the sun like this, it seems less lofty. Less untouchable.\nThen I looked down.\nMy gaze was met with flames and crumbling ground. The fallen buildings were moaning, the burned earth was howling, and the crawling roots of a flaming tree were screaming.\nWhere am I? What happened to this place? Is there anyone else left?\nI paced, then walked, then ran over the scorched soil, fruitlessly searching for fellow survivors. I needed to prove that I wasn't the culprit of the disaster, that I hadn't brought hell upon this place.\nAfter searching for what felt like forever, I found a hand exposed under the sun and prayed as I dug through the rubble. Finally, I saw the victim's face—it was Wolf.\nGrabbing the hand, I cried out just like I had when I first saw Cala's body. I'd long learned that asking 'why' was meaningless. All I could do was keep repeating, I'm sorry, I'm so sorry.\nSuddenly, the hand gripped me like a vice.\nWolf was still alive. Wolf was still alive! But...as that face I'd become so familiar with turned toward me, it morphed into something unrecognizable. Countless faces twisted and overlaid with each other until at last, they formed a giant black hollow.\nThe black hollow said to me, do not fear. Do not hate.\nThe black hollow said to me, this is fate, a tale already written. Love, pain, existence, death—they are nothing but lies.\nIt engulfed all of my emotions, thoughts, and words. All I could do was stare on in utter stillness.\nBut the hollow, seemingly having heard my answer, started to expand limitlessly—it devoured Wolf, me, the city, and even the sun above.\nThat was when I woke up. This is all I have dreamed of."}]},{"id":"diary-20702","title":"Past Correspondence","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"[A letter from Bayda-Benghazi, accompanied by a small bag of local produce]\nDear Nala,\nIt's been a while since we last spoke.\nThe coast rarely sees consecutive sunny days, but the weather has been notably good recently, and the Super-C cherry tomatoes have enjoyed a bumper harvest. I was chatting with Manda and she mentioned that you love them. I was surprised—I don't recall ever seeing you eat these fruity little snacks. Manda told me with a smile that although you would never ask for them, someone always managed to empty the fruit basket on the Leader's Hall table before anyone else could get a bite—and we all know you're the only one who would stay there.\nI picked out some of the plumper ones and dried them for you. Benghazi is so far from Veridia, so fresh cherry tomatoes would likely shrivel up on their journey. But don't worry, I've also prepared some seeds for you in the brown paper packet at the bottom of the bag so you can try growing some yourself.\nTake care of yourself, Nala. Manda and I miss you.\n\n[A letter from Bayda-Benghazi, written in childish, crooked handwriting and with numerous corrections]\nDear Nala,\nI'm very happy today, because Mom said, \"I have (scratched out) You have improved a lot. You can have a reward!\" I want to go play with you. But Mom said you're at a place called Very-deeya. I don't get it. She said it's very very very far, and I can only go when I grow up.\nBut I'm already 11. And Mom said I'm growing up, so that means soon I can come see you!\nI put Stacy by my bed. When you gave her to me you said, \"Stacy will protect you.\" But I know it's not Stacy keeping us safe. It's you!\nSo I told Mom, \"I want to be like Nala! I want to protect everyone and grow up and play with Nala!\" And Mom said I'm super sweet!\nToday was a good day!\n\n[A letter from Bayda-Benghazi, written on coarse paper, in imposing handwriting]\nEsteemed Leader,\nSalutations.\nThe training drills have spread throughout the town, with many among the younger generation joining in.\nOur armory is expanding, now provisionally covering all field squads.\nThe Leader's Hall was hit by a typhoon a few days ago, damaging the roof (there were no casualties as it was unoccupied). Repairs are underway.\nAll else is well.\nYou are deeply missed."}]},{"id":"diary-20703","title":"Nightmares","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"I dreamed of that river again.\nI saw how it meandered out of the mist only to disappear back into it, winding its way through all of Bayda-Benghazi. I've walked along its banks countless times, always with blade in hand.\nMost of the time, I impale the heads of my enemies on my blade's tip, their last terror-filled gaze serving as an apology to my people. Sometimes, I return bedraggled, remorseful, and wounded—a version of myself shattered and reassembled, my incompetence laid bare against the backdrop of a prolonged life.\nIn the dream, I can only move forward, staggering upstream. The stench of rotting corpses in the water, those submerged bones peering at me, they all seem so familiar—I should know who they are—as they hysterically plead for my help.\nI ask them over and over, who killed you? Was it a distant visitor from the stars? The vultures of the desert?\nI receive no reply.\nThe fear in this dream—not of the answer itself, but of the march toward it—is palpable.\nI've awoken countless times in a cold sweat, remembering—reliving—how I entrusted my people to others in such feeble weakness. Never have I had the chance to embrace any of the shadowy figures in this dream. They only push me away violently and scream in horror. I endure the bitterness in my slumber, then weep upon waking, trapped in the currents of this endless river.\nSo I start to run, my veins burning, my fear threatening to suffocate me. But I need to go faster, to see the culprit at the river's end before the dream fades away.\nI rush into the mist and finally, finally, I reach the river's end. A thunderous thrum surrounds me, deafening. I slowly realize it's the pounding of my own terrified heart.\nI look down at the water, and in its surface, I see my own face."}]},{"id":"diary-20704","title":"Receipts","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"[A stack of shopping receipts, neatly folded within the diary, each accompanied by a note in elegant handwriting]\n\n1. Veridia Textiles: Your Personal Wardrobe First Choice of the Iron Lords\nSummer Fresh Macaron Series Spaghetti Strap Dress: 1 item, pink Purchase Date: July 21\nWhen I handed the dress back to the clerk, I meant for her to put it back on the racks, not to take it to the checkout for packaging, and certainly not for Aiina to pay for it via the terminal without my consent! Next time, I'll make it clear that these airy, breezy clothes just aren't my style.\n2. Eternal Love—For the purest of vows. Tailor your bliss now! As recommended by the Iron Lords.\nImitation Radiancite Lovers' Rings: 1 pair, gift box included Purchase Date: July 24\nWho thought it would be a good idea to sell rings to a Ghost? And why in the world did Aiina buy a pair? To wear them on her mechanical appendages? Wait... She bought them the day before my blind date?!\n3. Don't waste your blood, sweat, and tears! Let us do the hard work of making your dreams come true! A favorite of the Iron Lords!\nPain-Free Rapid Muscle-Building Elixir: Lightbearer Edition, 1 bottle, for biceps and back Purchase Date: July 25\n...No, nobody can just drink a nutritional supplement and bulk up overnight, not even Lord Saladin. And does he even know he's endorsing so many products...?\n4. Let your true beauty shine through! Over 500 stores worldwide, adored by the Iron Lords!\nShop-to-It Fest Promotion: Classic Eyeshadow and Lipstick Set: 2 sets, earth tones Purchase Date: July 27.\nWolf says the women of Haven swear by this makeup brand—but that's no reason for Aiina to buy two identical sets of lipstick and eyeshadow. And to say this eyeshadow palette is adored by Lord Saladin is going a little too far.\n5. Officially licensed. A heartfelt tribute, penning the legends all around you. Exclusive Iron Lords collaboration.\nLegendary Red Sea Rift Lightbearer Card Set: 10 cards, Finnala edition Purchase Date: July 28.\n...What's this now? Why did Aiina buy ten identical cards? And where did they get the nerve to use my image without my consent? Did Lord Saladin really sign off on this?!"}]},{"id":"diary-20705","title":"The Past","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"Seeing that familiar emblem once more nearly made me lose my mind.\nIt's a scar that never healed, a rusted fang gnawing at my mind, a ghost haunting my dreams for years with no end in sight. I was so angry. I'm sure I must have been enraged beyond recognition because Aiina sounded on the verge of tears trying to calm me down, but I just wanted to ask—why? Why must the people I live to protect drag themselves back down and make a deal with Kandak again?\nDon't they know how duplicitous he is beneath that facade? How the sword he pledges will always be double-edged? During my brief rule over that territory, I felt overwhelmed on every level, and it was that snake who offered me an olive branch. He reached out, promising to aid our defenses in exchange for just a small portion of our food supplies on a regular basis.\nThe offer was too tempting for my weary soul to decline. I signed the agreement without much thought, and now, it has become an inescapable nightmare.\nAt first, Kandak seemed helpful, even providing aid in the form of armaments and dispatching patrols... Actions that now seem trivial, but that won my complete trust at the time, naively making me believe his ever-increasing demands were just means to better assist us.\nBut when the Fallen attacked, and the town fell to their bombardment, I was crushed and revived countless times, only to be met with a flippant message stating that stopping alien invasions was not part of our agreement.\nI could hear the sound of my ribs cracking, the agonized cries of those I served, and in a haze, I even heard Kandak laughing scornfully at my naivety. I stood at the city gates, unable to step back—not because I was holding the last line of defense, but because I was too afraid to look into the eyes of my people behind me.\nIt wasn't Kandak who cast them into the abyss—it was me, in my folly, paranoia, and stubbornness.\nThis betrayal, this self-loathing, is something for which I'll never forgive myself."}]},{"id":"diary-20706","title":"Training Class Notes","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"Monday's Schedule: Morning—10,000-meter warm-up run, Afternoon—3v3 free combat arena sparring.\nMonday's Menu: Fresh shrimp and bitter melon fern root salad, tender oil-free chicken breast salad, fresh orange juice.\nTuesday's Schedule: Morning—Session on Cabal troop types, Afternoon—Firearm disassembly, 20-meter target practice, obstacle shooting training.\nTuesday's Menu: Soft-boiled egg and quinoa salad, slow-braised beef with soba noodles, kale juice.\nWednesday's Schedule: Morning—150 weighted frog jumps, 200 weighted shuttle runs, Afternoon—1v99 sand table shooting exercise.\nWednesday's Menu: Szechuan pepper chicken breast with roasted cauliflower, low-fat mapo tofu, baby cucumber juice blend.\nThursday's Schedule: Morning—Ghost teamwork training (optional for non-Lightbearers), Afternoon—Melee weapons sparring.\nThursday's Menu: Soft-boiled egg and shrimp croissant, konjac oat chicken breast sandwich, tomato and orange juice.\nFriday's Schedule: Morning—Relic smelting theory, Afternoon—Group patrol of Veridia.\nFriday's Menu: Handmade chicken breast meatball soup, black pepper soba noodles with vinaigrette, kale juice.\n\nThe second week of Veridia's pilot civilian military training program has yielded promising results.\nAs of now, a total of 100 people have participated in the training. In the first week, 6 individuals dropped out. However, 6 were persuaded to return, and another 6 were invited to join. A total of 31 people were unable to keep up with the training pace. After additional personalized training sessions, all 31 caught up. There were 17 instances of frequent absences and 4 cases of regular absences. Additionally, 22 people gathered for meals outside due to complaints about the blandness of the light meals. Formal discussions have been held with all individuals involved, and 39 written apologies have been received.\nI look forward to the day this program is fully implemented throughout Veridia."}]},{"id":"diary-20707","title":"A Proposal to Lord Saladin II","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"Esteemed Lord Saladin,\nThank you for your response to my previous proposal. I have reflected on recent events and observed the mood in Veridia as you advised. I must concede now that my past experiences in Bayda-Benghazi may have led to a narrow-mindedness in my suggestions, marked by a certain degree of paranoia and extremism. I apologize for the content of my earlier recommendations and ask for your permission to propose further amendments to the statutes.\nChapter 2, Article 3.1, regarding the regulation of newcomers.\nFrom what I understand, due to the Cabal's sudden arrival and occupation, many people have flocked to Veridia from all over the Red Sea Rift. These are ordinary civilians who are displaced and defenseless, and as Lightbearers, we have a duty to protect them. Also, as the Cabal's actions have intensified, a significant number of civilians persecuted in the surrounding areas of the Red Sea Rift have come seeking refuge. Veridia welcomes people who are verified to pose no threat.\nHowever, I still wish to improve this statute. In addition to providing shelter for newcomers, I suggest Veridia encourage all citizens to participate in military exercises, ensuring at least basic physical fitness and weapons proficiency, to empower civilians with the ability to defend themselves. This would extend to both locals and newcomers.\nChapter 2, Article 4.7, regarding the mining of Radiancite.\nRecently, while patrolling the outskirts of Veridia, I encountered a group of civilians illegally mining Radiancite—a clear violation of the law. As such, I was ready to apprehend them. However, when I went to pursue them, I was injured by some patrolling Cabal, and it was the civilian ringleader who saved me. Hence, I agreed to his plea to understand the desperate situation he described to me.\nI followed him to his dwelling. It was merely a rundown shack on the outskirts of Veridia. They are people who couldn't leave their homes for various reasons after the Cabal invasion, thus becoming the \"forsaken\" of Veridia, eking out a living on the outskirts and driven to desperate measures, such as mining Radiancite.\nIt was then that I realized the folly of my previous proposal. Though it was not my intention, I too was complicit in the \"forsaking\" of these citizens. Yet I still had to punish them. I assigned them to work in Veridia's union and factories, substituting jail time with gainful employment and allowing them to earn a decent income. I asked Aiina if this was a perversion of the law, and she told me it wasn't; rather, this is the very purpose of the law's existence.\nChapter 3, Article 1.2, regarding the diplomatic policies of the Red Sea Rift.\nBefore outlining this suggestion, please allow me to apologize once more for my previously overzealous views. With the assistance of Lord Radegast and Wolf, I've gained a clearer perspective on the responsibilities of a lord and an Iron Wolf. They've shown me that humanity can unite to rebuild a new world after a major disaster.\nI look forward to the day those efforts come to fruition."}]},{"id":"diary-20708","title":"The Dinner","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"I never thought I'd get a dinner invitation from him, of all people. I always pictured him as someone who would be garrisoned in his dismantling site around the clock, forsaking food and drink in the name of research. Aiina, on the other hand, was delighted. She always likes seeing me mingle with others—although I think it's most likely because it means she gets to escape the training grounds for a while.\nI arrived a little late, and when I pushed the door open, I saw a table covered with all sorts of reports and charts, which made me step back out to double-check if I was in the right place. Thankfully, a plate of lasagna and a platter of grilled sausages were squeezed into a corner of the table, proving he'd at least remembered why we were there.\nWatching him frantically tidy up the papers and then engage in awkward small talk, which seemed like quite an unfamiliar exercise for him, was quite the sight. He asked what I had been up to lately—training, training, more training, fighting the Cabal...and essentially nothing else.\nOut of politeness, I asked about his recent exploits. It seemed he had been waiting for just this opportunity. He pulled out his reports once more and started rambling on. He talked about how he had found code signals on the Sentinel that cannot be traced to any known civilization, how these hollow codes might have their own consciousness, how his mentor was desperately searching for clues right up to her death... Most of the technical terms he used were so alien to me that I drifted off, half-convinced we were still in a Cabal base, with his incessant prattling ringing in my ears.\nLoud, obstinate, and relentless. It's nice to see some things never change.\nWhen I offered to split the bill at the end of the meal, I was surprised to learn from the waiter that my companion had already taken care of it—a surprisingly proactive gesture on his part. I tried to share the cost, but he started making a fuss, ranting about how I'm \"too by-the-book\" and how \"friends don't quibble over the check.\"\nWell then... We're friends now, are we? I must say, it's quite a novel concept for me. In the past, I always sorted people into the categories of lords, civilians, and enemies. This new term—a new fourth category—left me intrigued and somewhat at a loss, keen to delve into its meaning.\nBefore we parted ways, I stopped him and said, \"Next time, I'll treat you to dinner, Kris. I hope you'll bring along more of your findings.\"\nHe looked surprised for a moment, then quickly saluted with his fingers to his forehead and left with a grin."}]},{"id":"diary-11505","title":"Why Me?","sub":"Character diary · Ikora, the Hidden","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_115","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora, the Hidden"},"body":[{"p":"I may put on a highly confident facade in my letters to ???, but I know that I am not as confident as I portray myself.\nPerhaps I should discuss it with Ophiuchus, but...telling others of my weaknesses is itself something I struggle with.\nAnd so I will write to myself. At the end of the day, one cannot harbor secrets from themselves.\n\nSo...am I truly the best person for the job?\nPerhaps I can be calm, objective, and rational—as much as I can, that is. But will the members of the Hidden really support my judgment? They have come here to serve the Iron Lords, to serve Radegast. How will they find me trustworthy? If situations take a turn for the worst, if my choices are at odds with Radegast's...how will they convince themselves to support me as opposed to the founder of the Iron Lords?\nI have always known I am not the most likable of people. But I cannot change myself into someone humorous enough or capable of putting everyone at ease, let alone someone capable of making them smile.\nI am myself—or rather, it is this quality that makes me Ikora Rey.\n\nI will not change myself.\nBecause of that, all I can do is prove myself.\n\nA day will come when, even if they do not like me, they will understand: if they need help, a perspective based in reality, or a solution to their problems—they should seek out Ikora."}]},{"id":"diary-20709","title":"A Farcical Blind Date","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"May the Traveler bless Samantha so that she never introduces me to any more of her \"outstanding Lightbearer friends.\"\nShe's a sweetheart, always kind and caring, but she seems too invested in everyone's love life. She always asks with a worried look and tone about why I'm still single, as if not finding a partner right this instant means I'll die alone and miserable the very next second.\nTo make matters worse, Aiina started echoing her sentiments, urging me to meet this \"friend\" of hers—promising me the person was gentle, considerate, and sensitive. But she deftly changed the subject when I questioned why such a gem hadn't been snapped up yet.\nI reluctantly agreed and added this person's contact information under Samantha's watchful gaze. When I opened my communicator and tried to confirm the location of our date, Samantha's friend—someone with the username \"AAA Alienologist\"—sent several messages at an almost frightening speed.\n\"When can we meet?\"\n\"I can hardly wait! ♥\"\n\"You can bring some stuff from work.\"\n\"Oh, what I mean is, we can talk about your work.\"\n\"To show that I care about you!\"\n...It was uncomfortably forward, almost enough to make me queasy.\nFor once, Aiina wasn't reading over my shoulder. She was instead busy imagining my future married life, even going so far as deciding on a pink pacifier for my future child. Samantha seemed fairly happy as well. All this makes me wonder if I've overlooked such unique people due to my social circle being comprised almost entirely of military personnel.\nWe agreed to meet at a quiet forest-themed restaurant, where a face-to-face explanation and polite rejection seemed appropriate.\nMy mind was filled with endless possible scenarios, and I was even overcome with a sense of nervousness—something I hadn't felt in a long time, even during battles against the Cabal. When the bespectacled man looked at me, it felt as if his eyes were firing lasers from behind his lenses. He stood and shook my hand and asked his first question.\n\"I hear you deal with the Cabal often?\" \nI hesitated for a few seconds before confirming (albeit with some uncertainty), \"Yes... I do.\"\nNearly the second he heard this, he reached into the large backpack behind him and pulled out a pen, a pencil, colored pencils, a recording pen, and three notebooks of different sizes. He then sat rigidly in his seat and asked his second question.\n\"Can you describe, in as much detail as possible, the different types of Cabal you have encountered? Including their typical bodily dimensions, behaviors, interests, and religion. For quantitative data, please round to three decimal places.\"\n...\nThat was the most unbearable meal I'd ever had. For at least two hours, I was constantly answering this \"Alienologist's\" inquiries about the Cabal to, as he put it, help enrich his \"Dark Age Extraterrestrials Index.\"\nWhen he asked me, \"If I were to invite the Cabal to dinner, how much food do you think I should prepare? How fast do they eat? Would they be open to taking a picture with me after dinner?\" I couldn't take it any longer. I stood up and dryly answered, \"All I know is that this meal is over, sir.\"\nHe looked very regretful as he took my hand and repeatedly claimed he was looking forward to seeing me again. He stayed in his chair, watching as I paid for the entire meal and practically fled the restaurant.\nI didn't message him asking for his half of the bill. I was content to delete his contact information as fast as possible.\nWhat an utterly memorable experience—one I'll probably recall vividly fifty years from now. But at least, when I told Samantha all about it, she fell silent for a long while and didn't bring up the topic of relationships again."}]},{"id":"diary-20710","title":"Iron Wolves","sub":"Character diary · Finnala","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_207","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"[An audio clip recorded by Aiina, with some parts obscured by ambient noise]\n\n...\n\"...but Radegast chose you, didn't he? That means you two at least share the same goals. Or are you just following his lead?\"\n\"Of course not. In fact, Radegast and I disagree about quite a few things.\"\n\"As an Iron Wolf?\"\n\"No—as just Wolf. Do you always see eye to eye with Saladin?\"\n\"Of course... The great Iron Lord chose me to become an Iron Wolf. I...\"\n\"Come on, you can be honest with me, Nala.\"\n\"...He's a great leader, yes. But...there are times I just can't see things his way. It's not about being right or wrong, though. We just stand on different ground.\"\n\"Exactly, it's about where you stand. A stand taken by two is an agreement, by twenty a rule, and by two hundred, it becomes law.\"\n\"And if it's just one person?\"\n\"That's an inverted pyramid. The higher you climb, the more you've got to consider.\"\n\"Yes...you're right. Iron Lords stand at the top of that inverted pyramid. They must consider the direction of the entire territory—of humanity as a whole. They must look to the future, not the present.\"\n\"But we can, Nala.\"\n\"We...?\"\n\"Somebody has to support the base of that inverted pyramid. Even if it's sharp and narrow, the whole ideology hinges on it. That's what being an Iron Wolf is all about. I understand your dilemma—you're always trying to help Saladin think about the stance of the Iron Lords, which often leaves you lost in the confusion of these changing times. But in truth, you—we, the Iron Wolves—we've got to look in the directions the Iron Lords cannot see.\"\n\"...You mean...\"\n\"Think of it this way—any Iron Lord confronted with a runaway train would opt to prioritize the track with more lives at stake, but that doesn't mean they've forsaken the minority. For them—at least for Lord Radegast, he trusts that as his Iron Wolf, I can rescue those he can't.\"\n\"...I see what you're saying.\"\n\"Iron Lords choose their Iron Wolves, sure—but we also choose our Iron Lords. Trust your gut, Nala.\"\n\"Thank you, Wolf. I think I've found the answer I've been searching for.\""}]},{"id":"diary-10810","title":"To the Reader","sub":"Character diary · Estela","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_108","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Estela"},"body":[{"p":"To the reader/anyone who's read this far/Wolf,\n\nI don't know whether you'll find this diary or when you will see this. This is the evidence of my crimes, the record of the miseries I have brought and all the disasters I have spread. If anyone is to witness it all, then I hope it is you.\nThe nightmare began when I unknowingly and carelessly made a wish upon an Ahamkara. What I got in return was an unbreakable curse, an incurable wound. It's like snake venom. A self-proclaimed doctor once told me that the most important thing to do after being bitten by a venomous snake is to find out its species. I don't know when I will finally be done paying the price for that wish. All I do know, is my only hope is to find that snake and kill it—that's how I will atone for my endless sins.\nYou've heard their voices, haven't you? Those whispers are like auditory hallucinations, anywhere and everywhere, always finding a way in. When you feel sleepy, they echo in your ears. They're always lurking, desperate to be heard—behind you, in an afternoon shadow, in the reflections of a spoon.\nSo here I beg you: don't listen to them, don't trust their hollow lies, and don't promise them anything.\n\nWolf, I don't know why Bréc called you a \"player,\" but you are my first friend, and thus I trust you.\nIf you have read this diary to its end, you will understand that any attempts to approach me are unwise. I don't want to ruin you, Haven, or your life—they're all too precious.\nThat is why I had to leave the city and everything I cherished. It wasn't anyone's fault; rather, it was the best solution I had.\n\nIf you meet me again one day...please don't greet or approach me. Stay as far away as you can.\nThat is all I ask of you."}]},{"id":"diary-21103","title":"A Calling","sub":"Character diary · Kabr, the Resolute","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_211","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr, the Resolute"},"body":[{"p":"I sometimes still dream of that yellow earth, of the cold luster of armor reflecting light in the sand, of the smell of rust in the air.\nDuring one of our chats, Ikora told me the Vex shouldn't have appeared during our operation in Gibralter—unless, of course, they'd already predicted our mission. It was a premeditated ambush.\nPrediction. What a terrifying word...\nThe Vex are wholly unlike the foes I've encountered before. They record, lie in wait, and mimic. They devour any fragment of data they come into contact with, then gnaw on it until it's fully absorbed, granting them a complete understanding of the universe's creatures. They spread like a virus and lurk in the future, always one step ahead of us.\nThey do not latch onto weaknesses as we understand them, but logic, for thought itself is an Achilles heel.\nThis is the true reason the Vex are a sword hanging above humanity's neck.\nIkora says we have no knowledge of where the Vex came from; what we do know is they have existed since at least a billion years ago, and during their long history, they've latched onto and hollowed out planet after planet, building hidden bases deep in their crusts. In the copy of \"History of the Vex\" she lent me, I even saw mention of special realms they have on Venus and Mercury, independent of time and space.\nTime cannot kill them. It can merely let the dreams of those who've failed linger a while longer.\nI lost too much in that operation. My companions' lives shatter and dissipate like the visions in my blurred dreams. First was Bhate, with that massive beard of his. Then was Lehnin, who ran out of bullets... Louis, then Saina... In the end, even Roberto was powerless against them.\nI haven't felt fear in a long time. Perhaps that wasn't fear, but fury, or hatred...or maybe something else, something capable of making me tremble, something that causes pain to seep from my gums as I grit my teeth.\nSomething referred to as suffering.\nJust as it birthed me, so too did it birth my calling."}]},{"id":"diary-21104","title":"A Fireteam","sub":"Character diary · Kabr, the Resolute","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_211","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr, the Resolute"},"body":[{"p":"Pahanin told me a joke today. He said when he first met Praedyth, he was so nervous he didn't even shake his hand, afraid that Praedyth's Light would vaporize him.\nI laughed and told him how funny it was.\nBut two minutes later, I was really laughing because Praedyth said it was fine—when he first met Pahanin, he thought he was a big-mouthed idiot.\n\"And then?\" Pahanin asked. Praedyth replied that there was no \"and then.\"\nOnce I finished laughing, I asked them, \"Next time, could you not tell such a hilarious joke at the Fallen's front door? Also, which of you is covering me?\"\nMost of the time, our division of duties is very clear. I'm responsible for leading the assault, Praedyth is responsible for clean-up, and Pahanin's responsible for those special sorts of situations. But today, Pahanin thought Praedyth had it too easy, so they started arguing.\nI told them, \"Gentlemen, it doesn't matter who does it as long as we deal with the Fallen before they get right in our faces.\"\nPahanin rushed out, followed closely by Praedyth. They even stripped me of my role as lead, only to hide behind my barrier with their rear ends on fire. In the end, the Jiangshi guerrillas saved us. A kind lady among them consoled us that not every fireteam gets off to a good start—we just needed lots and lots of practice.\n\"Like we've been doing for the last three years?\" Praedyth asked, after which he declared he'd no longer be considering suggestions from idiots.\nPahanin then declared he'd write a book of \"Pahanin quotes,\" recording all of his conversations with us as well as all the insults Praedyth threw his way. The book of quotes would then be passed down forever, ensuring he'd always be remembered.\nThat joke was even funnier than the original. After all, Lightbearers don't age. So long as Praedyth and I are alive, Pahanin will never be forgotten."}]},{"id":"diary-21105","title":"A Revisited Reflection on a Book","sub":"Character diary · Kabr, the Resolute","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_211","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Kabr, the Resolute"},"body":[{"p":"Several passages have been painstakingly copied into the diary. The original reflections have been crossed out, and new text has been written.\n\n\"...But he obstinately believed that the distant sunrise was summoning him. Even though no one, not even himself, had ever seen the reality behind the glow, it burned in his heart like a flame, scorching him day and night. ...So he would fearlessly forge ahead, towards the mountains, towards the rivers, towards the unreachable beyond...\"\n—That's just the sun, isn't it? You can see it just by looking up. In my opinion, smart people don't chase the sun. Only the mysteries of the unknown are worth the journey. Imagine an unprecedented, unique discovery unveiling mysteries during your adventure, a discovery that you would go down in history for—what could possibly be more thrilling than this?\n—It's as Ikora said: the fact that the Vex are already taking premeditated actions against us indicates that the threat they pose to Earth is nearer than ever. What summons us to take action now isn't a concrete thing. Our calling is a matter of humanity's resistance, not just here on Earth, but also on Venus, on Mars, on Io. We shall guard these planets until all \"unchangeable\" futures become paradoxes.\n\n\"...He threw his spear, piercing the teeth and tongues of his enemies. His foes' heads bled, staining the desert sands red. He was so foolish and single-minded, yet also so brave and fearless, that his hulking form served as a banner on the battlefield. Everyone—even those who had hesitated to become his companions—gazed at him and cried out...They gathered around him, reveling in the fervor of their victory...\"\n—Yes! A truly wonderful adventure is one experienced with friends. Who wouldn't want to form a legion of their own? We'd defeat our enemies valiantly, then drink merrily. If I had my own legion, what would I name it...? Think hard, Kabr.\n—Ultimately, I did not name it \"Kabr's Legion.\" Praedyth rejected it outright, though Pahanin agreed to call it \"Kabr, Pahanin, and Praedyth's Legion.\" However, I don't think such a long name would fit on a notice board or leaderboard. Ultimately, we opted to not give ourselves some special name. Nothing fancy, just a fireteam.\n\n\"...It was the end of his journey... He shook his head sorrowfully and lamented—this wasn't his sunrise. His breath was stifled in that blinding, blazing light. His armor, shield, helmet, and belt had melted away, while a searing pain burned through his body... He died in an agonizing struggle, having never embraced the rising sun he'd chased.\"\n—Hmm... I still don't get it even after reading it three times, nor do I like the conclusion. Maybe I should pick a story with a happy ending next time\n—Though I still do not like this ending, it does indeed have its merits. I think I’ll send this book to Praedyth."}]},{"id":"diary-11503","title":"Unread Mail","sub":"Character diary · Ikora, the Hidden","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_115","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Ikora, the Hidden"},"body":[{"p":"Wu Ming >> Ikora Rey\nHowdy, Ikora!\nWhen are you gonna show off in the Iron Bar again?\nWhat I mean is, if you get another hankerin' for a gold medal, be sure to tell yours truly, k?\n\nAlways waiting for you at the tavern,\nWu Ming\n\nWu Ming >> Ikora Rey\nHey, Ikora.\nHow do you feel about this Wednesday? Third day of the week... Three's a pretty lucky number, wouldn't you say?\n\nStill waiting for the reigning champ to take her crown,\nWu Ming\n\nWu Ming >> Ikora Rey\nIkora, we're both smart cookies, so let's drop the pretense, yeah?\nIf you're willing to give a rising star a chance at the big leagues, I'll give you a rather sizeable \"consolation prize.\"\nYou pickin' up what I'm puttin' down?\n\nTan-2 >> Ikora Rey\nHi Ikora!\nI swear, that fight outside the city had nothing to do with me! I'll swear on anything, and I mean ANYTHING!\nYou know me, I'd never go looking for trouble! Those jerks definitely got the wrong guy. People always have a hard time telling Exos apart!\n\nHonest and law-abiding,\nTan-2\n\nSagira >> Ikora Rey\nI can't stand another second in this library!\nI wanna leave. Let ??? wait for the apocalypse with his books for all I care!\nListen, Ikora. I'll arrive in Haven in five days. Can you keep it a secret for me?\nAlso, if I haven't arrived in five days, be sure to come find me.\n\n??? >> Ikora Rey\nWhat do you think of the views presented in the book I sent you, \"Finding Light in the Darkness\"?\nI would quite like to hear your thoughts.\nHowever, I must remind you: be careful not to mention this book or its author to anyone. I do not wish to get on the Praxics' bad side. You have no idea how meddlesome they are."}]},{"id":"diary-30101","title":"Docking","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"Haven. Two thousand four hundred people. Less than a quarter can hold a gun. Three earthen ramparts. Six watchtowers.\nFallen vanguard: eighty kilometers northeast. Their forward units never probe. They hit walls head-on.\nBut Saladin deployed two mobile patrols to the northeast. The man's instincts are more reliable than the walls. The files underrated him. I'll correct it in the report.\n\nAt night, by the gangway. An old man mending a coat. A tiny oil lamp. Crooked stitches. Beside him, a child holding another lamp—motionless, like it was routine.\nI watched for a long time.\n\nThe Reef has no night. The artificial star is nailed to the sky, its face never shifts. Here the dark is real. In the dark: one lamp, one waiting child, one half-mended coat.\nI counted stitches. Stopped halfway.\nTurned. Walked two steps. Looked back.\nThe lamp was still on."}]},{"id":"diary-30104","title":"Nyx","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"When the Ahamkara spine went into the furnace, it sang. Not a sound. The trembling of a wish heated to its breaking point - old wishes. The sailors'. For travelers' safety. For children to survive winter.\nThe Void crystal went in. The singing stopped. Not fading. Silenced, pressed down. The crystal doesn't answer wishes. Inside it sat something heavier than silence. The old sailors say there's an invisible face behind the Void. They call it Nyx. I spoke that name to it. Not naming. Confirming.\nIt answered.\nSix hours. Furnace opened. No light inside. The light had been eaten.\nPhantom Edge lay in the center of the ashes. A streak of black in the spine - the crystal hadn't melted. It had cracked itself into the blade. That cross-section didn't reflect light, wasn't black either. Stare at it more than three seconds, and silence seeps from the other side.\nGrip the hilt. Something crawls across the skin. It confirming a touch. Fingertip to wrist bone, a cold that isn't cold.\nAfter that, every sheath-opening, that half-second arrived on time. The blade leaves the sheath, sound halves, shadows deepen one layer.\nShe wasn't looking at me. Her gaze just happened to fall."}]},{"id":"diary-30105","title":"Faded","sub":"Character diary · Siorra","quality":null,"art":"img_story_diary_301","filters":{"Kind":"Character diary","Character":"Siorra"},"body":[{"p":"I had a strange dream last night.\n\nIn the dream, I stood somewhere I didn't recognize. Cold light, like an archive before dawn. Someone was flipping through records—a scholar, or a historian, hard to say. His finger slid along a page and stopped at a name.\n\nSjur Eido. Queen's Wrath. The ink was clear, sharp, like it was engraved.\n\nHe nodded and kept flipping. His finger paused. There was a blank space. Not redacted. Not torn out. Just empty.\nThen he closed the book and left. No frown. No hesitation. Didn't even realize he'd skipped something.\n\nWhen I woke, Shimmer was hovering by the bed, asking what was wrong. I said I had a dream. It said it couldn't interpret dreams. I said I didn't need it to.\n\nSjur would probably take a dream like this seriously. Her dreams were always accurate. I didn't want to take it seriously.\nBut the dream was crystal clear when I woke. That blank space should have had a name..."}]},{"id":"story-20426","title":"Game of Cat and Mouse","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Key in hand, Umeko rushes to the Space Fortress with the now-conscious Wolf hot on her heels.\nJust as she's about to take back the member list, Wolf catches up to her...only for the two to be forced into a temporary alliance when the Fallen surround them. Once all the enemies have been dealt with, though, Umeko goes invisible. She attempts to leave with the member list, but Zev's scan reveals her. After a \"friendly\" exchange, Wolf takes the \"blueprint\" back from Umeko."}]},{"id":"story-20820","title":"Missing Person","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Veridia has welcomed a new guest—wait, Lady Efrideet should have arrived in the Red Sea Rift three days ago! But Saladin has yet to hear so much as a word from her...\nWith Lady Efrideet having found herself in some sort of trouble, Wolf volunteers to help locate her."}]},{"id":"story-210402","title":"Sandsea Heist","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Using Wolf's intel and some \"special\" artillery she procured from the black market, Maru seizes the truck of Radiancite and deems Wolf a trustworthy partner. She also begins making preparations for her ultimate plan."}]},{"id":"story-20821","title":"Efrideet","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"After Wolf defeated Zau'ul, the remaining Cabal legion garrisoned in the Boneyard fell into chaos, with the first site affected being their coliseum.\nFaced with the threat of runaway foes, Efrideet must take them out as quickly as possible—with a little help from her new sidekick, of course."}]},{"id":"story-10231","title":"The Omen","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Wolf receives a message from Finnala. It seems another threat now looms over the Red Sea Rift..."}]},{"id":"story-10176","title":"The Wind is Rising","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"With global communications fully restored, the Lightbearers begin planning their next attack on the House of Devils' base."}]},{"id":"story-20822","title":"A Lord's Life","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Efrideet wishes to make a request of Saladin, but the latter must first see to his duties as Iron Lord before discussing it with her."}]},{"id":"story-20701","title":"Vanishing Act","sub":"Character story · Finnala","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"Finnala invades Firebase Minos to rescue scouts from Cabal captivity, and one of them informs her of a strange metal the enemy seems to be frequently transporting into the base."}]},{"id":"story-10232","title":"Other-Side Echoes","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Through the intel Harrow left behind and a series of adventures, Wolf learns that the true threat in the Boneyard is an Ahamkara, Njorun. She now voraciously feeds on the wishes of Sand Eater Valus Zau'ul and her soldiers in hopes of reviving herself."}]},{"id":"story-20824","title":"Formalities","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Now, the primary obstacle in Efrideet's plans is Radegast. She must persuade him, but she soon realizes that simply meeting with Radegast will pose quite the challenge."}]},{"id":"story-20826","title":"A Normal Day","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"With her Reunion Day plans a bust, Efrideet decides to give Radegast a piece of her mind. But along the way, she finds herself surprisingly reuniting with some old friends..."}]},{"id":"story-20902","title":"\"Besiege Wei, Rescue Zhao\"","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Xuan Wei intends to set off on his journey once more, but he discovers the Cabal launching an attack on Veridia. Taking advantage of the Cabal's blind spot and attacking from behind, he breaks the siege of Veridia. In doing so, however, he finds out that his former subordinate, Agni, has also come to Veridia. He returns to town to meet her."}]},{"id":"story-210401","title":"Take the Bait","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"While passing through Veridia, Wolf volunteers to investigate a recent string of Radiancite thefts. Questioning and evidence both point the Lightbearer to a shifty resident, and following him reveals he's trading with a Ghost named Parrot. Wolf and Zev help Parrot collect Cabal armor in exchange for the stolen Radiancite, and the pair are ultimately introduced to his \"captain,\" Maru. She invites Wolf to play a card game and wins, albeit by cheating. As per their agreement, Wolf must provide intel on Cabal shipment of Radiancite—as well as half a truckload of the ore itself."}]},{"id":"story-20103","title":"To the Other Side","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"After the mix-up, Tan-2 tells Wolf that he needs Wolf's help to enter the Lanyue 5 factory in Jiangshi Metro, as it contains crucial information that would help Haven against the Fallen."}]},{"id":"story-10161","title":"New Target","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Mishra provides information regarding an artifact from the Fallen's home planet, Riis."}]},{"id":"story-20101","title":"Teen Trouble","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf meets a young Lightbearer named Tan-2 in Haven, who acts a little weird. Tan-2 seems to search for Wolf, unaware that the warm-hearted Lightbearer before him is the person he seeks."}]},{"id":"story-20504","title":"Operation: Rescue","sub":"Character story · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"The scribe's vague words left Kabr suspecting the scribe colluded with the Fallen to kidnap the Iron Bard and ruin the opening ceremony. The intrepid adventurer boldly delved into the sewers and fought tooth and nail to rescue Skorri... But little did he know, he would be in for quite the shock."}]},{"id":"story-20102","title":"Tan-2","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Tan-2 enters the Lanyue 5 factory. Guided by Yannick-11, an alien consciousness sharing their memory core, Tan-2 reaches a hidden lab deep within the factory. There, he finds an important recording and discovers that the lab is where Yannick conducts their research on transferring consciousness to other Exos."}]},{"id":"story-20502","title":"The Golden Drama","sub":"Character story · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"Kabr ventured to Haven to meet Iron Bard Skorri, who he'd looked up to for quite some time, yet the person he met was the bard's scribe. The scribe, worried over posters for the Iron Bar's opening ceremony, asked Kabr to help. Thus did Kabr travel to the Fallen-infested Old City Theater in search of samples."}]},{"id":"story-10191","title":"Bygone Shadows","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"The Ahamkara-corrupted Iron Lord Gareth was once a friend and ally of Radegast and Saladin. Several years ago, Radegast personally caused Gareth's final death, causing a rift between himself and Saladin. Now, Lord Saladin seems to be similarly possessed by a mysterious power, growing more stubborn by the day. Wolf and Finnala have attacked the Sand Eaters' Foundry, but this is far from enough."}]},{"id":"story-20104","title":"Pre-Operation Prep","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"To separate from Yannick's consciousness and end their current state of coexisting in the same body, Tan-2 follows Yannick's instructions, travels to Jiangshi Metro to find a usable energy source, activates his Relic, and prepares for the separation procedure."}]},{"id":"story-20106","title":"Severance Split","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"As Tan-2 prepares for the consciousness separation procedure, he returns to the lab where he'd previously found his Relic. However, this is part of Yannick-11's plot to erase him and take over his body. The two have a falling out and begin fighting for control. Yet when great danger approaches, Yannick ultimately chooses to protect Tan and disappears as a result."}]},{"id":"story-20108","title":"Retrace","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Recognizing Yannick's importance, Tan-2 decides to return to the lab. With Wolf's assistance, Tan accesses the database to search for traces of Yannick among the vast array of data fragments. After uncovering Yannick's past, Tan successfully locates Yannick's consciousness and re-imports it into their own memory core."}]},{"id":"story-10192","title":"Violent Explosion","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf and Veridia launch attacks from all sides, catching the Sand Eaters off guard and hijacking one of their Goliath Tanks."}]},{"id":"story-20702","title":"Unexpected Guests","sub":"Character story · Finnala","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"Now knowing that the metal the Cabal were transporting is typically used to make large war machines, Finnala returns to the firebase to conduct an investigation. There, she encounters a strange human named Kris, and the two manage to get a copy of the Cabal's plans."}]},{"id":"story-20712","title":"Urgent Mission","sub":"Character story · Finnala","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"The mysterious man provides a new location for the shield generator and demands Rossi-11 destroy it."}]},{"id":"story-210404","title":"Negotiation Prep","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Wolf brings Maru to meet Kevarrh. After gaining information on Baron Epakesk, she gets to work laying a new plan. She uses a captured Servitor to lure the Baron into a negotiation, and after overcoming his malicious \"test,\" the unlikely collaborators set their sights on the dangerous Cabal firebase."}]},{"id":"story-10177","title":"Operation: Avenging Arrow","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf infiltrates Issakis's hideout and accidentally witnesses his ascension."}]},{"id":"story-20506","title":"A Lapse in Judgment","sub":"Character story · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"The Iron Bard gave Kabr two choices, and ultimately, he came to a decision. What he didn't know was that a \"dramatic development\" awaited him—one he'd always dreamed of, yet never could have predicted."}]},{"id":"story-201002","title":"The Belly of the Beast","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"The Sand Eaters stumbled upon an underground Golden Age arsenal, within which are nanobot-armed missiles capable of destroying any metal object with ease. Jolder and her apprentices Rhea and Lesnar manage to catch up to the Sand Eaters as they're attempting to transport the weapons, defeating the commander and narrowly escaping an explosion within the arsenal."}]},{"id":"story-210406","title":"Temporary Alliance","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"As per the arrangement, Maru and the Baron's lackeys attack the firebase together. After a tough fight, they manage to steal the Radiancite alloy, but the Baron suddenly changes his tune. Maru, who had been planning to seize the opportunity to hijack the Fallen Skiff, has no choice but to fight the Baron."}]},{"id":"story-20501","title":"Gathering a Fireteam","sub":"Character story · Xuan Wei","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Xuan Wei"},"body":[{"p":"Hoping to rally a fireteam, Wolf and Zev decide to check out the tavern. There, they meet a youthful and energetic Lightbearer named Kabr, who is eager to share tales of his adventures. From how he describes it, he's lived through many an interesting experience..."}]},{"id":"story-201001","title":"One of a Kind","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"The famed Iron Champion Jolder and her two apprentices have just returned to Veridia from an expedition. They're given no time to rest, though, for a new problem has reared its head: Sand Eater soldiers have appeared at the Weathered Caves. Jolder easily eliminates them, but their goal remains a mystery..."}]},{"id":"story-20816","title":"Eradication","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"At last, Estela has found the core of Zelpachad's power, the one thing that can truly kill her: her skull. Zelpachad's attempt at using an endlessly looping mirage to trap her has ended in failure. At the last minute, Zelpachad leaves behind a terrible curse by making a wish to herself: whosoever kills her shall be met with an immense defeat. Wolf acts faster than Estela and destroys Zelpachad's skull in a blaze of Solar Light...and in doing so agrees to bear the burden of this hidden danger."}]},{"id":"story-20703","title":"The Puppet","sub":"Character story · Finnala","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"Kris brings the plans back to his lab for analysis, but he soon finds himself under Cabal siege, leaving Finnala no choice but to rescue him. Though the mechanic seemed to be a trustworthy ally, Aiina discovers an unexpected secret in Kris's terminal..."}]},{"id":"story-20421","title":"\"The Whisperers\"","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Wolf and Zev receive a distress message coming from the Old City, but upon arriving, they find only a body. As they are having a closer look, a Lightbearer claiming to be the deceased's companion appears. Wolf and Zev leave the body with her.\nOnce Wolf leaves, however, the \"companion's\" attitude changes, revealing not all is as it seems. It turns out that she and her Ghost are members of a secret organization known as the Whisperers, and this deceased \"companion\" was a traitor who fled with a stolen list of members. The pair have come to take back the list."}]},{"id":"story-210304","title":"Space Rescue","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Gwynn and Attal venture into the Fallen's space fortress to save the kidnapped captain. Once they find him, though, Gwynn realizes his is a familiar face."}]},{"id":"story-20704","title":"Final Decision","sub":"Character story · Finnala","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"The Light bomb in the firebase is seemingly ready to be deployed. Finnala must find a way to dismantle it, but she can't do it alone. After careful consideration, she chooses to place her trust in the \"traitor.\""}]},{"id":"story-20710","title":"Rossi-11","sub":"Character story · Finnala","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"Wolf receives a request from Finnala to rescue some mining truck drivers and investigate an unfamiliar Lightbearer who often lends a hand."}]},{"id":"story-20422","title":"Fox-Faced Operative","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Umeko heads to Jiangshi Metro in search of the traitor Lor's Ghost. She unexpectedly runs into Wolf, but she exercises caution and chooses not to approach. Once she gets a lead on the list, however, she discovers a surprising overlap between her target and Wolf's—the member list and the orbital railgun blueprints Haven is after have been mixed together.\nAlthough the Whisperer headquarters have yet to issue further instructions, Umeko and Kara make the prompt decision to trick Wolf into trusting them and taking them to Haven. Once they get more information, they'll decide how to proceed."}]},{"id":"story-20711","title":"Mask of Anonymity","sub":"Character story · Finnala","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"The mysterious man contacts Rossi-11 again. Using MacDuff's location as a bargaining chip, he demands Rossi-11 deal with a Cabal shield generator."}]},{"id":"story-20713","title":"Choose Again","sub":"Character story · Finnala","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Finnala"},"body":[{"p":"Shira sends a request for aid, hoping that Rossi-11 can rescue the trapped mining truck once again."}]},{"id":"story-20431","title":"Guest from the West","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Abaca from Veridia asks Wolf to look into the disappearance of some mining trucks. While on the job, Wolf encounters an unfamiliar Lightbearer investigating the same case.\nThe two Lightbearers, keeping their guard up, exchange information. Wolf ultimately decides to let the Lightbearer investigate with them to avoid unnecessary disruptions for both of them."}]},{"id":"story-20901","title":"A Ferocious Army","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf receives a request from Saladin to investigate strange Cabal movements at the Weathered Caves near Veridia. During the investigation, a strong, hulking Lightbearer appears and offers timely assistance. He calls himself Xuan Wei and claims to be searching for a place without war. Having helped Wolf, he bids farewell and leaves to continue his journey."}]},{"id":"story-20904","title":"Tiger's Prey","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Xuan Wei and Agni infiltrate the Cabal's firebase in search of a shearing module that can cut the Light barrier component they need from Sentinel wreckage. They encounter the Psion technician Zekhiir, and Agni discovers that the Light-suppressing technology he's developing may disable Veridia's barrier. They must stop him before it's too late."}]},{"id":"story-20906","title":"The Tiger's Protection","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Saladin and Wolf attack Zekhiir's production line. However, they have played right into the Psion's hand, leaving only Xuan Wei and Agni to protect Veridia. Unfortunately, Zekhiir gets the upper hand by luring Xuan Wei into a trap and holding him in place with Light-suppressing mines. But just in the nick of time, Agni uses the reverse engineered Light Suppressor she's developed to restore and empower Xuan Wei's connection to the Light. Ultimately, Zekhiir falls to Xuan Wei's fists."}]},{"id":"story-10153","title":"Emergency","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf heads to Jiangshi Metro to establish contact with the guerrillas and work towards restoring communication between Jiangshi and Haven."}]},{"id":"story-10154","title":"Iceclad Land","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf and Ayuela investigate the secrets behind the device controlling the weather."}]},{"id":"story-10155","title":"Imminent Storm","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf's fireteam eliminates the Fallen operating the Fulminator."}]},{"id":"story-10156","title":"Beneath the Ice","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf meets a fellow Lightbearer named Ikora, who is investigating the Hive, and the two fight these new foes in the Ascendant Realm."}]},{"id":"story-10157","title":"The Choice of Ikora Rey","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Ikora and Radegast disagree over whether to make the Hive's existence public knowledge. Ultimately, Ikora agrees to do things Radegast's way."}]},{"id":"story-10162","title":"Kevarrh's Loyalty","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"With Kevarrh's help, Wolf retrieves the artifact—a powerful weapon—from the crashed Ketch."}]},{"id":"story-10163","title":"Rekindling the Spark","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"The weapon is overloaded and damaged. Now, Wolf has to find a way to repair it."}]},{"id":"story-10164","title":"Hero's Trial I","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"With help from Xûr, Wolf retrieves a weapon component from the Realm of the Nine."}]},{"id":"story-210301","title":"Ice Field Phantoms","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"One of the Jiangshi guerrillas, Denzin, tells Wolf about a squad and a Lightbearer named Attal who went missing. Wolf heads to the Ice Field to investigate and encounters another Lightbearer, Gwynn, and the two discover the Hive have opened a new portal beneath the ice."}]},{"id":"story-210302","title":"Unexpected Guests","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Attal tells Gwynn that a new group of humans have appeared in Jiangshi Metro, but they're now under Fallen siege. The two rescue them and learn that their captain—a fellow Lightbearer—was taken by the Fallen."}]},{"id":"story-210306","title":"Unforgivable Sins","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"To determine whether the captain still remembers his past, Gwynn leaves a series of signals. Sure enough, the captain appears, and Gwynn gives chase. The captain must atone for his sins, and Gwynn's blade will decide his fate."}]},{"id":"story-20401","title":"Jiangshi Anomalies","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Mu Ying enlists Wolf to investigate Jiangshi's broken barriers. It is there that Wolf discovers Ning Fei to be the architect of this chaos, driven by his search for a certain Ketch."}]},{"id":"story-201003","title":"Ripples","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"The Sand Eaters haven't let the previous setback stop them from carrying out their plan to transport the warheads. Jolder fights them across the Red Sea Rift, intercepting and destroying two of the missiles. But during the battle, she discovers the Splicers have also come to the Rift to try seizing this dangerous technology for themselves. After she reports her findings to Lord Saladin, she has no choice but to tell Rhea and Lesnar that the selection of the next Iron Champion will have to be delayed, which the two apprentices are quite unhappy about."}]},{"id":"story-20403","title":"Headache","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"To test the chip's ability to nullify the headband's torment, Ning Fei installs it without Claudia's knowledge in the Lanyue 5 Factory's control room, and then proves its efficacy by staging an act of defiance to enrage her. This results in a rift forming between the pair."}]},{"id":"story-20404","title":"A Qualified Lightbearer","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Ning Fei stumbles upon a trove of damaged chips at a Jiangshi Metro laboratory and uncovers the fate of the missing civilians through a hologram. The two of them follow the clues to find the people whisked away by the Servitor. After triumphing over the Servitor, they witness a new hologram unveiling Ning Fei's past before he became a Lightbearer and the truth behind the illusions."}]},{"id":"story-202313","title":"Journey 1","sub":"Character story · Kabr","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Kabr"},"body":[{"p":"Journey 1"}]},{"id":"story-20406","title":"Ning Fei","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Together, Ning Fei and Claudia board the Ketch in search of a chip possessing the ability to block the headband's illusions. But within the Ketch, the Servitor ensnares Ning Fei in an illusory world using his headband. With Claudia's guidance, Ning Fei conquers the illusion, vanquishing the Servitor lurking in the Ketch's depths and seizing the chip."}]},{"id":"story-20405","title":"The Price of Heroics","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Ning Fei, now with his chip removed, plunges back into the illusion and discovers that the Servitor has brought the kidnapped civilians to the space elevator's base. Awakened, Ning Fei and Wolf unite to free them."}]},{"id":"story-210310","title":"Gwynn","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Gwynn enters the Hive portal to save Attal. It's connected to part of the Ascendant Realm, ruled by Ir Eruna. The Wizard tries to tempt Gwynn into becoming a pawn in her ritual, which would turn her into a Sword Logic vessel. The Wizard underestimates Gwynn's strength, though, and meets her end while attempting to flee."}]},{"id":"story-201005","title":"Unwelcome Visit","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"The Sand Eaters are hit with a covert assault from the Splicers while storing the nanobot-armed warheads in Firebase Minos. Jolder and her apprentices seize the opportunity and fight their way into the firebase to disarm the missiles, and during the chaos, Rhea and Lesnar hijack a Harvester and fly it back to Veridia. To their surprise, however the cabin is filled with nanobot-armed spider droids. Luckily, Jolder makes it back to Veridia just in time to disarm them, preventing a potential catastrophe."}]},{"id":"story-201007","title":"Close Call","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Jolder and Lord Radegast rendezvous at the Jiangshi Metro Weather Control Facility, where they must stop the Splicers from using the center's technology to spread nanobots throughout the atmosphere. Rhea and Lesnar pilot the Harvester they hijacked to aid their mentor in battle, but the Splicers' Remnant Captain Depikis manages to activate the weather controller before they can stop him. In a last-ditch effort, the apprentices risk their Ghosts being eaten alive and crash the ship into the machine. Fortunately, the nanobots hadn't yet activated, and the three Lightbearers avert the crisis without casualty.\nUpon their return to Haven, Jolder finally hosts the selection ceremony to decide the next Iron Champion, but neither Rhea nor Lesnar end up inheriting the title. Instead, they become Lady Jolder's Iron Wolves, and the Iron Champion is made history."}]},{"id":"story-20411","title":"Haunting in Haven?","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Residents near Haven's bazaar have asked Wolf to look into some strange noises they've been hearing. The trail of clues eventually reveals Attal to be the source. To Wolf's surprise, she's studying the Fallen's language."}]},{"id":"story-20412","title":"Strange Eliksni","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Attal tells Wolf of a unique Eliksni she met in Jiangshi Metro—an adult Fallen whose House had seemingly been decimated by the Devils—and how her attempt at friendly communication was a success."}]},{"id":"story-10165","title":"Hero's Trial II","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf retrieves the other weapon component from Morgran's hunting grounds."}]},{"id":"story-20414","title":"None to Rely On","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Some time later, Attal encountered the unique Eliksni survivor in Jiangshi Metro again. This time, though, she also met several Eliksni children. They had lost their Servitor, and without Ether, they were facing starvation... Naturally, Attal agreed to help the survivor gather materials to repair a Servitor."}]},{"id":"story-10166","title":"Reforging","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"The weapon is repaired, and the Satiyaaliksni Smart Bomb finds new life in Wolf's hands."}]},{"id":"story-20416","title":"Reliance and Pandora's Box","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Attal explains how the story ended. The Servitor the survivor wanted to fix went berserk, and if left unchecked, Jiangshi Metro may be hit by a massive, unpredictable explosion. Unfortunately, the survivor wasn't willing to let Attal defeat the rampaging Servitor..."}]},{"id":"story-10001","title":"The City of Light","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"A new Lightbearer wakes in the Old City ruins..."}]},{"id":"story-10002","title":"A Great Expedition","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf infuses the Sentinel's Light into the Relic. Its name shall be Wolf's Howl."}]},{"id":"story-10168","title":"Surge of Memories","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf and Ayuela solve the puzzle that her mother, Alechio, left behind and gain a crucial lead on the quantum tuner."}]},{"id":"story-10173","title":"Quantum Hunt","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Radegast makes a visit to Jiangshi Metro and helps Wolf seize the quantum tuner from the Fallen."}]},{"id":"story-10174","title":"Unexpected Twist","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf's next objective: an assault on the House of Devils-occupied Space Elevator."}]},{"id":"story-20424","title":"Among \"Wolves\"","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Umeko feigns being a lonely Lightbearer to join Wolf's mission of bringing the railgun blueprints back. In doing so, she secures the key to the Space Fortress.\nOnce they've finished, Umeko invites Wolf to Haven's \"Bad Old Time\" tavern under the guise of a celebratory drink. Wolf happily accepts."}]},{"id":"story-10175","title":"Into the Chasm","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf's fireteam enters the bottom of the Space Elevator and defeats the Prime Servitor, Umbliks. During the mission, they also learn that the House of Devils are building a fortress at the top of the elevator."}]},{"id":"story-10178","title":"The Guarding Triad","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"The House of Devils fortress, dubbed \"Eclipse Monolith,\" is headed by the Splicers' Archpriest, Issakis. To take him on, the Lightbearers must first eliminate his three primary defenses."}]},{"id":"story-20801","title":"Anonymous Message","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Ikora receives a cryptic signal from the Old City Library. She arrives at the signal's source only to find a barrier blocking the way. Fortunately, she is able to break the barrier with her Super, rescuing the signal's source, a Ghost named Sagira."}]},{"id":"story-20803","title":"The Prophet's Voice","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Ikora finds symbols left by ??? in Jiangshi Metro. Following the clues leads her to a portal into the Ascendant Realm."}]},{"id":"story-20805","title":"Conspiracy","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"With ???'s guidance, Ikora enters the Ascendant Realm and destroys the altars used to summon Crota, putting an end to the Hive's scheme."}]},{"id":"story-20432","title":"Deception","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Jaren pretends he's looking to enter the Radiancite smuggling business and gets a lead in Veridia: a boy raised by unemployed miners who is seeking help.\nJaren feigns willingness to help him and gains a key piece of information while heading to the cave to rescue the missing miners. Having learned the boy is connected to the target Jaren is investigating, he changes his attitude prior to beginning the rescue, demanding the boy help him get in contact with an extremely dangerous smuggler.\nThe boy has no choice but to agree to Jaren's demands if he wants the miners saved—but he isn't being entirely honest himself. He tricks Jaren into going further into the caves so he can escape with the miners. What the kid doesn't know, however, is that Jaren has already planned for this..."}]},{"id":"story-20434","title":"Iron Hand","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Jaren follows his tracker to Bobak and the missing miners' hiding spot and demands they cooperate with his plan: using the Radiancite as a cover to lure the target \"Maln\" to a trade.\nTo make the trade seem more realistic, Bobak leads Jaren to the Cabal-controlled Sandy Mines, where they can acquire enough Radiancite for the deal."}]},{"id":"story-20436","title":"Salvation","sub":"Character story · Jolder","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Jolder"},"body":[{"p":"Maln sees through the trap. He invites Jaren to the quarry for a final duel while also telling him he's trapped Bobak and the miners in the Foundry, where they could be in grave danger... As expected, Jaren decides to save them first, despite both him and Hartford knowing full well that Maln is bound to have a deadly trap waiting for them.\nSure enough, Maln's trap springs as Jaren is rescuing Bobak and his uncles. Jaren's Light is suppressed, significantly hindering his ability to fight. If Jaren were to head to the quarry for his duel with Maln in this condition..."}]},{"id":"story-10181","title":"Red Sea Reinforcements","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Radegast sends Wolf to the Red Sea Rift to reestablish contact with fellow Iron Lord Saladin, whose territory of Veridia is facing an invasion at the hands of the Cabal's Sand Eaters."}]},{"id":"story-20810","title":"Pandora's Box","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Wolf and Zev head to the Echo Grotto as part of an investigation to some mysterious Cabal cargo, but things take a turn for the bizarre once they intercept the box, and they find the space around them has seemingly transformed into an endless loop with no exit. A Lightbearer named Estela appears and informs Wolf that the loop is actually an Ahamkara's trap, and the two soon discover the box to be holding an Ahamkara bone."}]},{"id":"story-10193","title":"Path of Awakening","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Harrow shows Wolf her past and scenes within a dream. Summoned by an unknown entity, she must journey to the Red Sea Rift's depths to unravel the mystery."}]},{"id":"story-20811","title":"Estela","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Estela follows the trail left by an unfamiliar Ahamkara, which brings her to a Cabal mine overtaken by chaos. The Ahamkara's power has a grip on each and every soldier, and just as Estela goes to destroy the source of the magic, it influences her, too. Estela must confront her deepest fears if she is to have any hope of defeating the Ahamkara."}]},{"id":"story-20812","title":"Trance","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"As she hunts Zelpachad, Estela encounters a distraught father named Merlo making a wish to the Ahamkara, and she decides to help him find his missing daughter, Nora. In the course of her search, though, Estela finds the young girl has made her own wish..."}]},{"id":"story-10182","title":"Enigma","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Veridia's union president Harrow has mysterious predictive abilities. With Wolf's help, she acquires a strange box."}]},{"id":"story-20814","title":"Shadow","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"To destroy the wishing altar in the Red Sea Rift and prevent any further tragedies from unfolding, Estela completes three trials meant to prove she is a suffering wisher and trick the altar into letting her enter. However, she finds an unexpected guest there: Wolf. Together, they destroy the altar."}]},{"id":"story-21001","title":"The Guest","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"A guest from Felwinter Peak has come to Haven. She tells Wolf that she's received a strange signal using Awoken encryption, and her analysis has shown it to be coming from the Old City. This is an unexplored area of technology, and this signal may be something significant..."}]},{"id":"story-21002","title":"Connection","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"The now-conscious Awoken girl gives Helhest a choice she's been seeking for a long time. After careful consideration, Helhest decides to help upgrade and repair the device. This takes her to the Lanyue factory in search of the Awoken mothership's flight records."}]},{"id":"story-21004","title":"Retrace","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Helhest follows the Awoken mothership's flight records and is brought back to Felwinter Peak. There, she unexpectedly uncovers the truth of her own past."}]},{"id":"story-10183","title":"Silent Wish","sub":"Character story","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":null},"body":[{"p":"Harrow has long been tormented by the wishes of those around her, and any desires she hears will be made reality, albeit in a cruel fashion. This time, a wish invited a new enemy: a mechanical race called the Vex."}]},{"id":"story-21006","title":"Resolve","sub":"Character story · Cassian","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Cassian"},"body":[{"p":"Having resolved to aid the White Queen in summoning all members of the Outreachers, Helhest heads to the Shifting Gate to send a signal and receives an unexpected response."}]},{"id":"story-10201","title":"All In","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Although the Sand Eater threat facing Veridia grows more dire by the day, Saladin still refuses to accept Radegast's help. This leaves Wolf with no choice but to launch a dangerous attack in hopes of turning the tide."}]},{"id":"story-10202","title":"Groundbreaking","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Lord Saladin finally breaks free from the mysterious power's control, and Radegast's reinforcements arrive in Veridia just in time. The Lightbearers unite in an attack that devastates the Sand Eaters' firebase."}]},{"id":"story-10211","title":"Road of Subjugation","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Following the clues Harrow left behind, Wolf and Zev travel to the Red Sea Rift's Boneyard in search of a way to reach Njorun's true hideout."}]},{"id":"story-10212","title":"Mirage","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Wolf and Zev find Harrow in the illusory Leviathan Njorun has created. They learn a way to defeat the Ahamkara, but to do so, they must enter the heart of this \"palace.\""}]},{"id":"story-10213","title":"Edge of Hope","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Despite Zau'ul and the fake Harrow's attempts to stop them, Wolf and Zev finally rendezvous with the real Harrow. During this short reunion, they decide to split up. Harrow will use her connection with Njorun to monitor her within the Leviathan; meanwhile, Wolf will return to Veridia, report what's happened to the Iron Lords, and await Harrow's signal."}]},{"id":"story-10221","title":"Times of Crisis","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Wolf prevents Njorun from using Zau'ul's wish to accomplish her revival, but the crisis is far from over."}]},{"id":"story-10222","title":"Buried Soul, Fettered Bones","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"Wolf witnesses the truth of Harrow's identity inside the Leviathan. Several years ago, she fell from a cliff and, with her dying breath, made a wish to survive. Njorun granted it, and in doing so, turned her body into a vessel for her heart."}]},{"id":"story-10223","title":"Foretold End","sub":"Character story · Ikora","quality":null,"filters":{"Kind":"Character story","Character":"Ikora"},"body":[{"p":"To reach the source of the illusion and kill Njorun for good, Wolf must first explore the floating islands around the Leviathan and find three keys to open the way."}]}];